-네요 -네요 [-neyo] /-neyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to indicate that the speaker is impressed by a fact he/she learned anew from a past personal experience./-neyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to ask the listener for a consent about the speaker's guess or assumption./
-녀 -녀 [-nyeo] /-nyeo — A suffix used to mean a woman./
-년 -년 [-nyeon] /-nyeon — A suffix used to mean the year./
-농 -농 [-nong] /-nong — A suffix used to mean farming or a farmer./
-느냐 -느냐 [-neunya] /-neunya — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending referring to a question./
-느냐거든 -느냐거든 [-neunyageodeun] /-neunyageodeun — An expression used to indicate that the doubt or question raised by another person is the condition or basis for the following statement./
-느냐고 -느냐고 [-neunyago] /-neunyago — (informal addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used when asking a question that was already asked before./-neunyago — (informal addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used when asking again about another person's question./-neunyago — An expression used to convey the questions asked by the speaker or another person./
-느냐고요 -느냐고요 [-neunyagoyo] /-neunyagoyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used when asking a question that was already asked before./
-느냐기에 -느냐기에 [-neunyagie] /-neunyagie — An expression used to cite the question the speaker was asked as the reason or basis for the following statement./
-느냐길래 -느냐길래 [-neunyagilrae] /-neunyagillae — An expression used to cite the question the speaker was asked as the reason or basis for the following statement./
-느냐느니 -느냐느니 [-neunyaneuni] /-neunyaneuni — An expression used to indicate that someone is asking questions this way and that way./
-느냐는 -느냐는 [-neunyaneun] /-neunyaneun — An expression used to quote a certain question, and modify the following statement./
-느냐는구나 -느냐는구나 [-neunyaneunguna] /-neunyaneunguna — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey a question asked by another person to the listener with wonder./
-느냐는군 -느냐는군 [-neunyaneungun] /-neunyaneun-gun — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey the question of another person to the listener./
-느냐는데 -느냐는데 [-neunyaneunde] /-neunyaneunde — An expression used to quote the question the speaker was asked and add the speaker's own thoughts, questions, etc./-neunyaneunde — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to indirectly express what the speaker wants to say by conveying the question the speaker heard./
-느냐는데도 -느냐는데도 [-neunyaneundedo] /-neunyaneundedo — An expression used to convey the question asked by the speaker or another person, and to imply that the following content is different from or opposite to what is expected./
-느냐는데요 -느냐는데요 [-neunyaneundeyo] /-neunyaneundeyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to indirectly express what the speaker wants to say, by quoting the question the speaker was asked./
-느냐니 -느냐니 [-neunyani] /-neunyani — An expression used to quote the question asked by the listener or another person, and to reveal the emotion of the speaker about this./-neunyani — An expression used to convey what the speaker asked another person and add his/her answer or response./
-느냐니까 -느냐니까 [-neunyanikka] /-neunyanikka — An expression used to quote what the speaker asked another person and add his/her response or answer./
-느냐니까는 -느냐니까는 [-neunyanikkaneun] /-neunyanikkaneun — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to repeat the question the speaker asked earlier, when the listener did not answer./-neunyanikkaneun — An expression used to quote the question the speaker or another person asked and add his/her response or answer./
-느냐니까요 -느냐니까요 [-neunyanikkayo] /-neunyanikkayo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to ask the listener again to press, when the listener did not answer or seemed suspicious./
-느냐니깐 -느냐니깐 [-neunyanikkan] /-neunyanikkan — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to repeat the question the speaker asked earlier, when the listener did not answer./-neunyanikkan — An expression used to quote the question the speaker or another person asked and add his/her response or answer./
-느냐니요 -느냐니요 [-neunyaniyo] /-neunyaniyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to indicate that the speaker is surprised to hear the question or asks it again, because it is unexpected./
-느냐더군 -느냐더군 [-neunyadeogun] /-neunyadeogun — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey a question newly heard to the listener./
-느냐더군요 -느냐더군요 [-neunyadeogunyo] /-neunyadeogunyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to convey a question newly heard to the listener./
-느냐더니 -느냐더니 [-neunyadeoni] /-neunyadeoni — An expression used to mention the question asked earlier and continue to talk about a related situation./
-느냐더라고 -느냐더라고 [-neunyadeorago] /-neunyadeorago — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to say the question the speaker remembers from having heard it in person./
-느냐던데 -느냐던데 [-neunyadeonde] /-neunyadeonde — An expression used to mention the question asked by another person and relate it to the following content./-neunyadeonde — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to indirectly express what the speaker wants to say, by conveying someone's question./
-느냐던데요 -느냐던데요 [-neunyadeondeyo] /-neunyadeondeyo — (informal addressee-raising)  An expression used to indirectly say something, by conveying the question the speaker heard earlier, in an unfinished sentence./
-느냐데 -느냐데 [-neunyade] /-neunyade — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey the question asked by another person to the listener./
-느냐디 -느냐디 [-neunyadi] /-neunyadi — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to confirm the question asked by another person to the listener./
-느냐며 -느냐며 [-neunyamyeo] /-neunyamyeo — An expression used to indicate that someone was doing a certain act, while asking a certain question at the same time./
-느냐면 -느냐면 [-neunyamyeon] /-neunyamyeon — An expression used to assume that the preceding statement is asked as a question, and continue the sentence./
-느냐면서 -느냐면서 [-neunyamyeonseo] /-neunyamyeonseo — An expression used to indicate that someone was doing a certain act, while asking a certain question at the same time./
-느냐지만 -느냐지만 [-neunyajiman] /-neunyajiman — An expression used to indicate that the speaker admits the question or objection in the preceding statement, but that the following content is not relevant or opposite to this./
-느냔 -느냔 [-neunyan] /-neunyan — An expression used to quote a certain question, and modify the following statement./
-느냔다 -느냔다 [-neunyanda] /-neunyanda — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey the question heard from another person to the listener./
