-는 것 -는 것 [-neun geos] /-neun geot — An expression used to enable a non-noun word to be used as a noun in a sentence or to be used in front of '이다' (be)./
-는 것 같다 -는 것 같다 [-neun geos gatda] /-neun geot gatda — An expression used to indicate that the statement is a guess./
-는 길에 -는 길에 [-neun gile] /-neun gire — An expression used to indicate the process of or opportunity for a certain thing./
-는 김에 -는 김에 [-neun gime] /-neun gime — An expression used to indicate that one is doing a certain act, after the act mentioned in the preceding statement or while doing a similar behavior at the same time./
-는 대로 -는 대로 [-neun daero] /-neun daero — An expression used to indicate that something is the same as the present act or state mentioned in the preceding statement./-neun daero — An expression used to indicate someone does something upon or soon after the moment of a certain act or state./-neun daero — An expression used to indicate each and every act or state that appears./-neun daero — An expression used to indicate one does something as best as one can./
