-는 둥 마는 둥 -는 둥 마는 둥 [-neun dung maneun dung] /-neun dung maneun dung — An expression used to indicate that one does not do a certain act properly./
-는 듯 -는 듯 [-neun deus] /-neun deut — An expression used to guess that something said might be similar to the preceding state or situation./-neun deut — An expression used to indicate that something is in a state which could be one of two possibilities./
-는 듯싶다 -는 듯싶다 [-neun deussipda] /-neun deutsipda — An expression used to guess the content of the preceding statement./
-는 듯하다 -는 듯하다 [-neun deushada] /-neun deutada — An expression used to guess the content of the preceding statement./
-는 마당에 -는 마당에 [-neun madange] /-neun madang-e — An expression used to indicate that one is in a situation or position where something mentioned in the preceding statement has already occurred./
-는 만큼 -는 만큼 [-neun mankeum] /-neun mankeum — An expression used to indicate that the following content is proportional to the preceding content or of a similar level or quantity./-neun mankeum — An expression used to indicate that the preceding statement is the reason or basis for the following statement./
-는 모양이다 -는 모양이다 [-neun moyangida] /-neun moyang-ida — An expression used to guess that something is in progress or in a certain state, considering another fact or situation./
