-는 줄 -는 줄 [-neun jul] /-neun jul — An expression used to indicate that one either knows or does not know a certain fact or state./
-는 중이다 -는 중이다 [-neun jungida] /-neun jung-ida — An expression used to indicate that a certain thing is in progress./
-는 척하다 -는 척하다 [-neun cheoghada] /-neun cheokada — An expression used to indicate that one is pretending to do something or to be something, which is not true./
-는 체하다 -는 체하다 [-neun chehada] /-neun chehada — An expression used to indicate that one is pretending to do something or to be something, which is not true./
-는 탓 -는 탓 [-neun tas] /-neun tat — An expression used to indicate that the preceding statement is the reason or cause for the following negative phenomenon./
-는 통에 -는 통에 [-neun tonge] /-neun tong-e — An expression used to indicate the situation or cause of the bad result mentioned in the following statement./
-는 편이다 -는 편이다 [-neun pyeonida] /-neun pyeonida — An expression used to indicate that something has a certain tendency or is classified as such, instead of being sure of it./
-는 한 -는 한 [-neun han] /-neun han — An expression used to indicate that the preceding statement becomes the premise or condition for the act or state in the following statement./
