-아 가지고 -아 가지고 [-a gajigo] /-a gajigo — An expression used to indicate that the result or state of the act mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./-a gajigo — An expression used to indicate that the act or state mentioned in the preceding statement is the cause, means, or reason for the following statement./
-아 갖고 -아 갖고 [-a gajgo] /-a gatgo — An expression used to indicate that the result or state of the act mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./-a gatgo — An expression used to indicate that the act or state mentioned in the preceding statement is the cause, means, or reason for the following statement./
-아 계시다 -아 계시다 [-a gyesida] /-a gyesida — (honorific) An expression used to indicate that the state mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./
-아 나가다 -아 나가다 [-a nagada] /-a nagada — An expression used to indicate that the act mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./
-아 내다 -아 내다 [-a naeda] /-a naeda — An expression used to indicate that one has finally accomplished the act mentioned in the preceding statement by oneself./
-아 놓다 -아 놓다 [-a nohda] /-a nota — An expression used to indicate that a certain act mentioned in the preceding statement is completed and its result remains./-a nota — An expression used to stress that the state mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./
-아 달다 -아 달다 [-a dalda] /-a dalda — An expression used to demand that the act mentioned in the preceding statement be carried out./
-아 대다 -아 대다 [-a daeda] /-a daeda — An expression used to indicate that the act mentioned in the preceding statement is repeated or done to a greater degree./
-아 두다 -아 두다 [-a duda] /-a duda — An expression used to indicate that a certain act mentioned in the preceding statement is completed and its result remains./
-아 드리다 -아 드리다 [-a deurida] /-a deurida — (honorific) An expression used to indicate that one does the act mentioned in the preceding statement for a respected person./
-아 버릇하다 -아 버릇하다 [-a beoreushada] /-a beoreutada — An expression used to indicate that one repeats the act mentioned in the preceding statement habitually./
-아 버리다 -아 버리다 [-a beorida] /-a beorida — An expression used to indicate that the act mentioned in the preceding statement is completely done./
-아 보다 -아 보다 [-a boda] /-a boda — An expression used to indicate that one does the act mentioned in the preceding statement, as a test./-a boda — An expression used to indicate that one experienced the act mentioned in the preceding statement earlier./
-아 보이다 -아 보이다 [-a boida] /-a boida — An expression used to indicate that one feels or guesses something by the appearance of something mentioned in the preceding statement./
-아 봤자 -아 봤자 [-a bwassja] /-a bwatja — An expression used to indicate that it is useless anyway to try the act mentioned in the preceding statement./
-아 빠지다 -아 빠지다 [-a ppajida] /-a ppajida — An expression used to indicate that one is displeased with the state mentioned in the preceding statement which is very bad./
-아 오다 -아 오다 [-a oda] /-a oda — An expression used to indicate that the act or state mentioned in the preceding statement is continued as a certain set point of time is approaching./
-아 있다 -아 있다 [-a issda] /-a itda — An expression used to indicate that the state mentioned in the preceding statement is continued./
-아 주다 -아 주다 [-a juda] /-a juda — An expression used to indicate that one does the act mentioned in the preceding statement for someone./
-아 죽다 -아 죽다 [-a jugda] /-a jukda — An expression used to indicate that the state mentioned in the preceding statement is very severe./
-아다 -아다 [-ada] /-ada — A connective ending used when one does a certain act and does the following act based on the result of the preceding one./
-아다가 -아다가 [-adaga] /-adaga — A connective ending used when one does a certain act and does the following act based on the result of the preceding one./
-아도 -아도 [-ado] /-ado — A connective ending used when assuming or recognizing the truth of the preceding statement, although it is not related to or does not influence the following statement./
-아도 되다 -아도 되다 [-ado doeda] /-ado deoda — An expression used to indicate that a certain act is allowed or accepted./
