-옹 -옹 [-ong] /-ong — A suffix used to mean an old person./
-왕 -왕 [-wang] /-wang — A suffix used to mean a person or animal that is at the top of an area or range./
-요 -요 [-yo] /-yo — A connective ending used to list or contrast more than two things or facts./
-욕 -욕 [-yog] /-yok — A suffix used to mean a desire or a craving./
-용 -용 [-yong] /-yong — A suffix used to mean an object used for something or an object for that person./
