-으라든지 -으라든지 [-euradeunji] /-euradeunji — An expression used to choose one out of two orders./-euradeunji — An expression used to indicate that it does not matter whether one chooses any of many orders./
-으라디 -으라디 [-euradi] /-euradi — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to ask the listener what another person ordered or requested./
-으라며 -으라며 [-euramyeo] /-euramyeo — (informal addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used when the speaker confirms and asks questions about what he/she was ordered or demanded to do./-euramyeo — An expression used to question someone's order, recommendation, etc./-euramyeo — An expression used to report that someone was doing a certain act, while giving a certain order at the same time./
-으라면 -으라면 [-euramyeon] /-euramyeon — An expression used to assume that someone will give a certain order, which becomes the condition for the following statement./
-으라면서 -으라면서 [-euramyeonseo] /-euramyeonseo — (informal addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used when the speaker confirms and asks questions about what he/she was ordered or demanded to do./-euramyeonseo — An expression used to question someone's order, recommendation, etc./-euramyeonseo — An expression used to report that someone was doing a certain act, while giving a certain order at the same time./
-으라오 -으라오 [-eurao] /-eurao — (formal, moderately addressee-raising) An expression used to convey another person's order, request, etc./
-으라자 -으라자 [-euraja] /-euraja — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to suggest to the listener that the speaker and the listener demand a certain act from someone else./-euraja — An expression used to convey an order and to indicate that another act or incident occurs, upon the completion of the order./
-으라죠 -으라죠 [-eurajyo] /-eurajyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to confirm the order or request the speaker already knows, and ask a question about it./
-으라지 -으라지 [-euraji] /-euraji — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to ask the listener again about the order or suggestion heard earlier, or express the speaker's thought clearly./-euraji — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used when making sarcastic remarks or saying that the speaker does not care./
-으라지만 -으라지만 [-eurajiman] /-eurajiman — An expression used to admit to the order or request that the speaker heard before, and indicate that it is different from what the speaker thought it was./
-으락 -으락 [-eurag] /-eurak — A connective ending used when two contradictory acts or states repeat in turns./
-으란 -으란 [-euran] /-euran — An expression used to convey a certain order, modifying the following statement./
-으란다 -으란다 [-euranda] /-euranda — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey someone's order to the listener./
-으랄 -으랄 [-eural] /-eural — An expression used to convey an order, whose content modifies the following statement./
-으람 -으람 [-euram] /-euram — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used when asking oneself or complaining about a certain order or request./
-으랍니까 -으랍니까 [-eurabnikka] /-euramnikka — (formal, highly addressee-raising) An expression used to ask the listener about the order he/she already knows from having heard it./
-으랍니다 -으랍니다 [-eurabnida] /-euramnida — (formal, highly addressee-raising) An expression used to convey another person's order, request, etc./
-으랍디까 -으랍디까 [-eurabdikka] /-eurapdikka — (formal, highly addressee-raising) An expression used to ask the listener about the question the listener heard before./
-으랍디다 -으랍디다 [-eurabdida] /-eurapdida — (formal, moderately addressee-raising) An expression used to convey the order the speaker heard earlier./
-으래 -으래 [-eurae] /-eurae — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to convey another person's order, request, etc./-eurae — (informal addressee-lowering) An expression used to ask the listener about the order, request, etc., the listener already knows from having heard it./
-으래도 -으래도 [-euraedo] /-euraedo — An expression used to indicate that, despite the order or request to do a certain act, an irrelevant or opposing content follows in the sentence./
-으래라 -으래라 [-euraera] /-euraera — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) An expression used to tell someone to convey a certain order./
-으래서 -으래서 [-euraeseo] /-euraeseo — An expression used to indicate that the following content is based on the order heard from another person./
-으래서야 -으래서야 [-euraeseoya] /-euraeseoya — An expression used to convey an order and to question or make a negative judgment on it./
-으래야 -으래야 [-euraeya] /-euraeya — An expression used to indicate that the preceding statement, such as an order, request, etc., is the requirement for the following statement./
-으래요 -으래요 [-euraeyo] /-euraeyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to indirectly convey another person's order, request, etc./-euraeyo — (informal addressee-raising) An expression used to ask about the content of the order, request, etc., the listener knows from having heard it before./
-으랬는데 -으랬는데 [-euraessneunde] /-euraetneunde — An expression used to convey the order the speaker heard in the past, implying that the following content is opposite to or related to the order./
-으랴 -으랴 [-eurya] /-eurya — A connective ending used to imply an intention of doing all of several tasks./-eurya — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used to judge that something is not likely to happen and ask something in response./-eurya — (formal, highly addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used to ask the listener an opinion about an act the speaker is going to do./
-으랴마는 -으랴마는 [-euryamaneun] /-euryamaneun — An expression used to indicate that, although the speaker accepts the preceding statement, it does not affect the following statement./
-으러 -으러 [-eureo] /-eureo — A connective ending used to express the purpose of an action such as going and coming./
-으려 -으려 [-euryeo] /-euryeo — A connective ending used when one has an intention or desire of doing a certain act./-euryeo — A connective ending used to express the change of a movement or state that is soon to happen./
-으려거든 -으려거든 [-euryeogeodeun] /-euryeogeodeun — A connective ending used to indicate a condition for an event to happen, or to assume that such an event happened./-euryeogeodeun — An expression used to assume the case in which one has the intention or wish to do a certain act./
-으려고 -으려고 [-euryeogo] /-euryeogo — A connective ending used to indicate that one has an intention or desire of doing a certain act./-euryeogo — A connective ending used to indicate the change of a movement or state that is soon to happen./-euryeogo — (informal addressee-lowering) A sentence-final ending used to doubt a given situation and ask again about it./
-으려고 들다 -으려고 들다 [-euryeogo deulda] /-euryeogo deulda — An expression used to indicate that one is very eager to do a certain act mentioned in the preceding statement./
