가 가 [ga] /edge; verge — The perimeter or outer limits of a place or a thing./by; fringe — The surrounding area of a place./yes; pros; approval — An expression indicating one's agreement when voting for a certain proposal, as in a meeting./F mark; the lowest grade — The lowest mark when grades are divided into five categories (su, wu, mi, yang, and ga) in the grading system in Korean secondary schools./be allowed — The state in which a certain act is possible or allowed./ga — A postpositional particle referring to a subject under a certain state or situation, or the subject of an act./ga — A postpositional particle referring to the subject that is to be changed, or the subject that one denies./ga — A postpositional particle used to emphasize the preceding statement./
