귀히 귀히 [gwihi] /nobly — In the state of being in a high position, status, etc./valuably; preciously — In a manner which conveys that something is precious and valuable./
귓가 귓가 [gwisga] /rim of the ear — The area on the outer edge of one's ears./
귓가를 스치다 귓가를 스치다 [gwisgareul seuchida] /brush against the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound to vanish immediately after it is heard./
귓가를[귓가에] 맴돌다 귓가를[귓가에] 맴돌다 [gwisgareul[gwisgae] maemdolda] /hover around the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound which was heard before to keep coming up in one's mind./
귓가에 떠돌다 귓가에 떠돌다 [gwisgae tteodolda] /go around the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound which was heard before to keep coming up in one's mind./
귓가에서 떠나지 않다 귓가에서 떠나지 않다 [gwisgaeseo tteonaji anhda] /not leave the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound which was heard before to keep coming up in one's mind./
귓결 귓결 [gwisgyeol] /hearing by chance — An opportunity to be heard by chance without the intention of doing so./
귓구멍 귓구멍 [gwisgumeong] /earhole — The hole from the outside of the ears to the eardrum./
귓등 귓등 [gwisdeung] /back of the ear — The outer part of an auricle./
귓등으로 듣다 귓등으로 듣다 [gwisdeungeuro deudda] /listen with the back of one's ear — To listen to what others say in a careless and cursory manner./
귓등으로 흘리다[흘려보내다] 귓등으로 흘리다[흘려보내다] [gwisdeungeuro heulrida[heulryeobonaeda]] /let something flow along the back of one's ear — To listen to what others say in a cursory manner and forget it./
귓등으로도 안 듣다 귓등으로도 안 듣다 [gwisdeungeurodo an deudda] /not listen even with the back of one's ear — To listen to what others say in a careless and cursory manner./
귓바퀴 귓바퀴 [gwisbakwi] /earflap — The outer edge of the ears./
귓밥 귓밥 [gwisbab] /earlobe — The skin on the lower part of the ears./
귓병 귓병 [gwisbyeong] /ear infection — Ear disease./
귓불 귓불 [gwisbul] /earlobe — The skin on the lower part of the ears./
귓속 귓속 [gwissog] /inside of an ear; inner ear — The inside of an ear./
귓속말 귓속말 [gwissogmal] /whisper — The act of saying something quietly by putting one's mouth to another's ears, or such a whisper./
귓속말하다 귓속말하다 [gwissogmalhada] /whisper — To say something quietly by putting one's mouth to another's ears./
귓전 귓전 [gwisjeon] /rim of the ear — The area around an ear./
귓전에 맴돌다 귓전에 맴돌다 [gwisjeone maemdolda] /hover around the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound whch has been heard before to come up./
귓전에 아른거리다 귓전에 아른거리다 [gwisjeone areungeorida] /haunt the rim of one's ear — For a word or sound which has been heard before to come up./
귓전으로 듣다 귓전으로 듣다 [gwisjeoneuro deudda] /listen with the rim of one's ear — To listen to what others say in a careless and cursory manner./
귓전으로 흘리다 귓전으로 흘리다 [gwisjeoneuro heulrida] /let something flow along the rim of one's ear — To listen to what others say in a careless manner and neglect it./
귓전을 때리다 귓전을 때리다 [gwisjeoneul ttaerida] /hit the rim of one's ear — For a sound to be heard loudly./
귓전을 울리다 귓전을 울리다 [gwisjeoneul ulrida] /ring the rim of one's ear — For a sound to be heard as if it is coming from somewhere very close./
규격 규격 [gyugyeog] /standard — A figure or form chosen as the standard to follow./
규격 봉투 규격 봉투 [gyugyeog bongtu] /standard envelope — An envelope made according to standard sizes and formats in order to use for a specific purpose./
규격품 규격품 [gyugyeogpum] /standardized products — Goods made according to the fixed size or form of the standard./
규격화 규격화 [gyugyeoghwa] /standardization — The act of setting as standard a figure or form to be followed; the act of fitting something into such a figure or form./regimentation — The act of fitting an object, ideology, person, or institution into a specific frame or setting it in a particular direction./
규격화되다 규격화되다 [gyugyeoghwadoeda] /be standardized — For a figure or form to be set as standard to be followed, and for something to be fit into such a figure or form./be standardized — For an object, ideology, person, or institution to be fitted into a specific frame or set in a specific direction./
규격화하다 규격화하다 [gyugyeoghwahada] /standardize — To set a figure or form as a standard to be followed; to fit something into such a figure or form./standardize — To fit an object, ideology, person, or institution into a specific frame or set them in a specific direction./
규명 규명 [gyumyeong] /investigation — The act of finding out the truth by researching in detail./
규명되다 규명되다 [gyumyeongdoeda] /be investigated — For the truth to be found out by researching in detail./
규명하다 규명하다 [gyumyeonghada] /investigate — To find out the truth by researching in detail./
규모 규모 [gyumo] /size; scale; scope — The size or scale of an object or phenomenon./scale; systematic plan — A plan or system for spending money./
규범 규범 [gyubeom] /norms — The principles or behavior that people of a society have to follow and observe./
규범성 규범성 [gyubeomseong] /being normative — The quality or characteristic of the principles or behavior that people have to follow and observe./
규범적 규범적 [gyubeomjeog] /being normative — Being the principles or behavior that the people of a society have to follow and observe./normative — Being the principles or behavioral patterns that the people of a society have to follow and observe./
규범화 규범화 [gyubeomhwa] /standardization — The act of making something become the principles or behavior that the people of a society have to follow and observe./
규범화되다 규범화되다 [gyubeomhwadoeda] /be standardized — To become a principle or mode of conduct that the people of a society have to follow and observe./
규범화하다 규범화하다 [gyubeomhwahada] /standardize — To make something become a principle or mode of conduct that the people of a society have to follow and observe./
규수 규수 [gyusu] /maiden — (polite form) A maiden of another family./
규약 규약 [gyuyag] /regulation — Rules on the composition or management of an organization./
규율 규율 [gyuyul] /regulation — Rules made for people to observe in order to keep the order of a society or organization./
규장각 규장각 [gyujanggag] /Gyujanggak Library — The royal library built in the Joseon Dynasty, to store the writings or calligraphy of the kings; it also collected, edited, and published books on a national scale; it was closed during the Gabo Reform of 1894./
규정 규정 [gyujeong] /regulation; rule — The act of making something a rule; or the rule set in such a manner./stipulation; definition; determination — The act of deciding content, principles, meanings clearly; or things that have been decided in such a manner./
규정되다 규정되다 [gyujeongdoeda] /be prescribed — To be laid down as a rule./be stipulated — For the content, character, meaning, etc., of something to be clearly decided./
규정짓다 규정짓다 [gyujeongjisda] /prescribe — To lay something down as a rule./stipulate — To clearly decide the content, character, meaning, etc., of something./
규정하다 규정하다 [gyujeonghada] /prescribe — To lay something down as a rule./stipulate — To clearly decide the content, character, meaning, etc., of something./
규제 규제 [gyuje] /regulation — The act of restricting a person or group's activities by regulations or law./
규제되다 규제되다 [gyujedoeda] /be regulated — For a person's or group's activities to be restricted by regulations or law./
규제책 규제책 [gyujechaeg] /restriction policy — Measures or methods to restrict a person or group's activities by regulations or law./
규제하다 규제하다 [gyujehada] /regulate — To restrict a person's or group's activities by regulations or law./
규칙 규칙 [gyuchig] /rule — A law enacted so that many people will follow it./rule — An order or law occurring regularly in a certain kind of work or phenomenon./
규칙 활용 규칙 활용 [gyuchig hwalyong] /regular conjugation — In grammar, inflection of a verb or adjective in which its root stays unchanged while regular word endings are attached to the root./
규칙성 규칙성 [gyuchigseong] /regularity — The quality of showing consistent order in something or a phenomenon./
규칙적 규칙적 [gyuchigjeog] /regularity — Showing consistent patterns in something or a phenomenon./regular — Showing consistent patterns in something or a phenomenon./
규탄 규탄 [gyutan] /denouncement — An act of criticizing a mistake or wrongdoing./
규탄되다 규탄되다 [gyutandoeda] /be denounced — To be criticized for a mistake or wrongdoing./
규탄하다 규탄하다 [gyutanhada] /denounce — To criticize a mistake or wrongdoing./
규합 규합 [gyuhab] /rally — A gathering of power or people in order to achieve a goal./
규합되다 규합되다 [gyuhabdoeda] /be rallied; be mustered — For power or people to converge in order to achieve a goal./
규합하다 규합하다 [gyuhabhada] /rally; muster — To converge power or people in order to achieve a goal./
균 균 [gyun] /virus — A very small organism that makes food rot or people sick./
균등 균등 [gyundeung] /equality — The state of being treated the same without difference or variation./
균등하다 균등하다 [gyundeunghada] /equal; even — Being the same without difference or variation./
균등히 균등히 [gyundeunghi] /evenly; equally — In equal amounts without difference./
균열 균열 [gyunyeol] /crack — A gap made by a split in a given space; or such a gap./fall out — (figurative) A state of becoming distant or having different opinions./
균열되다 균열되다 [gyunyeoldoeda] /crack — For a gap to be made by a split in a given space./fall out; split — (figurative) To become estranged or come to have different opinions./
균열하다 균열하다 [gyunyeolhada] /crack — For a gap to be made by a split in a given space./fall out; split — (figurative) To become estranged or come to have different opinions./
균일 균일 [gyunil] /uniformity — The state of being the same without difference./
균일가 균일가 [gyunilga] /uniform price — The same price without variation./
균일성 균일성 [gyunilseong] /uniformity — The same nature or condition of something without variation./
균일하다 균일하다 [gyunilhada] /uniform — Being the same, without any differentiating aspects./
균형 균형 [gyunhyeong] /balance — A state of not tilting or leaning to one side./
균형적 균형적 [gyunhyeongjeog] /being balanced — Being even and stable without tilting or leaning toward any one side./balanced — Even and stable without tilting or leaning toward any one side./
귤 귤 [gyul] /tangerine; mandarin orange — A sweet-and-sour, orange-colored, round fruit of a tangerine tree, whose skin is peeled before eating./
그 그 [geu] /(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate people who are not the speaker or listener./(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned object or something the listener has in mind./that — A term referring to something near the listener or what the listener is thinking./that; the — A term referring to something mentioned earlier./that — A term referring to something uncertain or what the speaker does not want to specify./uh; um; er; erm — An exclamation used when the speaker is tongue-tied or has difficulty getting some words out of his/her mouth./
그 나물에 그 밥 그 나물에 그 밥 [geu namule geu bab] /that rice with those vegetables — For two people or things to be at almost the same level to such an extent that a difference is hardly noticeable./
그 아버지에 그 아들 그 아버지에 그 아들 [geu abeojie geu adeul] /that son for that father — An expression used to describe a son who resembles his father in a variety of aspects./
그 어머니에 그 아들[딸] 그 어머니에 그 아들[딸] [geu eomeonie geu adeul[ttal]] /that son[daughter] for that mother — An expression used to describe a son or a daughter to resemble his or her mother in a variety of aspects./
그간 그간 [geugan] /meantime — A very short period of time between a past event and another event./
그같이 그같이 [geugati] /like that — In that way, or so./
그거 그거 [geugeo] /(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate something close to the listener or something the listener has in mind./(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned object./(no equivalent expression) — (disparaging) The person./(no equivalent expression) — (endearing) The child./
그거참 그거참 [geugeocham] /alas; oh; wow — An exclamation used to express the feelings of contrition, regret or surprise./
그건 그렇고 그건 그렇고 [geugeon geureohgo] /admitting that as such — An expression used to admit to the comments made earlier and change topic./
그것 그것 [geugeos] /(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate something close to the listener, or something the listener has in mind./(no equivalent expression) — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned object./(no equivalent expression) — (disparaging) The person./(no equivalent expression) — (endearing) The child./
그것 봐(요)[봐라/보세요/보십시오] 그것 봐(요)[봐라/보세요/보십시오] [geugeos bwa(yo)[bwara/boseyo/bosibsio]] /Look at that(, please)[Look at that/Please, look at at/Can you look at that?] — An expression used when what one expected really happens./
그것도 그것도 [geugeosdo] /at that; to boot — On top of the comments made earlier; moreover./
그것도 그럴 것이 그것도 그럴 것이 [geugeosdo geureol geosi] /That is so for a reason — There is an inevitable and plausible reason for the facts mentioned earlier and the reason is./
그것참 그것참 [geugeoscham] /alas; oh; wow — An exclamation to express the feelings of contrition, regret, or surprise./
그게 그거다 그게 그거다 [geuge geugeoda] /That is that — For an object or task to have no difference with each other./
그곳 그곳 [geugos] /there — A pronoun used to indicate somewhere that is close to the listener./there — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned place./
그글피 그글피 [geugeulpi] /four days from today — The fourth day from today./
그까짓 그까짓 [geukkajis] /such — Only that extent of./
그깟 그깟 [geukkas] /such — Only that extent of./
그끄저께 그끄저께 [geukkeujeokke] /three days ago; two days before yesterday — The third day before today./three days ago — Three days ago./
그끄제 그끄제 [geukkeuje] /three days ago; two days before yesterday — The third day before today./three days ago — Three days ago./
그나마 그나마 [geunama] /nevertheless; still — With a sense of gratitude for something, although it is not good or enough./and that; at that; even that — With disappointment over something when others are unsatisfactory or insufficient./
그나저나 그나저나 [geunajeona] /anyway; anyhow — Setting it aside./
그날 그날 [geunal] /that day; the day — The day mentioned earlier./
그날그날 그날그날 [geunalgeunal] /day-to-day; everyday — Every single day./everyday — On each relevant day, on a daily basis./
그냥 그냥 [geunyang] /as it is; as it stands — In the manner of leaving something as it is./all the time — Continuously in such a state./without any conditions — With no strings attached./just — Without any intention or special meaning./
그냥저냥 그냥저냥 [geunyangjeonyang] /somehow; so-so — In the manner of barely enduring a certain circumstance or situation; tolerably; passably./
그네 그네 [geune] /swing — Play equipment in a playground whose two long dangling ropes hold a seat, on which a person swings back and forth./them — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned persons./
그네뛰기 그네뛰기 [geunettwigi] /geunettwigi — A person or two persons standing on a swing, holding the ropes, and swinging back and forth./
그녀 그녀 [geunyeo] /she; her — A pronoun used to indicate the previously-mentioned woman./
그늘 그늘 [geuneul] /shade — The dark area formed when the light is hidden by an object./influence — The protection or influence provided by someone realiable./hidden hardship — A difficult condition or environment of someone that is barely visible./worry — The facial expression of someone who is worried or troubled./
그늘이 지다 그늘이 지다 [geuneuli jida] /be shaded — For one's face to look dark due to concern or worry./
그늘지다 그늘지다 [geuneuljida] /be shady; be shaded — To have a shade as something blocks the light./be gloomy — For worry or anxiety to appear in a person's facial expression or attitude./be in the shade — To be in a difficult situation that is hardly noticed by others./
그다음 그다음 [geudaeum] /next; following — The time, place, turn, etc., that comes after something./
그다지 그다지 [geudaji] /little; not greatly — Not to a great degree, or not that much./so much — To that extent, or that much./
그담 그담 [geudam] /next; following — The time, place, turn, etc., that comes after something./
그대 그대 [geudae] /geudae — (polite form) A pronoun used to indicate the listener./geudae — (affectionate) A pronoun used to indicate the other person in a written document./
그대로 그대로 [geudaero] /itself — The state of being as it is./being as something was — The state of being identical to something./as it is; as it stands — Exactly as the original shape or state./like that — In the same way as that./
그도 그럴 것이 그도 그럴 것이 [geudo geureol geosi] /That is so for a reason — An expression used to explain an inevitable and plausible reason for the facts mentioned earlier./
그동안 그동안 [geudongan] /meantime; meanwhile — The previously-mentioned period, or a certain period of time before one sees or contacts someone again./
그득 그득 [geudeug] /to the full; to the brim — In a quantity or amount that is full to the limit./to capacity — In such a large amount that there is no empty space./in a widespread way — In a state in which smell, light, sound, etc., are spread all over a space./strongly — With a strong emotion or thought./
그득하다 그득하다 [geudeughada] /full — Being in full the quantity or number of something within a designated scope./crammed — Having so much of something that there is no room left over./widespread — A smell, light, sound, etc., being widespread in a certain space./full — A certain feeling or thought being extremely strong./bloated — Feeling full and bloated in the bowels due to poor digestion of consumed food./
그득히 그득히 [geudeughi] /to the full; to the brim — In a quantity or amount that is full to the limit./to capacity — In such a large amount that there is no empty space./in a widespread way — In a state in which smell, light, sound, etc., are spread all over a space./strongly — With a strong emotion or thought./
그따위 그따위 [geuttawi] /geuttawi — (disparaging) A pronoun used to indicate the subject of such a sort./like that — (disparaging) Such a kind of./
그딴 그딴 [geuttan] /like that — (disparaging) Such a kind of./
그때 그때 [geuttae] /that time; that moment; then — The previously-mentioned time./
그때그때 그때그때 [geuttaegeuttae] /according to circumstances; whenever — Whenever something happens or there is an opportunity./
그래 그래 [geurae] /okay; sure — An exclamation used when giving a positive answer that means 'I'll do so', 'Yes, it is', or 'I see.'/really — An exclamation used to indicate that the speaker marvels at or is slightly surprised by the words of the other party./eh — An exclamation used to emphasize something by asking about it again./geurae — A postpositional particle used when the speaker talks about what he/she says to the listener in a friendly manner./geurae — An abbreviated word for '그리하여' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./geurae — An abbreviated word for '그러하여' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그래 봤자 그래 봤자 [geurae bwassja] /even so — No matter what action or task one may do./
그래도 그래도 [geuraedo] /geuraedo — An abbreviated word for '그리하여도' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./geuraedo — An abbreviated word for '그러하여도' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그래서 그래서 [geuraeseo] /so; therefore — A word used when the preceding statement is the basis for the following statement./geuraeseo — An abbreviated word for '그리하여서' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./geuraeseo — An abbreviated word for '그러하여서' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그러거나 말거나 그러거나 말거나 [geureogeona malgeona] /whether someone does something or not — Regardless of whether someone does something or not./
그러게 그러게 [geureoge] /I told you so — A word used when one emphasizes that one's previous statement is right./right; I know; yeah — An exclamation used to indicate that the speaker supports or agrees with the words of the other party./
그러고 그러고 [geureogo] /geureogo — An abbreviated word for '그리하고' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./
그러그러하다 그러그러하다 [geureogeureohada] /being such and such — A term used when the speaker does not want to explain a certain fact, state, etc., in detail or in order to substitute for what was said earlier./so-so; middling — Just common, not so special./
그러나 그러나 [geureona] /but; however — A word used to indicate that a statement is the opposite of the following statement./geureona — An abbreviated word for '그리하나' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./geureona — An abbreviated word for '그러하나' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그러나저러나 그러나저러나 [geureonajeoreona] /anyway; anyhow — Putting it aside./anyway — An abbreviated word for '그리하나 저리하나'./anyway — An abbreviated word for '그러하나 저러하나'./
그러니 그러니 [geureoni] /geureoni — An abbreviated word for '그러하니' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그러니까 그러니까 [geureonikka] /so — For that reason, or therefore./that is to say — In other words, or put differently./so — To begin with./
그러니저러니 그러니저러니 [geureonijeoreoni] /geureonijeoreoni — An abbreviated word for '그러하다느니 저러하다느니' (saying this or that)./
그러다 그러다 [geureoda] /do so — To do what occurred or was stated previously./say so — To say so./
그러다가 그러다가 [geureodaga] /geureodaga — An abbreviated word for '그리하다가' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./
그러면 그러면 [geureomyeon] /if so — A conjunctive adverb used when the following statement is conditional upon the preceding one./then — A conjunction used when accepting the preceding statement or bulding on it to make a new claim./geureomyeon — An abbreviated word for '그리하면' (a conjugated form of '그리하다' (do so))./(no equivalent expression) — An abbreviated word for '그러하면' (a conjugated form of '그러하다' (be so))./
그러면 그렇지 그러면 그렇지 [geureomyeon geureohji] /I knew it; No wonder; There is no doubt that — An expression used when what one thought or expected really happens./I knew it; No wonder; There is no doubt that — An expression used when something has been going well for a while, but what has been worried about finally occurs./
