긴소매 긴소매 [ginsomae] /long sleeves — Sleeves that reach all the way down to the wrist, or clothes with long sleeves./
긴요하다 긴요하다 [ginyohada] /necessary; essential; indispensible — Very important and needed./
긴요히 긴요히 [ginyohi] /momentously; importantly — In an essential and crucial manner./
긴장 긴장 [ginjang] /nervousness; tension — The act of being alert without being able to relax./tension; strain — A situation or atmosphere in which two parties are not comfortable in their relationship and are likely to have fight./tension — A state in which muscles or nerves continue to contract or get excited./
긴장감 긴장감 [ginjanggam] /tension; being nervous — A feeling of alertness, not being relaxed./
긴장되다 긴장되다 [ginjangdoeda] /be nervous; be strained — To be alerted, not being relaxed./be strained — For a relationship to become disturbed and seem as if a dispute is about to happen./be tensed; be strained — For one's muscles or nerves to be consistently shrunk or excited./
긴장미 긴장미 [ginjangmi] /tension — The feeling that causes one not to relax, but to concentate./
긴장시키다 긴장시키다 [ginjangsikida] /tense; strain — To cause someone to be alerted, not being relaxed./stretch; strain — To cause one's muscles or nerves to be consistently shrunk or excited./
긴장하다 긴장하다 [ginjanghada] /be nervous; tense up; be strained — To be alerted, not being relaxed./tense up; be strained — For one's muscles or nerves to be consistently shrunk or excited./
