길 길 [gil] /road; street; way — A long stretch of ground space with a fixed width meant for people or cars to travel along./route; way — A fixed path in the sea or in the air that a ship or airplane travels regularly./stopover — An intermediate place that is traveled to before reaching a destination./process; path — The process of a person's living or a society's development over time./path — The act of moving toward the ideals of an individual or a society./duty; obligation — The duty or responsibility required for someone in a certain qualification or title./way; method — A method to do a certain thing./as soon as — The moment right after a certain act is completed./in-transit — The middle stage of going to a certain place./way; course — A term used to indicate a course or the middle of something./being glossy; being broken in — The state of an object used for a long time, with a surface made smooth and convenient for use./domestication; tameness — The act of training or educating a person or animal for a long time to make them obey and easy to control./gil — A bound noun that serves as a unit of length./
길(을) 뚫다 길(을) 뚫다 [gil(eul) ttulhda] /forge a road — To find a way./
길(이) 닿다 길(이) 닿다 [gil(i) dahda] /The road reaches — For a relationship to be established to do something./
길(이) 바쁘다 길(이) 바쁘다 [gil(i) bappeuda] /The road is busy — To be under a situation where one has to get to the destination promptly./
