꾸미다 꾸미다 [kkumida] /decorate; adorn — To decorate for something to look better./fabricate; make up — To fabricate something that is a lie or nonexistent as if it were true./write up; draw up — To make a document, report, book, etc., according to a format./(no equivalent expression) — To make a living./scheme; plot — To plan something and make it work./modify — In grammar, to make the state, quality, degree, etc., of another constituent more detailed or clearer./
꾸밈 꾸밈 [kkumim] /being flowery; being lavish — The act of making something look good or seem plausible./
꾸밈새 꾸밈새 [kkumimsae] /decoration; being well-groomed — The state of being decorated or well-groomed./
꾸밈없다 꾸밈없다 [kkumimeobsda] /plain; frank — Something being faithful to what it actually is without being artificially made to look nicer./
꾸밈없이 꾸밈없이 [kkumimeobsi] /plainly; frankly — Truthfully in the manner of showing something as it is without making it look good./
꾸밈음 꾸밈음 [kkumimeum] /mordent; grace note; ornament — In music, the musical note put around a main note, intended to diversify./
꾸벅 꾸벅 [kkubeog] /with a nod — A word describing the motion of bending forward and then raising one's head or body./drowsily — In the manner of falling asleep or dozing off while one is not aware of it./
