꾸역꾸역 꾸역꾸역 [kkuyeogkkuyeog] /with one's mouth stuffed — In the manner of stuffing food into one's mouth or chewing with one's mouth full./in droves; in a stream — In the manner of a lot of people or things swarming into or out of a place./unwillingly — In the manner of doing something against one's will./(no equivalent expression) — In the state of feeling a surge of a certain sentiment again and again./
꾸준하다 꾸준하다 [kkujunhada] /steady; constant; unflagging — Consistent, with almost no changes./
꾸준히 꾸준히 [kkujunhi] /steadily; persistently — Consistently./
