끈 끈 [kkeun] /string; rope — A thin, long object, used to tie or run through things./cord; strap — An object attached to another object, which is used to tie something or used as a handle./money-making means — A method to earn money./influence — A person or relation to rely on./relationship — (figurative) Karma or a relationship./tenacity — The continuation or lasting of a certain emotion or effort./
끈(이) 떨어지다 끈(이) 떨어지다 [kkeun(i) tteoleojida] /One's string falls off — For ways or means to live on to be cut off./
끈기 끈기 [kkeungi] /viscosity; glutinosity — The quality of being viscous./patience; persistence; endurance; tenacity — The quality of not giving up easily and continuing to endure./
끈끈이 끈끈이 [kkeunkkeuni] /flypaper — A very sticky object, which holds anything just touching it and which is used to catch mice or flies./
끈끈하다 끈끈하다 [kkeunkkeunhada] /sticky — Feeling that a gluey substance sticks to the skin./clammy — Unpleasant due to a feeling of dampness on the skin./close-knit; close — Having strong emotional bonds and intimate relations with each other./sticky — Having persistence in a glance or attitude enough to be unpleasant./
