끊기다 끊기다 [kkeunhgida] /snap; collapse; break — For a connected object such as a string, thread, cord, etc., to be cut and separated./be broken off; be cut off — For a relationship to be stopped from continuing./be stopped; be quitted — For something that one has been doing or thinking about to be stopped./be disconnected; be cut off — For the supply of electricity, water, etc., to be cut off./be stopped; be cancelled — For the delivery of newspaper, milk, etc., to be stopped./be blocked; be cut off — For a path to be blocked so that people or goods cannot come and go./be paused; be cut off — To be paused temporarily while talking./be deserted — For no one to come any longer./be killed; die — For a life to be stopped from continuing./be cut off; be disconnected — For the exchange of words or thoughts through the telephone or Internet to be cut off./be cut off — For a continued service to be cut off./
끊다 끊다 [kkeunhda] /cut — To cut a connected object such as a string, thread, cord, etc., and separate it./break off; cut off — To stop a relationship from continuing./stop; quit — To stop doing or thinking about something that one has been doing or thinking about continuously./stop; quit — To stop doing something that one has been doing habitually./disconnect; cut off — To cut off the supply of electricity, water, etc./stop; cancel — To stop the delivery of newspaper, milk, etc./block; cut off — To block a path to prevent a person or goods from coming and going./pause; cut off — To stop talking temporarily; to make another person stop talking temporarily./pause — To stop talking or reading temporarily in between words./buy; purchase — To buy a ticket, some cloth, etc./draw; issue; write — To issue a check, promissory note, document, etc./kill; die — To stop a life from continuing./hang up — To stop exchanging words or thoughts through the telephone or Internet./complete; finish — To complete a transaction or calculation./sign up; enroll — To pay and sign up for an academy, etc./achieve record — To make a record in a game that usually competes for time or speed./cut off — To stop an emotion, interest, etc., from continuing./
끊어지다 끊어지다 [kkeunheojida] /snap; collapse; break — For a connected object such as a string, thread, cord, etc., to be cut and separated./be broken off; be cut off — For a relationship to be stopped from continuing./be stopped; be quitted — For something that one has been doing or thinking about to be stopped./be disconnected; be cut off — For the supply of electricity, water, etc., to be cut off./be stopped; be cancelled — For the delivery of newspaper, milk, etc., to be stopped./be blocked; be cut off — For a path to be blocked so that people or goods cannot come and go./be paused; be cut off — To be paused temporarily while talking./be paused — To be paused temporarily between words while speaking or reading./be killed; die — For a life to be stopped from continuing./be cut off; be disconnected — For the exchange of words or thoughts through the telephone or Internet to be cut off./be cut off — For a continued service to be cut off./
끊이다 끊이다 [kkeunhida] /cease; be cut off — For something that was continued to be cut off./
