끌어내다 끌어내다 [kkeuleonaeda] /take something out — To pull an object outside./drag something; someone out — To make a person or animal come out by force./educe; elicit — To make someone express his/her thoughts, abilities, etc./
끌어내리다 끌어내리다 [kkeuleonaerida] /drag down; take down — To drag a person or object down./demote — To reduce to a lower level of authority or position./cut; bring down — To lower the level or figure of something./
끌어넣다 끌어넣다 [kkeuleoneohda] /take in; drag in — To drag someone or something in./get someone involved; drag into — To make someone be engaged in something./
끌어당기다 끌어당기다 [kkeuleodanggida] /pull; draw — To pull something close./draw; attract — To make something/someone gain attention, interest, etc./draw; attract — To make something/someone see something./
끌어대다 끌어대다 [kkeuleodaeda] /add — To add more details in order to explain./raise and provide money — To supply by obtaining resources, money, etc./
