나가다 나가다 [nagada] /go out; leave — To move from the inside to the outside of an area or space./go forward — To move forward./be spread — For objects, etc., to be made and spread across the society./be revealed; become known — For something to be revealed or become known through media sources./become known — For words, facts, rumors, etc., to become known./begin action — To go into action in a new place, area, etc./work — To go to work at a certain place./go — To go to a place with a purpose./attend; participate; run for — To attend a meeting, participate in a sports game, or run for a candidate in an election, etc./leave — To leave or get out of an area, space, or a place that one belonged to./maintain a certain attitude — To do something or maintain a certain attitude./be worth; weigh — For a price, weight, etc., to reach a certain extent./spend; receive — For money, objects, etc., to be given or spent./be worn out — For clothes, shoes, socks, etc., to be worn out or torn./break; injure — For an object, etc., to be broken or for one's body part to be hurt./become unconscious — To lose one's consciousness or mind./recover — To recover from an illness such as a cold, etc./be taken; be sold — For the contract of a house, room, etc., on sale to be completed./go off; go out — For the electricity to be cut off or an electric light to go off./work well — For an object with a blade to work well./be sold — For an object to be sold well./go to work — To go to do something./move — To move from where one lived to another place./progress; proceed — For something to be proceeded to a certain extent./nagada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate the continuation of the action of the preceding statement./
