낳다 낳다 [nahda] /give birth; deliver — To deliver a baby or egg out of one's womb./bring about — To form or bring about a certain outcome./cause the existence — To cause someone to appear, in a certain environment or situation./
낳은 정보다 기른 정이 더 크다 낳은 정보다 기른 정이 더 크다 [naheun jeongboda gireun jeongi deo keuda] /Affection from childrearing is bigger than that from childbearing — For the affection of those who bring up a child to be bigger and more valuable than that of those who give birth to one./
내 내 [nae] /creek — A stream bigger than a brook and smaller than a river./smell; scent — Air detected by the nose./I — A form of '나' (I), when the postpositional particle '가' is attached to it./throughout — Continuously from beginning to end./(no equivalent expression) — An abbreviated word for '나의(my)'/nae — A bound noun used to indicate that something is within a certain range or scope./
내 말이 그 말(이다) 내 말이 그 말(이다) [nae mali geu mal(ida)] /My word is that word — An expression used to show agreement with someone's opinion or suggestion./
