내려앉다 내려앉다 [naeryeoanjda] /sit down on — To sit down on something./collapse; cave in — For a building, bridge, etc., to collapse, or for a flat area to sink./become dark; become foggy — For fog, darkness, etc., to spread./be worried — To be worried with shock./be demoted — To be transferred to a lower position./
내려오다 내려오다 [naeryeooda] /step down — To come from a high place to a lower place, or from up to down./go to a rural area — To come to a rural area from a large city such as Seoul./step down; be demoted — To be transferred to a lower position from a high position./move southward — To move from the north to the south./be delivered — For a plan, news, order, etc., to be passed along by a superior so that a subordinate is notified of it./approach — To approach a certain set point./be passed down — To be handed down from the past up until now./walk down; step down — To walk down from a high place to a lower place./carry down — To carry something from a high place to a lower place./
