눈 눈 [nun] /eye — The sensory organ on the face of a person or animal that can see an object when stimulated by the light./seeing ability — The ability of an eye that can tell the existence or shape of an object./judgment — The ability to judge by seeing an object./viewpoint — The facial expression or attitude when seeing an object./direction of gaze — The path or direction of people's gaze./eye of a typhoon — The center of a typhoon./gradation; calibration — Lines drawn on a ruler, scale, thermometer, etc., to indicate the quantity or amount of something./mesh — A hole in between strings woven into a net./intersection — A point where a horizontal line and a vertical line meet on a go board./snow — Tiny white cotton-like pieces of ice forming and falling as the moisture in the atmosphere becomes frozen./bud — A sprout of a flower or leaf shooting forth on the branch or stem of a plant./
눈 가리고 아웅 눈 가리고 아웅 [nun garigo aung] /say fee-faw-fum with covering someone's eyes; bury one's head ostrich-like in the sand — The manner of trying to deceive someone with a shallow trick./
눈 감고 따라간다 눈 감고 따라간다 [nun gamgo ttaraganda] /follow with one's eyes closed — To follow other's opinions or arguments without expressing one's own opinion or view./
눈 감으면 코 베어 먹을 세상[인심] 눈 감으면 코 베어 먹을 세상[인심] [nun gameumyeon ko beeo meogeul sesang[insim]] /a world[an atmosphere in the society] where one's nose is cut off as soon as one closes one's eyes — An expression used to describe an atmosphere of a society which is very coldhearted and inhuman./
눈 깜짝할 사이 눈 깜짝할 사이 [nun kkamjjaghal sai] /the twinkle of an eye — A very brief moment./
눈 둘 곳을 모르다 눈 둘 곳을 모르다 [nun dul goseul moreuda] /not know where to put one's eyes — To be confused about where to watch since one does not know what is going on or is in an awkward or embarrassing situation./
눈 딱[꼭] 감다 눈 딱[꼭] 감다 [nun ttag[kkog] gamda] /squeeze the lids over the eyeballs — To stop thinking about other things any more./squeeze the lids over the eyeballs — To pretend not to have seen something that one saw./
눈 뜨고 도둑맞는다 눈 뜨고 도둑맞는다 [nun tteugo dodugmajneunda] /have something stolen before one's very eyes — To be deceived or suffer losses all the time while being clearly aware of it./
눈 뜨고 볼 수 없다 눈 뜨고 볼 수 없다 [nun tteugo bol su eobsda] /cannot watch something with one's eyes open — To dare not see a view in front of one since it is miserable and horrible or very shameful./
눈 뜨고 코 베어 갈 세상[인심] 눈 뜨고 코 베어 갈 세상[인심] [nun tteugo ko beeo gal sesang[insim]] /a world[an atmosphere in the society] where one's nose is cut off even when one opens one's eyes — An expression used to describe an atmosphere of a society which is very coldhearted and inhuman./
눈 뜨고(는) 못 보다 눈 뜨고(는) 못 보다 [nun tteugo(neun) mos boda] /cannot watch something with one's eyes open — To dare not see a view in front of one since it is miserable and horrible or very shameful./
눈 밖에 나다 눈 밖에 나다 [nun bakke nada] /be left out of someone's eyes — To lose someone's trust and be hated by him/her./
눈 위에 혹 눈 위에 혹 [nun wie hog] /a lump on one's eye — A person one dislikes very much and does not want to see./
눈 하나 깜짝 안 하다 눈 하나 깜짝 안 하다 [nun hana kkamjjag an hada] /not budge an eye at all — To behave or deal with others as usual in exactly the same attitude or air./
눈(에) 띄다 눈(에) 띄다 [nun(e) ttuida] /stand out in sight — To visually stand out./
눈(에) 어리다 눈(에) 어리다 [nun(e) eorida] /flicker in one's eyes — For an image to linger and keep coming to one's mind./
눈(을) 까뒤집다 눈(을) 까뒤집다 [nun(eul) kkadwijibda] /flip over one's eyes — To open one's eyes wide since one is very startled or to try to threaten someone./
눈(을) 돌리다 눈(을) 돌리다 [nun(eul) dolrida] /turn one's eyes — To give one's attention to other things./
눈(을) 뒤집다 눈(을) 뒤집다 [nun(eul) dwijibda] /overturn one's eyes — To be engrossed in something and lose one's senses./
눈(을) 똑바로 뜨다 눈(을) 똑바로 뜨다 [nun(eul) ttogbaro tteuda] /open one's eyes straight — To come back to earth and pay attention./
눈(을) 맞추다 눈(을) 맞추다 [nun(eul) majchuda] /contact each other's eyes — To look each other in the eyes./
눈(을) 밝히다 눈(을) 밝히다 [nun(eul) balghida] /light up one's eyes — To intently focus on looking for something./
눈(을) 붙이다 눈(을) 붙이다 [nun(eul) butida] /close one' eyes — To sleep./
눈(을) 속이다 눈(을) 속이다 [nun(eul) sogida] /deceive someone's eyes — To deceive someone by making him/her overlook something or using a certain means./
눈(을) 씻고 보다 눈(을) 씻고 보다 [nun(eul) ssisgo boda] /wash one's eyes and see — To be fully alert and intently watch something./
눈(을) 씻고 보려야 볼 수 없다 눈(을) 씻고 보려야 볼 수 없다 [nun(eul) ssisgo boryeoya bol su eobsda] /cannot wash one's eyes and see however hard one may try to — For something to be too rare to be found./
눈(을) 피하다 눈(을) 피하다 [nun(eul) pihada] /avoid eyes — Avoid someone's attention./
눈(이) 높다 눈(이) 높다 [nun(i) nopda] /have high eyes — To seek something sophisticated and good above a certain level./have high eyes — To have very keen insight and good judgement./
눈(이) 돌아가다 눈(이) 돌아가다 [nun(i) dolagada] /have one's eyes turn — To lose one's discernment due to astonishment or rage./One's eyes turn — To pay attention with interest./
눈(이) 뒤집히다 눈(이) 뒤집히다 [nun(i) dwijibhida] /One's eyes are overturned — To lose one's reason since one went through something shocking or is engrossed in something./
눈(이) 많다 눈(이) 많다 [nun(i) manhda] /There are a lot of eyes — For many people to see./
눈(이) 맞다 눈(이) 맞다 [nun(i) majda] /Each other's eyes meet — (slang) For a man and a woman to have a crush on each other./
눈(이) 벌겋다 눈(이) 벌겋다 [nun(i) beolgeohda] /have red eyes — To intently focus on seeking one's own interest./
눈(이) 삐다 눈(이) 삐다 [nun(i) ppida] /sprain one's eyes — (disapproving) To have a wrong idea of or make a misjudgement on a very clear business or situation./
