눈에 보이는 것이 없다 눈에 보이는 것이 없다 [nune boineun geosi eobsda] /Nothing is seen in one's sight — To be unable to make an accurate judgement on a business or situation./
눈에 불을 켜다 눈에 불을 켜다 [nune buleul kyeoda] /turn on the light in one's eyes — To be very greedy for or interested in something./turn on the light in one's eyes — To open one's eyes wide and furiously out of anger./
눈에 쌍심지가 나다[돋다/뻗치다/서다/솟다/오르다] 눈에 쌍심지가 나다[돋다/뻗치다/서다/솟다/오르다] [nune ssangsimjiga nada[dodda/ppeodchida/seoda/sosda/oreuda]] /Double wicks grow[sprout/spread/stand up/soar/rise] in one's eyes — To open one's eyes wide and furiously out of violent anger./
눈에 쌍심지를 켜다[돋우다/세우다/올리다] 눈에 쌍심지를 켜다[돋우다/세우다/올리다] [nune ssangsimjireul kyeoda[doduda/seuda/olrida]] /turn on[provoke/erect/raise] double wicks in one's eyes — To open one's eyes wide and furiously out of violent anger./
눈에 아른거리다 눈에 아른거리다 [nune areungeorida] /glimmer in one's eyes — For a memory about someone or a business to come to one's mind./
눈에 안경 눈에 안경 [nune angyeong] /glasses for one's eyes — An expression used to describe a situation where even something tenuous or shoddy looks good to someone who likes it./
눈에 약하려도 없다 눈에 약하려도 없다 [nune yagharyeodo eobsda] /be unable to get something even for eye medicine — For the least of something not to exist./
눈에 익다 눈에 익다 [nune igda] /be familiar with one's eyes — For something to be familiar to someone who has seen it before several times./
눈에 차다 눈에 차다 [nune chada] /be satisfied to one's eyes — To satisfy one and be to one's liking./
눈에 콩깍지가 씌었다 눈에 콩깍지가 씌었다 [nune kongkkagjiga ssuieossda] /One's eyes are covered with a pea pod — To be unable to make an accurate judgement or think straight./
눈에 핏발을 세우다 눈에 핏발을 세우다 [nune pisbaleul seuda] /make one's eyes bloodshot — To get angry or enraged to such an extent that one's eyes get bloodshot./
눈에 핏발이 서다 눈에 핏발이 서다 [nune pisbali seoda] /have bloodshot eyes — To get angry or enraged./
눈에 흙이 들어가다[덮이다] 눈에 흙이 들어가다[덮이다] [nune heulgi deuleogada[deopida]] /get soil in one's eyes[have one's eyes covered with soil] — To die and be buried./
눈에는 눈(을) 이에는 이(를) 눈에는 눈(을) 이에는 이(를) [nuneneun nun(eul) ieneun i(reul)] /An eye for an eye and a tooth for a tooth — The manner of doing harm to someone as much as he/she has done to oneself./
눈에서 번개가 번쩍 나다 눈에서 번개가 번쩍 나다 [nuneseo beongaega beonjjeog nada] /lightning flashes in one's eyes — For one's view to be suddenly darkened and for lights to flicker and go out in front of the eyes after one is hit hard in the cheek or head./
눈에서 벗어나다 눈에서 벗어나다 [nuneseo beoseonada] /get out of someone's eyes — To become free from someone's surveillance or restraint./
눈엣가시 눈엣가시 [nunesgasi] /thorn in the side; pain in the neck — A person whom one hates and does not want to see./
눈여겨보다 눈여겨보다 [nunyeogyeoboda] /take a close look; observe carefully — To look carefully with interest./
눈요기 눈요기 [nunyogi] /treat to the eye; feast for the eye — A state of feeling satisfied by just looking at something good or tasty./
눈웃음 눈웃음 [nunuseum] /smile with one's eyes — The smile made with one's eyes, not making a sound./
눈은 그 사람의 마음을 닮는다 눈은 그 사람의 마음을 닮는다 [nuneun geu saramui maeumeul dalmneunda] /One's eyes resemble one's mind — It is easy to guess someone's mind just by looking into his/her eyes./
눈은 마음의 거울 눈은 마음의 거울 [nuneun maeumui geoul] /The eyes are the mirror of the mind — A figurative expression meaning it is easy to guess someone's mind simply by looking into his/her eyes./
눈을 거치다 눈을 거치다 [nuneul geochida] /pass through one's eyes — To review or evaluate something such as writing./
눈을 곤두세우다 눈을 곤두세우다 [nuneul gonduseuda] /make one's eyes stand up upside-down — To have a furious look in one's eyes due to anger./
눈을 굴리다 눈을 굴리다 [nuneul gulrida] /roll one's eyes — To turn one's eyeballs every which way./
눈을 끌다 눈을 끌다 [nuneul kkeulda] /draw someone's eyes — To make one to watch something by arousing one's curiosity./draw someone's eyes — For something to be at the center of attention./
눈을 떠도 코 베어 간다 눈을 떠도 코 베어 간다 [nuneul tteodo ko beeo ganda] /One's nose is cut off even when one opens one's eyes — For the atmosphere of a society to be very coldhearted and inhuman./
눈을 떠야 별을 보지 눈을 떠야 별을 보지 [nuneul tteoya byeoleul boji] /One needs to open one's eyes if one wants to see a star — An expression used to advise someone to make efforts and preparations to achieve something./
눈을 의심하다 눈을 의심하다 [nuneul uisimhada] /doubt one's eyes — To not believe something or think it is strange doubting if one may have seen it wrong./
눈을 크게 뜨다 눈을 크게 뜨다 [nuneul keuge tteuda] /open one's eyes wide — To be fully alert and pay attention./
눈이 곤두서다 눈이 곤두서다 [nuni gonduseoda] /have one's eyes stand up upside-down — For one's eyes to have a furious look due to anger./
눈이 까뒤집히다 눈이 까뒤집히다 [nuni kkadwijibhida] /have one's eyes flipped over — To lose one's reason since one went through something shocking or is engrossed in  something./
눈이 낮다 눈이 낮다 [nuni najda] /have low eyes — To not have deep insight or sophisticated tastes./
눈이 동그래지다 눈이 동그래지다 [nuni donggeuraejida] /One's eyes become round — For one's eyes to become wide and round out of strong astonishment or doubt./
눈이 등잔만 하다 눈이 등잔만 하다 [nuni deungjanman hada] /One's eyes are as big as the size of an oil lamp — For one's eyes to become wide and round out of astonishment or fear./
눈이 뚫어지게[뚫어지도록] 눈이 뚫어지게[뚫어지도록] [nuni ttulheojige[ttulheojidorog]] /to such an extent that[until] one's eyes are pierced — The manner of looking at one direction straight without moving a hair./
눈이 무디다 눈이 무디다 [nuni mudida] /have blunt eyes — To lack in insight./
눈이 번쩍 뜨이다 눈이 번쩍 뜨이다 [nuni beonjjeog tteuida] /One's eyes become wide open — To suddenly come to one's senses./
눈이 보배다 눈이 보배다 [nuni bobaeda] /One's eyes are the treasure — To be excellent at remembering things to such an extent that one does not forget anything that one has ever seen./
눈이 빠지게[빠지도록] 기다리다 눈이 빠지게[빠지도록] 기다리다 [nuni ppajige[ppajidorog] gidarida] /wait desperately to such an extent that[until] one's eyes fall out — To wait very desperately for a long time./
눈이 시뻘겋다 눈이 시뻘겋다 [nuni sippeolgeohda] /have red-hot eyes — To intently focus on seeking one's own interest./
눈이 아무리 밝아도 제 코는 안 보인다 눈이 아무리 밝아도 제 코는 안 보인다 [nuni amuri balgado je koneun an boinda] /One cannot see one's own nose however bright it is — To be unable to completely know oneself however smart one might be./
눈이 열리다 눈이 열리다 [nuni yeolrida] /One's eyes are opened — To gain insight and a discerning eye to understand things./
눈이 오나 비가 오나 눈이 오나 비가 오나 [nuni ona biga ona] /when it snows and when it rains — Always; all the time; at all times./
눈이 저울이라 눈이 저울이라 [nuni jeoulira] /One's eyes are the scale — For one's eye measurement of something to be exactly correct just like it was gauged with a scale./
눈이 캄캄하다 눈이 캄캄하다 [nuni kamkamhada] /One's eyes are pitch-dark — To be in a state where one is confused and unable to think straight./One's eyes are pitch-dark — To be illiterate./
눈이 트이다 눈이 트이다 [nuni teuida] /One's eyes are opened up — To become able to make a judgement on an object or phenomenon./
눈이 핑핑 돌아가다 눈이 핑핑 돌아가다 [nuni pingping dolagada] /One's eyes spin round and round very quickly and dizzily — For something to be so busy or a change to be so fast that one can hardly keep up with it./
눈인사 눈인사 [nuninsa] /knowing glance; greeting with a nod — A greeting by exchanging glances without saying a word./
눈자위 눈자위 [nunjawi] /white of the eye; part of the eyeball — The white part of an eyeball./
눈짐작 눈짐작 [nunjimjag] /rule of thumb — An act of guessing a size, quantity, state, etc., roughly by the eye./
눈짐작하다 눈짐작하다 [nunjimjaghada] /measure by the eye — To estimate a size, quantity, state, etc., roughly by guesswork./
눈짓 눈짓 [nunjis] /eye gesture — An act of moving the eyes to tell someone about something or order someone to do something./
눈짓하다 눈짓하다 [nunjishada] /make an eye gesture — To move the eyes to tell someone about something or order someone to do something./
눈초리 눈초리 [nunchori] /tail of the eye — The outer corner of the eye which tapers towards the ear./look — A look or gaze directed towards something./
눈총 눈총 [nunchong] /glare; angry stare; fierce stare — Eyes looking at someone sharply in hatred of or with a dislike for him/her./
눈총(을) 맞다 눈총(을) 맞다 [nunchong(eul) majda] /get a fierce stare; meet with a glare — To be hated by someone./
눈총(을) 쏘다 눈총(을) 쏘다 [nunchong(eul) ssoda] /shoot a glare — To stare fiercely./
눈치 눈치 [nunchi] /tact; sense; wits — An ability to understand and know someone's mind or situation even though they have said nothing./sign; look; face — One's attitude or facial expression that lets others guess one's real intention or situation./
눈치(가) 다르다 눈치(가) 다르다 [nunchi(ga) dareuda] /show a different look from usual; show a different face from usual — For one's attitude or behavior to be strange and different from usual./
눈치(가) 보이다 눈치(가) 보이다 [nunchi(ga) boida] /Someone's face is seen — To care about someone's feelings or attitude./
눈치(가) 빠르다 눈치(가) 빠르다 [nunchi(ga) ppareuda] /have quick wits — To understand and know someone's mind or situation even though they have said nothing./
눈치(를) 보다 눈치(를) 보다 [nunchi(reul) boda] /see someone's face; study someone's face — To study someone's feeling or attitude./
눈치(를) 보이다 눈치(를) 보이다 [nunchi(reul) boida] /show a sign; show a face; hint — To express one's thought through a facial expression, behavior, etc., not saying it directly./
눈치(를) 살피다 눈치(를) 살피다 [nunchi(reul) salpida] /see someone's face; study someone's face — To study someone's feeling or attitude./
눈치채다 눈치채다 [nunchichaeda] /sense — To see and realize a situation, another person's feelings or secret, etc./
눈치코치 눈치코치 [nunchikochi] /sense; wit — (emphasizing form) (slang) Tact./
눈치코치 다 알다 눈치코치 다 알다 [nunchikochi da alda] /know everything with one's wit — To guess and know someone's mind or the situation./
눈치코치도 모르다 눈치코치도 모르다 [nunchikochido moreuda] /have no sense and know nothing — To not understand someone's mind or the situation at all./
눈칫밥 눈칫밥 [nunchisbab] /meal offered unwillingly — A meal that one eats self-consciously under the scrutiny of someone who has offered it./
눈칫밥(을) 먹다 눈칫밥(을) 먹다 [nunchisbab(eul) meogda] /eat a meal offered unwillingly; eat another's salt — To live uncomfortably while being attentive to others' remarks, behavior, and thoughts, and not expressing one's thoughts./
눋다 눋다 [nudda] /be scorched; scorch; be singed — For food or something to burn a little and turn golden yellow./
눌러놓다 눌러놓다 [nulreonohda] /press something under; put a weight on — To put something heavy on things piled up loosely or an elastic thing in order to reduce their or its volume by hardening them or it./suppress; bring under control; oppress — To prevent someone from speaking or behaving rashly./
눌러쓰다 눌러쓰다 [nulreosseuda] /pull low one's hat or cap — To wear one's hat tightly so that it covers one's forehead./press down one's pen in writing — To press down one's pencil, etc., in writing./
눌러앉다 눌러앉다 [nulreoanjda] /stay; settle — To remain in one place./stay on one's job — To continue to work in one's place of work or position, not leaving it./
눌리다 눌리다 [nulrida] /be pressed down — For the weight or force of someone or something to be applied to another./be overwhelmed; be crushed — To become depressed due to an atmosphere or force./be repressed; be suppressed — For one's feeling or thought to be controlled so that it is not revealed./scorch; singe — To burn food or something a bit so that it turns golden yellow./
눌변 눌변 [nulbyeon] /being not a good speaker; being not good with words; being uncommunicative — A poor speaker who often stumbles over words./
눌어붙다 눌어붙다 [nuleobutda] /be scorched; burn; burn to the bottom of a pot or pan — For food to get burned and stick to the bottom of a pot or pan./settle down; stay on — To stay in one place and not leave for a long time./
눌은밥 눌은밥 [nuleunbab] /nureunbap; scorched rice — A dish made by pouring boiling water on scorched rice stuck to a rice cooking pot./
눕다 눕다 [nubda] /lie down; lay oneself down; lie — For a person or animal to lie with the back or flank horizontally to touch a certain place./be confined to bed; be ill in bed — To not be able to get up because one is sick./
눕히다 눕히다 [nubhida] /lay — To make a person or animal lie with the back or flank horizontally to touch a certain place./lay horizontally; put down broadways — To put something down sideways./
뉘다 뉘다 [nwida] /lay — To make a person or animal lie with the back or flank horizontally to touch a certain place./lay horizontally; put down broadways — To put something down sideways./make someone urinate; let someone defecate — To make someone discharge urine or feces from the body./
뉘앙스 뉘앙스 [nwiangseu] /nuance; subtle difference in meaning — A subtle difference in ways of talking, expression, etc., or the feeling or atmosphere caused by this difference./
뉘엿거리다 뉘엿거리다 [nwiyeosgeorida] /be going to set; be about to sink — For the sun to be going down little by little beyond the mountain or horizon./feel nausea; feel sick — To be sick at the stomach and feel like vomiting./
뉘엿뉘엿 뉘엿뉘엿 [nwiyeosnwiyeos] /nwiyeotnwiyeot — In the manner of the sun going down little by little beyond the mountain or horizon./nwiyeotnwiyeot — In the state of being sick at the stomach and feeling like vomiting./
뉘엿뉘엿하다 뉘엿뉘엿하다 [nwiyeosnwiyeoshada] /going to set; going to sink — The sun going down little by little beyond the mountain or horizon./feeling nausea; feeling sick — Sick at the stomach and feeling like vomiting./
뉘엿대다 뉘엿대다 [nwiyeosdaeda] /be going to set; be about to sink — For the sun to be going down little by little beyond the mountain or horizon./feel sick; feel nausea — To be sick at the stomach and feel like vomiting./
뉘엿하다 뉘엿하다 [nwiyeoshada] /being about to set; being ready to sink — The sun being on the verge of going down./
뉘우치다 뉘우치다 [nwiuchida] /introspect; examine oneself — To realize one's mistake and reflect on oneself./
뉘우침 뉘우침 [nwiuchim] /repentance; penitence; contrition — Realizing one's fault and reflecting on oneself and one's behavior./
뉴스 뉴스 [nyuseu] /news — A broadcast program that delivers new reports./news — New information unveiled for the first time./
뉴질랜드 뉴질랜드 [nyujilraendeu] /New Zealand — An island country in the southeastern part of the continent of Oceania; it is a major producer of wool, dairy products, etc.; its major languages are English and Maori; its capital is Wellington./
느글거리다 느글거리다 [neugeulgeorida] /nauseate; feel sick; feel nausea — To feel queasy and sick at the stomach continuously so much as to feel like vomiting./
느글느글 느글느글 [neugeulneugeul] /queasily — In the state of feeling queasy and sick at the stomach continuously so much as to feel like vomiting./
느글느글하다 느글느글하다 [neugeulneugeulhada] /nauseate; feel sick; feel nausea — To feel queasy and sick at the stomach continuously so much as to feel like vomiting./feeling sick; feeling nausea — Feeling queasy and sick at the stomach continuously so much as to feel like vomiting./greasy; heavy; thick — Food being very oily./nauseating; sickening; nauseous — Someone's behavior, way of speaking, etc., being disgusting and detestable./
느글대다 느글대다 [neugeuldaeda] /nauseate; feel sick; feel nausea — To feel queasy and sick at the stomach continuously so much as to feel like vomiting./
느긋이 느긋이 [neugeusi] /comfortably; in a relaxed manner; at ease — With composure, not hurrying./
느긋하다 느긋하다 [neugeushada] /comfortable; relaxed; carefree — Keeping one's composure and not hurrying./
느껍다 느껍다 [neukkeobda] /overflowing with; being deeply moved; being deeply impressed — One's heart being filled and choked with a certain emotion./
느끼다 느끼다 [neukkida] /sob; blubber; whimper — To cry sorrowfully while gulping down one's tears./be out of breath; pant — To gasp for breath./feel — To perceive a certain stimulus through a sensory organ such as the nose, skin, etc./feel — To experience a certain emotion in one's mind./realize; become aware of — To know a certain truth by realizing it in one's mind./think — To think about or perceive a certain subject or situation in a certain way./experience; know — To experience something in person and understand it./
느끼하다 느끼하다 [neukkihada] /oily; greasy; fatty — Food containing oil so much as to make someone feel nausea./nauseated; queasy — Feeling nausea because one has eaten a lot of oily food./nauseating; disgusting — Food being sickening because its taste, smell, etc., does not meet one's liking./disgusting; sickening — Someone's way of behaving, speaking, etc., being greasy and thus making others feel rather nauseated./
느낌 느낌 [neukkim] /feeling; sense; impression — A sense, mood, emotion, etc. felt in one's body and mind./
느낌표 느낌표 [neukkimpyo] /exclamation mark — A name for the punctuation mark '!' which, coming at the end of a sentence, expresses emphatic feelings./
느닷없다 느닷없다 [neudaseobsda] /abrupt; unexpected — Something happening very unexpectedly and suddenly./
느닷없이 느닷없이 [neudaseobsi] /abruptly; all of a sudden — In the manner of happening very unexpectedly and suddenly./
느려지다 느려지다 [neuryeojida] /slow — For the time taken to do something to increase./slow — For the time taken for something to be done to increase./weaken; slow — For force or energy to become weak./
느리다 느리다 [neurida] /slow; sluggish — Taking a long time to do something./slow — Taking a long time for something to happen./gentle — Being in a mild situation or condition./slow — Not quick-tempered./slow — A speech or sound being made slowly and thus being long and drawn-out./
느리터분하다 느리터분하다 [neuriteobunhada] /very slow — A person's behavior or personality being slow, making others feel irritated./
느림뱅이 느림뱅이 [neurimbaengi] /slowpoke; dawdler — (disparaging) A very lazy or slow-moving person./
느림보 느림보 [neurimbo] /slowpoke; dawdler — (disparaging) A very lazy, or slow-moving person or animal./
느릿느릿 느릿느릿 [neurisneuris] /sluggishly — A word describing the manner of moving very slowly./loosely — In the state of the texture of something being loose or rough./
느릿느릿하다 느릿느릿하다 [neurisneurishada] /sluggish — Moving very slowly./loose — The texture of something being loose or rough./
느릿하다 느릿하다 [neurishada] /sluggish — Moving rather slowly./
느물거리다 느물거리다 [neumulgeorida] /behave snakily; talk insidiously — To speak or behave habitually in a wicked and insidious manner./
느물느물 느물느물 [neumulneumul] /craftily; insidiously — A word describing the manner of speaking or behaving sneakily and slyly./
느물느물하다 느물느물하다 [neumulneumulhada] /behave snakily; talk insidiously — To habitually speak or behave in a wicked and insidious manner./
느물대다 느물대다 [neumuldaeda] /behave snakily; talk insidiously — To habitually speak or behave in a wicked and insidious manner./
느슨하다 느슨하다 [neuseunhada] /loose — Being in a loose state because a tied string, knot, etc., has come slightly undone./loose — Being in a loose state because a screw is not tightly fastened./relaxed — Having no tension in the mind./loose; negligent — A regulation, system, etc., being not strict./
느슨히 느슨히 [neuseunhi] /loosely — In a loose state as a tied string or knot, etc., which has come slightly undone./loosely — In a loose state as a screw which is not tightly fastened./slackly — Without tension in the mind./loosely; negligently — In a manner of a regulation, system, etc., being not strict./
느지막이 느지막이 [neujimagi] /rather late — In such a manner that it feels like it is late./
느지막하다 느지막하다 [neujimaghada] /rather late — Feeling like it is late./
느직하다 느직하다 [neujighada] /latish — The time or hour being a little late./having time — Having enough time before a deadline./loose — Strings, a knot, etc. being loose./somewhat slow — One's movements or behavior being a little slow./
느타리버섯 느타리버섯 [neutaribeoseos] /oyster mushroom — A brownish or whitish mushroom similar to a shell./
느티나무 느티나무 [neutinamu] /zelkova tree — A long-lived, tall tree, whose straight stem and branches bear small and round leaves densely./
늑골 늑골 [neuggol] /rib; costa — Bow-like bones in one's chest, the twelve pairs on the left and right side which protect organs such as the lungs and heart./
늑대 늑대 [neugdae] /wolf — A carnivorous beast that looks similar to a dog, and lives as a pack./wolf — (figurative) A man who likes to seduce women./
늑막 늑막 [neugmag] /pleura — One of two thin two-fold membranes surrounding both lungs./
늑막염 늑막염 [neugmagyeom] /pleurisy — An inflammation in a pleura, whose symptoms include a sharp pain in the side, fever, cough, and if severe, shortness of breath./
늑장 늑장 [neugjang] /dawdle; linger — An attitude of moving slowly and dawdling./
는 는 [neun] /neun — A postpositional particle used to indicate that a certain subject contrasts with something else./neun — A postpositional particle used to indicate that a certain subject is the topic of a sentence./neun — A postpositional particle used to indicate an emphasis./
는 고사하고 는 고사하고 [neun gosahago] /-neun gosahago — An expression used to mention the preceding content which is impossible or difficult, and indicate that the following content, which is easier, is also difficult./
는 말할 것도 없고 는 말할 것도 없고 [neun malhal geosdo eobsgo] /neun malhal geotdo eopgo — An expression used to indicate that the preceding statement is naturally so, and that, compared to that, the following statement is also as such./
는 물론 는 물론 [neun mulron] /-neun mullon — An expression used to indicate that the whole sentence, including the preceding statement, is naturally so./
는커녕 는커녕 [neunkeonyeong] /neunkeonyeong — A postpositional particle used to imply negation by emphasizing the preceding statement./
늘 늘 [neul] /always — Invariably, all the time./often — Frequently, in ordinary times./
늘그막 늘그막 [neulgeumag] /one's old age; later years of one's life — The time of life when one becomes old./
늘다 늘다 [neulda] /be extended — For the length, area, volume, etc., of something to become longer or bigger than before./multiply; grow — For numbers, quantities, etc., to become greater than before./increase; rise — For power, energy, force, etc., to become stronger than before./improve; make progress — To become better at something as one's talent, ability, etc., improves./increase; improve — For one's fortune to improve./be extended — For time or a period to become longer./
늘리다 늘리다 [neulrida] /extend; enlarge — To make the area or volume of something bigger than before./multiply; raise — To make something increase in number or quantity./increase — To make power, energy or force stronger than before./improve; build up — To improve one's ability or talent, so that one is better at something./increase (wealth) — To make oneself become better off, or make one's fortune become greater./extend — To make time or a period longer than before./
늘씬 늘씬 [neulssin] /soundly; harshly — So severely that someone can hardly move his body./
늘씬하다 늘씬하다 [neulssinhada] /slender; svelte — Having a thin body, being tall, and thus looking stylish./slim — Attractively thin and tall./
