달다 달다 [dalda] /heat up; become red-hot — For an uninflammable thing such as metal and stone to be heated and become very hot./blush; flush — For one's face to become hot because one has a fever, or is excited or shy./be impatient; fret — To feel nervous and anxious because one is concerned about something./hang; stick; fasten — To hang, stick, or fasten an object to something./install — To install a device or machine./add — To add an explanation, condition, etc., to a writing or speech./name — To give a name or title./record — To write in an account book./attach; link — To join objects in order for them to be connected./bring along — To make someone follow another person when going or coming to a place./be constantly sick — To constantly have minor illnesses and frequently be sick./weigh; measure — To figure out the weight of something with a balance./request; ask for — For the listener to get the speaker to have or enjoy something./sweet — Tasting like honey or sugar./delicious; tasty — Delicious in a way that stimulates one's appetite and makes one want to try the dish./satisfactory — Satisfactory in a way that pleases one./deserving — Accepting something as being deserved./dalda — An auxiliary verb indicating that the listener does an action meaning the preceding statement for the speaker./
