되다 되다 [doeda] /become — To have a new status or position./become; turn — To change or transform into something or someone else./come; fall — To reach a certain timing or state./reach — To reach or get to a certain quantity./amount to; reach — For the quantity or charge of a certain subject to be a certain amount, or for the location to be a certain place./be of virtue — To have great character and virtue as a human./feel; become — To be in a certain mental state./become; make — To be in a certain relationship with someone./be made of; be made from — To consist of a certain ingredient or component./be made up of; be composed of; consist of — To consist of a certain shape or structure./be under — For a document or papers to be written under the name of a certain person or organization./be completed; be finished — For a certain object or phenomenon to be created or made./work; go well — For something to work out well./grow well — For a plant to grow well./run down — For the function or life of a certain object to come to an end./get to; become — To reach a certain situation or state./be supposed to; be bound to; be scheduled to; be designed to — To be decided by destiny or be stipulated by rules or procedures./be required to; should; have to; need to; ought to — For something to have to be realized./do; be enough — To be all right or no problem./be allowed; be permitted; can; may — For something to be possible or allowed./get — To be done in by someone./become; constitute; make — To be in a state that has a special meaning./thick; hard-boiled — Rice or dough, etc., that is hard due to lack of moisture./tight — A rope being taut, not slack or loose./hard; tough — A task being so hard that it is difficult to deal with./severe; intense — Very bitter or harsh./
