두런대다 두런대다 [dureondaeda] /exchange whispers; whisper in a group — For several people to talk continuously in a low and quiet voice./
두런두런 두런두런 [dureondureon] /in affectionate whispers; with an affectionate murmur — A word imitating the sound of several people talking continuously in a low and quiet voice./
두런두런하다 두런두런하다 [dureondureonhada] /exchange whispers; whisper in a group — For several people to talk continuously in a low and quiet voice./
두렁 두렁 [dureong] /levee; ridge between rice paddies — A bank or a mound which becomes the boundary of two paddies or fields./
두레 두레 [dure] /dure — An organization of farmers in rural areas, who agree to give a hand to one another during busy periods./
두레박 두레박 [durebag] /durebak — A wooden bucke that is used to scoop water out of a well by pulling a rope attached to it./
두려움 두려움 [duryeoum] /fear — A feeling of fear and concern, or such a feeling./
두려워하다 두려워하다 [duryeowohada] /fear; dread; be afraid; be terrified — To want to avoid something or someone as one feels scared or fearful./be worried; be nervous; mind — To be worried, insecure, or reluctant./be reluctant to meet — To feel difficult or reluctant to meet another person./
두렵다 두렵다 [duryeobda] /fearful; scared — So afraid and frightened as to feel like avoiding something or someone./afraid — Feeling anxious and uneasy./
두령 두령 [duryeong] /boss — Usually the leader of an illegal organization such as a group of thieves./
두루 두루 [duru] /without exception — Evenly and variously without missing a thing or being partial./
두루낮춤 두루낮춤 [durunajchum] /informal addressee-lowering — A sentence-closing predicate that does not express deference to the listener./
두루높임 두루높임 [durunopim] /informal addressee-raising — A sentence-closing predicate that expresses moderate deference to the listener./
두루두루 두루두루 [duruduru] /without exception — Evenly and variously without missing a thing; both this and that./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing one getting along with everyone, although not on very close terms./
두루마기 두루마기 [durumagi] /durumagi — A traditional Korean male overcoat usually worn, when a man goes out./
두루마리 두루마리 [durumari] /roll — A roll of toilet paper or long paper./
