 — To have something in hand./raise; lift — To lift something from below in an upward motion./take; give — To find and give a certain fact or example./have; eat — (honorific) To eat./deulda — An auxiliary verb used when actively doing an action in the preceding statement./deulda — An auxiliary verb used when doing the preceding action as if to rush someone into doing it./
