디스코 디스코 [diseuko] /disco — Freestyle dance danced to lively music./
디스크 디스크 [diseukeu] /disk — A flat, round surface that contains a number of songs, which allows one to listen to the music through a phonograph or stereo system./slipped disk — Illness caused by bones in the back or neck being pushed back, pressing the nerves nearby./disk — A flat plate-shaped cartilage between the bones in the spine, which contributes to buffers shock./disk — A round-shaped plate used as an auxiliary memory unit in a computer./
