따로따로 따로따로 [ttarottaro] /individually; separately — Singly without being together with or being mixed with others./
따르다 따르다 [ttareuda] /follow — To go with someone behind him/her on the same track./equal; match — To reach the same level as an advanced one./respect — To be near or follow someone because one likes or respects him/her./obey; conform to — To do exactly as in a decided law, procedure, practice, or someone's opinion./go along; travel along — To walk on a certain line, in a direction, etc./do as someone does — To do as someone else does./happen together — For a certain incident to happen with another incident at the same time./depend on; be based on — To be based on a certain condition, standard, or situation./be proportional to — To be proportional to something./be based on — To be decided according to a certain thing./pour; spill — To tilt an object that contains liquid and have the liquid flow out, little by little./
따르르 따르르 [ttareureu] /rumbling — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of a small object rolling on a hard floor or shaking./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of sewing a thin cloth by a sewing machine./ting-a-ling — A word imitating the sound of a telephone, alarm, etc., ringing./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing the movement of unwinding thread, a long strap, etc., from a reel or winding it on a reel all at once./
따르릉 따르릉 [ttareureung] /ting-a-ling — A word imitating the sound of the small bell of a bicycle, a doorbell, telephone, alarm, etc., ringing./
