딱따구리 딱따구리 [ttagttaguri] /woodpecker — A bird that makes a hole in a tree with its hard beak and eats bugs in the tree./
딱딱 딱딱 [ttagttag] /with snaps; snappingly; with cracks — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of a hard object breaking or hitting against another hard object again and again./one after another; in the same breath — In the manner of continuous movements, happenings, etc., stopping or ceasing at the same time or in succession./decisively — In the manner of cutting off or behaving very resolutely and daringly in succession./broad — In a state in which all of several people straighten up their shoulders, puff their chests out, or open their eyes or mouths wide at the same time or in succession./precisely — In a state in which all of several things are in harmony precisely in number, amount, size, situation, etc./one after another; at once — In the manner of several people or things running into one another at the same time or in succession./strongly — In a state in which several people or things stand firmly without moving, at the same time or in succession./firmly — In a state in which several things stick to something tightly at the same time or in succession./
