딸부자 딸부자 [ttalbuja] /family with many daughters — A person, parents or a family with many daughters./
딸아이 딸아이 [ttalai] /daughter; little girl — One's daughter who is little./daughter — A term used to address one's daughter in front of others./
딸애 딸애 [ttalae] /daughter; little girl — One's daughter who is little./daughter — A term used to address one's daughter in front of others./
딸자식 딸자식 [ttaljasig] /daughter — A child who is female./
땀 땀 [ttam] /sweat — A clear salty liquid that is excreted through the skin when one is hot, sick or nervous./sweat — (figurative) Hard work or effort./stitch — A mark made when a threaded needle goes into and then comes out of something one time./stitch — A unit for counting the marks made when a threaded needle goes into and comes out of something./
땀(을) 빼다 땀(을) 빼다 [ttam(eul) ppaeda] /drain sweat — To go through hardships such as something very tough or difficult./
땀(을) 흘리다 땀(을) 흘리다 [ttam(eul) heulrida] /shed sweat — To exert a lot of power and effort./
땀구멍 땀구멍 [ttamgumeong] /pore — A small hole in the skin through which sweat passes./
땀내 땀내 [ttamnae] /smell of sweat — An unpleasant smell from a sweaty body or clothes./
땀띠 땀띠 [ttamtti] /heat rash — A rash on the skin caused by sweat./
땀방울 땀방울 [ttambangul] /beads of sweat — Small drops of sweat like water drops./
땀자국 땀자국 [ttamjagug] /sweat stains — Stains caused by perspiration on clothes, etc./
땀투성이 땀투성이 [ttamtuseongi] /being full of sweat — A state of the body or clothes being soaked because of sweating too much./
땅 땅 [ttang] /ground; land — The part of the earth that consists of soil or stones instead of water./territory; land — The territory of a nation./town — A region or province./plot; land; property — An inhabitable place where one can construct buildings or farms./land; soil — Soil or its characteristic./ground; place — An environment or basis in which one can enjoy his/her rights or work./land — A society or world./
땅 짚고 헤엄치기 땅 짚고 헤엄치기 [ttang jipgo heeomchigi] /swimming while touching the ground — An expression that refers to a very easy task./
땅(이) 꺼지게[꺼지도록] 땅(이) 꺼지게[꺼지도록] [ttang(i) kkeojige[kkeojidorog]] /in the manner of[as if] making land sink — The manner of drawing a very deep and loud sigh./
땅값 땅값 [ttanggabs] /land value — The price of land./
땅거미 땅거미 [ttanggeomi] /dusk; twilight — The slight darkness between sunset and night./
땅굴 땅굴 [ttanggul] /tunnel — A path or road dug underground./pit; hollow; burrow — A long, deep hole made like a tunnel by digging in the ground./
땅기다 땅기다 [ttanggida] /be cramped — To have a very tightening, pulling feeling./
땅꾼 땅꾼 [ttangkkun] /snake hunter; snake seller — A person who makes a living by hunting and selling snakes./
땅끝 땅끝 [ttangkkeut] /land's end — The very end of land./end of the earth — (figurative) The furthest place./
땅덩어리 땅덩어리 [ttangdeongeori] /land mass; territory — Land belonging to a bordered region such as that of a nation or continent./
땅덩이 땅덩이 [ttangdeongi] /land mass; territory — Land belonging to a bordered region such as that of a nation or continent./
땅따먹기 땅따먹기 [ttangttameoggi] /ttangttameokgi — land-winning game; land expansion game: A children's game in which a player flicks a small stone and wins the area the stone lands on./
땅딸막하다 땅딸막하다 [ttangttalmaghada] /dumpy; chunky — A person being small and having a wide frame./
땅딸보 땅딸보 [ttangttalbo] /shorty; Humpty-Dumpty — (teasing) A short and stout person./
땅딸이 땅딸이 [ttangttali] /shorty; Humpty-Dumpty — (teasing) A short and stout person./
땅딸하다 땅딸하다 [ttangttalhada] /dumpy; chunky — A person being small and having a wide frame./
땅뙈기 땅뙈기 [ttangttwaegi] /small patch of land — A small plot of field, rice paddy, or land/
땅마지기 땅마지기 [ttangmajigi] /small plot of land — Small patch of field or paddy./
땅문서 땅문서 [ttangmunseo] /land registry certificate — A document proving that a parcel of land is legally owned by its holder./
땅바닥 땅바닥 [ttangbadag] /bare ground — Ground not covered with anything./
땅볼 땅볼 [ttangbol] /ground ball; grounder — A ball batted in a baseball game or kicked in a soccer game, which then rolls on the ground./
땅속 땅속 [ttangsog] /underground — A place below the ground./
땅에 떨어지다 땅에 떨어지다 [ttange tteoleojida] /fall to the ground — For the authority or morale to decrease to such an extent as to be irrecoverable./
땅에서 솟았나 하늘에서 떨어졌나 땅에서 솟았나 하늘에서 떨어졌나 [ttangeseo sosassna haneuleseo tteoleojyeossna] /Did it rise from the ground, or fall from the sky? — An expression to describe a situation where something that was not expected appears./
땅을 칠 노릇 땅을 칠 노릇 [ttangeul chil noreus] /a situation that makes one pound the ground — Something that makes one furious and feels is unfair./
땅콩 땅콩 [ttangkong] /peanut — A savory type of reddish brown nut which grows in the soil inside a thick shell and thin inner skin./
땋다 땋다 [ttahda] /braid; plait — To divide hair or threads into two or more sections, twist them, and make them into one./tie a hair ribbon — To put a daenggi, a traditional Korean hair ribbon, at the end of braided hair./
때 때 [ttae] /time — A certain moment or part of time./meal — The time for having a meal./perfect time; right moment — A perfect time for doing something./time — The time when a certain phenomenon or event occurs./certain case — A state of being in a certain case./time — A state of being during a certain period./season — A season subdivided according to a change in climate, such as spring, summer, fall, and winter./dirt — A substance that is formed on the clothes or body when filthy dust particles coagulate or when dead skin and dust get mixed together./taint; defilement — A wordly quality that lacks innocence./
때 빼고 광내다 때 빼고 광내다 [ttae ppaego gwangnaeda] /remove the dirt and polish — To wash clean and adorn oneself for a good occasion or an important appointment./
때가 빠지다 때가 빠지다 [ttaega ppajida] /The dirt is removed — For an awkward or dowdy look to disappear./
때깔 때깔 [ttaekkal] /good looks and color — A pleasing appearance and color./
때늦다 때늦다 [ttaeneujda] /late — Late for the appointed time./belated — Being past the appropriate time./out of season — Being past the season/
때다 때다 [ttaeda] /burn — To set fire in a fireplace or fuel hole./
때때로 때때로 [ttaettaero] /occasionally — From time to time, depending on the situation./
때때옷 때때옷 [ttaettaeos] /children's colorful clothes — Pretty and colorful clothes for children./
때려누이다 때려누이다 [ttaeryeonuida] /knock down; knock flat — To make someone fall by striking him/her with a clenched fist or a tool./knock out; defeat — To win completely in a competition or fight./
때려눕히다 때려눕히다 [ttaeryeonubhida] /knock down; knock flat — To make someone fall by striking him/her with a clenched fist or a tool./knock out; defeat — To win completely in a competition or fight./
때려잡다 때려잡다 [ttaeryeojabda] /beat and catch — To catch and beat someone with a fist or club, etc./attack hard — To attack another person, group, army, etc., strongly so that they cannot rise again./guess — To guess a situation or condition by looking closely at circumstances./
때려죽이다 때려죽이다 [ttaeryeojugida] /knock to death — To kill a person or animal ruthlessly./
때려치우다 때려치우다 [ttaeryeochiuda] /quit; give up — (slang) To quit a job or what one has been engaged in./
때로 때로 [ttaero] /occasionally — Depending on the situation./sometimes — Once in a while./
때를 벗다 때를 벗다 [ttaereul beosda] /take off the dirt — For a young or dowdy look to disappear./
때리는 시어머니보다 말리는 시누이가 더 밉다 때리는 시어머니보다 말리는 시누이가 더 밉다 [ttaerineun sieomeoniboda malrineun sinuiga deo mibda] /It is not the mother-in-law who beats you, but the sister-in-law who tries to stop her that is more hateful — Those who pretend to care, but in fact do harm and speak ill of you are more hateful./
때리다 때리다 [ttaerida] /hit; beat; strike; smack; slap; punch — To hit hard and give pain with a hand or something in hand./hit; beat; strike; bump; crash; knock — For an object to be struck hard into another object./criticize; attack; lash; bash — To criticize a certain fault with words or writing in a sharp manner./hit; beat; strike — To give huge emotional resonance or shock./do carelessly; do randomly; do haphazardly — (disparaging) To do something carelessly and randomly./
때린 놈은 다리 못 뻗고 자도 맞은 놈은 다리 뻗고 잔다 때린 놈은 다리 못 뻗고 자도 맞은 놈은 다리 뻗고 잔다 [ttaerin nomeun dari mos ppeodgo jado majeun nomeun dari ppeodgo janda] /Those who have beaten a person cannot sleep with their legs stretched out, but those who have been beaten can sleep with their legs stretched out — Those who do harm to others feel anxious while those who are done harm feel easy./
때마침 때마침 [ttaemachim] /just in time — Properly at a given time./
때맞추다 때맞추다 [ttaemajchuda] /be on time — To do something on time./
때문 때문 [ttaemun] /because; because of — A cause or reason for a certain incident./
때밀이 때밀이 [ttaemili] /body scrubber — A person who scrubs people's bodies as a job in a public bathhouse./body scrub — An act of rubbing dirt off the body./
때수건 때수건 [ttaesugeon] /washcloth — A small cloth made of rough fabric so that dirt on the body is easily removed./
때우다 때우다 [ttaeuda] /solder; tinker — To block a hole or crack with something./eat lightly — To substitute a meal with a simple snack./supplement; substitute — To supplement or substitute something with another thing./have a smaller misfortune — To avoid a form of major bad luck by substituting it with a form of small trouble./kill time — To spend spare time doing something else./
때움질 때움질 [ttaeumjil] /soldering; brazing — The act of blocking a hole or gap with another thing./mending — The act of stitching a piece of worn-out clothing, shoes, etc./temporary fix — The act of fixing mistakes as needed./
때움질하다 때움질하다 [ttaeumjilhada] /solder; braze — To block a hole or gap with another thing./mend — To stitch a worn out clothing, shoe, etc./fix temporarily — To fix mistakes as needed./
땔감 땔감 [ttaelgam] /fuel — Material used to make a fire./
땔나무 땔나무 [ttaelnamu] /firewood; fuelwood — Chopped wood that is used as fuel./
땜 땜 [ttaem] /patching; soldering — The act of covering a hole or gap with certain material./darning; patching — The act of darning a worn-out item of clothing, shoes, etc./patching; temporary measure — The act of correcting what is wrong on an impromptu basis./because; because of — A cause or reason for a certain incident./
땜장이 땜장이 [ttaemjangi] /tinker — A person whose job it is to repair things by filling cracks and holes./
땜질 땜질 [ttaemjil] /soldering; brazing — The act of blocking a hole or gap with another thing./mending — The act of stitching a piece of worn-out clothing, shoes, etc./temporary fix — The act of fixing mistakes as needed./
땜질하다 땜질하다 [ttaemjilhada] /solder; braze — To block a hole or gap with another thing./mend — To stitch a piece of worn-out clothing, shoes, etc./fix temporarily — To fix mistakes as needed./
땟국 땟국 [ttaesgug] /dirt — Dirty sweat or water./
땡 땡 [ttaeng] /pair — Two cards of the same denomination in a hwatu game./good luck; good fortune — (slang) Unexpected good luck or good fortune come upon by chance./
땡감 땡감 [ttaenggam] /unripe persimmon — A persimmon that is unripe and astringent./
땡땡 땡땡 [ttaengttaeng] /clang-clang — A word imitating the sound of beating a metal object like a bell, a bowl, etc./
땡땡이 땡땡이 [ttaengttaengi] /loafing; being idle — The state of being lazy and not doing one's duty by being sly./
땡땡이중 땡땡이중 [ttaengttaengijung] /priest only in name; unworthy priest — A Buddhist monk who lacks knowledge about prayers and Buddhism, deserving no respect./
땡땡이치다 땡땡이치다 [ttaengttaengichida] /loaf; be idle — To be lazy and not do one's duty by being sly./
땡땡하다 땡땡하다 [ttaengttaenghada] /swollen; bloated — A person's body being taut as a result of weight gain or swelling./compact; packed — Too solid and hard to be compressed or dented./
땡볕 땡볕 [ttaengbyeot] /scorching sun — A blazing sunlight that beats down harshly./
땡전 땡전 [ttaengjeon] /penny; red cent — A trivial amount of money./
떠가다 떠가다 [tteogada] /float away — For an object, etc., to float in the air or on water, away from the speaker./
떠꺼머리 떠꺼머리 [tteokkeomeori] /tteokkeomeori — pigtail; pigtailed person: (archaic) A long and braided hairstyle of a single man or single woman who is old enough to get married, or a person in that hairstyle./
떠나가다 떠나가다 [tteonagada] /leave; depart — To move from a place where one has been to another place./reverberate with — For a sound to be made that is so noisy and loud as to vibrate the surrounding area./
떠나다 떠나다 [tteonada] /leave; depart — To move from a place where one has been to another place./leave — To get out of a place where one has been or part with people whom one has known, in order to move to another place or meet other people./be estranged from; cut oneself from — To sever one's relations with something or some people, or become unrelated to them./set forth — To set out to do something./start off; leave — To begin a journey./pass away — (euphemism) To die./
떠나보내다 떠나보내다 [tteonabonaeda] /let go — To let someone leave a place where he/she has been and go to another place./
떠나오다 떠나오다 [tteonaoda] /leave — To leave a place where one has been and come to another place./
떠내다 떠내다 [tteonaeda] /scoop — To scoop up liquid and carry it outside./scoop up; ladle out — To scoop what is floating on water./dig up — To dig the top grass or soil only./fillet; slice — To slice off the flesh of fish or meat./
떠내려가다 떠내려가다 [tteonaeryeogada] /be carried away; be washed away — To float in the water and go with the flow./
떠내려오다 떠내려오다 [tteonaeryeooda] /float down — To float in the water and come with the flow./
떠넘기다 떠넘기다 [tteoneomgida] /shift onto — To shift one's task or responsibility to someone against his/her will./
떠다니다 떠다니다 [tteodanida] /float — To move here and there, floating on the air or water./drift; float — To stroll here and there, not deciding on one's destination./
떠다밀다 떠다밀다 [tteodamilda] /push; thrust; shove — To push an object, etc., in full strength and make it advance./shift one's responsibility onto — To pass one's task or responsibility on to someone against his/her will./
떠돌다 떠돌다 [tteodolda] /wander; roam — To move from place to place, not staying long in one place./drift; hover — To float in the air or water, and move around./circulate; go around — For a rumor or words to spread widely./
떠돌아다니다 떠돌아다니다 [tteodoladanida] /wander; roam — To move from place to place, without a fixed place to stay./drift; hover — To float in the air or water, and move around./circulate; go around — For a rumor or words to continue to spread widely./
떠돌이 떠돌이 [tteodoli] /wanderer; drifter; vagabond — A person who wanders around here and there without a fixed home./
떠들다 떠들다 [tteodeulda] /clamor; make a noise — To speak noisily in a loud voice./speak loudly — To tell or say something loudly./spread — To speak about something here and there, spreading it./insist — To insist on one's opinion or position over and over./talk freely — For many people to pick a topic and say many things about it./uncover; lift — To uncover or raise a part of something that has been covered or hidden./
떠들썩하다 떠들썩하다 [tteodeulsseoghada] /clamor; make noise — For a lot of people to talk loudly./boisterous; uproarious — Noisy as a lot of people talk./turbulent; disturbed; agitated — Noisy and confused due to a rumor or event./
떠듬거리다 떠듬거리다 [tteodeumgeorida] /stammer; stutter — To speak or read haltingly./
떠듬대다 떠듬대다 [tteodeumdaeda] /stammer; stutter — To speak or read haltingly./
떠듬떠듬 떠듬떠듬 [tteodeumtteodeum] /in a stammering manner; stammeringly — In the manner of hesitating, or losing control of one's tongue in speaking or reading./
떠듬떠듬하다 떠듬떠듬하다 [tteodeumtteodeumhada] /stammer; stutter — To speak or read haltingly./
떠름하다 떠름하다 [tteoreumhada] /astringent — A bit bitter-tasting./reluctant — Not very inclined to do something./
떠맡기다 떠맡기다 [tteomatgida] /charge; lay — To thrust a task or responsibility on someone./
떠맡다 떠맡다 [tteomatda] /take on; assume — To take over a task or responsibility./
떠먹다 떠먹다 [tteomeogda] /scoop up; ladle; spoon up — To eat food by scooping it up with a spoon, etc./
떠먹이다 떠먹이다 [tteomeogida] /spoon-feed — To scoop up food with a spoon, etc., and feed it to someone./
떠메다 떠메다 [tteomeda] /carry on the shoulder — To lift up and put something heavy over one's shoulder or back./take responsibility — To take charge of a certain work or responsibility./
떠밀다 떠밀다 [tteomilda] /push; thrust; shove — To make something move forward by applying power to it./dump on — To forcibly shift a task or responsibility onto someone./
떠밀리다 떠밀리다 [tteomilrida] /be pushed; be thrust; be shoved — To come to move something forward by power applied to it./
떠받다 떠받다 [tteobadda] /butt — To hit or push someone or something with a head or horns./
떠받들다 떠받들다 [tteobaddeulda] /support; lift — To support something on the bottom and raise it high./take good care of — To pay respect to or treat someone well./respect — To deem someone respectable and serve him/her well./
떠받치다 떠받치다 [tteobadchida] /support — To support something on the bottom to keep it from collapsing or falling./bolster — To support a country, organization, etc., so that it stays strong./
떠받히다 떠받히다 [tteobadhida] /be butted — To be hit or pushed hard by a head or horns./
떠벌리다 떠벌리다 [tteobeolrida] /exaggerate; brag — To exaggerate and speak about an unimportant thing here and there./
떠벌이다 떠벌이다 [tteobeolida] /set up in a large scale — To start or open a project, business, etc., on a large scale./
떠보다 떠보다 [tteoboda] /sound out — To find out someone's thought by stealth./
떠안기다 떠안기다 [tteoangida] /charge; lay — To thrust a task or responsibility on someone./
떠안다 떠안다 [tteoanda] /take on; assume — To take over a task or responsibility./
떠오다 떠오다 [tteooda] /come floating — For an object, etc., to float in the air or on water and approach the speaker./
떠오르다 떠오르다 [tteooreuda] /rise; come up — To float and go upward./come across one's mind; strike — For a memory to be brought back; for an idea to occur to one./appear — For a certain expression to be revealed on one's face./emerge — To appear as the object of attention./
떠올리다 떠올리다 [tteoolrida] /recall; recollect — To bring back one's memory or come up with an idea that one could not think of./show — To make a certain expression revealed on one's face./
떡 떡 [tteog] /tteok; rice cake — A dish made by steaming or boiling grain powder such as injeolmi, rice cake coated with red bean powder or soy bean powder, and songpyeon, half-moon-shaped rice cake, etc./mat — (figurative) Hair that is matted due to lack of washing, etc./broad — In a state in which one's chest and shoulders are wide, or one's eyes and mouth are open wide./all of a sudden — In the manner of meeting suddenly./strongly — In the state of standing firmly./strongly — In the state of adhering tightly to something./
떡 먹듯 떡 먹듯 [tteog meogdeus] /like eating tteok, rice cake — Easily; unconcernedly or indifferently./
떡 본 김에 굿 한다 떡 본 김에 굿 한다 [tteog bon gime gus handa] /perform a gut, an exorcism, as tteok, rice cake, is in sight — To have a good chance by accident to do something that one has planned to do./
떡 본 김에 제사 지낸다 떡 본 김에 제사 지낸다 [tteog bon gime jesa jinaenda] /perform an ancestral rite as tteok, rice cake, is in sight — To have a good chance by accident to do something that one has planned to do./
떡 주무르듯 떡 주무르듯 [tteog jumureudeus] /like kneading tteok, rice cake — As one wishes or likes./
떡 줄 사람은 생각지도 않는데 김칫국부터 마신다 떡 줄 사람은 생각지도 않는데 김칫국부터 마신다 [tteog jul sarameun saenggagjido anhneunde gimchisgugbuteo masinda] /drink kimchitguk, kimchi liquid, in advance even if the one who has some tteok, rice cake, is not thinking about giving them to others at all — To behave based on the hasty assumption that one will get something when the person who has that something is not even thinking about giving it away./
떡- 떡- [tteog-] /tteok- — A prefix used to mean small or young./
떡가루 떡가루 [tteoggaru] /tteokgaru; rice powder — A grain powder milled to be made into tteok, rice cake./
떡값 떡값 [tteoggabs] /tteokgap — money for rice cakes; bonus: (figurative) A special allowance given to employees on national holidays such as Seollal and Chuseok, Korean Thanksgiving Day./tteokgap — money for rice cakes; bribe: (figurative) Money offered to a helpful person in order to court his/her favor./
떡고물 떡고물 [tteoggomul] /tteokgomul — Flour sprinkled on tteok, rice cake, in order to improve its shape and taste./throw-in; extra; addition — (figurative) A small extra profit obtained while doing something./
떡국 떡국 [tteoggug] /tteokguk; sliced rice cake soup — A dish made by cutting garaetteok, rice cake stick, into thin slices and boiling them in clear broth./
떡국을 먹다 떡국을 먹다 [tteoggugeul meogda] /eat tteokguk, sliced rice cake soup — To age one year./
떡두꺼비 떡두꺼비 [tteogdukkeobi] /strong baby boy — (figurative) A newborn baby that is big and healthy./
떡메 떡메 [tteogme] /tteokme; rice cake hammer — A large wooden hammer used to pound cooked rice to make tteok, rice cake./
떡밥 떡밥 [tteogbab] /paste bait — Bait made by adding bean flour or pupa powder to rice bran, kneading the mix, and dividing it into small lumps./tteokbap — Rice cooked to make tteok, rice cake./
떡방아 떡방아 [tteogbanga] /tteokbang-a; rice pounding — The act of pounding rice to make it into tteok, rice cake, or the pounder itself./
떡볶이 떡볶이 [tteogbokki] /tteokbokki — Boiled rice cake with seasoning, made by boiling garaetteok, rice cake stick, vegetables, seasonings such as soy sauce, gochujang, red chili paste, etc./
떡시루 떡시루 [tteogsiru] /tteoksiru; earthenware steamer — Round clayware with small holes in its bottom, used to steam tteok, rice cake./
