떡이 생기다 떡이 생기다 [tteogi saenggida] /gain tteok, rice cake — To gain benefit./
떡잎 떡잎 [tteogip] /seed leaf — The first leaf emerging from soil as the seed sprouts./
떨거지 떨거지 [tteolgeoji] /dregs — (disparaging) Worthless people who are a burden although they belong to a group./
떨구다 떨구다 [tteolguda] /glance down — To glance down./drop — To make something above move down./drop; leave out — To drop or leave behind what one has been holding./leave behind — To make someone fall behind or be left out./bend one's head — To bend one's head down./reduce; discount — To lower a price or amount./use up — To use up something that has been used./lose — To make someone or something lose a value, position, honor, etc./shake off — To shake something very hard so that it falls off./drop; stop thinking — To drop a bad thought or feeling./drop; fail — To make someone not passing or not picked in a test, contest, etc./
떨기 떨기 [tteolgi] /cluster — A lump of stems that have sprouted from a root./tteolgi — bunch: A unit for counting clustered flowers or grass, etc./
떨꺼덕 떨꺼덕 [tteolkkeodeog] /click — A word imitating the sound made when big and hard objects hit each other./
떨꺽 떨꺽 [tteolkkeog] /click — A word imitating the sound made when big and hard objects hit each other./
떨다 떨다 [tteolda] /shake; tremble — For something to be shaken repeatedly and fast in a narrow range./pinch a penny; be cheap; be a miser — To be very stingy and afraid of spending money./tremble; shudder; shiver — To feel cold or very scared./tremble — To shake a part of one's body or whole body, fast and repeatedly./shake — For one's voice to vibrate more than usual./act recklessly — To repeat a certain act lightly and carelessly./shake off — To beat or shake off something that has been hung or stuck./use up; spend all — To use up all the money or goods./stop thinking — To get rid of a thought or feeling./sell out; buy all — To sell out all the leftovers or buy them./
떨떠름하다 떨떠름하다 [tteoltteoreumhada] /astringent — A little bit bitter-tasting./reluctant; disinclined — Unwilling to do something./
떨렁 떨렁 [tteolreong] /jingle; tinkle — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of a big bell, hanging object, etc., swaying./suddenly; unexpectedly — In the state of feeling one's heart lurch or sink when one is suddenly frightened or scared./
떨리다 떨리다 [tteolrida] /tremble — For a part of one's body or whole body to be shaken fast and repeatedly./be shaken — For one's voice to vibrate more than usual./be shaken off; be beaten off; fall off — For something hanging from or attached to something else to be detached from it./
떨어내다 떨어내다 [tteoleonaeda] /shake off; beat off — To make something hanging from or attached to something else, detached from it./
떨어뜨리다 떨어뜨리다 [tteoleotteurida] /drop — To let something at the top fall to the bottom./drop; lose — To drop or miss something that one has hold./leave behind — To make someone fall behind or leave someone behind./reject; sift out — To make someone fail to pass an examination or be picked in a selection./depreciate; degrade; debase — To lower the degree or level of something./lower; lessen — To make a figure such as a price and temperature become lower./wear out — To make clothes, shoes, etc., wear out  and thus not be used anymore./exhaust; run out — To consume all of something that one has been using./devalue; demean — To make value, status, honor, etc., lost./lower — To make one's eyes or a part of one's body face downward./move away — To widen the distance from something./separate — To make people break up or estranged from each other./
떨어지다 떨어지다 [tteoleojida] /fall; drop — To move downwardly./fall; be reduced to — To fall into a certain state or situation./fall into; be handed over; be taken over — For one's area, fortress, etc. to be handed over to the enemy./arrive; get to; reach — To get off or arrive at a certain location./be disaffected toward; take a disgust at; be put off by — To lose affection for or become estranged from someone./fall on; be assigned — For an urgent task or mission to be assigned./be given; be sent; be delivered — For an order or permission to be given./fall behind; lag behind; be inferior to; fall short of — For the level of something to fall short of something else./fail in; lose; be defeated; be unsuccessful — To miss the cut in an exam, election, competition, etc./lag; be left behind; separate from — To not go together with or follow but lag or remain behind./fall off; come off; be removed — For something clung or attached to something to become split or torn off./fall; drop; slip — For something held to slip and come out./leave; lose contact with; be separated from; be severed; be cut off — To have one's relationship severed or broken off with someone./be away from; be off from; be apart from — To have a certain distance./fall; drop; decline; decrease — For a price, temperature, level, etc. to become lower or go down./be cured; be healed; recover from; get over — For a disease or habit to disappear./go down; sink — For the sun or moon to set in the west./be gained; be earned — For a profit to be generated./run out of; be out of — For nothing to be left because a lack of something is not supplemented./be lost; be spoiled — For an appetite to disappear./dry up; be cut off — For a task to finish./wear out; wear away; fray; become threadbare — For clothes or shoes to become useless as they are old and worn out./die; pass away — For one's breath to be cut off./miscarry — For a fetus to die./be clearly divided without a remainder — For a certain figure to be divided without a remainder in division./fall short of; be left unpaid — For an amount or a portion of a price to be unpaid./be uttered; be said — For words to be uttered./be turned on; be given — For a designated signal to appear./be lost; diminish; weaken; be reduced — For something that has existed or been obtained to disappear./
떨어지지 않는 발길 떨어지지 않는 발길 [tteoleojiji anhneun balgil] /steps that are hard to take — Steps of a person who does not want to leave or go./
떨어트리다 떨어트리다 [tteoleoteurida] /drop — To let something at the top fall to the bottom./drop; lose — To drop or miss something that one has hold of./leave behind — To make someone fall behind or leave someone behind./lower — To make one's eyes face downward./lower; lessen — To make a figure such as a price and temperature become lower./wear out — To make clothes, shoes, etc., wear out  and thus not be used anymore./exhaust; run out — To spend all of something that one has used./devalue; demean — To lower or impair the degree or level of value, reputation, status, quality, etc./lower — To make one's head face downward./reject; sift out — To make someone fail to pass an examination or be picked in a selection./move away — To widen the distance from something./separate — To make people break up or become estranged from each other./
떨이 떨이 [tteoli] /remainder offered at a cheap price — The act of selling all the remaining stock at a cheap price, or the products./
떨이하다 떨이하다 [tteolihada] /offer remainder at a cheap price — To sell all the remaining stock at a cheap price./
떨치다 떨치다 [tteolchida] /become well known — To spread or publicize one's name or influence./shake off — To shake something very hard so that it falls off./stop thinking — To drop a bad thought or feeling./
떫다 떫다 [tteolbda] /astringent; puckery — Bitter- and rough-tasting./displeasing; unpalatable — Displeased because someone's remark or behavior is not right./
떳떳이 떳떳이 [tteostteosi] /honorably — Confidently without hesitation in the face of a challenge./
떳떳하다 떳떳하다 [tteostteoshada] /dignified; unshamed — Having a clear conscience; holding one's head up./
떵떵 떵떵 [tteongtteong] /with hot air — In the manner of affirming recklessly./boastfully; high on the hog — In the manner of boasting of one's authority or wealth./
떵떵거리다 떵떵거리다 [tteongtteonggeorida] /be boastful — To boast of one's authority or wealth./
떵떵대다 떵떵대다 [tteongtteongdaeda] /be boastful — To boast of one's authority or wealth./
떼 떼 [tte] /group; aggregation — Many people or animals gathered at one place./pestering; begging for something — The act of asking for an unreasonable thing insistently./
떼거리 떼거리 [ttegeori] /group; gang; band — (slang) A group of persons or animals that act together with the same purpose./
떼거지 떼거지 [ttegeoji] /beggars in groups — Beggars hanging about in groups./victims — (figurative) A group of people who collectively face hardships as a result of a flood, earthquake, war, etc./crowd; party; group — (slang) A mob of people moving about in crowds./
떼구루루 떼구루루 [ttegururu] /rumbling — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of a somewhat large, hard object rolling on a hard floor./
떼굴떼굴 떼굴떼굴 [ttegulttegul] /rolling — A word describing the movement of a large, hard object or a person rolling continuously./
떼다 떼다 [tteda] /take off; detach; remove — To separate something attached or connected to each other./take out of; take from; take away from; deduct; set aside — To take a part out of the whole of something./turn away from; break away from; separate from; distance from — For one's mind to turn away from something or someone./take one's eyes off — To take one's gaze off of something./buy wholesale; purchase wholesale; get wholesale — To purchase a large quantity of goods at once to sell them back as a business./separate from; pull apart from; take away from — To leave something or someone that one was together with alone./take a step; walk — To move in steps./first words — To begin to talk./abort — To abort a baby./finish up — To finish learning something./issue — To write up and give or receive documents such as a check, bill or certificate./wean off — To stop doing something that was done daily at an early stage of development./
떼돈 떼돈 [ttedon] /fortune — A large amount of money./
떼먹다 떼먹다 [ttemeogda] /not pay back — To not return money, an object, etc., that one borrowed from someone./embezzle — To take possession of someone's money or object through unlawful means./
떼밀다 떼밀다 [ttemilda] /thrust aside; force aside — To push something in full strength./
떼쓰다 떼쓰다 [ttesseuda] /fret; badger — To demand or strongly insist on something so as to do as what one wants./
떼어 놓은 당상 떼어 놓은 당상 [tteeo noheun dangsang] /a high government post that is set aside — An expression used to describe a situation where one is so sure that something will definitely go as planned./
떼어먹다 떼어먹다 [tteeomeogda] /not pay back — To not return money, an object, etc., that one borrowed from someone./embezzle — To take possession of someone's money or object through unlawful means./
떼이다 떼이다 [tteida] /be cheated — To fail to receive money or goods that one is subject to receive from someone./
떼쟁이 떼쟁이 [ttejaengi] /insistent person — A person who often throws a tantrum to get what he/she wants./
떼죽음 떼죽음 [ttejugeum] /mass death — The death of many things, such as people, animals or plants, at the same time./
뗏목 뗏목 [ttesmog] /raft — An object made to float by joining logs side by side to carry a person or object./
