뚜벅대다 뚜벅대다 [ttubeogdaeda] /make clear footsteps — For the sound of walking with clearly audible footsteps to be heard./
뚜벅뚜벅 뚜벅뚜벅 [ttubeogttubeog] /struttingly — A word imitating the sound or describing the movement of walking continuosly, making clear sounds of footsteps./
뚜벅뚜벅하다 뚜벅뚜벅하다 [ttubeogttubeoghada] /make clear footsteps — For the sound of walking with clearly audible footsteps to be heard./
뚜벅이다 뚜벅이다 [ttubeogida] /make clear footsteps — For the sound of walking with clearly audible footsteps to be heard./
뚜쟁이 뚜쟁이 [ttujaengi] /matchmaker — (disparaging) A person in the middle who introduces a man and a woman to each other so that they can get married./
뚝 뚝 [ttug] /with a thud — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of a big object or waterdrop, etc., falling./with a heavy snap — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of a big, hard object being broken or cut./with a strike — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of hitting a hard object one time./in the manner of snapping something off — In the manner of picking or nipping something off something else it is clinging or attached to without hesitation./all of a sudden; abruptly — In the manner that something stops suddenly./resolutely — In the manner of speaking or behaving very firmly and definitely./completely — In the state of something having been completely used up./drastically; remarkably — In the manner that a grade, ranking, etc., falls or a degree gets weak very conspicuously./considerably far away — Being located quite distantly./
뚝딱 뚝딱 [ttugttag] /easily; fast — A word describing one handling a job easily without a pause./
뚝딱거리다 뚝딱거리다 [ttugttaggeorida] /pound — For one's heart to throb continuously from being startled or in fear./hammer — To make a sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly; to make something, making such a sound./
뚝딱대다 뚝딱대다 [ttugttagdaeda] /pound — For one's heart to throb continuously from being startled or in fear./hammer — To make a sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly; to make something, making such a sound./
뚝딱뚝딱 뚝딱뚝딱 [ttugttagttugttag] /pounding — In a state in which one's heart beats rapidly and heavily./with a hammering sound — A word imitating the sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly./easily; fast — A word describing one handling a job easily and continuously without a pause./
뚝딱뚝딱하다 뚝딱뚝딱하다 [ttugttagttugttaghada] /pound — For one's heart to throb continuously from being startled or in fear./hammer — To make a sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly; to make something, making such a sound./handle well — To handle tasks continuously and easily without hesitation./
뚝딱이다 뚝딱이다 [ttugttagida] /pound — For one's heart to throb continuously from being startled or in fear./hammer — To make a sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly; to make something, making such a sound./
뚝딱하다 뚝딱하다 [ttugttaghada] /hammer — To make a sound of hitting a hard object repeatedly; to make something, making such a sound./
뚝뚝 뚝뚝 [ttugttug] /in drops; drip — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of big objects or waterdrops, etc., falling repeatedly./with snaps; with cracks — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of big, hard objects being broken and cut repeatedly./knocking; rapping — A word imitating the sound or describing the act of hitting a hard object repeatedly./in the manner of snapping something off — In the manner of picking or nipping something off something else it is clinging or attached to, without hesitation and repeatedly./drastically; remarkably — In the manner that a grade, ranking, etc., falls or a degree gets weak very conspicuously./very far away — Being located distantly./
뚝뚝하다 뚝뚝하다 [ttugttughada] /hard; stiff — The base of something being strong and solid./tough; blunt — A person's speech, behavior, facial expression, etc., being not soft or gentle, and thus not seeming kind./
뚝배기 뚝배기 [ttugbaegi] /ttukbaegi; earthenware pot — A black or brown earthenware vessel in which jjigae, stew, is cooked or gukbap, rice soup, is served./
뚝배기보다 장맛이 좋다 뚝배기보다 장맛이 좋다 [ttugbaegiboda jangmasi johda] /The taste of soy sauce is better than ttukbaegi, a black or brown earthenware vessel; Don't judge a book by its cover — Even though the exterior of something is humble, the content inside it is much better and excellent./
뚝심 뚝심 [ttugsim] /perseverance; endurance — A strong energy and patience to endure or bear a difficulty./
뚫다 뚫다 [ttulhda] /dig; pierce; bore — To make a hole./unclog; open through — To break through something that is blocked./make one's way through; pierce — To push one's way through an obstacle./go through — To overcome difficulties or an ordeal./pierce; penetrate; master — To realize the truth or secrets of learning by studying deeply./pierce; foresee — To guess what someone thinks, or predict the future./find a way — To discover a way or method to resolve a problem./
뚫리다 뚫리다 [ttulhrida] /have a hole; be pierced — For a hole to be made./be unclogged; become clear — For something blocked to be broken through./be resolved; be overcome — For an ordeal or difficulties to be surmounted./be found — For a way or method to resolve a problem to be discovered./
뚫어지다 뚫어지다 [ttulheojida] /be punched; be pierced — For a hole or crack to be created./be connected; be made — For a path to be made or connected./stare at; fix one's eyes on — To pay attention to and focus on something for a long time./
뚱기다 뚱기다 [ttunggida] /pluck the strings — To pull and release stretched strings, etc., to make sounds or to move./hint; imply — To give a hint so that the other person can notice./
뚱딴지 뚱딴지 [ttungttanji] /dunce; dope — A person with bizarre and foolish behavior or a way of thinking./
뚱땅거리다 뚱땅거리다 [ttungttanggeorida] /drum and twang — For the sound of beating several musical instruments or hard objects hard and continuously to be heard; to make such a sound./
뚱땅대다 뚱땅대다 [ttungttangdaeda] /drum and twang — For the sound of beating several musical instruments or hard objects hard and continuously to be heard; to make such a sound./
뚱땅뚱땅 뚱땅뚱땅 [ttungttangttungttang] /drumming and twanging — A word imitating the sound of beating several musical instruments or hard objects hard and continuously./
뚱땅뚱땅하다 뚱땅뚱땅하다 [ttungttangttungttanghada] /drum and twang — For the sound of beating several musical instruments or hard objects hard and continuously to be heard; to make such a sound./
뚱뚱보 뚱뚱보 [ttungttungbo] /fatso — (teasing) A person who is fat./
뚱뚱이 뚱뚱이 [ttungttungi] /fatso — (teasing) A person who is fat./
뚱뚱하다 뚱뚱하다 [ttungttunghada] /fat; corpulent — A person's body being wide as a result of putting on weight./swollen — A part of something protruding as it has swelled up./
뚱보 뚱보 [ttungbo] /fatso — (teasing) A person who is fat./
뚱하다 뚱하다 [ttunghada] /taciturn; reticent — Not talking much and being unkind and not gentle./sour; sullen — Unpleasant or morose due to dissatisfaction with something or someone./
뛰놀다 뛰놀다 [ttwinolda] /romp; frisk — To play while jumping here and there./beat — For a heart or pulse to beat strongly./
뛰는 놈 위에 나는 놈 있다 뛰는 놈 위에 나는 놈 있다 [ttwineun nom wie naneun nom issda] /There are those who run, and there are those who fly above them; There is no limit to excellence; There may be blue and better blue — One should guard against conceit because however excellent one may be, there is always someone else who is better./
뛰다 뛰다 [ttwida] /jump; hop; leap — To make a body jump high./beat; throb; pulsate — For a pulse, heartbeat, etc., to move in a flutter./soar; skyrocket — For a price to suddenly go up greatly./react strongly — To be very angry or surprised and show a strong reaction./spatter; sprinkle — For water drops, soil, pieces of something, etc., to be raised high via the force of an action, and be sprinkled all the place./jump up and down — To jump high and fall again to another place./press on; propel — To stand on a swing and press one's feet down hard on its footboard to make it swing back and forth in the air./stomp; play seesaw — To step on one end of a wooden panel, stomp, and jump up and down./run; race; dash — To move forward in quick steps./serve as; work as; play as — To work with a certain qualification./take off; make off; get away; run away; bolt — (slang) To run away./work hard; try hard — To be active in doing something./run — To run and pass somewhere./work from place to place — To work by busily going around several work places./
뛰어 보았자 부처님 손바닥 뛰어 보았자 부처님 손바닥 [ttwieo boassja bucheonim sonbadag] /be in the Buddha's palm however far one goes — To be unable to escape to a far away place irrespective of whatever one does or however hard one tries to run away./
뛰어가다 뛰어가다 [ttwieogada] /run; go running — To run and go to a certain place very fast./run past — To pass a place by running./
뛰어나가다 뛰어나가다 [ttwieonagada] /run out — To go running out quickly./run out of — To go running quickly out of somewhere./
뛰어나다 뛰어나다 [ttwieonada] /remarkable; outstanding — A person's ability, etc., being better or more excellent than others./
뛰어나오다 뛰어나오다 [ttwieonaoda] /run out — To come running out quickly./run out of — To come running quickly out of somewhere./
뛰어내리다 뛰어내리다 [ttwieonaerida] /jump down; leap down — To jump down from a high place./jump off; leap from — To throw oneself out of a certain place./jump down — To jump down from a certain place quickly./
뛰어넘다 뛰어넘다 [ttwieoneomda] /jump over; vault over — To jump high and pass over a certain object or place./skip — To skip a required process, order, or stage./overcome — To get over a difficult situation./excel — To excel a certain range or level by far./
뛰어놀다 뛰어놀다 [ttwieonolda] /run and play — To play while jumping here and there./
뛰어다니다 뛰어다니다 [ttwieodanida] /jump about; run about — To run around here and there./run around — (figurative) To busily move about here and there./
뛰어들다 뛰어들다 [ttwieodeulda] /thrust oneself into — To run fast and enter a place suddenly./dive into — To jump from a high place into water./enter with a risk — To go in a dangerous place, taking a risk./butt into — To actively participate in a certain work, activity, incident, etc./
뛰어야 벼룩 뛰어야 벼룩 [ttwieoya byeorug] /be a flea however far one goes — To be unable to escape to a far away place irrespective of whatever one does or however hard one tries to run away./
뛰어오다 뛰어오다 [ttwieooda] /come running — To run and come to a certain place very fast./run and pass — To pass a place by running./
뛰어오르다 뛰어오르다 [ttwieooreuda] /jump up; bounce — For one's body to jump high from a low place./skyrocket; soar — For a rank or price to surge./run and go up — To run up a certain place fast./
뛰쳐나가다 뛰쳐나가다 [ttwichyeonagada] /rush out; leap out — To go bursting out quickly./rush out of; leap out of — To get out of or leave somewhere suddenly./
뛰쳐나오다 뛰쳐나오다 [ttwichyeonaoda] /rush out; leap out — To come bursting out quickly./rush out of; leap out of — To come out of or leave somewhere suddenly./
뜀뛰기 뜀뛰기 [ttwimttwigi] /jumping; leaping — An action in which one puts one's feet together and then makes the body rise upwards to go forward or higher, or such a sports game./
뜀뛰다 뜀뛰다 [ttwimttwida] /jump; leap — To move forward or go up by surging upward on one's feet together./
뜀박질 뜀박질 [ttwimbagjil] /run; jump — The act of moving forward or going up by surging upward on one's feet together./running fast — The act of moving fast on foot./
뜀박질하다 뜀박질하다 [ttwimbagjilhada] /jump; leap — To move forward or go up by surging upward on one's feet together./run fast — To move fast on foot./
뜀질 뜀질 [ttwimjil] /run — The act of moving forward or going up by surging upward on one's feet together./running — The act of moving fast on foot./
뜀질하다 뜀질하다 [ttwimjilhada] /jump; leap — To move forward or go up by surging upward on one's feet together./run fast — To move fast on foot./
뜀틀 뜀틀 [ttwimteul] /vaulting horse — Sports equipment one jumps over after running toward it and placing one's hands on it, or the kind of gymnastics using this equipment./
뜨개질 뜨개질 [tteugaejil] /knitting — The act of using hands to knit clothes or gloves, etc., with string or yarn./
뜨개질하다 뜨개질하다 [tteugaejilhada] /knit — To use hands to knit clothes or gloves, etc., with string or yarn./
뜨거운 맛을 보다 뜨거운 맛을 보다 [tteugeoun maseul boda] /have a hot taste; taste the heat — To be harshly scolded or go through difficulties./
뜨거워지다 뜨거워지다 [tteugeowojida] /become hot; grow warm — For the temperature of something to rise as if it were near fire./become hot — For a human body to become hotter than a normal temperature./blush — For one's face to blush because one is embarrassed or shy./become passionate — (figurative) For an emotion, passion, etc., to become fierce./
뜨겁다 뜨겁다 [tteugeobda] /hot — (temperature) High./hot — (body temperature)  high/hot — Feeling blushed due to shame or embarrassment./strong; warm; passionate — (figurative) Intense and strong in feeling, passion, etc./
뜨고도 못 보는 당달봉사 뜨고도 못 보는 당달봉사 [tteugodo mos boneun dangdalbongsa] /a bat-blind person whose eyes are open, but unable to see — A naïve person who does not know or notice something even if he/she sees it with his/her own eyes./
뜨끈뜨끈하다 뜨끈뜨끈하다 [tteukkeuntteukkeunhada] /piping hot; steaming hot — Very warm and hot./
뜨끈하다 뜨끈하다 [tteukkeunhada] /fairly hot — Quite warm and hot./
뜨끔거리다 뜨끔거리다 [tteukkeumgeorida] /tingle; sting — To feel a pain as if one has burnt oneself, has been pricked or beaten./feel a prick of conscience — To feel uncomfortable because something bothers one./
뜨끔대다 뜨끔대다 [tteukkeumdaeda] /tingle; sting — To feel a pain as if one has burnt oneself, has been pricked or beaten./feel a prick of conscience — To feel uncomfortable because something bothers one./
뜨끔뜨끔 뜨끔뜨끔 [tteukkeumtteukkeum] /pricking; tingling — In the state of feeling as if one has burnt oneself, or has been pricked or beaten./in the state of feeling a prick of conscience — In the state of feeling uncomfortable because something bothers one./
뜨끔뜨끔하다 뜨끔뜨끔하다 [tteukkeumtteukkeumhada] /tingle; sting — To feel a pain as if one has burnt oneself, has been pricked or beaten./feel a prick of conscience — To feel uncomfortable because something bothers one./pricking; tingling — Continuously feeling as if one has burnt oneself, has been pricked or beaten./feeling a prick of conscience — Continuously feeling uncomfortable because something bothers one./
뜨끔하다 뜨끔하다 [tteukkeumhada] /pricking; tingling — Feeling as if one has burnt oneself, has been pricked or beaten./feeling a prick of conscience — Feeling uncomfortable because something bothers one./
뜨내기 뜨내기 [tteunaegi] /wanderer; roamer — A person who wanders about without a place to settle down./being casual — A work done on and off, once in a while./
뜨다 뜨다 [tteuda] /float; buoy — To stay on water or in the air, or to jump upward./get loose; come off — For a crack to form as something does not stick well./be excited; be upbeat — (figurative) To become a state that is unsteady and disarranged, not composed./be cheated — To be unable to receive what was lent./appear; be present — (slang) For someone fearful or dreadful to appear at a certain place./become popular — (slang) To become famous as one gains popularity./wither; be rotten — For stacked straw, grass, etc., to be rotten or to turn yellow./ferment — For malted rice, or dried, brick-shaped lump of fermented soybeans, etc., to undergo fermentation./grow sallow — For one's face to become swollen and yellowish due to sickness./depart; leave — To leave one place for another./die — To die, leaving the world behind./cut off; cut out — To tear or fall apart from one big mass./scoop up — To scoop up something out of water./scoop put; spoon out — To scoop or take out water or powder in a container./spoon up — To take food with a spoon and eat some./slice — To cut meat, etc., in many thin pieces./shape; spread thin — To spread paper, laver, etc., on a frame to make it into a sheet of paper, laver, etc./cut out — To cut out or cut off a piece of cloth from a bigger piece of cloth to make clothes./open — To open one's closed eyes./look at — To make one's eyes look like a specific shape./knit; weave — To knit or weave clothes, nets, etc., using thread, strings, cords, etc./sew — To sew a cloth etc., using a needle./tattoo — To paint something or write in letters on one's skin using an ink-dipped thread./copy; imitate — To make or print something by copying something that already exists./record; copy — To record something or copy a recorded material./guess; sound; fathom — To say or do something to find out what the other person has in mind./cauterize with moxa — To rub moxa, place it on a patient's skin, and kindle it to cure a disease./slow — A person's movement being slow and taking a long time./insensitive — A  person not noticing or caring about other people's feelings./quiet; taciturn — Not talking much./blunt; dull — The blade of a knife being not sharp./slow to heat up — An object such as an iron, etc., being not heated up well./distant — The distance between two places being quite long./infrequent — Not happening often./
뜨듯이 뜨듯이 [tteudeusi] /warmly — In an appropriately high temperature, not high to the extent in which it is hot./
뜨듯하다 뜨듯하다 [tteudeushada] /warm — A temperature being not hot but appropriately high./
뜨뜻미지근하다 뜨뜻미지근하다 [tteutteusmijigeunhada] /tepid; lukewarm — The temperature of something feeling slightly warm, not hot enough./lukewarm; tepid — A person's personality or way of working being indecisive and not clear./
뜨뜻이 뜨뜻이 [tteutteusi] /warmly — In an appropriately high temperature, not high to the extent in which it is hot./
뜨뜻하다 뜨뜻하다 [tteutteushada] /warm — A temperature being not hot but appropriately high./
뜨물 뜨물 [tteumul] /washing water of rice — Opaque white water after washing grains./
뜨악하다 뜨악하다 [tteuaghada] /unpleasant; reluctant — Feeling unsatisfied, uneasy, or uncomfortable./
뜨이다 뜨이다 [tteuida] /be opened — For a closed eye to open./be seen — To be seen in the eyes./be noticeable — For a certain state to be more noticeable than usual./become interested — To become very curious at hearing unexpected news./
뜬구름 뜬구름 [tteungureum] /floating cloud — A cloud that floats around in the sky./fleeting thing; ephemeral thing — (figurative) A fleeting wordly affair, or a life without a certain direction or goal./
뜬구름(을) 잡다 뜬구름(을) 잡다 [tteungureum(eul) jabda] /catch a flying cloud — To pursue something vague and vain./
뜬금없다 뜬금없다 [tteungeumeobsda] /abrupt — Someone's act or remark being sudden and absurd./
뜬금없이 뜬금없이 [tteungeumeobsi] /out of the blue; out of nowhere — In such a manner that someone's act or remark is sudden and absurd./
뜬눈 뜬눈 [tteunnun] /wide-awake eyes — The eyes of a person who cannot sleep at night and is fully awake./
뜬소문 뜬소문 [tteunsomun] /false rumor — A rumor that is going around without solid proof./
뜯기다 뜯기다 [tteudgida] /have money taken; be stripped of — To have one's money or goods taken away by someone despite one's resistance./be removed; fall off — For something stuck to be torn off or fall off./be pulled; be plucked — For hair, grass, etc., to be removed or pulled./be separated; be torn apart — For a part or an element to be torn off or fall off one mass./be bitten — To be bitten by an insect, etc./be bitten — To have someone or an animal bite off and eat grass or other tough food./be plucked; be removed — To make someone remove or pull hair, grass, etc./
뜯다 뜯다 [tteudda] /remove — To tear something stuck off or make it fall off./pluck; pull; pick — To remove or pull hair, grass, etc./bite — To bite off and eat grass or other tough food./separate; take apart — To make a part or an element be torn or fall off one mass./suck blood — For an insect, etc., to suck blood./pluck the strings — To pluck the strings of a string instrument to make sounds or play the instrument./take someone's money — To take someone's money or goods away despite his/her resistance./
뜯어고치다 뜯어고치다 [tteudeogochida] /mend; rebuild — To correct or mend something wrong or bad./
뜯어내다 뜯어내다 [tteudeonaeda] /take off; tear off; pick — To tear apart or make something torn that was previously attached./tear apart; cut apart — To take a part or an element off one mass./extort; pluck — To badger or threaten someone for money or goods and receive it./
뜯어말리다 뜯어말리다 [tteudeomalrida] /stop; pull apart — To take fighting people apart and try to end the fight./
뜯어먹다 뜯어먹다 [tteudeomeogda] /sponge off — To badger someone for money or goods and take it away despite someone's resistance./
뜯어보다 뜯어보다 [tteudeoboda] /open and look at — To open what has been sealed or wrapped and search inside./scrutinize — To take a careful look at one after another./
뜰 뜰 [tteul] /yard — Flat, empty land that adjoins a house./
뜸 뜸 [tteum] /(no equivalent expression) — A process of steaming or boiling food in which the heat is turned off and the vessel is left closed for long minutes so the food is cooked evenly./moxa cautery; moxibustion — In oriental medicine, a method of treatment in which a small portion of kindled moxa is placed on the patient's skin for the heat to spread inside the body./
뜸(을) 들이다 뜸(을) 들이다 [tteum(eul) deulida] /let something settle in its own steam — To pause for a while when working or talking to make others anxious or curious./
뜸하다 뜸하다 [tteumhada] /infrequent; scarce — Something being rare or uncommon these days although it was not in the past./
뜻 뜻 [tteus] /intention; opinion; wish; cause — A thought or opinion in one's mind./meaning — Meaning that is contained in words, a writing or action./significance; meaning; commitment — The value or importance of an affair or action./
뜻글자 뜻글자 [tteusgeulja] /ideogram — A letter that represents a certain meaning by itself./
뜻깊다 뜻깊다 [tteusgipda] /meaningful; significant — The value or importance of something being large./
뜻대로 뜻대로 [tteusdaero] /one's own way — As one has decided or as one wishes./
뜻밖 뜻밖 [tteusbakk] /being unexpected — A thing that one did not expect or think of./
뜻밖에 뜻밖에 [tteusbakke] /unexpectedly — In the manner of being against one's expectation or thought./
뜻을 두다 뜻을 두다 [tteuseul duda] /lay one's will — To have the intention to do or become something./
뜻을 받다 뜻을 받다 [tteuseul badda] /receive the will of others — To take over and follow another's thought./
뜻을 세우다 뜻을 세우다 [tteuseul seuda] /establish one's will — To establish a goal to achieve./
뜻이 맞다 뜻이 맞다 [tteusi majda] /The wills of both people match each other — To be of one mind or share the same thought./
뜻이 있는 곳에 길이 있다 뜻이 있는 곳에 길이 있다 [tteusi issneun gose gili issda] /Where there is a will, there is a way — If there is a will to do something, a way will be found to do it./
뜻있다 뜻있다 [tteusissda] /having an ambition; having an interest — Wanting to do something./secret — Having an unrevealed story./meaningful — Worthy or worthwhile./
뜻풀이 뜻풀이 [tteuspuli] /definition — The act of explaining the meaning of a difficult word or writing in a way that it is easy to understand./
뜻풀이되다 뜻풀이되다 [tteuspulidoeda] /be defined — For the meaning of a difficult word or writing to be explained in a way that it is easy to understand./
뜻풀이하다 뜻풀이하다 [tteuspulihada] /define — To explain the meaning of a difficult word or writing in a way that it is easy to understand./
뜻하다 뜻하다 [tteushada] /mean; intend — To have an intention to do something./forecast; expect — To think ahead or expect that something may happen./mean; indicate — To have or indicate a certain meaning./
띄다 띄다 [ttuida] /be seen — To be seen in the eyes./be noticeable — For a certain state to be better noticed than usual./become interested — To become curious strongly to hear an unexpected news./space; distance — To increase a spatial distance./
띄어쓰기 띄어쓰기 [ttuieosseugi] /word spacing — The act of separating words by the insertion of spaces when writing, or the rules on such spacing./
