물리다 물리다 [mulrida] /be sick and tired of; have had enough — To become so much sick and tired of someone or something that one hates to face him/her/it again./be bitten — To be pressed so hard by the teeth of an animal that it would create a wound./be stung — For flesh to be stung by an insect's proboscis such as a mosquito's, etc./be taken — (slang) For something or someone of interest to be owned by someone else./return — To make someone return what one has bought to its original owner and receive one's money back./recover — To return something done already to its former state./delay; put off; postpone — To delay a pre-decided date./turn; shift — To make someone or something move to another position or move him/her/it./hand over; leave; bequeath — To hand over a property, title, etc., to someone./be bitten — To make teeth or lips hold and press something so that it does not fall or slip out./gag — To put something into someone's mouth./make repay — To make someone pay what he/she is supposed to repay./make recover; make compensate — To make someone pay for the damage he/she caused by giving money or by recovering it./
