바락바락 바락바락 [baragbarag] /frantically; fiercely — A word describing one suddenly and repeatedly losing one's temper or yelling loudly./
바람 바람 [baram] /wind — The movement of air that is caused by changes in atmospheric pressure or by a human or machine./air — The air that is pumped into a hollow space such as the interior of a ball or tube./affair; extramarital affair — The act of being secretly in love with someone of the opposite sex./wind; craze; fashion — A short fad, atmosphere or ideological trend in society./palsy — (slang) A disease that causes diziness, fainting, covulsion, etc., followed by paralysis./overstatement; exaggeration — The act of exaggerating something./hot seat — An unstable position that is susceptible to criticism or influence./instigation — The act of inciting someone else to do something that he/she had no intention of doing./false hope — (figurative) A mind that is carried away or a thought that has occurred./flash — The quality of being very quick./wish; desire — Longing for something to happen as one thinks./baram — A bound noun used to indicate that what was just mentioned is the cause or reason for the following proposition./baram — A bound noun used to indicate the way a person is dressed./
바람 부는 대로 살다 바람 부는 대로 살다 [baram buneun daero salda] /live as wind blows — To live at the mercy of the surrounding circumstances./
