바람(을) 잡다 바람(을) 잡다 [baram(eul) jabda] /catch wind — To incite someone to do something absurd./
바람개비 바람개비 [baramgaebi] /pinwheel — A toy with sails of paper cut into multiple strips, bent into waves, and then pinned to a stick so that they revolve in the wind./
바람결 바람결 [baramgyeol] /movement of breeze — A movement of wind blowing mildly in a specific direction./being indirectly; being second-handedly — A state in which one hears about something indirectly./
바람기 바람기 [baramgi] /force of wind; the feeling of wind — The force or feeling of wind blowing./flirtness; wantonness; womanizing — A state of being careless about romantic relationships./
바람나다 바람나다 [baramnada] /have an affair — To have an inappropriate relationship with another person even though one is married or in a relationship./
바람둥이 바람둥이 [baramdungi] /playboy — A person whose love life is complicated such as being in a relationship with more than one member of the opposite sex, etc./
바람막이 바람막이 [barammagi] /windbreak — The act of blocking the wind, or an object used for such a purpose./
바람맞다 바람맞다 [barammajda] /be stood up — To end up wasting one's time, as a date or someone one planned to meet does not show up./have a stroke — To have a stroke./
바람맞히다 바람맞히다 [barammajhida] /stand a person up — To end up wasting another person's time by not showing up for a date, appointment, etc./
