반사 작용 반사 작용 [bansa jagyong] /reflex — A phenomenon in which light, radio wave, etc., changes direction when it hits an object in its path./reflex action — A body's unconscious response toward a certain stimulus./reaction — One's state of being deeply absorbed in something or trying to completely avoid something, as one is influenced by a certain incident./
