반포되다 반포되다 [banpodoeda] /be proclaimed; be promulgated — To be announced and made known broadly./
반포지효 반포지효 [banpojihyo] /being extremely devoted to one's parents — Filial love as evidenced by a grown-up child taking very good care of his/her parent./
반포하다 반포하다 [banpohada] /proclaim; promulgate — To announce and make known broadly./
반품 반품 [banpum] /return — The act of returning an already purchased product, or the product returned./
반품하다 반품하다 [banpumhada] /return — To return an already purchased product./
반하다 반하다 [banhada] /be attracted; be enchanted — To be attracted by someone or something as if one were enchanted./be opposed to — To be opposite or contrast to something./go against; break; violate — To not do as someone's opinion, law, etc., states, and to break it./
반항 반항 [banhang] /defiance; disobedience; rebellion — The act of confronting, attacking or colliding with another person or object./
반항심 반항심 [banhangsim] /rebelliousness; hostility — An urge to confront, attack or collide with another person or object./
반항아 반항아 [banhanga] /rebel; rebellious child — A child who confronts, attacks or collides with another person or object, or a grown up acting in such a way./
반항적 반항적 [banhangjeog] /being rebellious; being defiant — A state of showing the attitude of confronting, attacking or colliding with another person or object./rebellious; defiant — Showing the attitude of confronting, attacking or colliding with another person or object./
반항하다 반항하다 [banhanghada] /defy; disobey; rebel — To confront, attack or collide with another person or object./
반핵 반핵 [banhaeg] /being anti-nuclear — The act of opposing matters related to nuclear energy./
반향 반향 [banhyang] /reverberation; resonance — A reaction to a certain event or a phenomenon's influence on the world./echo; reverberation — A phenomenon in which the sound of an object hitting an obstacle is reflected and heard again./
반환 반환 [banhwan] /return; restoration — The act of returning something that was taken or borrowed./return — The act of going back the way one came from./
반환되다 반환되다 [banhwandoeda] /be returned; be restored — For something taken or borrowed to be returned./
반환점 반환점 [banhwanjeom] /halfway point; turning point — The location where athletes change directions at a marathon, walking race, etc., or a sign that indicates the location./
반환하다 반환하다 [banhwanhada] /return; restore — To return something that was taken or borrowed./return — To go back the way one came from./
받다 받다 [badda] /receive; get — To take something that someone else has given or sent./collect; receive; get — To collect money or an item that someone else gives./receive; get; be affected by; be influenced by — To be affected or influenced by someone else's behavior or psychological action./receive; get; obtain — To get a score or degree./buy; get; purchase; source — To buy in large quantity to resell to a number of people./catch — To catch with a hand something that falls from the sky or comes toward oneself./receive; get — To be affected by a situation./receive; get; be exposed to — To receive or be exposed to light, wind, etc./receive; get — To receive or respond to an action such as a request, application, inquiry, attack, signal, etc./receive; get — To have a decision or ruling imposed on oneself./be generous; pamper — To be generous to a person when he/she acts like a baby or behaves strangely after drinking alcohol./receive; get — To receive or let in a person./be shot; be gunned; be hit — To be shot by a gun or hit by a sword, etc./add; take over — To sing or speak right after someone else speaks as kind of response./deliver — To help a woman deliver a baby./collect — To collect the seed of a plant or the egg of an animal./buy; get — To purchase an alcoholic beverage, etc./collect; fill — To let something that flows or falls into a container, etc./go well with; look good — For a color or shape to go well with something./be agreeable — For food, etc. to be agreeable./stay; go well with — For makeup to stay./look better — To look better in a photo than in real life./butt; gore — To hit someone or something hard with a head, horn, etc./resist; confront — (slang) To confront and argue with someone who acts inappropriately./
받들다 받들다 [baddeulda] /respect; serve — To take care of someone with respect; to cherish someone./obey; follow — To cherish a teaching, order, etc., and follow it./raise; lift — To lift an object with a hand or hands holding its bottom./
받아 놓은 당상 받아 놓은 당상 [bada noheun dangsang] /a high government post that was received — A situation where something looks beyond doubt and very certain./
받아 놓은 밥상 받아 놓은 밥상 [bada noheun babsang] /a table that was received — A situation where something looks beyond doubt and very certain./
받아넘기다 받아넘기다 [badaneomgida] /return — To hit the ball coming across and send it back to the opposing team./retail — To buy goods at wholesaler's prices and sell them to another person./parry; sing readily — To take over someone's remark or song, and to continue it without hesitating./parry — To evade an attack skillfully./
받아들이다 받아들이다 [badadeulida] /receive; take; accept — To collect and receive money, goods, etc., from people./accept; adopt — To not block an incoming culture or goods, and to make it one's own./accept; take — To grant someone's demand, request, etc./accept; admit — To let someone join a certain organization, group, etc., as a new member./accept; admit; take; face — To admit, understand, or accept a certain fact, state, etc./follow — To agree to an opinion, criticism, etc., and follow it./
받아먹다 받아먹다 [badameogda] /be fed — For a person or animal to eat what another person or animal feeds./take bribe — (slang) To receive and keep money, goods, etc./take; accept; receive — (slang) To receive money for something or doing something./
받아쓰기 받아쓰기 [badasseugi] /dictation — The act of listening to what another person says or reads aloud and writing it down, observing grammatical rules./
받아쓰다 받아쓰다 [badasseuda] /dictate — To write down what someone says or reads./
받아치다 받아치다 [badachida] /receive and give back — To answer upon hearing someone's criticism, joke, etc./
받은 밥상을 찬다 받은 밥상을 찬다 [badeun babsangeul chanda] /kick a table that was received — To kick away the fortune that has fallen in one's lap./
받잡다 받잡다 [badjabda] /receive; take; accept — (honorific) To take what someone gave or sent./
받치다 받치다 [badchida] /support — To put an object or body part under another object or body part./wear together — To wear certain clothes that are matching in color or shape together./(no equivalent expression) — To write a consonant under a vowel in the Korean alphabet./support — To support in order to do something well./hold — To hold up an umbrella, parasol, etc., to block the rain or sunlight./
받침 받침 [badchim] /support; prop — An object that supports the bottom of another object./final consonant — A consonant written under the vowel of a syllable when writing in the Korean alphabet./
받침대 받침대 [badchimdae] /prop; support — An object used to support an object or a part of one's body./
받침돌 받침돌 [badchimdol] /socle; bondstone; footstone — A stone placed under another object./
받침소리 받침소리 [badchimsori] /supporting sound — The sound of consonants that are used as supports in syllables./
받히다 받히다 [badhida] /be butted; be gored — For a part of a person or object to hit another object hard./
발 발 [bal] /foot — The bottom most part of a human's or animal's leg./leg — A short part that sticks out to support the bottom of a piece of furniture, etc., for balance./footwork; step — (figurative) Walk/step — The unit of counting steps./bal — blind: An object made by weaving reeds, narrow bamboo strips, etc., or hanging multiple strands of strings, etc., which is used to keep something from being seen./strand — Narrow and long strands such as strings, noodles, etc./shot — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the number of bullets, shells, arrows, etc./
발 벗고 나서다 발 벗고 나서다 [bal beosgo naseoda] /go out barefoot — To throw oneself into something actively./
발 없는 말이 천 리 간다 발 없는 말이 천 리 간다 [bal eobsneun mali cheon ri ganda] /Words without feet go one hundred kilometers — Once uttered, words tend to spread far and wide in an instant./
발(을) 구르다 발(을) 구르다 [bal(eul) gureuda] /stamp one's feet — To be very anxious and impatient./
발(을) 끊다 발(을) 끊다 [bal(eul) kkeunhda] /cut off one's foot — To stop going somewhere or to cut off a relationship with someone./
발(을) 들여놓을 자리 하나 없다 발(을) 들여놓을 자리 하나 없다 [bal(eul) deulyeonoheul jari hana eobsda] /There is no space to set foot upon — To be very crowded by people with little or no space to enter or sit./There is no space to set foot upon — To be messy with a lot of stuff scattered around./
발(을) 디디다 발(을) 디디다 [bal(eul) didida] /step with one's foot — To join a certain group or organization, or participate in a certain task./
발(을) 디딜 틈이 없다 발(을) 디딜 틈이 없다 [bal(eul) didil teumi eobsda] /There is no gap to set one's foot in — To be very busy and crowded./
발(을) 벗다 발(을) 벗다 [bal(eul) beosda] /take off one's feet — To take off one's shoes or socks, or wear nothing on one's feet./
발(을) 붙일 곳이 없다 발(을) 붙일 곳이 없다 [bal(eul) butil gosi eobsda] /have no place to attach one's foot — Have no place to settle down./
발(을) 빼다[씻다] 발(을) 빼다[씻다] [bal(eul) ppaeda[ssisda]] /pull out[wash] one's feet — To sever one's relationship with something and no longer get involved in it./
발(을) 뻗고[펴고] 자다 발(을) 뻗고[펴고] 자다 [bal(eul) ppeodgo[pyeogo] jada] /sleep with one's feet stretched out[straightened out] — To sleep in a carefree mood without any concerns./
발(을) 뻗다[펴다] 발(을) 뻗다[펴다] [bal(eul) ppeodda[pyeoda]] /stretch[straightened out] one's feet — To be relieved as one no longer has to be concerned about something or try hard./
발(을) 뻗을 자리를 보고 누우랬다 발(을) 뻗을 자리를 보고 누우랬다 [bal(eul) ppeodeul jarireul bogo nuuraessda] /It is said that you may want to lie down after checking the place where you will stretch your feet — It is advisable to think about the consequences of something before starting to work on it./It is said that you may want to lie down after checking the place where you will stretch your feet — It is advisable to behave depending on time and place./
발(이) 길다 발(이) 길다 [bal(i) gilda] /have a long foot; be in time for a treat — To be blessed with things to eat as a result of a chance visit to a place that offers food./
발(이) 넓다[너르다] 발(이) 넓다[너르다] [bal(i) neolbda[neoreuda]] /have a wide[spacious] foot — To be close to or acquainted with many people./
발(이) 뜨다 발(이) 뜨다 [bal(i) tteuda] /One's feet float — To visit a certain place once in a while./
발(이) 맞다 발(이) 맞다 [bal(i) majda] /Feet coordinate with each other — For the same foot of many people to reach the ground at the same time when they walk together./Feet coordinate with each other — For words or behavior of many people to be in good harmony when working together./
발(이) 묶이다 발(이) 묶이다 [bal(i) mukkida] /have one's feet tied up — To be in a situation where one cannot move one's body or do other things./
발(이) 빠르다 발(이) 빠르다 [bal(i) ppareuda] /have a fast foot — To quickly come up with a countermeasure against something./
발(이) 짧다 발(이) 짧다 [bal(i) jjalbda] /have a short foot — To have no chance to eat something for free as one has shown up after others have eaten all the food offered./
발가락 발가락 [balgarag] /toe — The front end part of one's foot that is divided into five sections./
발가벗기다 발가벗기다 [balgabeosgida] /strip; denude — To make someone take off his/her all clothes to be naked./
발가벗다 발가벗다 [balgabeosda] /be stripped; be denuded — To take off one's all clothes to be naked./
발가숭이 발가숭이 [balgasungi] /naked body — An unclothed body./naked mountain; treeless mountain — (figurative) A mountain that has its soil revealed due to scarcity of grass or trees./bare branches — (figurative) A tree that has bare branches because all of its leaves have fallen./being broke; being penniless — (figurative) A person who has nothing because he/she spent or lost all of his money or wealth./
발각 발각 [balgag] /detection; disclosure; discovery — A hidden thing being exposed and becoming known./
발각되다 발각되다 [balgagdoeda] /be disclosed; be revealed — For a concealed incident to become uncovered and known./
발간 발간 [balgan] /publication — The act of making a book, newspaper, magazine, etc./
발간되다 발간되다 [balgandoeda] /be published — For a book, magazine, etc., to be made./
발간하다 발간하다 [balganhada] /publish — To make a book, newspaper, magazine, etc./
발갛다 발갛다 [balgahda] /reddish; bright-red — Red in a bright and pale way./
발개지다 발개지다 [balgaejida] /turn light red — To become light red./
발걸음 발걸음 [balgeoleum] /gait — The act of moving one's foot from one spot to another./visit — The act of coming and going./
발걸음을 끊다[안 하다] 발걸음을 끊다[안 하다] [balgeoleumeul kkeunhda[an hada]] /cut off[not do] one's visit — To no longer come or go./
발걸음을 재촉하다 발걸음을 재촉하다 [balgeoleumeul jaechoghada] /hurry one's gait — To go quickly and hurriedly./
발걸음이 떨어지지 않다 발걸음이 떨어지지 않다 [balgeoleumi tteoleojiji anhda] /One's gait cannot be lifted — To hesitate to leave as one feels uneasy./
발걸이 발걸이 [balgeoli] /footrest; footrail; rung — A thing placed under a desk or chair to rest one's foot on./stirrup — One part of a saddle where one puts one's feet  when riding a horse./
발견 발견 [balgyeon] /discovery; detection — The act of finding out for the first time a thing that has not been discovered yet or was unknown to the world./
발견되다 발견되다 [balgyeondoeda] /be discovered; be found — For a thing that has not been discovered yet or was unknown to the world to be found out for the first time./
발견하다 발견하다 [balgyeonhada] /discover; find — To find out for the first time a thing that has not been discovered yet or was unknown to the world./
발광 발광 [balgwang] /luminescence; radiation — A state of emitting light./
발광체 발광체 [balgwangche] /luminous body; luminary — An object that emits light by itself./
발광하다 발광하다 [balgwanghada] /luminesce; radiate — To emit light./
발군 발군 [balgun] /being outstanding; being exceptional — A state of being outstanding among others./
발굴 발굴 [balgul] /excavation; dig — The act of digging something that is buried underground, or a pile of earth or stones./hunt; discovery — The act of discovering something that is outstanding or not widely known./
발굴되다 발굴되다 [balguldoeda] /be excavated; be dug — For something that is buried underground, or a pile of earth or stones to be dug out./be hunted; be discovered — For something that is outstanding or not widely known to be discovered./
발굴지 발굴지 [balgulji] /digs; findspot — A place where ancient tombs, relics, remains, etc., were found and dug up./
발굴하다 발굴하다 [balgulhada] /excavate; dig — To dig something that is buried underground, or a pile of earth or stones./hunt; discover — To discover something that is outstanding or not widely known./
발굽 발굽 [balgub] /hoof — A big, hard toenail at the end of herbivores' feet such as horses, cows, etc./
발그레 발그레 [balgeure] /ruddily — In the state of being lightly reddish./
발그레하다 발그레하다 [balgeurehada] /ruddy; flushed; rubicund — Lightly reddish./
발그스름하다 발그스름하다 [balgeuseureumhada] /reddish — Slightly red./
발급 발급 [balgeub] /issue — The act of making and giving a certificate, etc., at an institution./
발급되다 발급되다 [balgeubdoeda] /be issued — For a certificate, etc., to be made and given by an organization./
발급하다 발급하다 [balgeubhada] /issue — For an organization to make and give a certificate, etc./
발기 발기 [balgi] /erection — An act in which male genitalia swells or stands straight./initiation — An act of a group in taking the lead in planning and starting a new task with a certain purpose and will./
발기다 발기다 [balgida] /open up; crack open — To peel or remove the skin of something so that its content is exposed./tear to pieces — To tear paper, a cloth, etc., and make it into pieces./dig up; ferret out — To dig into a hidden secret, etc./
발기되다 발기되다 [balgidoeda] /erect — For the male genitalia to swell or become erect./be initiated — For a new task to be planned and started at a group's initiative for a certain purpose and mission./
발기발기 발기발기 [balgibalgi] /to tatters; to shreds — In the manner of violently tearing something into several pieces./
발기인 발기인 [balgiin] /initiator; proponent — A person who takes the lead in proposing to start a certain task and develops ways to put it into action./
발기하다 발기하다 [balgihada] /erect — For the male genitalia to swell or become erect./initiate — For a group to take the lead in planning and starting a new task for a certain purpose and mission./
발길 발길 [balgil] /step — A step that one takes forward./visit — The act of people coming and going./kick — A foot that is stretched forward forcefully./
발길에 채다[차이다] 발길에 채다[차이다] [balgile chaeda[chaida]] /be kicked by a step — To be treated with contempt and trampled./be kicked by a step — To be very common./
발길을 끌어당기다 발길을 끌어당기다 [balgileul kkeuleodanggida] /pull one's step — To make someone come toward oneself./
발길이 내키지 않다 발길이 내키지 않다 [balgili naekiji anhda] /One's steps are reluctant — To be reluctant to go somewhere./
발길이 떨어지지 않다 발길이 떨어지지 않다 [balgili tteoleojiji anhda] /One's step would not be taken off — To be unable to leave as one feels uneasy./
발길이 무겁다 발길이 무겁다 [balgili mugeobda] /One's step feels heavy — To feel reluctant or unwilling to do something./
발길질 발길질 [balgiljil] /kick — The act of kicking with one's foot./
발길질하다 발길질하다 [balgiljilhada] /kick — To kick something or someone with one's foot./
발꿈치 발꿈치 [balkkumchi] /heel — The back end of one's foot./tip of one's toe — (figurative) The lowest level of one's ability or attention./
발끈 발끈 [balkkeun] /in a fit of rage — In the manner of getting angry suddenly, failing to suppress one's anger./
발끈하다 발끈하다 [balkkeunhada] /be quick to anger; be short-tempered — To fail to hold one's anger and explode with rage./
발끝 발끝 [balkkeut] /the tip of the toes; tiptoe — The end of the toe./tip of toes — (figurative) The lowest level of one's ability or qualification./
발놀림 발놀림 [balnolrim] /footwork — The movement of one's feet when walking or doing sports./
발단 발단 [baldan] /beginning; root; source — The beginning or origin of something./
발단되다 발단되다 [baldandoeda] /begin; be originated; be rooted — For a certain event to come to happen or begin for the first time./
발단하다 발단하다 [baldanhada] /begin; originate — For a certain event to happen or begin for the first time./
발달 발달 [baldal] /development; growth — The process of becoming bigger, better in one's body, emotion, intelligence, etc./development — The process of reaching a higher level in a phenomenon such as academics, technology, civilization, society, etc./development — A gradual growth of the power, size, etc., of something./
발달되다 발달되다 [baldaldoeda] /be developed; be grown — For one's body, emotion, intelligence, etc., to be developed or matured./be developed — For a phenomenon such as academics, technology, civilization, society, etc., to reach a higher level./be developed — For the power, size, etc., of something to grow gradually./
발달사 발달사 [baldalsa] /history of development — The history of the development of a certain field./
발달시키다 발달시키다 [baldalsikida] /develop — To develop or mature one's body, emotion, intelligence, etc./develop — To make a phenomenon such as academics, technology, civilization, society, etc., reach a higher level./develop — To make the power, size, etc., of something grow gradually./
발달하다 발달하다 [baldalhada] /develop — For one's body, emotion, intelligence, etc., to be developed and matured./develop — To reach a higher level in a phenomenon such as academics, technology, civilization, society, etc./develop — For the power, size, etc., of something to grow gradually./
발대식 발대식 [baldaesig] /kick-off ceremony; launching ceremony — An official event designed to announce that a certain group has been organized, ready to start its activities./
발돋움 발돋움 [baldodum] /tiptoeing — The act of standing on one's tiptoes in order to raise one's height or walk silently./development — The process of developing a matter or situation to a better state./
발돋움하다 발돋움하다 [baldodumhada] /stand on one's tiptoes — To stand on one's tiptoes in order to raise one's height or walk silently./develop — To develop a matter or situation to a better state./
발동 발동 [baldong] /arousal; stimulation — The arousal of a matter, thought, etc./ignition — The act of initiating combustion in an engine, etc./exercise — The exercise of legal authority, etc., by a national institution./
발동기 발동기 [baldonggi] /motor; engine — A machine that produces electric power./
발동되다 발동되다 [baldongdoeda] /be aroused — For a matter, thought, etc., to be aroused./be exercised — For legal authority, etc., to be exercised by a national institution./
발동하다 발동하다 [baldonghada] /arouse — For a matter, thought, etc., to start occurring./exercise — For a national institution to exercise legal authority, etc./
발뒤꿈치 발뒤꿈치 [baldwikkumchi] /heel — The rounded part of the back of one's foot below the ankle./tip of one's toe — (figurative) The lowest level of one's ability or attention./
발등 발등 [baldeung] /the top of the foot — The top part of the foot./
발등(을) 찍히다 발등(을) 찍히다 [baldeung(eul) jjighida] /have the top of one's foot stabbed — To be betrayed by someone whom one trusted./
발등에 불(이) 떨어지다 발등에 불(이) 떨어지다 [baldeunge bul(i) tteoleojida] /A fire drops on top of one's foot — For something to suddenly strike./
발등을 찍다 발등을 찍다 [baldeungeul jjigda] /stab the top of one's foot — To ruin or do harm to something./
발딱 발딱 [balttag] /all of a sudden; quickly — In the manner of standing up suddenly from the position of lying down or sitting down./on one's back — In the manner of lying back or leaning back suddenly./
발라내다 발라내다 [balranaeda] /strip off; debone — To pick bones from fish or separate meat from bones./
발라당 발라당 [balradang] /on one's back — A word describing one falling down backward with his/her arms and legs stretched fully./cheekily — A word describing one being cheeky, not being pure or innocent./
발랄하다 발랄하다 [balralhada] /cheerful — One's facial expression, behavior, way of speaking, image, etc., being bright and lively./
발랑 발랑 [balrang] /on one's back — A word describing one falling down backward with his/her arms and legs stretched fully./cheekily — A word describing one being cheeky, not being pure or innocent./with inside out — A word describing something being turned inside out./
발레 발레 [balre] /ballet — A dance that originated in Europe, which has a certain plot and is performed on the stage to classical music./
발령 발령 [balryeong] /appointment — An act of issuing directives with regard to the appointment, dismissal, or transfer of a person to or from a certain position or title ; or such a directive./issuance — An act of issuing a warning against danger or emergency./
발령되다 발령되다 [balryeongdoeda] /be appointed; be assigned — For directives to be issued with regard to the appointment, dismissal, or transfer of a person to or from a certain position or title./be issued — For a warning against danger or emergency to be issued./
발령하다 발령하다 [balryeonghada] /appoint; assign — To issue directives with regard to the appointment, dismissal, or transfer of a person to or from a certain position or title./issue — To issue a warning against danger or emergency./
발로 발로 [balro] /manifestation; expression; display — A state in which something hidden reveals its presence, or an act of making it appear on the surface./
발리다 발리다 [balrida] /remain on; be spread; be stuck to — For something to be attached to or left behind on something./
발림 발림 [balrim] /sweet talk; flattery — The act of making someone feel good or flattering him/her with sweet words or lies./
발맞추다 발맞추다 [balmajchuda] /keep pace with — (figurative) To tune a thought, goal, etc., to a certain direction./
발매 발매 [balmae] /putting something on the market; releasing — An act of issuing and selling a certain product, or putting it up for sale./
발매기 발매기 [balmaegi] /vending machine — A machine that automatically sells tickets, goods, etc., when money is inserted./
발매되다 발매되다 [balmaedoeda] /be put on the market; be released — For a certain product to be issued and sold, or to be put up for sale./
발매하다 발매하다 [balmaehada] /put on the market; release — To issue and sell a certain product, or put it up for sale./
발명 발명 [balmyeong] /invention — An act of conceiving and creating a new technology or product for the first time./
발명가 발명가 [balmyeongga] /inventor — A person who professionally comes up with and makes new technologies or objects that did not exist before./
발명되다 발명되다 [balmyeongdoeda] /be invented — To conceive and create a new technology or product for the first time./
발명왕 발명왕 [balmyeongwang] /great inventor — A person who invented many things./
발명품 발명품 [balmyeongpum] /invention — A new thing that one creates by thinking of something that has been non-existent./
발명하다 발명하다 [balmyeonghada] /invent — To conceive and create a new technology or product for the first time./
발모 발모 [balmo] /hair growth — Hair growing on one's body such as on the head, etc./
발목 발목 [balmog] /ankle — The part that joins the leg and the foot./
발목(을) 잡히다 발목(을) 잡히다 [balmog(eul) jabhida] /be seized by one's ankle — To be tightly tied to a certain task and unable to escape from it./be seized by one's ankle — To have one's weakness seized on by others./
발목을 잡다 발목을 잡다 [balmogeul jabda] /seize one's ankle — To have someone tightly tied to a certain task and unable to escape from it./seize one's ankle — To seize upon someone's weakness./
발목이 묶이다 발목이 묶이다 [balmogi mukkida] /have one's ankles tied up — To be unable to escape from a certain place./
발문 발문 [balmun] /epilogue; postscript — A passage at the end of a book that contains a brief description of the story and compliments for its author./
발밑 발밑 [balmit] /being at one's feet; being underfoot — Surface beneath or below one's feet, or the surrounding area./
발바닥 발바닥 [balbadag] /sole — The flat underside of the foot that touches the ground when one is standing or walking./
발바닥에 불이 나다 발바닥에 불이 나다 [balbadage buli nada] /One's soles are on fire — To get around here and there hurriedly and quickly./
발바리 발바리 [balbari] /spaniel — A small-sized dog with short legs and long fur./loafer; roamer — (slang) A person who roams around without nothing to do./
발발 발발 [balbal] /shakingly; shiveringly — In the state of trembling continously with excitement, nervous tension, fear, cold, etc./grudgingly — In the manner of begrudging losing even trifling things./crawlingly — In the manner of crawling with small movements, lying on one's stomach./crawlingly — (figurative) In the manner of behaving servilely while humbling oneself in order to please another person./restlessly; actively — In the manner of going around busily./outbreak — Sudden occurrence of a major incident such as a war, etc./
발발되다 발발되다 [balbaldoeda] /break out — For a major incident such as a war, etc., to come to occur suddenly./
발발하다 발발하다 [balbalhada] /break out — For a major incident such as a war, etc., to occur suddenly./
발버둥 발버둥 [balbeodung] /struggling; writhing — The act of twisting and thrashing as one sits or lies on one's back, bending and stretching out one's two legs alternately./struggle; trying desperately — The act of trying very hard to do something with all one's might or using every means possible./
발버둥질 발버둥질 [balbeodungjil] /fluttering; squirming — The act of struggling by bending and straightening one's two legs in turns quickly while sitting or lying down./struggling — The act of struggling hard with all kinds of strength and methods./
발버둥질하다 발버둥질하다 [balbeodungjilhada] /flutter; squirm — To struggle by bending and straightening one's two legs in turns quickly while sitting or lying down./struggle — To struggle hard with all kinds of strength and methods./
발병 발병 [balbyeong] /footsoreness — A pain in the foot due to much walking or other reasons./occurrence of disease — A state in which one becomes ill or catches a disease./
발병되다 발병되다 [balbyeongdoeda] /occur; develop — To become ill or catch a disease./
발병률 발병률 [balbyeongryul] /incidence rate — A rate that shows the likelihood of catching a certain disease or the number of people with the disease./
발병하다 발병하다 [balbyeonghada] /occur; develop — To become ill or catch a disease./
발보다 발가락이 더 크다 발보다 발가락이 더 크다 [balboda balgaragi deo keuda] /The toe is bigger than the foot — For something secondary to be more or bigger than something primary./
발본색원 발본색원 [balbonsaegwon] /eradication; rooting out — An act of completely removing the underlying causes of something bad so as to keep it from occurring again./
발본색원하다 발본색원하다 [balbonsaegwonhada] /eradicate; root out — To completely remove the underlying causes of something bad so as to keep it from occurring again./
발부 발부 [balbu] /issuance — An act of issuing a variety of documents or certificates, as in public agencies./
발부되다 발부되다 [balbudoeda] /be issued — For a variety of documents or certificates to be issued by a public agency./
발부리 발부리 [balburi] /tip of the toe — The very front end of one's foot./
발부하다 발부하다 [balbuhada] /issue — For a public agency or the like to issue a variety of documents or certificate./
발붙이다 발붙이다 [balbutida] /depend on; rely on — To depend on something or find a place to live in a certain place, and finally settle down./step on — To step and stand on a certain spot./
발뺌 발뺌 [balppaem] /excuse; pretext; evasion — The act of making an excuse to deflect responsibility for a matter related to oneself, or something that you were told to do./
발뺌하다 발뺌하다 [balppaemhada] /make an excuse; make a pretext; evade — To make an excuse to deflect responsibility for a matter related to oneself./
발사 발사 [balsa] /firing; launch; setting off — An act of shooting an arrow, firing a gun or cannon, sending out a rocket, electric and sound waves, etc./
발사되다 발사되다 [balsadoeda] /be fired; be launched; be set off — For an arrow to be shot, a gun or cannon to be fired, or rocket to be launched or electric and sound waves to be sent out./
발사음 발사음 [balsaeum] /sound of fire — The sound of shooting an arrow, gun, bomb, rocket or the release of radio waves, sound waves, etc./
발사하다 발사하다 [balsahada] /fire; launch; set off — To shoot an arrow, fire a gun or cannon, launch a rocket, send out electric and sound waves, etc./
발산 발산 [balsan] /release — The act of revealing one's emotions, sadness, desire, etc., and getting rid of them or it./diffusion — The wide diffusion of heat, light, smell, etc./
발산되다 발산되다 [balsandoeda] /be released — For one's emotions, sadness, desire, etc., to be revealed, or to be revealed and be gotten rid of./be diffused — For heat, light, smell, etc., to be widely spread./
발산하다 발산하다 [balsanhada] /release — To reveal one's emotions, sadness, desire, etc., or to reveal and get rid of them or it./diffuse — To spread heat, light, smell, etc., widely./
발상 발상 [balsang] /beginning; dawn; origin — A historically meaningful event appearing for the first time or beginning./idea; thinking — The act of coming up with a thought, or an idea gained in such a way./
발상지 발상지 [balsangji] /cradle; birthplace — A place where a historically meaningful event appears for the first time or begins./
발상하다 발상하다 [balsanghada] /begin; dawn; originate — For a historically meaningful event to appear for the first time or begin./conceive an idea; think — To come up with a thought./
발생 발생 [balsaeng] /occurrence; outbreak — A happening of an event or generation of a matter./
발생되다 발생되다 [balsaengdoeda] /occur; be generated — For an event to come to happen or a matter to come into being./
발생량 발생량 [balsaengryang] /amount generated — Amount of something that comes into being or occurs./
발생률 발생률 [balsaengryul] /incidence rate; occurrence rate — The rate of something happening or being generated./
발생지 발생지 [balsaengji] /birthplace; cradle — The place where an event happened or a matter generated./
발생하다 발생하다 [balsaenghada] /occur; generate — For an event to come to happen or a matter to come into being./
발설 발설 [balseol] /divulging; revealing; disclosing — The act of telling another person a fact that should be hidden./
발설되다 발설되다 [balseoldoeda] /be divulged; be leaked — For a fact that should be hidden to be revealed to another person./
발설하다 발설하다 [balseolhada] /divulge; reveal; disclose — To reveal to another person a fact that should be hidden./
발성 발성 [balseong] /vocalization — An act of making a sound with a voice, or the sound uttered in such a way./
발성 기관 발성 기관 [balseong gigwan] /vocal organ — A body part used to make a sound such as a tongue, vocal cord, etc./
발성되다 발성되다 [balseongdoeda] /be vocalized — For a vocal sound to be made./
발성하다 발성하다 [balseonghada] /vocalize — To make a voce sound./
발소리 발소리 [balsori] /footstep — The sound of the feet touching the ground when walking./
발송 발송 [balsong] /sending; forwarding — The act of sending an object, letter, document, etc., by mail, delivery service, etc./
발송되다 발송되다 [balsongdoeda] /be sent; be forwarded — For an object, letter, document, etc., to be sent by mail, delivery service, etc./
발송자 발송자 [balsongja] /sender — A person who sends goods, letters, documents, etc. by mail or courier./
발송하다 발송하다 [balsonghada] /send; forward — To send an object, letter, document, etc., by mail, delivery service, etc./
발신 발신 [balsin] /mailing; sending; transmission — An act of sending out a letter, an electrical signal, radio, etc./
발신되다 발신되다 [balsindoeda] /be mailed; be sent; be transmitted — For a letter, an electrical signal, radio broadcast, etc., to be sent out./
발신음 발신음 [balsineum] /dial tone — The sound of sending signals when making a phone call to others./
발신인 발신인 [balsinin] /addresser; sender — A person who is sending a mail, electronic signal, etc./
발신자 발신자 [balsinja] /sender; addresser; caller — A person who is sending a mail, electronic signal, etc./
발신하다 발신하다 [balsinhada] /mail; send; transmit — To send out a letter, an electrical signal, radio broadcast, etc./
발아 발아 [bala] /sprout — Young plant growth such as a shoot or bud./germination — A new shoot from a seed./beginning — (figurative) A state in which a thing, event, idea, etc., starts./
발아래 발아래 [balarae] /the scene below one's feet — The place that is right under where one is standing, or the place that one can look down at from where he/she is standing./no match — (figurative) A level that is lower than the lowest level of one's competence./
발아래로 보다 발아래로 보다 [balaraero boda] /see someone as no match for oneself — To look down on or underestimate someone./
발아하다 발아하다 [balahada] /sprout — For new buds or shoots of grass or a tree to come out./germinate — For a new shoot to come out from a seed./begin — (figurative) For a thing, event, idea, etc., to start./
발악 발악 [balag] /struggling; desperateness — The act of struggling desperately by employing all sorts of actions or moves./
발악하다 발악하다 [balaghada] /struggle; act desperately — To struggle desperately by employing all sorts of actions or moves./
발안 발안 [balan] /initiation; proposal; initiative — The act of coming up with and then presenting a new idea or plan, or such an idea or plan./proposal; suggestion — The act of presenting an agenda to be discussed in a meeting./
발암 발암 [balam] /carcinogenesis — The development of a cancer, or the formation of cancer./
발암성 발암성 [balamseong] /carcinogenicity — The quality of a substance that gets into the body and causes a cancer./
발야구 발야구 [balyagu] /kickball — A sports game with rules similar to baseball, but, in which a ball is kicked, not hit./
발언 발언 [baleon] /comment; remark; statement — The act of saying something to express one's opinion, or a statement made for such a purpose./
발언권 발언권 [baleongwon] /right to speak — The right to present an opinion in a meeting./voice; say — The authority or influence exerted by the act of presenting one's own opinion./
발언하다 발언하다 [baleonhada] /comment; remark; state — To say something to express one's opinion./
발에 채다[차이다] 발에 채다[차이다] [bale chaeda[chaida]] /be kicked by a foot — To exist here and there and be common./
발열 발열 [balyeol] /heating; exothermicity — A state of being heated, or the act of generating heat./fever; febrility — A state in which one's temperature becomes high or such a symptom./
발원 발원 [balwon] /source — The start of flowing water, or such a thing./origin — The first formation or occurrence of an idea, social phenomenon, etc., or such a thing./riverhead; source — The source of flowing water./origin — The place where an idea, social phenomenon, etc., first occurred or was formed./offering a prayer — The act of making a wish to a god or Buddha, or such a wish./
발원지 발원지 [balwonji] /source — A place where a current of water starts./cradle; birthplace — A place where an idea or social phenomenon etc., starts or occurs for the first time./
발원하다 발원하다 [balwonhada] /rise — For flowing water to start./originate — For an idea, social phenomenon, etc., to occur or start for the first time./offer a prayer — To make a wish to a god or the Buddha./
발육 발육 [balyug] /growth; development — The growth of an organism./
발육되다 발육되다 [balyugdoeda] /grow; develop — For an organism to come to grow./
발육하다 발육하다 [balyughada] /grow; develop — For an organism to grow./
발을 달다 발을 달다 [baleul dalda] /add a foot — Add words to what was already said./
발음 발음 [baleum] /pronunciation — The act of making a speech sound, or such a speech sound./
발음 기관 발음 기관 [baleum gigwan] /pronunciation organ — Each bodily organ which is used to speak or make a sound./
발음되다 발음되다 [baleumdoeda] /be pronounced — For the sounds of human speech to be made./
발음하다 발음하다 [baleumhada] /pronounce — To make the sounds of human speech./
발의 발의 [balui] /proposal; suggestion — The act of proposing an item that should be deliberated and discussed in a meeting, or such an item./
발의하다 발의하다 [baluihada] /propose; suggest — To propose an item that should be deliberated and discussed in a meeting./
발이 내키지 않다 발이 내키지 않다 [bali naekiji anhda] /One's feet are reluctant — To be disinclined or hesitate to do something./
발이 닳다 발이 닳다 [bali dalhda] /One's feet have worn out — To visit a certain place very often or move very busily./
발이 떨어지지 않다 발이 떨어지지 않다 [bali tteoleojiji anhda] /One's foot cannot be lifted — To be unable to leave with ease due to concern, worry or wistfulness./
발이 뜸하다 발이 뜸하다 [bali tteumhada] /give a sparce foot — To seldom visit a certain place where one used to go often./
발이 손이 되도록 빌다 발이 손이 되도록 빌다 [bali soni doedorog bilda] /beg desperately to such an extent that one's feet become hands — To ask for someone's forgiveness desperately./
발이 익다 발이 익다 [bali igda] /One's feet are familiar with something — To be familiar with a certain street as one has been there many times./
발이 잦다 발이 잦다 [bali jajda] /have a frequent foot — To visit a certain place often./
발이 저리다 발이 저리다 [bali jeorida] /have a numb foot — To feel anxious or uneasy because one did something wrong./
발인 발인 [balin] /departure of a funeral procession — The act of moving the body of a dead person from the funeral hall to the grave or crematory, or such a process./
발자국 발자국 [baljagug] /footprint; footmark — A mark on the ground, left by a foot or shoe./step — A measure of the distance from raising to landing of a foot./
발자취 발자취 [baljachwi] /footprint; trace — A trace left by stepping on something, or a sound made in such a situation./footprint; trace — (figurative) One's past journey in life./
발작 발작 [baljag] /seizure — A symptom of a disease, emotion, movement, etc., occurring suddenly and violently./
발작하다 발작하다 [baljaghada] /have a seizure — For a symptom of a disease, emotion, movement, etc., to occur suddenly and violently./
발장구 발장구 [baljanggu] /paddling — An act of raising and lowering one's feet./
발재간 발재간 [baljaegan] /foot skills — A talented usage of one's feet./
발전 발전 [baljeon] /development; advancement — The act of moving forward to a better state or higher step./progress; growth — The act of unfolding in a certain direction./electricity generation — The act of generating electricity./
발전기 발전기 [baljeongi] /developing period — A period of moving forward to an advanced stage/electric generator; dynamo — A machine that changes kinetic energy or potential energy into electric energy./
발전되다 발전되다 [baljeondoeda] /be developed; be advanced — To move forward to a better state or higher step./be in progress; be developed — To unfold in a certain direction./
발전사 발전사 [baljeonsa] /development history — The history of development./
발전상 발전상 [baljeonsang] /improvement; development — The state or status of something having made progress or achieved development./
발전성 발전성 [baljeonseong] /potential — The possibility of future growth./
발전소 발전소 [baljeonso] /power plant — A place equipped with facilities that generate electricity by running the generator with water power, thermal power, nuclear power, wind power, tidal power, solar power, geothermal heat, etc./
발전시키다 발전시키다 [baljeonsikida] /develop — To make something advance to a better state or higher step./progress; develop — To make something unfold in a certain direction./
발전적 발전적 [baljeonjeog] /being expansive; being developmental — A state of moving forward to a better state or higher stage./developmental — Advancing to a better state or higher step./
발전하다 발전하다 [baljeonhada] /develop — To advance to a better state or higher step./progress; develop — To unfold in a certain direction./
발정 발정 [baljeong] /rut; estrus — An animal's instinctive arousal of sexual excitement./sexual excitement — (slang) A person's arousal of sexual excitement./
발정하다 발정하다 [baljeonghada] /be in rut — For an animal to be sexually excited instinctively./be sexually excited — (slang) For a person to be sexually excited./
발족 발족 [baljog] /starting; beginning; inauguration — The state in which a newly formed institution, organization, etc., gets into action or the act of starting activities in such a way./
발족되다 발족되다 [baljogdoeda] /be launched; be inaugurated — For a new institution, organization, etc., to be formed and put into action./
발족시키다 발족시키다 [baljogsikida] /start; begin; inaugurate — To form a new institution, organization, etc., and come to begin their activitie./
발족하다 발족하다 [baljoghada] /start; begin; inaugurate — For a newly formed institution, organization, etc., to get into action; to start activities in such a way./
발주 발주 [balju] /ordering — The act of ordering goods, services, etc., in a big-scale transaction such as a construction or service supply project./
발주자 발주자 [baljuja] /orderer; contractor — A person who orders goods, services, etc., in a big-scale transaction such as a construction or service supply project./
발주하다 발주하다 [baljuhada] /order — To order goods, services, etc., in a big-scale transaction such as a construction or service supply project./
발진 발진 [baljin] /rash — Many small boils on one's skin due to fever, or such a boil./takeoff — A battleship, airplane, rocket, etc., setting out and moving forward./
발진하다 발진하다 [baljinhada] /rash — For many small boils to appear on one's skin, due to fever./take off — For a battleship, airplane, rocket, etc., to set out and move forward./
발질 발질 [baljil] /kick — The act of kicking with one's foot./
발짓 발짓 [baljis] /moving a foot — The act of moving a foot./foot gesture — The act of moving a foot to signal something./
발짝 발짝 [baljjag] /step — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the number of steps./
발찌 발찌 [baljji] /anklet; ankle bracelet — A round accessory for wearing on the ankle to dress up oneself./
발차 발차 [balcha] /departure — A bus, train, etc., departing./
발차기 발차기 [balchagi] /kick — The movement of kicking in sports./
발차하다 발차하다 [balchahada] /depart — For a bus, train, etc., to depart./
발착 발착 [balchag] /departure and arrival — The departure and arrival of a train, airplane, etc./
발췌 발췌 [balchwe] /extracting; extract; excerpt — An act of singling out necessary or important parts from a book or text; or a piece of writing extracted from the source./
발췌되다 발췌되다 [balchwedoeda] /be excerpted; be culled — To form a new institution, organization, etc., and come to begin their activities./
발췌하다 발췌하다 [balchwehada] /extract; cull — To extract necessary or important parts selectively from a book or text./
발치 발치 [balchi] /direction of foot — The side where one's feet are when lying on one's back./direction of foot — The side where one's feet are when standing up./base; bottom — The side where one's feet are when standing up./
발칙하다 발칙하다 [balchighada] /insolent; impertinent — One's behavior or remark being very rude and displeasing./
발칵 발칵 [balkag] /in a fit of rage — In the manner of getting angry suddenly./in a turmoil — In the state of being in uproar or commotion as something happens unexpectedly./violently; in the manner of bursting open — In the manner that someone opens the door or the door is opened suddenly./
발탁 발탁 [baltag] /selection; choice — The choice of a particular person among many people./
발탁되다 발탁되다 [baltagdoeda] /be selected; be chosen — For a particular person to be chosen among many people./
발탁하다 발탁하다 [baltaghada] /select; choose — To choose a particular person among many people./
발톱 발톱 [baltob] /toenail — The hard part that is covering and protecting the end of the toe./
발파 발파 [balpa] /blasting — An act of drilling a hole into a rock or solid object, putting an explosive into the hole, and then blowing it up./
발파되다 발파되다 [balpadoeda] /be blasted; be blown up — For a hole to be drilled into a rock or solid object, an explosive to be put into the hole, and then blown up./
발파하다 발파하다 [balpahada] /blast; blow up — To drill a hole into a rock or solid object, put an explosive into the hole, and then blow it up./
발판 발판 [balpan] /foothold; footing — A thing for putting one's foot on./stool; footrest — A thing that one stands on to make one look taller./foothold; base; foundation — (figurative) A basis for achieving a certain goal./pedal — The part of a musical instrument or machine, etc., that one presses with a foot to operate it./springboard — A device for helping a player with his/her power for jumping in gymnastics, athletics, swimming, diving, etc./
발포 발포 [balpo] /promulgation; proclamation — A governmental institution announcing a legislation, policy, etc., publicly./firing; shooting — The act of shooting a gun or cannon./
발포되다 발포되다 [balpodoeda] /be proclaimed; be promulgated — For a legislation, policy, etc., to be announced publicly by a government institution./
발포하다 발포하다 [balpohada] /proclaim; promulgate — For a governmental institution to announce a legislation, policy, etc., publicly./fire; shoot — To shoot a gun or cannon./
발표 발표 [balpyo] /announcement; presentation; release; roll out — The act of revealing and announcing a certain fact, result, work of art, etc., to the world./
발표되다 발표되다 [balpyodoeda] /be published; be released; be rolled out — For a certain fact, result, work of art, etc., to be revealed and announced to the world./
발표문 발표문 [balpyomun] /statement — A written statement containing an announcement./
발표자 발표자 [balpyoja] /speaker; presenter — A person who officially reveals and announces a certain fact, opinion or position./
발표하다 발표하다 [balpyohada] /publish; release; roll out — To reveal and announce a certain fact, result, work of art, etc., to the world./
발표회 발표회 [balpyohoe] /meeting; conference; concert; exhibition — A public meeting which presents or showcases artistic or academic achievements in creative areas such as dance or music./
발하다 발하다 [balhada] /bloom — For a flower to bloom./create; rise — For a certain energy, light, sound, etc., to be created or make this happen./order; announce — To publicize the law or give an order./
발해 발해 [balhae] /Balhae Kingdom — A country that existed from the year 698 to 926 in Manchuria and in the northern part of the Korean Peninsula; a country established by Dae Jo-yeong after the fall of the Goguryeo Kingdom by gathering the remaining people of the Goguryeo Kingdom and the Mohe tribes; although the country was so powerful that it was known as the &quot;Flourishing Land in the East&quot;, it was defeated by the Khitans in 926./
발행 발행 [balhaeng] /publication — The act of publishing a book, newspaper, etc./issuance — The act of issuing the currency, securities, official documents, etc./
발행되다 발행되다 [balhaengdoeda] /be published — For a book, newspaper, etc., to be published./be issued — For the currency, securities, official documents, etc., to be issued./
발행인 발행인 [balhaengin] /publisher — A person who publishes a book or newspaper, etc./issuer — A person who issues a note, check, bond, etc., which has a public function./
발행자 발행자 [balhaengja] /publisher — A person who publishes a book or newspaper, etc./issuer — A person who issues a note, check, bond, etc., which has a public function./
발행하다 발행하다 [balhaenghada] /publish — To publish a book, newspaper, etc./issue — To issue the currency, securities, official documents, etc./
발현 발현 [balhyeon] /revelation; manifestation — A state in which a quality or hidden mentality emerges to the surface./
발현되다 발현되다 [balhyeondoeda] /be revealed; be manifested — For a hidden quality or spiritual value to emerge to the surface./
발현하다 발현하다 [balhyeonhada] /reveal; manifest — For a hidden quality or spiritual value to emerge to the surface; or make such a thing emerge./
발호 발호 [balho] /domineering state — The act of wielding one's authority arbitrarily and behaving as one likes./
발호하다 발호하다 [balhohada] /dominate; prevail — To wield one's authority arbitrarily and behave as one likes./
발화 발화 [balhwa] /ignition — A state in which something catches fire and starts to burn./uttering; pronouncing — The act of letting out spoken sounds, or words uttered in such a way./
발화되다 발화되다 [balhwadoeda] /be ignited — To catch fire and start to burn./be uttered; be pronounced — For spoken words to come out./
발화하다 발화하다 [balhwahada] /ignite — To catch fire and start to burn./utter; pronounce — To let out spoken sounds./
발효 발효 [balhyo] /coming into effect; becoming effective — The state of a treaty, legislation, official document, etc., entering into force or putting such things into force./fermentation — Chemical reaction in which organic matter is decomposed and altered by yeast or microorganisms./
발효되다 발효되다 [balhyodoeda] /come into effect; be effective — For a treaty, legislation, official document, etc., to enter into force./be fermented — For organic matter to be decomposed and altered by yeast or microorganisms./
발효법 발효법 [balhyobeob] /zymotechnics — A method of using yeast or microorganisms to decompose and alter an organic matter./
발효시키다 발효시키다 [balhyosikida] /bring into force — To make a treaty, legislation, official document, etc., enter into force./ferment — To use yeast or microorganisms to decompose and alter organic matter./
발효유 발효유 [balhyoyu] /fermented milk — A beverage made by putting in yeast or lactobacillus in milk and fermenting it./
발효하다 발효하다 [balhyohada] /come into effect; bring into force — For a treaty, legislation, official document, etc., to enter into force or to put such things into force./ferment — For organic matter to be decomposed and altered by yeast or microorganisms./
발휘 발휘 [balhwi] /display; exhibition — The act of showing a talent, capacity, etc., well./
발휘되다 발휘되다 [balhwidoeda] /be displayed; be exhibited — For a talent, capacity, etc., to be displayed./
발휘하다 발휘하다 [balhwihada] /display; exhibit — To show a talent, capacity, etc., well./
발흥 발흥 [balheung] /sudden rise; sudden thriving — A state in which an ideology, a country, force, etc. rises suddenly and gains power./
발흥되다 발흥되다 [balheungdoeda] /be risen suddenly; start to thrive suddenly — For an ideology, a country, force, etc., to come to rise suddenly and gain power./
발흥하다 발흥하다 [balheunghada] /rise suddenly; thrive suddenly — For an ideology, a country, force, etc., to rise suddenly and gain power./
밝기 밝기 [balggi] /brightness — The degree of brightness of light or lighting./brightness — The degree of brightness of color./
밝다 밝다 [balgda] /be light — To become light after dark./break; dawn — To become morning after night./light; brilliant; luminous — The light emanating from something being bright./bright — A place being light as a result of getting a lot of sun./light — A color being not dark or impure./keen; sharp — Eyesight or hearing being good./courteous; well-behaved — Polite./clean — Sound and fair./cheerful; bright — A facial expression, personality, mood, etc., being lively and pleasant./good at; clever — Knowing well about something and dealing with it perfectly./bright; promising — One's expected future being positive./well acquainted with; familiar with — Knowing a lot about something./
밝아지다 밝아지다 [balgajida] /brighten; lighten — To turn bright./
밝은색 밝은색 [balgeunsaeg] /bright color — A bright, vivid color./
밝혀내다 밝혀내다 [balghyeonaeda] /reveal; disclose; discover — To judge the truth, value, or right and wrong of something and show the result./
밝혀지다 밝혀지다 [balghyeojida] /be illuminated; be lightened; be brightened — For a thing emitting light to become bright./be revealed; be disclosed — For the truth, value, right and wrong , fact, etc., of something to be revealed and made known./
밝히 밝히 [balghi] /brightly — In a bright light, etc./clearly — Clearly and surely./
밝히다 밝히다 [balghida] /light up; brighten up — To light up a dark place with a torch, lamp, etc./light; turn on — To set a fire or turn on a light, etc./stay up — To stay awake and spend the night./be crazy for — To like something too much, without trying to hide it./study; clarify — To find out a certain fact, value, whether something is right or wrong, etc./reveal; disclose — To tell an unknown fact to someone or spread it to the public./give hope — To give hope for the future./
밟다 밟다 [balbda] /step on — To put one's foot or feet on someone or something and press him/her/it./bully — (figurative) For a stronger person to bully a weak person./pace; step; tread — To put feet on an object and stand on it or to tread on it./go through; undergo — To go through a certain procedure, process, etc., in order./follow; trail after; shadow — To follow someone secretly./go through; experience — To experience a certain incident./arrive — (figurative) To arrive in a certain place./
밟히다 밟히다 [balbhida] /be stepped — To be pressed by a foot or feet./be shadowed; be followed — To be followed by someone./be bullied — For a weak person to be bullied by a stronger person./
밤 밤 [bam] /night; evening — The period of dark hours from sunset to sunrise the next day./chestnut — A brown fruit, encased in a prickly burr with a bitter-tasting inner skin, which can be eaten raw, cooked or boiled./
밤거리 밤거리 [bamgeori] /night streets — Dark streets after sunset./
밤길 밤길 [bamgil] /night street — Dark streets after sunset./
밤나무 밤나무 [bamnamu] /chestnut tree — A tree that produces thin, long, white flowers in the early summer and bears chestnuts in the fall./
밤낚시 밤낚시 [bamnakksi] /night fishing — The act of fishing at night./
밤낮 밤낮 [bamnaj] /all day; day and night — Day and night./always; around the clock — All the time; days and nights./
밤낮없이 밤낮없이 [bamnajeobsi] /always; around the clock — All the time; days and nights./
밤낮을 가리지 않다 밤낮을 가리지 않다 [bamnajeul gariji anhda] /not distinguish between day and night — To continue to do something without taking a rest./
밤낮이 따로 없다 밤낮이 따로 없다 [bamnaji ttaro eobsda] /A day and a night are not separate from each other — To continue to do something without taking a rest day and night./
밤눈 밤눈 [bamnun] /night vision — Vision related to being able to see things at night./
밤늦다 밤늦다 [bamneujda] /late at night — Being an advanced hour of the night./
밤말 밤말 [bammal] /secret — Words spoken at night./
밤말은 쥐가 듣고 낮말은 새가 듣는다 밤말은 쥐가 듣고 낮말은 새가 듣는다 [bammaleun jwiga deudgo najmaleun saega deudneunda] /Words spoken at night are heard by a bird, words spoken in the daytime are heard by a rat — Words even made carefully and secretly are bound to be known by others./
밤무대 밤무대 [bammudae] /nightclub — A stage where people sing and dance in bars, nightclubs, etc./
밤바다 밤바다 [bambada] /night sea — Sea at night./
밤바람 밤바람 [bambaram] /night breeze; night wind — Wind that blows at night./
밤배 밤배 [bambae] /night boat — A boat that sails at night./
밤비 밤비 [bambi] /night rain; evening rain — Rain at night./
밤사이 밤사이 [bamsai] /overnight — The time from the evening to the morning./
밤새 밤새 [bamsae] /overnight — The time from the evening to the next day morning./
밤새껏 밤새껏 [bamsaekkeos] /through the night — Continuously from night until next morning./
밤새는 줄(을) 모르다 밤새는 줄(을) 모르다 [bamsaeneun jul(eul) moreuda] /1. Not to know one stays up all night — Not to realize that time is passing due to being immersed or engrossed in something/
밤새다 밤새다 [bamsaeda] /stay up — For morning to come after a night./
밤새우다 밤새우다 [bamsaeuda] /sit up all night; stay up all night — To spend a night without sleeping./
밤새움 밤새움 [bamsaeum] /staying up all night — Staying up all night without sleeping./
밤색 밤색 [bamsaeg] /chestnut; nutbrown color; maroon — The color of a well-ripened chestnut's skin./
밤샘 밤샘 [bamsaem] /staying up all night — Staying up all night without sleeping./
밤샘하다 밤샘하다 [bamsaemhada] /sit up all night; stay up all night — To spend a night without sleeping./
밤손님 밤손님 [bamsonnim] /thief; burglar — (figurative) A thief that steals other people's possessions at night./
밤송이 밤송이 [bamsongi] /chestnut burr — A chestnut encased in a prickly hard burr, or such a burr./
밤안개 밤안개 [bamangae] /night fog — Fog that forms at night./
밤알 밤알 [bamal] /chestnut — Individual chestnut./
밤이슬 밤이슬 [bamiseul] /night dew — Dew that forms during the night./
밤일 밤일 [bamil] /night work — A night shift./sex; sexual intercourse — (euphemism) Sexual intercourse between a man and a woman with their sexual organs./
밤일하다 밤일하다 [bamilhada] /work at night — To work at night./have sexual intercourse — (euphemism) For a man and a woman to have sexual intercourse with their sexual organs./
밤잠 밤잠 [bamjam] /night sleep — Sleep at night./
밤중 밤중 [bamjung] /midnight; dead of the night — The middle of the night./
밤차 밤차 [bamcha] /night bus; night train — A bus or train that runs at night./
밤참 밤참 [bamcham] /midnight snack — Food eaten at night after dinner./
밤톨 밤톨 [bamtol] /chestnut — Each chestnut fruit./
밤톨만 한 녀석[놈] 밤톨만 한 녀석[놈] [bamtolman han nyeoseog[nom]] /a fellow[guy] who is as small as a chestnut — A person who is young or has a small frame./
밤하늘 밤하늘 [bamhaneul] /night sky — The sky at night./
밥 밥 [bab] /steamed rice; rice — A dish made by boiling rice and other grains until the water has cooked away./meal — Food that is eaten at particular times of the day./feed — Food that animals eat./interests — Something that one should take possession of./pushover — (figurative) Someone who is used or sacrificed by someone else./
밥 구경(을) 하다 밥 구경(을) 하다 [bab gugyeong(eul) hada] /sightsee rice — To have a meal after a long time./
밥 구경을 못하다 밥 구경을 못하다 [bab gugyeongeul moshada] /be unable to sightsee rice — To be unable to have a meal at all./
밥 먹듯 하다 밥 먹듯 하다 [bab meogdeus hada] /as if eating rice — To do something very frequently./
밥 먹을 때는 개도 안 때린다 밥 먹을 때는 개도 안 때린다 [bab meogeul ttaeneun gaedo an ttaerinda] /You should not beat the dog when it is eating rice — It is advised to not scold or rebuke someone when he/she is eating even if he/she did something seriously wrong./
밥 빌어다가 죽을 쑤어 먹을 놈[자식] 밥 빌어다가 죽을 쑤어 먹을 놈[자식] [bab bileodaga jugeul ssueo meogeul nom[jasig]] /a guy[fellow] who would beg for rice and cook juk, rice porridge, with it — A person who is not only lazy, but also stupid./
밥 안 먹어도 배부르다 밥 안 먹어도 배부르다 [bab an meogeodo baebureuda] /be full even without eating rice — To be very satisfied because something good happens./
밥(을) 벌다 밥(을) 벌다 [bab(eul) beolda] /earn rice — To work and get paid to make a living./
밥(을) 주다 밥(을) 주다 [bab(eul) juda] /give rice — To wind up a spring to make a clock work./
밥거리 밥거리 [babgeori] /ingredients for rice — The ingredients for cooking rice./job; work — Things to do for to make a living./
밥그릇 밥그릇 [babgeureus] /rice bowl — A bowl for holding rice./job; work — (slang) A job for making a living./
밥내 밥내 [babnae] /rice smell — The smell from cooked rice./
밥맛 밥맛 [babmas] /the taste of rice — The taste of steamed rice./appetite — The appetite to eat a meal./
밥맛(이) 떨어지다 밥맛(이) 떨어지다 [babmas(i) tteoleojida] /One's appetite drops — For the words or behavior of someone to be unpleasant and disgusting./
밥맛(이) 없다 밥맛(이) 없다 [babmas(i) eobsda] /have no appetite — To be unpleasant and upset with someone and have no inclination toward dealing with him/her./
밥물 밥물 [babmul] /water for boiling rice — Water poured into a pot or kettle for cooking rice./rice water — The thick water overflowing a kettle when rice is boiling./
밥반찬 밥반찬 [babbanchan] /side dish — Food to eat along with rice./
밥벌이 밥벌이 [babbeoli] /job — Something that one does in order to make one's living./living — Earnings just enough to make a living./
밥벌이하다 밥벌이하다 [babbeolihada] /work for a living — To work for a living./work for a living — To earn just enough to make a living./
밥상 밥상 [babsang] /dining table — A table used to set food on, or a table with food./
밥상머리 밥상머리 [babsangmeori] /dining table — Any one side of a set dining table or a spot near it./
밥상보 밥상보 [babsangbo] /bapsangbo — wrapping cloth for the dining table: A wrapping cloth to cover a set dining table./
밥솥 밥솥 [babsot] /rice pot; rice cooker — A cooker for making rice./
밥숟가락 밥숟가락 [babsudgarag] /spoon — A piece of tableware that is used to scoop steamed rice./what little food — (figurative) A small quantity of steamed rice./
밥숟가락(을) 놓다 밥숟가락(을) 놓다 [babsudgarag(eul) nohda] /put down one's spoon — (slang) To die./
