밥숟갈 밥숟갈 [babsudgal] /spoon for rice — An implement for scooping rice./small amount of rice — (figurative) A small amount of cooked rice./
밥술 밥술 [babsul] /spoon — A piece of tableware that is used to scoop steamed rice./what little food — (figurative) A small quantity of steamed rice./
밥술(을) 놓다 밥술(을) 놓다 [babsul(eul) nohda] /put down one's spoon — (slang) To die./
밥술깨나 먹다 밥술깨나 먹다 [babsulkkaena meogda] /eat a spoon — To make a good living./
밥술이나 뜨다[먹다] 밥술이나 뜨다[먹다] [babsulina tteuda[meogda]] /scoop up[eat] a spoon — To make a decent living./
밥알 밥알 [babal] /grain of cooked rice — A grain of cooked rice./
밥알을 세다 밥알을 세다 [babaleul seda] /count the grains of rice — To have a meal in a reluctant and slow manner just making a gesture of eating./
밥알이 곤두서다 밥알이 곤두서다 [babali gonduseoda] /A grain of rice stands upside-down — To be angry or upset to such an extent that one gets indigestion./
밥은 열 곳에 가 먹어도 잠은 한 곳에서 자랬다 밥은 열 곳에 가 먹어도 잠은 한 곳에서 자랬다 [babeun yeol gose ga meogeodo jameun han goseseo jaraessda] /You have to sleep at one place even if you may eat rice at ten different places — People are advised to live in a fixed residence./
밥장사 밥장사 [babjangsa] /restaurant business — A business of making and selling meals./
밥장사하다 밥장사하다 [babjangsahada] /sell food; run a restaurant — To make and sell meals./
밥주걱 밥주걱 [babjugeog] /rice paddle; rice spatula — An implement shaped like a spoon used to scoop up rice./
밥주발 밥주발 [babjubal] /bapjubal — brass rice bowl: An open-top container with a cover, which is made of brass and used to serve rice./
밥줄 밥줄 [babjul] /livelihood — (slang) An occupation or means to make a living./
밥줄이 끊기다[끊어지다] 밥줄이 끊기다[끊어지다] [babjuli kkeunhgida[kkeunheojida]] /The livelihood is cut off — (slang) To lose one's job./
밥집 밥집 [babjib] /small restaurant — An eating place that sells simple meals of rice with a few side dishes./
밥통 밥통 [babtong] /rice container; rice cooker — A container for holding or keeping rice./stomach — (slang) The stomach./good-for-nothing — (disparaging) A person who only eats rice without contributing his or her share of work./
밥투정 밥투정 [babtujeong] /grumbling over one's food — A complaint about the food when eating./
밥투정하다 밥투정하다 [babtujeonghada] /grumble over one's food — To complain about the food when eating./
밥풀 밥풀 [babpul] /grain of rice — A grain of a boiled rice./rice paste — A thing made by mashing steamed rice to glue something./
밥하다 밥하다 [babhada] /cook rice — To cook rice./cook; fix a meal — To prepare a meal./
밧줄 밧줄 [basjul] /rope — A rope interwined thickly with three strands of hemp, etc./
방 방 [bang] /room — A space enclosed by walls for residential or business purposes./shot — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the number of shots in firing a gun or cannon, or the number of times explosives are set./swing; jab — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the frequency of hitting someone with a fist or club./shot — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the frequency of taking  photos./bang — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the frequency of farting./
