방공 방공 [banggong] /anticommunism — The act of deterring or keeping in check communism./
방공호 방공호 [banggongho] /air-raid shelter; dugout — A facility set up underground in order to escape bombardment attacks from cannons, missiles, etc., or from air raids./
방과 방과 [banggwa] /dismissal of a class — The finishing of school for the day, or school letting out./
방관 방관 [banggwan] /onlooking — An act of observing something without taking part in it./
방관자 방관자 [banggwanja] /onlooker — A person who observes something without taking part in it./
방관적 방관적 [banggwanjeog] /onlooking — A state in which one observes something without taking part in it./onlooking; indifferent — Just looking at a certain incident on the sideline, rather than stepping forward to handle it./
방관하다 방관하다 [banggwanhada] /look on; remain an idle onlooker — To just look at a certain incident on the sideline, rather than stepping forward to handle it./
방광 방광 [banggwang] /bladder — A body organ shaped like a bag, which stores urine and passes it out of the body./
방구들 방구들 [banggudeul] /banggudeul — A system that heats up the floor with fire, hot water, electricity, etc./
방구석 방구석 [bangguseog] /corner of a room — The four corners of a room./room; inside of a room — (slang) A room or the inside of a room./
방귀 방귀 [banggwi] /fart — A foul-smelling gas in the body that is expelled through the anus./
