벨벳 벨벳 [belbes] /velvet — Cloth dense with short, smooth pile./
벨트 벨트 [belteu] /belt — A strip worn around the waist of a garment./belt — A strip-shaped device hung on two wheels to deliver power./
벼 벼 [byeo] /rice plant; rice — The agricultural plant that produces rice as a fruit, or such a fruit./
벼 이삭은 익을수록 고개를 숙인다 벼 이삭은 익을수록 고개를 숙인다 [byeo isageun igeulsurog gogaereul suginda] /Rice plants tend to bow their heads as they grow ripe; The boughs that bear most hang lowest — A person who has an excellent ability and high status tends to be more modest./
벼농사 벼농사 [byeonongsa] /rice farming — Planting, growing, and harvesting rice./
벼락 벼락 [byeorag] /lightning — A natural phenomenon where a flash of light occurs in the sky accompanied by a loud boom./harsh scolding — (figurative) An extremely severe reproof or scolding./thunder; rush — (figurative) The quality of being very quick./sudden splash — (figurative) Having water poured on oneself unexpectedly./
벼락 맞을 소리 벼락 맞을 소리 [byeorag majeul sori] /remarks that may be struck by lightning — An evil remark that deserves to be punished by Heaven./
벼락 치듯 벼락 치듯 [byeorag chideus] /as if lightning strikes — Very fast./as if lightning strikes — Suddenly in a loud and noisy sound./
벼락(을) 맞다 벼락(을) 맞다 [byeorag(eul) majda] /be struck by lightning — To be punished for one's wrongdoing./be struck by lightning — To be severely rebuked or scolded./
벼락(이) 내리다[떨어지다] 벼락(이) 내리다[떨어지다] [byeorag(i) naerida[tteoleojida]] /Lightning falls[drops] — For an unexpected accident or disaster to occur./Lightning falls[drops] — To be severely rebuked or scolded./
벼락공부 벼락공부 [byeoraggongbu] /cramming for an examination — A sudden spurt of studying just before an examination, after having studying very little at other times./
벼락부자 벼락부자 [byeoragbuja] /overnight millionaire; the new rich — A person who became rich overnight./
벼락출세 벼락출세 [byeoragchulse] /sudden success — A sudden rise in one's status or frame./
벼락치기 벼락치기 [byeoragchigi] /hasty preparation; hurried job — A hurried preparation just before an event, after having done very little in advance./
벼랑 벼랑 [byeorang] /precipice — A steep, rugged side of a cliff or mountain./
벼랑길 벼랑길 [byeoranggil] /cliff; precipice — A narrow, dangerous path leading to a rugged and steep cliff./
벼랑에 몰리다 벼랑에 몰리다 [byeorange molrida] /be driven to a precipice — To fall into or be put in a dangerous situation./
벼랑에 서다 벼랑에 서다 [byeorange seoda] /stand on a precipice — To fall into or be put in a dangerous situation./
벼루 벼루 [byeoru] /byeoru — inkstone: A tool usually made of stone, used to rub ink sticks in./
벼룩 벼룩 [byeorug] /flea — An extremely small, harmful insect that lives on human or animal blood and spreads diseases./
벼룩도 낯짝이 있다 벼룩도 낯짝이 있다 [byeorugdo nachjjagi issda] /Even a flea has a mug — People have face to save just like even a very small flea has a mug./
벼룩시장 벼룩시장 [byeorugsijang] /flea market — The market where secondhand goods are sold and bought cheaply./
벼룩의 간을 내먹는다 벼룩의 간을 내먹는다 [byeorugui ganeul naemeogneunda] /take out and eat the liver of a flea — To take advantage of someone in a very difficult situation./
벼르다 벼르다 [byeoreuda] /look forward to; be determined; watch for — To wait and see for something, being determined to do it./
벼슬 벼슬 [byeoseul] /(no equivalent expression) — (archaic) A position or title of a public official who works for a state./position; post — (slang) A position or title./
벼슬길 벼슬길 [byeoseulgil] /career in government — (archaic) The way to become a government official./
벼슬길에 오르다 벼슬길에 오르다 [byeoseulgile oreuda] /be on the career in government — (archaic) To become a government official to manage state affairs./
벼슬살이 벼슬살이 [byeoseulsali] /being in government service — (archaic) A state of living as a public official who works for a state./
벼슬아치 벼슬아치 [byeoseulachi] /public servant — (archaic) A public official who works for a state./
벼슬자리 벼슬자리 [byeoseuljari] /official position — (archaic) A government post./
벼슬하다 벼슬하다 [byeoseulhada] /byeoseulhada — (archaic) To become a public official who works for a state./
벽 벽 [byeog] /wall — Any of the parts that enclose a room or house./wall — (figurative) A reality or situation that is hard to overcome./wall — (figurative) The state of a relationship or exchange being severed or discontinued./
벽(을) 쌓다 벽(을) 쌓다 [byeog(eul) ssahda] /stack up a wall — To cut off a relationship or stop caring about something./
벽걸이 벽걸이 [byeoggeoli] /hooked object — An object that is hung on the wall or pillar for use./
벽계수 벽계수 [byeoggyesu] /clean stream — A stream that is so clean that it looks blue./
벽난로 벽난로 [byeognanro] /fireplace — A stove installed in the wall inside a house./
벽돌 벽돌 [byeogdol] /brick — A square stone used for constructing a house or building./
벽돌담 벽돌담 [byeogdoldam] /brick wall — A wall built with bricks in order to enclose a house or building, etc./
벽돌장 벽돌장 [byeogdoljang] /brick — A piece of brick./
벽돌집 벽돌집 [byeogdoljib] /brick house — A house built mainly with bricks and having no pillar things./
벽두 벽두 [byeogdu] /outset; start — The very beginning; the beginning of a period or occurrence./
벽면 벽면 [byeogmyeon] /wall — The surface of  a wall./
벽보 벽보 [byeogbo] /poster — A notice put up on a wall or bulletin board so that a lot of people can read it./
벽보판 벽보판 [byeogbopan] /poster board — A board on which posters are put up./
벽시계 벽시계 [byeogsigye] /wall clock — A clock that is hung on the wall or a pillar./
벽안 벽안 [byeogan] /blue eyes — Eyes with blue irises./
벽에 부딪히다 벽에 부딪히다 [byeoge budijhida] /be bumped against a wall — To face an obstacle or difficulty./
벽에도 귀가 있다 벽에도 귀가 있다 [byeogedo gwiga issda] /Even a wall has ears — You have to be careful about what you say because rumors spread even if it seems nobody hears./
벽장 벽장 [byeogjang] /built-in closet — A closet built by making a space inside the wall and installing doors on it, in which clothes, bedclothes, etc., can be stored./
벽지 벽지 [byeogji] /remote area — A secluded area that is far from an urban area./wallpaper — Wall covering made of paper which is attached to the wall with glue/
벽창호 벽창호 [byeogchangho] /pigheaded person; headstrong person — A very obstinate and inflexible person who does not take others' advice./
벽체 벽체 [byeogche] /wall structure — The parts that form the walls of a building./
벽촌 벽촌 [byeogchon] /remote village — A secluded village that is far from other villages./
벽화 벽화 [byeoghwa] /mural painting — A painting drawn on the wall of a building, cave, grave, etc./
변 변 [byeon] /feces; stool — Dung and urine; a word usually used to indicate dung./side — The edge of a place, an object, etc./side — A line that is a component of a figure in math./mishap; mischance — A sudden accident or strange happening./
변경 변경 [byeongyeong] /frontier; border — An area forming the boundary between two countries./change; alteration — The act of changing something in a different or new way./
변경되다 변경되다 [byeongyeongdoeda] /be changed; be altered — To be changed in a different or new way./
변경하다 변경하다 [byeongyeonghada] /change; alter — To change something in a different or new way./
변고 변고 [byeongo] /mishap; trouble — A sudden accident that happens unexpectedly./
변괴 변괴 [byeongoe] /unusual miseries; weird happening — An incomprehensible, strange happening or accident./
변기 변기 [byeongi] /toilet — A piece of equipment installed in a bathroom for a person to use when urinating or defecating./
변덕 변덕 [byeondeog] /caprice; fickleness — A frequent change in opinion, behavior, feeling, etc./
변덕맞다 변덕맞다 [byeondeogmajda] /whimsical; changeable; inconstant — Words, behavior, feelings, etc., often changing capriciously./
변덕스럽다 변덕스럽다 [byeondeogseureobda] /whimsical; changeable; inconstant — Words, behavior, feelings, etc., often changing capriciously./
변덕이 죽 끓듯 하다 변덕이 죽 끓듯 하다 [byeondeogi jug kkeulhdeus hada] /One's fickleness is like the juk, rice porridge, that is being boiled — For words, behavior or feelings to be fickle and frequently change./
변덕쟁이 변덕쟁이 [byeondeogjaengi] /fickle person; whimsical person — A person whose words, behavior, feelings, etc., often change capriciously./
변동 변동 [byeondong] /change; fluctuation — A situation or state changing into a different situation or state./
변동되다 변동되다 [byeondongdoeda] /be changed; be fluctuated — For a situation or state to be changed into a different situation or state./
변동시키다 변동시키다 [byeondongsikida] /change; fluctuate — To change a situation or state into a different situation or state./
변동하다 변동하다 [byeondonghada] /change; fluctuate — For a situation or state to change into a different situation or state./
변두리 변두리 [byeonduri] /outskirts; environs — The border of a region./
변란 변란 [byeonran] /upheaval; catastrophe — A huge disaster or fight that can put a nation in a dangerous situation./
