변리사 변리사 [byeonrisa] /patent lawyer — A person who manages affairs on behalf of an applicant so that he/she can get a patent for the invention of an object or method, etc./
변명 변명 [byeonmyeong] /excuse; justification — The act of explaining reasons to someone for the errors or mistakes one has made in order to seek his/her understanding or forgiveness./
변명하다 변명하다 [byeonmyeonghada] /make an excuse; justify — To explain reasons to someone for the errors or mistakes one has made in order to seek his/her understanding or forgiveness./
변모 변모 [byeonmo] /transformation — The shape or appearance of something being changed, or such a shape or appearance./
변모되다 변모되다 [byeonmodoeda] /be transformed — For the shape or appearance of something to be changed./
변모시키다 변모시키다 [byeonmosikida] /transform — To change the shape or appearance of something./
변모하다 변모하다 [byeonmohada] /transform — For the shape or appearance of something to change./
변발 변발 [byeonbal] /Chinese queue — A traditional male hairstyle of Mongolia or Manchuria, in which the front of the head is shaved off while the hair on the back is braided into a pigtail./
변방 변방 [byeonbang] /remote area; frontier — An area that is far from an urban area, or an area on the border between two countries./
변변찮다 변변찮다 [byeonbyeonchanhda] /not so good; poor — Being below par or average in appearance, personality, etc./not enough; insufficient; scanty — Not having enough of things such as household goods, clothing, food, etc./poor; inferior; unsatisfactory — Inferior to others in family background, ability, etc./
변변하다 변변하다 [byeonbyeonhada] /good-looking; decent; satisfactory — Being above par or average in appearance, personality, etc./enough; sufficient; decent — Having a sufficient amount of good household items, clothing, food, etc./fairly good; satisfactory — Not being inferior to others in family background, ability, etc./
변변히 변변히 [byeonbyeonhi] /respectably — In a state where one's appearance, personality, etc., are at a higher level than normal./enough — In a state in which salutation, clothes, food, etc., have been prepared properly and sufficiently./decently — In a state in which one's family or ability, etc., are not below that of others./
변별 변별 [byeonbyeol] /distinction; discrimination — The act of distinguishing between similar things./
변별되다 변별되다 [byeonbyeoldoeda] /be discriminated; be distinguished — For similar things to be distinguished./
변별하다 변별하다 [byeonbyeolhada] /discriminate; distinguish — To distinguish between similar things./
변복 변복 [byeonbog] /disguise — A state in which a person is wearing unusual clothes so that others cannot recognize him/her, or such attire./
변비 변비 [byeonbi] /constipation — A symptom in which feces are not excreted well as they have become hard after remaining in the large intestine too long./
변사 변사 [byeonsa] /silent-film narrator — A person who introduced the story of a silent movie to the audience and provided dialogues of its characters in mimetic voices./accidental death — A death from an unexpected disaster or accident./
변사자 변사자 [byeonsaja] /person accidentally killed — A person who dies in an unexpected disaster or accident./person dying an unnatural death — A person who is suspected to have been killed by a criminal./
변사체 변사체 [byeonsache] /body of person accidentally killed — The body of a person who died in an unexpected disaster or accident./body of person dying an unnatural death — The body of a person who is suspected to have been killed by a criminal./
변상 변상 [byeonsang] /paying back; reimbursement — The act of paying back borrowed money./compensation — The act of paying someone money for inflicting damage, or restoring something to its former state./indemnification — The act of paying money or an expensive item for doing something wrong./
변상하다 변상하다 [byeonsanghada] /pay back; reimburse — To pay back borrowed money./compensate; pay back — To pay someone money for inflicting damage, or restore something to its former state./indemnify — To pay money or an expensive item for doing something bad./
변색 변색 [byeonsaeg] /discoloration — The act of making something change color; the act of changing color./(no equivalent expression) — A change in one's facial expression because of anger or surprise./camouflage — The way that an animal changes its body color according to the color of its surroundings./
변색되다 변색되다 [byeonsaegdoeda] /be discolored — For the color of an object to be changed./(no equivalent expression) — For one's facial expression to cause to change because one gets angry or surprised./
변색하다 변색하다 [byeonsaeghada] /discolor — For the color of an object to be changed; for the color to change./(no equivalent expression) — For one's facial expression to change because one gets angry or surprised./camouflage — For an animal to change its body color according to the color of its surroundings./
변성기 변성기 [byeonseonggi] /age at which one's voice breaks — The age at which a male child's voice changes to that of an adult due to the change in the vocal cords./
변소 변소 [byeonso] /lavatory — A place where people can urinate or defecate./
변수 변수 [byeonsu] /variable — A factor that can bring about a change to a certain thing./variable — A number that can change into other different values within a certain range./
변신 변신 [byeonsin] /transformation — The act of changing an appearance or attitude in a different way from before./
변신술 변신술 [byeonsinsul] /transformation technique — Technique or magic that changes one's appearance./
변신하다 변신하다 [byeonsinhada] /transform — To change an appearance or attitude in a different way from before./
변심 변심 [byeonsim] /change of heart — A state in which a person's mind has changed./
변심하다 변심하다 [byeonsimhada] /change one's mind — For one's mind to change./
