변함없이 변함없이 [byeonhameobsi] /same; invariably — The same all the time without being changed./
변혁 변혁 [byeonhyeog] /revolution — The act of changing something into a quite different one quickly and suddenly./
변혁기 변혁기 [byeonhyeoggi] /period of change — A period when something changes into a different form quickly and suddenly./
변혁되다 변혁되다 [byeonhyeogdoeda] /be revolutionized; be reformed; be changed — To be changed into a quite different form quickly and suddenly./
변혁하다 변혁하다 [byeonhyeoghada] /revolutionize; reform; change — To change something into a quite different form quickly and suddenly./
변형 변형 [byeonhyeong] /deformation — A state in which the form, shape, property, etc., of something has changed, or the act of changing it./
변형되다 변형되다 [byeonhyeongdoeda] /be deformed — For the form, shape, property, etc., of something to be changed./
변형하다 변형하다 [byeonhyeonghada] /deform — To change the form, shape, property, etc., of something./
변호 변호 [byeonho] /defense — The act of arguing and making an excuse for another person./defense — In law, the act of the defense counsel speaking on the side of the defendant at a trial./
변호사 변호사 [byeonhosa] /lawyer — A person who is legally qualified to defend a defendant or plaintiff and to professionally deal with law-related matters./
변호인 변호인 [byeonhoin] /counsel — A person who defends a suspect or the accused in a criminal action./
변호하다 변호하다 [byeonhohada] /defend — To argue and make an excuse for another person./defend — In law, for the defense counsel to speak on the side of the defendant at a trial./
변화 변화 [byeonhwa] /change — A state in which the shape, condition, property, etc., of something have been altered./
변화되다 변화되다 [byeonhwadoeda] /be changed — For the shape, condition, property, etc., of something to be altered./
