보급되다 보급되다 [bogeubdoeda] /be diffused; be distributed — For something to be spread widely, and reach many places to allow people to enjoy it./be supplied; be distributed — For goods to be provided for people who need them./
보급소 보급소 [bogeubso] /distributor; distributing agency — An office that is in charge of distributing goods to people who need them./
보급품 보급품 [bogeubpum] /supply — Goods that are given to people who need them./
보급하다 보급하다 [bogeubhada] /diffuse; distribute — To spread something widely so that it reaches many places and people can enjoy it./supply; distribute — To provide goods for people who need them./
보기 보기 [bogi] /example — A thing that is shown as a representative in order to explain or prove something./
보기 좋게 보기 좋게 [bogi johge] /looking good — An expression used when a person enjoys another's mishap and makes a sarcastic comment about it./
보기 좋은 떡이 먹기도 좋다 보기 좋은 떡이 먹기도 좋다 [bogi joheun tteogi meoggido johda] /If tteok, rice cake, looks good, it will also taste good — If the appearance of something is good, its content also tends to be good./If tteok, rice cake, looks good, it will also taste good — It is sometimes necessary to make the appearance of something good as well as its content./
보내다 보내다 [bonaeda] /send — To make a person, goods, etc., go somewhere else./dispatch — To send someone on a certain mission or for a specific purpose./send; have someone marry — To marry off someone./send; have someone join — To have someone belong to an organization./express — To express one's feelings so that the other person can know./send; let someone leave — To have someone leave./pass time; spend time — To have time pass./die — To die and part with someone./send; let someone participate — To have someone participate in a sports game, gathering, etc./deliver; convey — To have content conveyed./
보내오다 보내오다 [bonaeoda] /send over — To have someone or something move and move near the receiving person./appreciate; thank — To express one's heart to someone./
보너스 보너스 [boneoseu] /bonus — Extra money that one receives beyond one's regular pay, according to one's achievement or contribution./
보는 눈이 있다 보는 눈이 있다 [boneun nuni issda] /have eyes to see — To have an ability to make an accurate evaluation of someone or something./
보다 보다 [boda] /see; look at; notice — To perceive with eyes the existence or appearance of an object./watch; see; enjoy — To enjoy or appreciate an object with eyes./read; look at; take a look at — To read and understand the words, pictures and symbols in a book, newspaper, map, etc./look at; take a look at; look in — To inspect an object to understand its content or state./meet; see — To meet a person for a purpose./take care of; look after; guard — To watch out for or take care of something./look at; assess; judge from — To perceive and assess an incident or situation./have told — To try to predict the future or fate by fortune-telling and etc./take — To take a test to assess one's knowledge or ability./work on; work; take care of; do business — To work on or handle a task./achieve; reach; get to — To achieve certain results./prepare; fix; make — To prepare a dining table, spleeping place, etc./relieve, do — (euphemism) To defecate or urinate./have — To have as a new family member./suffer; experiecne; gain; make — To suffer, experience or gain something./examine; see — For a doctor to examine a patient./subscribe to — To receive and read a newspaper or magazine regularly./taste; sample — To eat a small amount to distinguish a flavor./badmouth; speak ill of — To reveal and talk about somone else's shortcomings, etc./notice; recognize; see — To notice someone else's shortcomings or weaknesses./wait for; await; look for — To see if it's the right opportunity, moment or time./see; take a look at — To take a careful look at something before deciding to buy it./purchase; buy; get — To purchase something at a market./judge from — To judge based on evidence./see — To direct one's action towards something./take into account; consider — To take into account someone else's situation./depend on; rely on; count on — To desire or depend on./meet; see — To meet a person./attend; go to — To attend a service at a Christian church./think of; see; regard; consider — To evaluate or assess./try — An auxiliary verb used to indicate testing to do an action in the preceding statement./experience — An auxiliary verb used when one has already experienced an action in the preceding statement./boda — An auxiliary verb indicating when one first does an action meaning the preceding statement and thinks of its consequence later./boda — An auxiliary verb used when one realizes a fact anew in the following statement, or becomes a state in the following statement after doing an action in the preceding statement./boda — An auxiliary verb used when one realizes a fact anew in the following statement, or becomes a state in the following statement while doing an action in the preceding statement./boda — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the act or state mentioned in the preceding statement is guessed by or is known to the speaker, though not precisely./boda — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the speaker has an intention to do the act mentioned in the preceding statement./boda — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the speaker is worried or afraid that the situation mentioned in the preceding statement may happen./boda — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the state mentioned in the preceding statement is a cause for the following statement./more — More than, when compared to something./boda — A postpositional particle that indicates the subject of a comparison when comparing different things./
