보들보들하다 보들보들하다 [bodeulbodeulhada] /very soft — Very smooth to the touch./
보듬다 보듬다 [bodeumda] /hug tightly — To hug someone tightly so that the chests of two people meet./
보따리 보따리 [bottari] /bottari — cloth-wrapped package; pack; bundle; package: A box wrapped in a piece of cloth./bunch — (figurative) The idea, thought, story, etc., that one has in one's mind./bottari — wrapping: The unit of counting groups of things wrapped in pieces of cloth./
보따리(를) 싸다 보따리(를) 싸다 [bottari(reul) ssada] /pack a bottari, a bundle — To completely quit one's task or job./
보따리장수 보따리장수 [bottarijangsu] /bottarijangsu — peddler; packman: A person who travels around selling goods without owning a stationary store./job hopper — (figurative) A person who keeps changing his/her job without being able to settle in one place./
