보선 보선 [boseon] /by-election — An abbreviated word for by-election./
보송보송 보송보송 [bosongbosong] /in a dry and soft state — In the state of being smooth and having dried well without moisture./softly — In a state in which one's skin or face is fair and smooth./in small beads — In a state in which sweat is excreted in small amounts, here and there./fuzzily — In a state in which very small, soft tufts of hair or the like have grown on something./
보송보송하다 보송보송하다 [bosongbosonghada] /dry and soft — Smooth and well-dried without moisture./soft — One's skin or face being fair and smooth./fuzzy — Having very small, soft hairs or the like grown on something./
보수 보수 [bosu] /conservation — The attitude of sticking to traditional systems or methods and being reluctant to accept new ones eagerly./reward; repay — The act of rewarding someone for doing something for which one is grateful, or such a reward./pay; reward; compensation — Money or things that a person gets in return for his/her work or effort./repair — The act of fixing old or broken parts of a building or facility./
보수 공사 보수 공사 [bosu gongsa] /repair work; maintenance work — A construction method used to mend an old or broken building or facility./
