보신각 보신각 [bosingag] /Bosingak Pavilion — A bell pavilion in Seoul built to hang Bosingakjong Bell; every year on December 31st at midnight, Bosingakjong Bell is rung 33 times to bring in the New year./
보신탕 보신탕 [bosintang] /bosintang — A soup boiled with dog meat as the primary ingredient, made to invigorate a weak person./
보쌈 보쌈 [bossam] /bossam; napa wraps with pork — A dish made by boiling the head of a cow, pig, etc., of which the bones have been picked out, and then wrapping the boiled beef or pork in thin cloth, hardening the wrapped meat by pressing it under a heavy object, and then slicing the hardened meat./bossam — A dish of thin-sliced boiled pork eaten with the tender inner leaves of kimchi cabbages, bossamkimchi, wrapped kimchi, etc./
