부르다 부르다 [bureuda] /call for; call out for; gesture — To ask someone to come or draw his/her attention through words or actions./call out; check; do — To check by reading aloud names or a list of names./say; read; dictate — To say something to be recorded or repeated by another./sing — To sing to a tune./quote — To quote a price or value./chant; shout; say — To say out loud a slogan or cheer./cause; bring about; lead to; result in — For actions or words to bring about a relevant result./call; beckon — To cause someone to act for a cause./call in; summon; fetch — To ask for someone to come./call; name; refer to; address — To call or name someone something./full — Feeling one's stomach is stuffed after eating food./(belly) big — Having a large belly due to pregnancy./bulging; bellied — An object bulging in the middle./
부르르 부르르 [bureureu] /tremblingly; shiveringly — A word describing the motion of shivering with large, light movements./at a simmer — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of a large amount of liquid boiling lightly./with a sudden rage — In the manner of suddenly getting angry./
부르릉 부르릉 [bureureung] /with a cough — A word imitating the sound made when a car, motorcycle, etc., starts./
부르릉거리다 부르릉거리다 [bureureunggeorida] /roar; make a vroom sound — The sound made when a car, motorcycle, etc., starts to move; or to make such a sound./
부르릉대다 부르릉대다 [bureureungdaeda] /roar; make a vroom sound — The sound made when a car, motorcycle, etc., starts to continue; or to make such a sound./
