부르쥐다 부르쥐다 [bureujwida] /double up one's fists — To clench one's fists./clutch; grip — To hold something tightly./
부르짖다 부르짖다 [bureujijda] /shout; yell; cry out — To scream out or say loudly in excitement./cry for; advocate — To give an opinion or argue ardently./
부르트다 부르트다 [bureuteuda] /blister — To have a bleb that is filled with fluid./chap — For one's skin to peel off or crack due to dryness or cold./swell — For one's skin to puff up as a result of being bitten by an insect or bug./
