빈민 빈민 [binmin] /poor people; the poor; the needy — A population that is poor./
빈민가 빈민가 [binminga] /poor community; slum — A neighborhood populated by poor people./
빈민층 빈민층 [binmincheung] /poor people; the poor; the needy — A class of people living in poverty./
빈발하다 빈발하다 [binbalhada] /occur frequently; often happen — For certain incidents or phenomena to happen frequently./
빈방 빈방 [binbang] /vacant room; empty room — An empty room that is not lived in./empty room — A room without anyone in it./
빈번하다 빈번하다 [binbeonhada] /frequent — The number of certain incidents, phenomena, etc., being high./
빈번히 빈번히 [binbeonhi] /frequently — In a high number of occurrences of certain incidents, phenomena, etc./
빈부 빈부 [binbu] /rich and poor; wealth and poverty — A collective term for being rich and poor./
