빈정빈정하다 빈정빈정하다 [binjeongbinjeonghada] /tease; banter — To sneer at, be sarcastic about, or make fun of someone./
빈주먹 빈주먹 [binjumeog] /hand; empty fist; nothing — A fist with nothing in it./scratch; nothing — (figurative) The state of lacking something that is really needed to get the job done./
빈주먹만 들다 빈주먹만 들다 [binjumeogman deulda] /carry empty fists — To start working without anything./
빈집 빈집 [binjib] /vacant home — A vacant house where no one lives./empty house — A house currently empty as all its dwellers are outside./
빈천 빈천 [bincheon] /poverty and lowliness — A collective term for being poor and lowly./
빈천하다 빈천하다 [bincheonhada] /impoverished and humble — Poor and lowly./
빈축 빈축 [binchug] /frowning; scowling; being under fire — A state of being subject to a bad reputation or hatred./
빈칸 빈칸 [binkan] /empty column — An empty column on the page of a book, etc./empty part — An empty part not filled in./
빈털터리 빈털터리 [binteolteori] /being penniless; being broke; person without money — A person who loses all of his/her wealth and has nothing left./
빈틈 빈틈 [binteum] /crack; gap — The vacant space between two objects that are apart./loophole — An incomplete or weak point./
빈틈없다 빈틈없다 [binteumeobsda] /not missing — Not missing something or not having a vacant part./be perfect — Having no incomplete or weak point./
빈틈없이 빈틈없이 [binteumeobsi] /without a missing part — Without missing something or without having a vacant part./perfectly — Without an incomplete or weak point./
