빌려주다 빌려주다 [bilryeojuda] /lend — To lend goods, money, etc., to someone for a certain period of time on the condition of taking them back or receiving a price later./lend — To lend a venue or facility for a certain period of time./
빌리다 빌리다 [bilrida] /borrow; rent — To borrow goods, money, etc., from someone for a certain period of time on the condition of returning them or paying a price later./get — To receive help from a person, object, etc./take; quote — To use a certain form, theory, or someone's writing or speaking./use an opportunity — To take advantage of an opportunity to do something./
빌미 빌미 [bilmi] /reason; cause — A reason or cause behind an unfortunate event or someone's falling into a bad situation./excuse; pretext — An excuse for doing something./
빌붙다 빌붙다 [bilbutda] /sponge off; mooch off — To rely on someone to get power, money, etc./
빌빌 빌빌 [bilbil] /slowly — A word describing one moving slowly with little energy./lazily — A word describing one not doing anything and strolling here and there./
빌빌거리다 빌빌거리다 [bilbilgeorida] /move slowly — To keep moving slowly with little energy./fool around; idle away — To not do anything and stroll here and there continuously./
