빠개지다 빠개지다 [ppagaejida] /be cleaved; be chopped — For a hard thing to split and have a crack or be divided into pieces./
빠끔 빠끔 [ppakkeum] /deeply; clearly — A word describing a small hole, crack, etc., being deep and noticeable./slightly — A word describing a door, etc., opening slightly without a sound./through an opening — A word describing something being seen a little, through a small crack or hole./with puffs — A word describing one smoking a cigarette by opening and closing his/her mouth./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing a fish, etc., drinking water or breathing in air, by opening and closing its mouth./
빠끔빠끔 빠끔빠끔 [ppakkeumppakkeum] /with puffs — A word describing one smoking a cigarette by repeatedly opening and closing his/her mouth./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing a fish, etc., drinking water or breathing in air, by repeatedly opening and closing its mouth./
빠끔하다 빠끔하다 [ppakkeumhada] /deep; clear — A small hole, crack, etc., being deep and noticeable./slight — A door, etc., opening slightly without a sound./
빠끔히 빠끔히 [ppakkeumhi] /deeply; clearly — A word describing a small hole, crack, etc., being deep and noticeable./slightly — A word describing a door, etc., opening slightly without a sound./through an opening — A word describing something being seen a little, through a small crack or hole./
