뻐끔하다 뻐끔하다 [ppeokkeumhada] /puff — To keep smoking a cigarette while letting in and out its smoke./open and close — For a fish, etc., to keep drinking water or letting in air, while opening and closing its mouth./
뻐드렁니 뻐드렁니 [ppeodeureongni] /bucktooth; protruding front teeth — A tooth that sticks out a little bit./
뻑뻑 뻑뻑 [ppeogppeog] /scrapingly; with a scratching sound — A word imitating the sound or describing the action of repeatedly and vigorously scratching or rubbing a floor or the surface of something./roughly — A word imitating the sound or describing the action of repeatedly tearing off a piece of tough paper, cloth, etc./in the manner of scrubbing — A word describing the action of rubbing something repeatedly so that it becomes glossy./close; short — In the state of having one's hair or beard cut or shaved very short./stubbornly; obstinately — In the manner of keeping insisting unreasonably./with puffs — A word imitating the sound or describing the motion of drawing on a cigarette very hard and over and over./
뻑뻑하다 뻑뻑하다 [ppeogppeoghada] /thick; stiff — Not soft due to little moisture./thick — Having too many solid ingredients in a soup compared to the amount of liquid./tight — Tight because there is no time, money, etc., to spare./stiff — Rigid and inflexible./stiff — Something being hard to be moved because it is too tight./
