뻔히 뻔히 [ppeonhi] /obviously — In the manner that the result, state, etc., of something is seen clearly./
뻗다 뻗다 [ppeodda] /stretch; extend; run — For a branch, vine, root, etc., to reach far; to make it reach far./stretch; reach; run — For a road, river, mountain range, etc., to extend in a certain direction./grow; develop — For energy, an idea, force, etc., to appear or spread./straighten; stretch — To stretch a part of the body that is bent./hold out; stretch out — To extend one's hand or arm to reach something./croak; kick the bucket — (slang) To die or be completely drained of energy and collapse./
뻗대다 뻗대다 [ppeoddaeda] /resist; hold out; hold fast to — To persistently refuse to do something./hold one's ground; not be budged — To steel one's body and withstand something./
뻗쳐오르다 뻗쳐오르다 [ppeodchyeooreuda] /soar up; go up — For a column of water, flames, etc., to rise strongly./
뻗치다 뻗치다 [ppeodchida] /stretch; extend; run — (emphasizing form) For a branch, a vine, root, etc., to reach far./stretch; reach; run — (emphasizing form) For a road, river, mountain range, etc., to extend in a certain direction./grow; develop — (emphasizing form) For energy, an idea, force, etc., to appear or spread./straighten — (emphasizing form) To stretch a part of the body that is bent./hold out; stretch out — (emphasizing form) To extend one's hand or arm to reach something./
뻗히다 뻗히다 [ppeodhida] /be straightened — For a part of the body that is bent to be stretched./
뻘겋다 뻘겋다 [ppeolgeohda] /crimson; deep red — Darkish deep red./
뻘게지다 뻘게지다 [ppeolgejida] /redden; blush; become red — To turn red./
뻘뻘 뻘뻘 [ppeolppeol] /freely; in the manner of running around — In the manner of going around very busily./profusely; drippingly — In the state of sweating a lot./
뻣뻣이 뻣뻣이 [ppeosppeosi] /stiffly — A word describing an object being stiff and hard, not soft./sternly — A word describing one having a stiff and unkind personality or attitude, instead of one pleasing to others./
뻣뻣하다 뻣뻣하다 [ppeosppeoshada] /stiff — A word describing an object being stiff and hard, not soft./sternly — Having a stiff and unkind personality or attitude, instead of one pleasing to others./
뻥 뻥 [ppeong] /boom; pop — A word imitating the sound made when a balloon, bomb, etc., explodes suddenly and loudly./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when a big hole is made, or describing the scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when a ball, etc., is kicked strongly, or describing the scene./
뻥긋하다 뻥긋하다 [ppeonggeushada] /open one's mouth to speak — To open one's mouth slightly to speak about something./open one's mouth quietly — To open one's mouth without making a sound./
뻥뻥 뻥뻥 [ppeongppeong] /boom; pop — A word imitating the sound made when a balloon, bomb, etc., explodes suddenly, repeatedly, and loudly./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when big holes are made repeatedly, or describing the scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when balls, etc., are kicked strongly and repeatedly, or describing the scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing one speak loudly with a confident attitude, although he/she is not able to achieve what is promised./
뻥튀기 뻥튀기 [ppeongtwigi] /puffed snack — A snack made by puffing rice, potato, corn, etc./exaggeration — (figurative) The act of exaggerating something./
뻥하다 뻥하다 [ppeonghada] /dumbfounded; bemused; stunned — Being in a daze as if one is out of one's mind./
