뼈(가) 빠지게 뼈(가) 빠지게 [ppyeo(ga) ppajige] /to such an extent that one's bones fall out — Enduring a physical pain for a long time./
뼈가 녹다[녹아나다] 뼈가 녹다[녹아나다] [ppyeoga nogda[noganada]] /have one's bones melt — To go through difficulties or hardships./
뼈가 휘도록 뼈가 휘도록 [ppyeoga hwidorog] /to such an extent that one's bones are bent — Enduring a physical pain for a long time./
뼈다귀 뼈다귀 [ppyeodagwi] /single bone — A single piece of bone./bones — (disparaging) Bones./
뼈대 뼈대 [ppyeodae] /build — The bones that form the structure of the human body./frame — The structure that forms the skeleton of a building etc./synopsis — The plot or gist of a story./prestige; tradition — (figurative) The quality of having a long history of being of a high status./
뼈대(가) 있다 뼈대(가) 있다 [ppyeodae(ga) issda] /have a frame — For the social position or status of one's family to have been high for generations./
뼈대가 굵어지다 뼈대가 굵어지다 [ppyeodaega gulgeojida] /One's frame becomes thick — To grow older and bigger to become almost an adult./
뼈도 못 추리다 뼈도 못 추리다 [ppyeodo mos churida] /be unable to pull one's bones together — To challenge someone beyond one's match and end up being severely beaten up or humiliated./
