뼈를 묻다 뼈를 묻다 [ppyeoreul mudda] /bury one's bones — To be committed and faithful to a group or organization for one's whole life./
뼈마디 뼈마디 [ppyeomadi] /joint — A point at which bones meet and are connected./
뼈만 남다 뼈만 남다 [ppyeoman namda] /Only the bones are left — To become too thin because one has not eaten for a long time or has been sick./
뼈만 앙상하다 뼈만 앙상하다 [ppyeoman angsanghada] /Only the bones are skinny — To become too thin because one has not eaten for a long time or has been sick./
뼈아프다 뼈아프다 [ppyeoapeuda] /painful; bitter — A feeling of regret or remorse, etc., being so strong as to be carved in one's bones in a metaphorical sense./
뼈에 사무치다 뼈에 사무치다 [ppyeoe samuchida] /pierce one's bones — For a grudge or pain to be very strong./
뼈에 새기다 뼈에 새기다 [ppyeoe saegida] /engrave on one's bones — To bear in mind not to forget./
뼈와 살로 만들다 뼈와 살로 만들다 [ppyeowa salro mandeulda] /make something part of one's bones and flesh — To make experience, thoughts or theories completely one's own./
뼈와 살이 되다 뼈와 살이 되다 [ppyeowa sali doeda] /become bones and flesh — To be helpful./
뼈저리다 뼈저리다 [ppyeojeorida] /painful; bitter — A feeling of regret or remorse, etc., being so strong as to be carved in one's bones in a metaphorical sense./
