뽑다 뽑다 [ppobda] /pull; pick; pluck — To pull at a thing stuck somewhere so as to make it come out./draw; extract — To make liquid inside something come outside./choose; select — To decide by choosing one among many./elect; select — To elect someone for a certain purpose./sing — To sing a song./withdraw — To take money out of a bank account./root out; eradicate — To make unnecessary things disappear./take out; pull — To make something inside come out in a thin, long shape./buy; get — To make food or things inside a machine like a vending machine come outside by paying money./print — To make a photo appear on photographic paper or print a document on paper./buy; get — To buy a new car, etc./dress up — To dress up nicely./
뽑아내다 뽑아내다 [ppobanaeda] /pull out; pluck out — To pull at a thing stuck or inserted somewhere so as to make it come out./choose; single out — To choose one among many according to a certain criteria./draw; extract — To take liquid inside something outside./get back; make profit — To take back as profits as much as money or funds as were invested./sing — To make a long sound or sing a song./score; gain points — To score a point in a sports game./
뽑히다 뽑히다 [ppobhida] /be pulled; be picked; be plucked — For a thing stuck somewhere to be pulled at so to come out./be drawn; be extracted — For liquid inside something to come outside./be chosen; be singled out — To be distinguished and chosen among many things./
