사각대다 사각대다 [sagagdaeda] /swish; whoosh — For the sound of rice, barley, wheat, etc., being cut to be repeatedly made./crunch — For the sound of snow falling or stepping on snow to be repeatedly made./scribble; scratch — For the sound of writing something down on paper to be repeatedly made./crunch; munch — For the sound of a cookie, pear, apple, etc.,  being chewed to be repeatedly made./rustle — For the sound of a thin, crisp object such as a reed or starched cloth, etc., being rubbed on something to be repeatedly made; or to make such a sound repeatedly./
사각사각 사각사각 [sagagsagag] /(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when rice, barley, wheat, etc., is repeatedly cut./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made repeatedly when it snows or one steps on snow./with a munching sound — A word imitating the sound made when a cookie, pear, apple, etc., is repeatedly chewed./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when such thin and crisp object as reed or starched cloth, etc., is repeatedly rubbed on something./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when one writes something down repeatedly on paper./
