사기 사기 [sagi] /morale; fighting spirit — An energetic spirit to achieve something or win./porcelain; pottery; earthenware; ceramic ware — A white and smooth tableware made by baking particles of clay, minerals, etc., or a variety of items made from such a ceramic material./swindling; fraud; deception; cheating — An act of deceiving others in the pursuit of one's own interest./
사기극 사기극 [sagigeug] /show for deceiving; scheme for swindling — (figurative) A fake plan or show to deceive others in the pursuit of one's own interest./
사기꾼 사기꾼 [sagikkun] /swindler; fraud; cheater — A person who deceives others in the pursuit of his/her own interests./
사기당하다 사기당하다 [sagidanghada] /be conned; be duped; be swindled — To be harmed materially and mentally by being deceived by someone./
