사람 사람 [saram] /human; man — A being that is capable of thinking, makes and uses languages and tools and lives by forming a society with others./person; native — A person who belongs to a region, family, organization, etc./talent; reponsible member — A being that has certain qualifications or character./personality — The personality or character of a person./dude — The word that is used to refer to or call a person that one feels close to./other; other person — The word that refers to an unspecified person other than oneself./prominent figure — An extraordinary person./people — A worker or a person hired to work on a project or assignment./person — The unit of counting the number of people./
사람 같지 않다 사람 같지 않다 [saram gatji anhda] /be not like a human — To not have a manner or character that one is expected to have as a person./
사람 나고 돈 났지 돈 나고 사람 났나 사람 나고 돈 났지 돈 나고 사람 났나 [saram nago don nassji don nago saram nassna] /It is not that money comes before a man, but that a man comes before money — A person is more valuable than money, and not vice versa./
사람 살려 사람 살려 [saram salryeo] /Please, save a man! — An expression used to ask for help in a life-threatening emergency./
사람 속은 천 길 물속이라 사람 속은 천 길 물속이라 [saram sogeun cheon gil mulsogira] /The mind of a man is a thousand fathoms — It is very difficult to know what a person has in mind./
사람 위에 사람 없고 사람 밑에 사람 없다 사람 위에 사람 없고 사람 밑에 사람 없다 [saram wie saram eobsgo saram mite saram eobsda] /No human is above a human, and no human is below a human — People are entitled to equal rights from birth./
사람 죽여 놓고 초상 치러 준다 사람 죽여 놓고 초상 치러 준다 [saram jugyeo nohgo chosang chireo junda] /kill a man and hold a funeral for him/her — To try to give someone help after having done harm to him/her by one's mistake./
사람 죽이다 사람 죽이다 [saram jugida] /kill a human — For something to give someone a hard time./kill a human — To do something unexpected and make someone embarrassed./kill a human — To fascinate someone./
사람 팔자 시간문제 사람 팔자 시간문제 [saram palja siganmunje] /The destiny of a man is a matter of time — An expression meaning no one knows what a person's future holds as his/her life can suddenly change anytime./
사람(을) 버리다 사람(을) 버리다 [saram(eul) beorida] /spoil someone's personality — To make someone become a bad person./
사람(을) 잡다 사람(을) 잡다 [saram(eul) jabda] /catch a human — To kill a person./catch a human — To give someone a hard time by severely harassing him/her./
사람(이) 되다 사람(이) 되다 [saram(i) doeda] /become a human — To become a person who has moral and personal qualities that one is expected to have as a person./
사람됨 사람됨 [saramdoem] /personality; character — A frame of mind or nature possessed by a certain individual./
사람마다 저 잘난 맛에 산다 사람마다 저 잘난 맛에 산다 [sarammada jeo jalnan mase sanda] /Every man lives on the flavor of his/her own pride — People tend to think they are the best no matter what others think./
사람은 겪어 보아야 알고 물은 건너 보아야 안다 사람은 겪어 보아야 알고 물은 건너 보아야 안다 [sarameun gyeokkeo boaya algo muleun geonneo boaya anda] /One should experience a man to know him/her better, and one should cross the water to know it better — You have to get along with someone for a long time to completely know what he/she is because appearance can sometimes be deceptive./
사람은 죽으면 이름을 남기고 범은 죽으면 가죽을 남긴다 사람은 죽으면 이름을 남기고 범은 죽으면 가죽을 남긴다 [sarameun jugeumyeon ireumeul namgigo beomeun jugeumyeon gajugeul namginda] /People leave a name when they die, and tigers leave leather when they die; He who leaves the fame of good works after him does not die — The most important thing in a person's life is to do something worthy during his/her lifetime to help the later generations to gain honor./
사람은 지내봐야 안다 사람은 지내봐야 안다 [sarameun jinaebwaya anda] /One should experience a man to know him/her better — You have to get along with someone for a long time to completely know what he/she is because appearance can sometimes be deceptive./
사람은 헌[때 묻은] 사람이 좋고 옷은 새 옷이 좋다 사람은 헌[때 묻은] 사람이 좋고 옷은 새 옷이 좋다 [sarameun heon[ttae mudeun] sarami johgo oseun sae osi johda] /Good people are those who are old[soiled], and good clothes are those that are new — When it comes to a product, a new one is good, but when it comes to a person, an old, familiar and close one is good./
사람의 마음은 하루에도 열두 번 사람의 마음은 하루에도 열두 번 [saramui maeumeun haruedo yeoldu beon] /The mind of a man changes twelve times a day — An expression meaning a person's life is very prone to change./
사람의 새끼는 서울로 보내고 마소 새끼는 시골[제주]로 보내라 사람의 새끼는 서울로 보내고 마소 새끼는 시골[제주]로 보내라 [saramui saekkineun seoulro bonaego maso saekkineun sigol[jeju]ro bonaera] /The young of a human should be sent to Seoul, and the young of horses and oxen should be sent to the rural area[Jejudo Island] — An expression to advise that young people should study in a big city to achieve success while animals should be bred in a rural area to grow fat./
사람이 굶어 죽으란 법은 없다 사람이 굶어 죽으란 법은 없다 [sarami gulmeo jugeuran beobeun eobsda] /There is no law that lets a man starve to death — People are bound to survive and eke out an existence anyway even when they are very much short of food./
사람이 세상에 나면 저 먹을 것은 가지고 나온다 사람이 세상에 나면 저 먹을 것은 가지고 나온다 [sarami sesange namyeon jeo meogeul geoseun gajigo naonda] /A man is born with what he/she will eat — People have their own ways to survive whether they have a talent or not./
사람이 죽으란 법은 없다 사람이 죽으란 법은 없다 [sarami jugeuran beobeun eobsda] /There is no law that lets a man die — People are bound to come up with a way to survive no matter how difficult their situation may be./
사람이면 다 사람인가 사람이라야 사람이지 사람이면 다 사람인가 사람이라야 사람이지 [saramimyeon da saraminga saramiraya saramiji] /A human cannot be a human even if he/she is a human, but can be a human if he/she becomes a human — A person who does not behave like a decent human being is considered the same as an animal./
사랑 사랑 [sarang] /love — The state of being sexually attracted to and having strong affection for a person./love — The attitude of sincerely caring about someone out of affection./care — The attitude of trying to help and understand others./love — The attitude of liking or enjoying something very much./love — A person that one loves and cares about dearly../guest room; reception room — A room where usually a master of a house stays and receives his guests, being detached from a main building of the house./
사랑니 사랑니 [sarangni] /wisdom tooth — A molar newly appearing at the far end of the mouth later in life./
사랑방 사랑방 [sarangbang] /sarangbang — room for men: A room separate from the main building of the house where the male owner lived and received guests./
사랑스럽다 사랑스럽다 [sarangseureobda] /lovely; adorable — So cute as to evoke a feeling of affection./
사랑은 내리사랑 사랑은 내리사랑 [sarangeun naerisarang] /Love is the elders' love for the young — A senior tends to give love to his/her junior, but not vice versa./
사랑을 속삭이다 사랑을 속삭이다 [sarangeul sogsagida] /whisper love — For lovers to have a conversation of love./whisper love — For a man and a woman to have a romantic relationship and go out with each other./
사랑의 보금자리 사랑의 보금자리 [sarangui bogeumjari] /a love nest — A new home made by lovers./
