사회악 사회악 [sahoeag] /social evil; social ill; social problem — An array of problems such as gambling, prostitution, poverty, crime, etc that stem from a social contradiction and harm all members of a society./
사회의식 사회의식 [sahoeuisig] /social consciousness — A common attitude or belief of all members in a society such as ethics, customs, ideologies, etc., that fundamentally regulate an individual's way of thinking or behavior./
사회인 사회인 [sahoein] /member of society — An individual as a member of a society./worker; civilian — A person who does not belong to a specific group such as a school, military, etc., but works freely in the general society./
사회자 사회자 [sahoeja] /host; master of ceremonies; chairperson; moderator — A person who presides over a gathering, meeting, ceremony, etc./
사회적 사회적 [sahoejeog] /being social — A state of relating to a society or having a social nature./social — Relating to a society or having a social nature./
사회주의 사회주의 [sahoejuui] /socialism — An ideology or a movement to realize a social system hoping to surpass capitalism by socializing the means of production without recognizing privately-owned property./
사회주의 국가 사회주의 국가 [sahoejuui gugga] /socialist state — A country based on the economic ideology that is against the private property system and aims at realizing an economically-equal society./
사회학 사회학 [sahoehag] /sociology; social studies — A field of study that deals with all the social phenomena, principles of an organization, etc./
사회화 사회화 [sahoehwa] /socialization — A state of one acquiring a social nature so that he/she can live as a member of a society, or such an act./communalization — An act of changing a private entity or ownership to a public entity or ownership, or such an act./
사회화되다 사회화되다 [sahoehwadoeda] /be socialized — For one to acquire a social nature so that he/she can live as a member of a society./communalize — For a private entity or ownership to be changed to a public entity or ownership./
사회화하다 사회화하다 [sahoehwahada] /socialize — For one to acquire a social nature so that he/she can live as a member of a society, or to make one have such a nature./be communalized — For a private entity or ownership to be changed to a public entity or ownership, or to change so./
사후 사후 [sahu] /time after death — The time after one's death./being after the fact; being post; being subsequent; being ex-post facto — A time after a work is done, or one finishes a work./
사후 약방문 사후 약방문 [sahu yagbangmun] /seek medicine after death; the doctor after death; After death comes a doctor; prescription after death — To come up with a belated measure against something that has already gone wrong./
사흘 사흘 [saheul] /three days — Three days./the third day — The third day of each month./
사흘이 멀다 하고 사흘이 멀다 하고 [saheuli meolda hago] /as if three days are too long — For an event to repeat at a short interval or very frequently./
삭감 삭감 [saggam] /cut; reduction; curtailment; slashing — An act of cutting and lessening./
삭감되다 삭감되다 [saggamdoeda] /be cut; be reduced; be curtailed; be slashed — To be cut and lessened./
삭감하다 삭감하다 [saggamhada] /cut; reduce; curtail; slash — To cut and lessen./
삭다 삭다 [sagda] /decay; wear thin; molder — For something to rot or become weak because it is old./become watery; become sloppy — For something thick to become washy./ferment; develop flavor — For food such as kimchi, jeotgal, salted seafood, etc., to come to taste good after undergoing fermentation./be digested; be assimilated — For food to digest./be appeased; be alleviated; melt away — For one's tension or anger to be allayed./die out; go out — For fire to be reduced to ashes or be extinguished./fade; lose vigor — For someone's face or body to lose vitality./decrease — For coughing, phlegm, etc., to stop or be relieved./
삭막하다 삭막하다 [sagmaghada] /dreary; bleak — Solitary and desolate./
삭발 삭발 [sagbal] /shaving of the head; tonsure — An act of having one's hair cut so short that it cannot be grasped, or such a hairstyle./
삭발하다 삭발하다 [sagbalhada] /shave one's head — To have one's hair cut so short that it cannot be grasped./
삭신 삭신 [sagsin] /whole body; being all over — A body's muscles and joints./
삭이다 삭이다 [sagida] /digest — To digest food./calm; soothe — To relieve stress or anger./calm; soothe — To stop or soothe one's cough, phlegm, etc./
삭제 삭제 [sagje] /deletion; removal; elimination — An act of removing or erasing./
삭제되다 삭제되다 [sagjedoeda] /be deleted; be removed; be eliminated — To be removed or erased./
삭제하다 삭제하다 [sagjehada] /delete; remove; eliminate — To remove or erase something./
삭풍 삭풍 [sagpung] /north wind in winter — A cold wind that blows in from the north in winter./
삭히다 삭히다 [saghida] /ferment — To ferment food such as kimchi, jeotgal, salted seafood, etc., to make it taste good./
삯 삯 [sags] /wage; pay — Money paid or things given in return for doing something./fare; charge; fee — Money that a person pays for using a thing or facility./
산 산 [san] /mountain — A landmass that rises much higher than flat ground and usually contains trees, grass, rocks, etc./acid — A substance that produces a hydrogen ion when dissolved in water, and is neutralized when combined with a base./
산 (사람) 입에 거미줄 치랴 산 (사람) 입에 거미줄 치랴 [san (saram) ibe geomijul chirya] /A living (person's) mouth would not be cobwebbed ; Everyday brings its bread with it — People are bound to survive and eke out an existence anyway even when they are very much short of money and food./
산 넘어 산이다 산 넘어 산이다 [san neomeo sanida] /One climbs over a hill only to face yet another hill; from smoke into smother; out of the frying pan into the fire — For difficulties to linger and become more serious as time goes by./
