산란기 산란기 [sanrangi] /spawning season; breeding season — A season of producing eggs./
산란하다 산란하다 [sanranhada] /spawn; lay eggs — To produce eggs./disarranged — Confused because things are in disorder./upset; restless — Mentally distraught and unsettled./
산림 산림 [sanrim] /forest — A collective term for mountain and woods, or the woods in the mountain./
산마루 산마루 [sanmaru] /ridge; top of hill; top of mountain — The highest spot in a chain of mountains or hills./
산만하다 산만하다 [sanmanhada] /distracted — One's mind or attitude being disoriented due to lack of order and consistency./
산맥 산맥 [sanmaeg] /mountain range; mountain belt — A series of mountains or hills connected together in a line./
산모 산모 [sanmo] /woman after childbirth; mother — A woman who has recently given birth to a baby./
산문 산문 [sanmun] /prose — A writing such as a novel, an essay, etc., which is created without following a fixed rule like the number of words or metrical format./
산문가 산문가 [sanmunga] /prose writer; prosaist — A person who writes prose well./
산문시 산문시 [sanmunsi] /prose poem — A proselike poem written without a division of lines or fixed metrical format./
산물 산물 [sanmul] /product — A thing produced in a certain place./fruit — (figurative) A thing or phenomenon created by something./
산발하다 산발하다 [sanbalhada] /have messy hair — To wear one's hair uncombed and messy./
