산세 산세 [sanse] /terrain of mountain; features of mountain — The physical feature of a mountain./
산소 산소 [sanso] /grave; tomb — (polite form) A person's tomb./graveyard; burial ground — A place with a grave./oxygen — A substance contained profusely in the air, which is indispensible to man for breathing./
산소통 산소통 [sansotong] /oxygen tank; oxygen cylinder — A container that holds compressed oxygen./
산속 산속 [sansog] /heart of mountain; being deep in a mountain — A place deep inside a mountain./
산송장 산송장 [sansongjang] /living corpse — A person who is alive but as good as dead./
산수 산수 [sansu] /mountains and waters; landscape; scenery — A natural landscape with mountains and waters./
산수화 산수화 [sansuhwa] /sansuhwa — landscape painting: A type of oriental painting that depicts a beautiful natural scene./
산술 산술 [sansul] /arithmetic; calculation — A way of simple numerical calculation that can be used in everyday life./
산술적 산술적 [sansuljeog] /being arithmetical — A numerical representation by means of simple calculation of figures./arithmetical — Expressing something numerically by means of simple calculation of figures./
