살 살 [sal] /flesh; weight — The tender part of the human or animal body that covers the bones./meat — The tender part contained inside the shell of a crab, a clam, etc./flesh — The part other than the seed under the skin of a fruit or plant./skin — The outer surface of human or animal flesh./meat — The part other than the fat, tendons, bones, etc., of an animal or fish./rib; stretcher; spoke — One of the parts that constitute the frame of a window, fan, kite, wheel, etc./sal — A pattern on tteok, rice cake, which has been printed by putting the rice cake into a rice cake mold./beam; ray; flow — The strong energy of the sun, sunshine, fire, flowing water, etc./line — A line of wrinkles or creases./tooth — One of the fine parts that project from the shaft of a comb./fishing weir; fishgarth — A barrier for catching fish, which is made by installing a wooden fence across a river and then hanging a net in the middle of it./arrow — A thin, long, and sharp stick that is put on the bow string and pulled back and that, upon release, travels a great distance./years old — A bound noun that serves as a unit for counting years of age./
