설 설 [seol] /Seol — One of the national holidays in Korea; on the first day of the year by the lunar calendar, families and relatives gather to hold an ancestral ritual called charye and the young perform sebae, a traditional Korean bow, to their elders; people have tteokguk, sliced rice cake soup, and enjoy folk games such as yunnori, a traditional Korean family board game, as well as neolttwigi, riding a standing see-saw, and yeonnalligi, kiteflying./Seol — A generic term referring to both the Lunar New Year and the Solar New Year./theory; view; opinion — A view or theory./rumor; speculation — A story circulating among people./
