쓰이다 쓰이다 [sseuida] /be written — For some letters to be written by drawing strokes on paper with a writing instrument such as a pencil, pen, etc./be written; be composed; be put down — For one's thought, feeling, etc., to be expressed by being written on paper, etc./be written; be made — For a document of a certain form such as an application, contract, etc., to be drawn up./be written; be composed — For notes of a song that has come across one's mind to be written on a musical note./be used; be made use of — For a certain material, tool, method, etc., to be taken to do something./be employed; be hired — To receive a certain amount of money and work./be employed; be put — To be given a certain position or task and work./be spent; be consumed — For time or money to be put into doing something./be exerted; be used; be exercised — For one's energies or efforts to be put into doing something./be used; be spoken — For a certain language or certain words to be used./
쓰임새 쓰임새 [sseuimsae] /use; usage — The scope of something's usage./
쓱 쓱 [sseug] /on the quiet; by stealth; quietly — A word describing the movement of pushing something out or going into somewhere quietly and stealthily./stealthily; furtively — A word describing the movement of vanishing stealthily so that others do not know./quickly — A word describing the movement of passing quickly./lightly; deftly — A word describing the motion of rubbing or wiping something lightly./quickly and quietly — A word describing a person acting quickly and quietly./
쓱쓱 쓱쓱 [sseugsseug] /rubbing; scrubbing — A word describing the movement of rubbing or scrubbing something lightly./with ease; without trouble — In the manner of doing something easily./
