씨 씨 [ssi] /seed — The hard substance inside the fruit of a plant that will bud and grow./sperm — The source of an animal's birth and reproduction./seed — (figurative) A source from which something can grow in the future./lineage — (disparaging) The bloodline of a family./seed — A word referring to the seed of a plant or animal./Mr.; Ms.; Mrs. — A bound noun used to address or call out to a certain person deferentially./
씨 뿌린 자는 거두어야 한다 씨 뿌린 자는 거두어야 한다 [ssi ppurin janeun geodueoya handa] /Those who have sown the seeds must harvest them — You should take responsibility for the result of your action./
