아 아 [a] /a — The name of the vowel &quot;ㅏ&quot; in the Korean alphabet./oh; ah — An exclamation uttered when the speaker expresses his/her surprise, embarrassment, impatience, or urgency./oh; wow; ah — An exclamation uttered when the speaker expresses his/her delight or excitement./oh; aww; oh no — An exclamation uttered when the speaker expresses the feelings of worry, anxiety, regret, or lamentation./umm; ahem — An exclamation uttered before the speaker begins his/her words when he/she talks to someone or attracts someone's attention./oh; aha; oh yeah — An exclamation uttered when the speaker realizes something he/she did not know./a — A postpositional particle used to address a friend, younger person, animal, etc./
