아귀다툼 아귀다툼 [agwidatum] /argument; quarrel — The act of two or more people blaming and fighting with one another, to fulfill their own desire./
아기 아기 [agi] /baby — An infant that feeds on breast milk./baby; honey — (tender) A young daughter or daughter-in-law./baby — (endearing) An animal's little baby, or young plant./
아기자기하다 아기자기하다 [agijagihada] /harmonious; picturesque — Small things being in exquisite harmony and looking lovely./interesting; happy; pleasant — Having pleasure derived from small things./
아까 아까 [akka] /a moment ago — A little while ago./a little while ago; a moment ago — A minute ago./
아까워하다 아까워하다 [akkawohada] /grudge — To be not generous with something./
아깝다 아깝다 [akkabda] /regrettable — A little sad because one has lost something valuable./precious; valuable — Not wanting to give up something or give it to someone because it is important./regrettable — Deplorable because something is not fully used./
아끼다 아끼다 [akkida] /save; cut back on — To handle and use something cautiously instead of using it recklessly because one recognizes its value./love; value — To take care of and value someone or something./
아끼다 똥 된다 아끼다 똥 된다 [akkida ttong doenda] /If you save something too much, it will become dung — If you save something too much, you will lose it or it will become useless./
