아뇨 아뇨 [anyo] /no; no sir; no ma'am — An exclamation uttered when the speaker gives a negative answer to a question asked by his/her elder or superior./
아늑하다 아늑하다 [aneughada] /cozy; snug — Feeling comfortable and peaceful as if one is covered by something warmly and softly./cozy; snug — Having a warm and comfortable atmosphere./
아는 것이 병[탈] 아는 것이 병[탈] [aneun geosi byeong[tal]] /Knowing too much is a disease; Where ignorance is bliss, it is folly to be wise; Ignorance is the peace of life — An expression meaning inaccurate or unclear knowledge can become a cause for concern./Knowing too much is a disease; Where ignorance is bliss, it is folly to be wise; Ignorance is the peace of life — An expression used to describe a situation where one feels at ease if one knows nothing about something, but worries if one knows about it./
아는 길도 물어 가랬다 아는 길도 물어 가랬다 [aneun gildo muleo garaessda] /You should ask the way even if you already know how to get to your destination; Make assurance doubly sure; Better ask the way than go astray — An expression used to advise that one should double check even something that one knows well in order to avoid making mistakes./
아는 놈 당하지 못한다 아는 놈 당하지 못한다 [aneun nom danghaji moshanda] /You can never defeat someone who knows more than you do — It is hard to win against someone who has full knowledge and understanding of something./
아니 아니 [ani] /not — Used to express negation or denial./even — Used to emphasize a fact./no; nope; no way — An exclamation uttered when the speaker gives a negative answer to the question asked by his/her junior or someone of a similar age or position./what; no way; oh no — An exclamation uttered when the speaker is surprised, impressed, has doubts, or feels that something is strange./
아니 땐 굴뚝에 연기 날까 아니 땐 굴뚝에 연기 날까 [ani ttaen gulttuge yeongi nalkka] /No chimney discharges smoke without fire; Where there is smoke, there is fire; There is no smoke without fire — An expression meaning there is no effect without a cause./No chimney discharges smoke without fire; Where there is smoke, there is fire; There is no smoke without fire — An expression meaning there is no rumor without some grounds./
아니꼽다 아니꼽다 [anikkobda] /disgusting; sickening; distasteful — Unpleased because someone's words or behavior are irritating./
