아니다 아니다 [anida] /not — Used to negate a fact or statement./not — Used to express a wonder or guess and strongly affirm a fact or statement at the same time./
아니야 아니야 [aniya] /no; no way; absolutely not — An exclamation uttered when answering negatively in an emphatic and resolute manner./
아니요 아니요 [aniyo] /no; no sir; no ma'am — An exclamation uttered when the speaker gives a negative answer to the question of his/her elder or superior./
아니하다 아니하다 [anihada] /anihada — An auxiliary verb used to negate the act depicted by a preceding verb./anihada — An auxiliary adjective used to negate the state depicted by a preceding adjective./
아닌 게 아니라 아닌 게 아니라 [anin ge anira] /really — An expression meaning that a fact has turned out to be true./
아닌 말로 아닌 말로 [anin malro] /It is nonsensical to say so, but — Although it may be too extreme to say so./
