어필하다 어필하다 [eopilhada] /attract; allure — To attract someone by rousing his/her interest or giving off one's charm./complain; appeal — To remonstrate with the referee rather than accepting his/her judgment in a sports game./
어학 어학 [eohag] /linguistics — An academic field that studies languages./studying foreign languages — The act of learning a foreign language, or speaking or writing in a foreign language./
어학연수 어학연수 [eohagyeonsu] /going to another country for a language course; attending overseas language program — An act of learning a foreign language and culture by going to a country that speaks the language./
어학원 어학원 [eohagwon] /language school; language institute — A private institution that teaches foreign languages./
어항 어항 [eohang] /fish bowl; fish tank — A container made of glass, used for keeping and raising fish./fishing port — A port where fishing vessels stay, preparing for going out to the sea or transporting fish caught to the land./
어허 어허 [eoheo] /oh; right — An exclamation uttered when the speaker realizes something he/she failed to think of before./no — An exclamation uttered when the speaker feels dissatisfied or uneasy./
어허허 어허허 [eoheoheo] /ha ha — A word imitating the sound of laughing in a refined, clear, and dignified manner./
어험 어험 [eoheom] /ahem — An exclamation uttered when the speaker coughs in a dignified manner./ahem — A coughing sound made intentionally by the speaker to let others sense his/her presence./
어획 어획 [eohoeg] /catch — An act of catching or digging out life in the sea or river, or the thing caught./
어획고 어획고 [eohoeggo] /catch; haul — A quantity of living things that one catches or dig out in the sea or river, or an aggregate of their value./
어획량 어획량 [eohoegryang] /catch; haul — A quantity of living things that one catches or dig out in the sea or river./
어휘 어휘 [eohwi] /vocabulary; stock of words; lexicon — The number of words used within a particular scope; or the aggregate of such words./
어휘력 어휘력 [eohwiryeog] /vocabulary; stock of words — The ability to show one's knowledge of language by using a variety of words in an appropriate manner./
어휘집 어휘집 [eohwijib] /vocabulary; wordbook — A book that contains a collection of words./
어휴 어휴 [eohyu] /argh; augh; phew; pew — An exclamation uttered when the speaker feels exhausted, stunned, or frustrated./
어흥 어흥 [eoheung] /growl — A word immitating the sound of a tiger crying./
억 억 [eog] /ah; argh; eek — An exclamation uttered when the speaker is surprised or falls suddenly./hundred million — The number that is the product of ten thousand times ten thousand./
억누르다 억누르다 [eognureuda] /suppress; control; contain — To contain oneself to stop certain feelings, psychological phenomena, etc., from occurring or appearing./suppress; oppress — To pressure someone into not acting freely./
억눌리다 억눌리다 [eognulrida] /be suppressed; be controlled; be contained — To contain oneself to stop certain feelings, psychological phenomena, etc., from occurring or appearing./be suppressed; be oppressed — To be pressured into not acting freely./
억대 억대 [eogdae] /hundreds of millions — An extremely large number of something that can be specified by hundreds of millions./
억류 억류 [eogryu] /detainment; confinement — An act of forcing someone to stay./
억류되다 억류되다 [eogryudoeda] /be detained; be confined — To be forced to stay./
억류하다 억류하다 [eogryuhada] /detain; confine — To force someone to stay./
억만 억만 [eogman] /millions of; billions of — (figurative) Countless number of./
억만장자 억만장자 [eogmanjangja] /billionaire — A person who has an incalculably enormous amount of wealth./
억새 억새 [eogsae] /eulalia; silver grass — A tall plant with long and thin leaves, which is dried and then used to cover a roof, or feed animals./
억새밭 억새밭 [eogsaebat] /field of eulalia — A field full of eulaila./
억세다 억세다 [eogseda] /strong; tenacious — One's behavior or will to make good one's resolution being firm and strong./tough; hard — A fish's bones, a plant's stem, starched cloth, etc., being very stiff and solid./brawny; sturdy — One's arms, legs, build, etc., being very big, tough, and strong./extreme; intense — The degree of something being very high or severe./tough; blunt — One's way of talking, etc., being very rough and brusque./
억수 억수 [eogsu] /heavy rain; pouring rain — Torrential rain like the pouring of water./torrents; flood; pouring — A state of being very extraordinary in quantity, extent, etc./
억압 억압 [eogab] /suppression; oppression — An act of restraining someone from acting freely by using power or authority./
억압당하다 억압당하다 [eogabdanghada] /be suppressed; be oppressed — For the free movement of someone or something to be restricted by power or authority./
억압되다 억압되다 [eogabdoeda] /be suppressed; be oppressed — For the free movement of someone or something to be restricted by power or authority./
억압적 억압적 [eogabjeog] /being suppressive; being oppressive; being repressive — A state of restraining someone from acting freely./suppressing; oppressing — Restricting the free movement of someone or something./
억압하다 억압하다 [eogabhada] /suppress; oppress — To restrict the free movement of someone or something by power or authority./
억양 억양 [eogyang] /intonation; accent — An act of changing the rise and fall of the voice, or such a change./
억울하다 억울하다 [eogulhada] /feeling mortified; feeling chagrined — Feeling distressed and frustrated because one has suffered damage although one did not do anything wrong./
억장 억장 [eogjang] /one's heart; one's mind — (slang) A person's heart or state of mind./
억제 억제 [eogje] /suppression; control; repression — The act of suppressing feelings, desires, impulses, etc., to stop them from occurring./control; restraint; suppression — The act of suppressing something to stop it from exceeding a level or limit./
억제되다 억제되다 [eogjedoeda] /be suppressed; be controlled; be repressed — For feelings, desires, impulses, etc., to be suppressed and stopped from occurring./be controlled; be restrained; be suppressed — For something to be suppressed and stopped from exceeding a level or limit./
억제책 억제책 [eogjechaeg] /deterrent — A policy for restraining and stopping something from going beyond a certain degree or limit./
억제하다 억제하다 [eogjehada] /suppress; control; repress — To suppress feelings, desires, impulses, etc., to stop them from occurring./control; restrain; suppress — To suppress something to stop it from exceeding a level or limit./
억지 억지 [eogji] /groundlessness; unnaturalness; unreasonableness — An obstinate will to push ahead with something that has a low chance of success./
억지 춘향(이) 억지 춘향(이) [eogji chunhyang(i)] /coerced Chunhyang, the heroine of Korean classical novel 'The Story of Chunhyang' — A situation where one makes something happen by force or something happens by force./
억지로 억지로 [eogjiro] /reluctantly; forcibly — In an unreasonable and forcible way that does not meet common sense or the situation./
