억지웃음 억지웃음 [eogjiuseum] /forced smile; strained smile — A smile that one forces unwillingly./
억척 억척 [eogcheog] /being unyielding; being persistent; being relentless — An attitude of doing everything very stubbornly and persistently despite any difficulties; or a person with such an attitude./
억척같이 억척같이 [eogcheoggati] /toughly; determinedly; relentlessly — In a very rough and persistent manner./
억척스럽다 억척스럽다 [eogcheogseureobda] /tough; determined; relentless — Having a very rough and persistent attitude in doing something regardless of difficulties./
억측 억측 [eogcheug] /speculation; conjecture; supposition — An act of guessing without any reason or evidence, or such a guess./
언 발에 오줌 누기 언 발에 오줌 누기 [eon bale ojum nugi] /discharge one's urine on one's frozen feet — Something whose effects are short-lived and even aggravate the situation in the long-term./
언감생심 언감생심 [eongamsaengsim] /not daring to do something; being unthinkable — An expression literally meaning one cannot dare to do something, referring to a state in which one has never thought or dreamt about doing such a thing./
