없다 없다 [eobsda] /non-existent — (for a person or thing to be) Not existent in reality./lacking — (for a fact or phenomenon to be) Not existent in reality./not materializing — (for an affair or symptom to be) Not occurring/few; little — (for something to be) Not much in quantity./poor — Poor due to lack of money, assets, etc./impossible; unable — (for something to be) Not possible./being not — (for a person, thing, phenomenon, etc. to be) Not occupying a spot or space at a certain location./being not — (for a human or animal to be) Not staying or living in a certain place./rare — Very scarce./being not — Not included within a certain scope./lacking — Not having something or not possessing a credential, ability, etc./not having — Not having a person with whom one is in a certain relation./being not — (for something to be) Not occurring to someone./there being no — Unable to materialize due to a reason or a lack of possibility./lacking; disrespectful — Lacking distinction between top and bottom, left and right, higher and lower statuses, etc./
없애다 없애다 [eobsaeda] /eliminate; get rid of; eradicate — To make a certain matter, phenomenon, symptom, feeling, etc., disappear./remove; take away — To make something that has occupied a place or space, disappear./deprive; take away — To dispossess someone of his/her money, right, ability, etc./kill — To kill a person, animal, insect, etc./
없어지다 없어지다 [eobseojida] /be gone; disappear — For a certain thing, symptom, etc., to not appear anymore./be lost; be missing — For a person, object, phenomenon, etc., to not occupy or exist in a certain place or space anymore./be not valid — For a reason, possibility, etc., to be not acceptable./disappear; vanish — To leave a certain place, and thus come to be unseen./
없이 없이 [eobsi] /without — Without any matter, symptom, etc./without — In a state in which there are not much of something./without — In a poor state due to lack of money, wealth, etc./(no equivalent expression) — In a state in which something is not possible./without — In a state in which a person, object, phenomenon, etc., does not exist or occupy a certain place or space./without — In the state of not having a certain object, qualification, ability, etc./without — In a state in which one does not have anyone with whom one has a certain relationship./without — In a state in which nothing happens to someone./without — In a state in which a reason, possibility, etc., has not been found./without — Without a distinction between up and down, left and right, statuses, etc./
