올라가다 올라가다 [olragada] /go up; rise; ascend — To move from the bottom to the top, or from a lower place to a higher one./go up to the capital; go up to Seoul — To go to the capital city from a provincial area./advance — To move one's position to a higher organization or department./go northward; go up — To go from the south to the north./go ashore; go on shore — To move from water to land./go to heaven — (figurative) To die./be submitted; be sent — For the document, etc., of a sub-organization to be submitted to an upper organization./go up — To keep going from a certain point to a place that looks rather high./go back; trace back — To go toward a source by going back to the past./be promoted; be raised — For one's rank, position, etc., to become higher./improve — For quality, a level, etc., to become higher./go up; rise; soar — For a numerical value such as temperature, prices, etc., to increase or become higher./go up; go upstream — To go against the current of water./increase — For force, energy, passion, etc., to increase gradually./be built; rise — For a building, etc., to be constructed./climb; ascend — To go toward a high place./
올라붙다 올라붙다 [olrabutda] /be on — To get closer to a high place./gain weight — To put on weight./
올라서다 올라서다 [olraseoda] /stand on — To climb to a high place and stand on it./elevate — To rise to a high position or level./
올라앉다 올라앉다 [olraanjda] /sit on — To go to a higher place and sit on it./move up to; occupy — To get a promotion and thus occupy a higher position./be positioned in a higher place — For something to be put in a higher place./
올라오다 올라오다 [olraoda] /come up; rise; ascend — To move from a lower place to a higher one./come up — To come toward a higher place against the water current./come to the capital; come to Seoul — To come to a central city like Seoul  from a provincial area; to come to the central department from a department in a provincial area./advance to — To move from a lower grade to a higher one in a school year, position, etc./advance to — To make it to a certain ranking./go ashore; go on shore — To move from water to land./come up — To move from the bottom toward the top./be put — For food, etc., to be set on the table./be submitted; be sent — For a document, etc., of a sub-organization to be submitted to a higher-level organization./be uploaded — For content to be posted on a computer network, electronic bulletin board, etc./throw up — For something that one ate to come out through one's throat./well up — For something deep in one's mind to come out./come up — To come toward a high place./
올라타다 올라타다 [olratada] /get on — To get on a vehicle./climb — To climb on top of something./
올려놓다 올려놓다 [olryeonohda] /put something on — To place something on something./put; write — To fill in something on something./put someone or something on — To make one's rank, social status, grade, etc., improve./improve — To make a certain state or condition become better./increase — To make a price become higher./
올려다보다 올려다보다 [olryeodaboda] /look up — To lift one's head and look upwards./respect — To serve someone with respect./
