응모되다 응모되다 [eungmodoeda] /be applied for — To sign up for a contest, etc./
응모자 응모자 [eungmoja] /applicant — A person who has signed up for a contest, etc./
응모작 응모작 [eungmojag] /entry — A work that has been submitted to a contest, etc./
응모하다 응모하다 [eungmohada] /apply for; enter — To participate in a recruitment, invitation, contest, etc./
응보 응보 [eungbo] /retribution; nemesis — In Buddhism, the pleasure and agony that are the result of good and evil deeds./
응분 응분 [eungbun] /being due; being appropriate — The state of being suitable for one's position or level./
응석 응석 [eungseog] /playing on another's affection — An act of a pestering and misbehaving of a child who was raised by grown-ups who has pampered the child./
응석꾸러기 응석꾸러기 [eungseogkkureogi] /pampered child; spoiled child — A pestering, ill-mannered child raised by grown-ups who have pampered the child./
응석받이 응석받이 [eungseogbadi] /pampering a child — An act of tolerating a pestering, ill-mannered child and accepting all his/her demands./pampered child; spoiled child — An ill-mannered child raised by grown-ups who have pampered the child./
응수 응수 [eungsu] /response — An act of dealing with the remark or behavior of someone./
응수하다 응수하다 [eungsuhada] /respond — To deal with the remark or behavior of someone./
응시 응시 [eungsi] /staring — An act of focusing on one spot and continuously watching it attentively./application — An act of applying for a test./
응시자 응시자 [eungsija] /applicant — A person who applies for a test./
응시하다 응시하다 [eungsihada] /stare — To focus on one spot and keep watching it attentively./apply for a test — To apply for a test./
응애 응애 [eungae] /with a cry — A sound imitating a baby's cry./
응애응애 응애응애 [eungaeeungae] /with a cry — A sound imitating a baby's continued cry./
응어리 응어리 [eungeori] /muscle knot; lump — A muscle that has knotted hard./bitterness; ill feeling — An unresolved bad feeling that remains in one's mind./(no equivalent expression) — Something that is deeply embedded in something./core — A part of a fruit where there is or are a stone or seeds./clot — A sticky lump formed as liquid has coagulated./
응어리지다 응어리지다 [eungeorijida] /have an unpleasant feeling; have an ill feeling — For an unresolved bad feeling to remain like a lump in one's mind./coagulate — For liquid to become a sticky lump./
응얼거리다 응얼거리다 [eungeolgeorida] /murmur — To continuously read or sing in an indistinct voice./murmur; mumble; mutter — To continuously say something so indistinctly as to be hardly heard by others./grumble — To say one's complaints to oneself in an indistinct voice./
응얼대다 응얼대다 [eungeoldaeda] /murmur — To continuously read or sing in an indistinct voice./murmur; mumble; mutter — To continuously say something so indistinctly as to be hardly heard by others./grumble — To say one's complaints to oneself in an indistinct voice./
응얼응얼 응얼응얼 [eungeoleungeol] /murmuringly — A word describing the sound or the motion of continuously reading or singing in an indistinct voice./murmuringly; mutteringly; mumblingly — A word describing the sound or motion of continuously saying something so indistinctly as to be hardly heard by others./grumblingly; mutteringly — A word describing the sound or motion of saying one's complaints to oneself in an indistinct voice./
응얼응얼하다 응얼응얼하다 [eungeoleungeolhada] /murmur — To continuously read or sing in an indistinct voice./murmur; mumble; mutter — To continuously say something so indistinctly as to be hardly heard by others./grumble — To say one's complaints to oneself in an indistinct voice./
응용 응용 [eungyong] /application — An act of using a certain theory or knowledge appropriately for a concrete project or another field./
응용되다 응용되다 [eungyongdoeda] /be applied — For a certain theory or knowledge to be used appropriately for a concrete project or another field./
응용하다 응용하다 [eungyonghada] /apply — To use a certain theory or knowledge appropriately for a concrete project or another field./
응원 응원 [eungwon] /cheering — In a sports game, etc., an act of encouraging players by singing, clapping, etc./support — An act of encouraging or helping someone better perform, next to him/her./
응원가 응원가 [eungwonga] /fight song; cheering song — A song sung to cheer players in a sports game, etc./
응원군 응원군 [eungwongun] /reinforcements; troop support — The troops sent to help out other troops engaged in a battle./
응원단 응원단 [eungwondan] /cheering squad — In a sports game, a group of people gathering to encourage players by singing, clapping, etc./
응원석 응원석 [eungwonseog] /cheering section — The seats for supporters in a sports game./
응원전 응원전 [eungwonjeon] /pep rally; cheering — (figurative) In a sports game, an act of groups of supporters cheering enthusiastically for their teams against the other teams./
응원하다 응원하다 [eungwonhada] /cheer — In a sports game, etc., to encourage players by singing, clapping, etc./support — To encourage or help someone better perform, next to him/her./
응전 응전 [eungjeon] /reply to a battle — An act of fighting back, after being attacked or challenged by the opposite person, forces, etc./
응전하다 응전하다 [eungjeonhada] /reply to a battle — To fight back, after being attacked or challenged by the opposite person, forces, etc./
응접 응접 [eungjeob] /reception — An act of welcoming a guest, attending or serving food./
응접실 응접실 [eungjeobsil] /living room — A room for receiving and serving a guest or guests./
응집 응집 [eungjib] /cohesion; condensation — The state of scattered substances, groups, power, etc., being combined and united./
응집되다 응집되다 [eungjibdoeda] /be cohered; be condensed — For a scattered substance, group, power, etc., to be combined and united./
응집력 응집력 [eungjibryeog] /cohesiveness — The power that makes people, who belong to a certain organization or group, be united as one./
응집하다 응집하다 [eungjibhada] /cohere; condense — For scattered substances, groups, power, etc., to be combined and united, or to make this happen./
응징 응징 [eungjing] /punishment; chastisement — The act of punishing and rebuking someone so that he/she realizes and regrets his/her wrongdoing./subjugation — The act of attacking the enemy country and making it succumb by using armed force./
응징되다 응징되다 [eungjingdoeda] /be punished; be chastised — For someone to be punished and rebuked so that he/she realizes and regrets his/her wrongdoing./be subjugated — For the enemy country to be attacked and succumb./
응징하다 응징하다 [eungjinghada] /punish; chastise — To punish and rebuke someone so that he/she realizes and regrets his/her wrongdoing./subjugate — To attack the enemy country and make it succumb by using armed force./
응찰 응찰 [eungchal] /bidding — An act of participating in a bidding./
응찰하다 응찰하다 [eungchalhada] /enter a bid — To participate in a bidding./
응축 응축 [eungchug] /condensation; concentration — The process of becoming smaller by being solidified into a mass./condensation — A state in which various meanings, emotions, etc., are concentrated and converged./condensation — A process in which gas changes into liquid when the temperature goes down or pressure is applied to it./
응축되다 응축되다 [eungchugdoeda] /condense; be condensed — To become smaller by being solidified into a mass./condense — For various meanings, emotions, etc., to come to be concentrated and converged./condense — For gas to come to change into liquid when the temperature goes down or pressure is applied to it./
응축하다 응축하다 [eungchughada] /condense — To become smaller by being solidified into a mass./condense — For various meanings, emotions, etc., to be concentrated and converged./condense — For gas to change into liquid when the temperature goes down or pressure is applied to it./
응하다 응하다 [eunghada] /respond; answer; accept — To answer or respond to a question, request, demand, etc., or act on it./
응혈 응혈 [eunghyeol] /coagulation; coagulated blood — The process of blood flowing out of the body and becoming coagulated, or such coagulated blood./emotional scar — A feeling of pain, sadness, resentment, etc., that lingers in one's heart, or such a state./
응혈이 지다 응혈이 지다 [eunghyeoli jida] /have coagulated blood — To have or come to have pains deep in one's heart./
의 의 [ui] /ui — The name of the vowel 'ㅢ' in the Korean alphabet./ui — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the referent of the following word is owned by, belongs to, is related to, originates from, or is the object of what the preceding word indicates./ui — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the referent of the preceding word is the object of the act that the following word means./ui — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the referent of the preceding word limits the properties or amount of the referent of the following word or that two words are on an equal footing./ui — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the referents of the preceding word and the following one are in relation to the whole and a part./ui — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the referent of the preceding word is the object of a metaphor for the referent of the following word./ui — A postpositional particle used to modify the following word with the meaning properties of the preceding postpositional word./justice; righteousness — A righteous principle that one should follow and respect as a person./loyalty — The righteous duty and principle that should be followed in the relations between the king and his lieges./relationship; ties — A bond between two persons who are not of the same blood, which is like a blood relation./sense; meaning — The meaning of a letter or piece of writing./
의거 의거 [uigeo] /being based; being grounded — The state of being based on a certain fact, principle, etc./dependence — The state of depending on certain power./holding; standing one's ground; taking to fastness — The act of defending a certain area while screening oneself behind a mountain or a river in the area./heroic deed; patriotic deed — An act of rising and doing the right thing for justice./
의거하다 의거하다 [uigeohada] /be based; be grounded — To be based on a certain fact, principle, etc./hold; stand one's ground; take to a fastness — To defend a certain area while screening oneself behind a mountain or a river in the area./depend on; rely on — To depend on certain power./
의견 의견 [uigyeon] /opinion — A thought one has after making one's own judgment on a certain object or phenomenon./
의견서 의견서 [uigyeonseo] /statement — A document containing a certain opinion./
의결 의결 [uigyeol] /decision; resolution — An act of making a decision about something through discussion, or such a decision./
의결되다 의결되다 [uigyeoldoeda] /be decided; be resolved — For something to be decided through discussion./
의결하다 의결하다 [uigyeolhada] /decide; resolve — To make a decision about something through discussion./
의경 의경 [uigyeong] /auxiliary police — An abbreviated word for auxiliary police./
의과 의과 [uigwa] /medical course — In a university, the department studying the treatment, prevention, theory, skills, etc., of human diseases./
의관 의관 [uigwan] /attire; full dress — The attire a man wears on a formal occasion./
의구심 의구심 [uigusim] /doubt — The fear from not trusting someone./
의기 의기 [uigi] /morale — The positive and strong mind of trying to do something./righteous mind — The excellent mind that deserves to be respected./spirit — The mind a person is born with, or the state as it appears to be when viewed from the outside./
의기소침 의기소침 [uigisochim] /depression — The state of losing one's confidence and energy./
의기소침하다 의기소침하다 [uigisochimhada] /depressed — Being in the state in which one has lost one's confidence and energy./
의기양양 의기양양 [uigiyangyang] /elation; triumphant air — An expression on one's face that appears satisfied and proud, as one has achieved what one wanted to achieve./
의기양양하다 의기양양하다 [uigiyangyanghada] /elated; triumphant — Having an expression on one's face that appears satisfied and proud, as one has achieved what one wanted to achieve./
의기투합 의기투합 [uigituhab] /mutual understanding — The state in which people share an intention or wish, and cooperate to achieve it./
의기투합하다 의기투합하다 [uigituhabhada] /understand each other — For people to share an intention or wish, and cooperate to achieve it./
의논 의논 [uinon] /discussion — An act of sharing opinions about a certain topic./
의논되다 의논되다 [uinondoeda] /be discussed — For opinions to be shared about a certain topic./
의논하다 의논하다 [uinonhada] /discuss — To share opinions about a certain topic./
의당 의당 [uidang] /justly; as a matter of course; deservedly — Naturally because it is right to do so./
의도 의도 [uido] /intention; purpose; aim — One's idea or plan to do something./
의도적 의도적 [uidojeog] /being intentional; being deliberate — An act of doing something on purpose in order to make a certain plan or idea become realized./intentional; deliberate; intended — Doing something on purpose in order to make a certain plan, idea, or will be realized./
의도하다 의도하다 [uidohada] /intend; aim; design — To think or plan to do something./
의례 의례 [uirye] /formality; ceremony; courtesy — A certain manner and procedure for carrying out an event; an event carried out according to a certain manner and procedure./
의례적 의례적 [uiryejeog] /being formal — The quality of following a certain manner and procedure for carrying out an event./being perfunctory — The quality of having just form, without sincerity./formal — Following a certain manner and procedure for carrying out an event./perfunctory — Having just form, without sincerity./
의례히 의례히 [uiryehi] /habitually; customarily — As one has done from the past./
의롭다 의롭다 [uirobda] /righteous — Having the right mind for doing a right thing./
의뢰 의뢰 [uiroe] /commission; commissioning — The act of entrusting someone with something./
의뢰인 의뢰인 [uiroein] /client — A person who entrusts someone with something./
의뢰하다 의뢰하다 [uiroehada] /commission; ask; request — To entrust someone with something./
의료 의료 [uiryo] /medical care; medical service; medical treatment — The act of curing a wound or disease by using medical skills; such a job./
의료 보험 의료 보험 [uiryo boheom] /medical insurance — Social insurance that helps a person receive medical treatment or save medical costs when he/she is hurt or sick./
의료계 의료계 [uiryogye] /medical world; medical circles — A field of activity in which people cure wounds or diseases by using medical skills./
의료기 의료기 [uiryogi] /medical instrument; medical appliance — An instrument used for curing an injury or disease./
의료비 의료비 [uiryobi] /medical expenses; medical bill — Money spent in curing an injury or disease./
의료인 의료인 [uiryoin] /health care provider; healthcare worker — A person whose job it is to cure diseases./
의료진 의료진 [uiryojin] /medical team — A group of people who professionally treat injured or sick people./
의류 의류 [uiryu] /clothes; clothing; garments — All kinds of clothes, including T-shirts, shirts, pants, etc./
의리 의리 [uiri] /justice; righteousness — A principle that one should follow as a moral person./loyalty; fidelity — A moral, righteous principle that one should follow in a relationship with a person./brotherhood; ties — A bond which is like a blood relation between two persons who are not of the same blood./
의무 의무 [uimu] /duty; responsibility; obligation — Something that one should do as a matter of course./duty; obligation — Something that one is required to do mandatorily by law./
의무 경찰 의무 경찰 [uimu gyeongchal] /auxiliary police — The job of assisting the police to fulfill one's duty of national defense, instead of serving in the military; a person who does such a job./
의무 교육 의무 교육 [uimu gyoyug] /compulsory education — A common education that one should have compulsorily when one reaches a certain age according to the state law./
의무감 의무감 [uimugam] /sense of duty; sense of obligation — A sense that one ought to do something given to one./
의무실 의무실 [uimusil] /infirmary — A facility installed in the military in order to cure emergency patients or slightly wounded people./
의무적 의무적 [uimujeog] /being mandatory; being obligatory; being compulsory — The quality of having to be done as a matter of duty./mandatory; obligatory; compulsory — Having to be done as a matter of duty./
의무화 의무화 [uimuhwa] /making something mandatory; making something obligatory — The act of making something compulsory./
의무화되다 의무화되다 [uimuhwadoeda] /become mandatory; become compulsory — To come to be something that should be done./
의무화하다 의무화하다 [uimuhwahada] /make something mandatory; make something obligatory — To make something compulsory./
의문 의문 [uimun] /doubt; question — The state of being doubtful of something; a doubtful problem or truth./
의문 대명사 의문 대명사 [uimun daemyeongsa] /interrogative pronoun — A pronoun used to ask a question, such as who, what, where, etc./
의문 부호 의문 부호 [uimun buho] /question mark — The name given to the punctuation mark &quot;?&quot;, which expresses doubt or inquiry./
의문문 의문문 [uimunmun] /interrogative sentence — A sentence made in order to ask the listener a question and receive an answer to it./
의문사 의문사 [uimunsa] /interrogative — A word indicating the subject of the question in an interrogative sentence./
의문스럽다 의문스럽다 [uimunseureobda] /questionable; doubtful; dubious — Uncertain or having something that cannot be trusted./
의문시되다 의문시되다 [uimunsidoeda] /come into question; be questionable; be doubted — To be considered to have a part that one cannot understand completely or trust./
의문시하다 의문시하다 [uimunsihada] /have doubts about; doubt — To consider something to have a part that one cannot understand completely or trust./
의문점 의문점 [uimunjeom] /doubtful point; doubt; question — A part that one cannot understand completely or trust./
의문형 의문형 [uimunhyeong] /interrogative mood — A conjugational form of a predicate or predicative particle '이다' (be) used when asking someone about something./
의뭉 의뭉 [uimung] /being double-faced; being sly; being double-hearted — The quality of pretending to be foolish and ignorant, but actually being not so./
의뭉스럽다 의뭉스럽다 [uimungseureobda] /double-faced; sly; double-hearted — Pretending to be foolish and ignorant, but actually being not so./
의뭉하다 의뭉하다 [uimunghada] /double-faced; sly; double-hearted — Pretending to be foolish and ignorant, but actually being not so./
의미 의미 [uimi] /meaning; sense — What a word, sentence, sign, etc., means./implication — The true meaning hidden in a certain matter, action, phenomenon, etc./significance; meaning — The value or importance that a certain matter, action, phenomenon, etc., has./
의미론 의미론 [uimiron] /semantics — A field of study in logic that studies the relations of signs and their referents./semantics — A field of study in linguistics that studies the meaning of language./
의미심장하다 의미심장하다 [uimisimjanghada] /meaningful; significant; full of meaning — Having a profound meaning./
의미하다 의미하다 [uimihada] /mean; signify; imply — For a word, sentence, sign, etc., to mean something./imply; stand for — For a certain matter, action, phenomenon, etc., to mean something./
의병 의병 [uibyeong] /loyal army; loyal soldier — An army that the people of a country organizes of their own accord in order to repel a foreign enemy; a soldier of such an army./
의복 의복 [uibog] /clothes; garment — An item that one wears to cover his/her body, protect himself/herself from cold, heat, etc., and look fashionable./
의부증 의부증 [uibujeung] /delusional jealousy; delusion of infidelity — A morbid symptom that excessively doubts one's husband's conduct./
의분 의분 [uibun] /righteous indignation; righteous anger — Anger felt about an unrighteous matter./
의붓아버지 의붓아버지 [uibusabeoji] /stepfather — A man who becomes one's new father by marrying one's mother./
의붓어머니 의붓어머니 [uibuseomeoni] /stepmother — A woman who becomes one's new mother by marrying one's father./
의붓자식 의붓자식 [uibusjasig] /stepchild — A child brought by one's new spouse when one remarries./
의사 의사 [uisa] /mind; intention — One's will to do something./martyr; patriotic martyr — A righteous person who sacrificed himself/herself for his/her country and people./doctor; physician — A person with the relevant qualifications whose job it is to examine and cure patients./
의사 표시 의사 표시 [uisa pyosi] /declaration of intent — A contract, will, etc., which expresses one's intent so that it has legal effects./expression of one's intention — The act of expressing one's will to do something./
의사당 의사당 [uisadang] /assembly hall — A building where the members of an assembly gather and have a meeting./
의사록 의사록 [uisarog] /minutes — A record of the process or decisions of a meeting./
의사소통 의사소통 [uisasotong] /communication — The act of interchanging one's thoughts, words, etc., with another./
의사소통하다 의사소통하다 [uisasotonghada] /communicate — To interchange one's thoughts, words, etc., with another./
의상 의상 [uisang] /clothes; garment — An item that one wears to cover one's body./costume — Clothes that an actor or actress, or dancer wears for the stage./
의생활 의생활 [uisaenghwal] /clothing habits — The act of wearing clothes or life related to clothes./
의석 의석 [uiseog] /seat — A seat prepared for a meeting./seat — A seat on which a member sits in the National Assembly or a local assembly./
의석수 의석수 [uiseogsu] /number of seats — The number of seats occupied by the members of the National Assembly or a local assembly; the number of such members./
의성어 의성어 [uiseongeo] /onomatopoeic word; onomatopoeia — A word that imitates the sound made by a person, animal, object, etc./
의술 의술 [uisul] /medical technique; art of medicine — A technique for curing a disease or injury; a technique related to medical science./
의식 의식 [uisig] /consciousness — An ability to perceive or understand something while being awake./awareness — A feeling or thought about a certain object or matter, which is created among individuals or in a group./ceremony; function — An event carried out according to a certain manner and procedure./
의식 구조 의식 구조 [uisig gujo] /way of thinking — Values or thoughts of a certain person or group; their structure./
의식 불명 의식 불명 [uisig bulmyeong] /coma — A state in which a person has lost his/her consciousness./
의식되다 의식되다 [uisigdoeda] /be felt — For a certain thing, phenomenon, etc., to be realized or felt./
의식적 의식적 [uisigjeog] /being conscious — The state of doing something intentionally as one knows or has realized it for oneself./conscious — Doing something intentionally in a state in which one knows or has realized it for oneself./
의식주 의식주 [uisigju] /food, clothing, and shelter — Clothes, food, and a house, which are the necessities of life./
의식하다 의식하다 [uisighada] /be conscious of; tend to — To pay special attention to something./be aware of — To realize or feel a certain phenomenon or something./
의식화 의식화 [uisighwa] /consciousness raising — The act of making someone have awareness about something by realizing or thinking about it./
의식화되다 의식화되다 [uisighwadoeda] /become aware of something — To come to be aware of something by realizing or thinking about it./
의식화하다 의식화하다 [uisighwahada] /raise awareness about something — To make someone aware of something by realizing or thinking about it./
의심 의심 [uisim] /doubt; distrust; mistrust — The mind of considering something to be uncertain or not believing someone or something./
의심나다 의심나다 [uisimnada] /have a doubt; doubt; be doubtful of — To come to have the mind of considering something uncertain or mistrusting it./
의심되다 의심되다 [uisimdoeda] /have a doubt; doubt; be doubtful of — To come to have the mind of considering something uncertain or mistrusting it./
의심스럽다 의심스럽다 [uisimseureobda] /doubtful; questionable; suspicious — Having some parts that are uncertain and thus incur distrust./
의심쩍다 의심쩍다 [uisimjjeogda] /doubtful; questionable; suspicious — Having some parts that are uncertain and thus incur distrust./
의심하다 의심하다 [uisimhada] /doubt; distrust; mistrust — To consider something to be uncertain or not believe someone or something./
의아 의아 [uia] /dubiosity; suspicion — The state of considering something doubtful and strange./
의아스럽다 의아스럽다 [uiaseureobda] /rather dubious; rather suspicious — Rather questionable and strange./
의아심 의아심 [uiasim] /suspicion; dubiosity; doubt — The mind of considering something doubtful and strange./
의아하다 의아하다 [uiahada] /dubious; suspicious — Questionable and strange./
의안 의안 [uian] /bill; measure; matter — An item that is to be discussed in a meeting./
의약품 의약품 [uiyagpum] /pharmaceuticals; medical supplies; medicines — Drugs that are used for curing diseases./
