이 이 [i] /louse — A blood-sucking insect with a flat body measuring 1-4 mm in length that lives on the body of a human or an animal./louse — A blood-sucking insect with a light grey body measuring 1-4 mm in length that lives on the head of a human or an animal./i — The name of the vowel 'ㅣ' in the Korean alphabet./tooth — A part in the human or animal mouth that is used to bite something or chew food./teeth — The sharp, jagged part of a tool./indented part — An indented part of a tool or machine that fits into a part of another tool or machine./person; man — A bound noun that means &quot;a person.&quot;/this — A pronoun used to indicate something near the speaker or what the speaker is thinking./this — A pronoun referring to something mentioned in the immediately preceding sentence./this — A pronoun referring to &quot;this person.&quot;/this — The word that is used to refer to a person who is close to the speaker or something that the speaker is thinking of./this — A word that is used to refer to something which was just mentioned./i — A postpositional particle referring to a subject under a certain state or situation, or the agent of an action./i — A postpositional particle referring to the subject that is to be changed, or the subject that one denies./i — A postpositional particle used to emphasize the preceding statement./two — The number that is the sum of one and one./two — Being the number two./second — Being the second number in a sequence./
