이득 이득 [ideug] /profit; gain — The act of making a profit; the profit./
이든 이든 [ideun] /ideun — A postpositional particle used when it does not matter which one is chosen./
이든지 이든지 [ideunji] /ideunji — A postpositional particle used when it does not matter which one is chosen./
이듬해 이듬해 [ideumhae] /next year; following year — The year right after something happened./
이등 이등 [ideung] /second; second class — A rank or grade that comes second among many things./
이등변 삼각형 이등변 삼각형 [ideungbyeon samgaghyeong] /isosceles triangle — A triangle that has two sides of equal length./
이등병 이등병 [ideungbyeong] /private; ordinary seaman; airman — The lowest rank in the military./
이등분 이등분 [ideungbun] /bisection — The act of dividing something into two equal parts./
이따 이따 [itta] /a little later; a short time later — After a while./
이따가 이따가 [ittaga] /a little later; a short time later — After a while./
이따금 이따금 [ittageum] /now and then; on occasion; occasionally — Once in a while./
이따위 이따위 [ittawi] /something of this kind — (disparaging) A pronoun used to indicate the subject of this sort./this kind of; like this — (disparaging) Of this sort./
이딴 이딴 [ittan] /like this — (disparaging) This kind of./
이때 이때 [ittae] /this time; this moment; this instant — Just now; the time mentioned in the very previous moment./
이때껏 이때껏 [ittaekkeos] /so far; until now — Up to this time./
이라 이라 [ira] /ira — A postpositional particle used when quoting something as it is./
이라고 이라고 [irago] /irago — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the preceding statement was a quote./irago — A postpositional particle used to indicate that one is not happy with the preceding statement./irago — A postpositional particle that indicates the cause or reason for the following content./irago — A postpositional particle meaning that everything is the same without exception./irago — A postpositional particle used when emphasizing and pointing to something./
이라고는 이라고는 [iragoneun] /-iragoneun — An expression used to mention something with emphasis on it./
이라곤 이라곤 [iragon] /iragon — An expression used when mentioning something with emphasis on it./
이라도 이라도 [irado] /irado — A postpositional particle used to indicate that it is not the best option but the most acceptable among many options./irado — A postpositional particle used when it is similar to other cases./irado — A postpositional particle used when being attached to a word that expresses time or amount, and intending to emphasize its meaning./irado — A postpositional particle used when explaining something by giving an example of a similar thing./irado — A postpositional particle that indicates the speaker's doubt or question about an unclear fact./
이라든가 이라든가 [iradeunga] /iradeun-ga — A postpositional particle used when listing things in which the choice of any one does not matter./
이라든지 이라든지 [iradeunji] /iradeunji — A postpositional particle used when giving an example of, or listing things in which the choice of any one does not matter./
이라야 이라야 [iraya] /iraya — A postpositional particle used when the thing is only possible as a precondition of something./iraya — A postpositional particle used to imply that one is speaking in such a way that one does not think something is important./
이라야만 이라야만 [irayaman] /irayaman — A postpositional particle used when the preceding statement is an essential condition for the following statement./
이란 이란 [iran] /iran — A postpositional particle used to explain or emphasize something by specially choosing it as the topic./
이랑 이랑 [irang] /ridge — A small bank or hill forming the boundary between two rice fields or patches./ridge and furrow — A ridge and furrow in the plowed field./ridge — (figurative) The state of hollow shapes and swollen ones appearing alternately./irang — A postpositional particle used to indicate that something is being compared or used as a criterion for comparison./irang — A postpositional particle that indicates the person whom one is doing something with./irang — A postpositional particle used to indicate the subject one is doing something with./irang — A postpositional particle used to connect the preceding and following nouns./
이래 이래 [irae] /irae — An abbreviated word for '이리하여' (a conjugated form of '이리하다' (do in this way))./irae — An abbreviated word for '이러하여' (a conjugated form of '이러하다' (be like this))./since — A bound noun meaning from a certain point of time in the past until now; after that./
이래도 이래도 [iraedo] /iraedo — An abbreviated word for '이러하여도.'/
이래도 한세상 저래도 한세상 이래도 한세상 저래도 한세상 [iraedo hansesang jeoraedo hansesang] /Everyone has only one lifetime whether he/she lives it this way or that — An expression meaning everyone is equally given one life regardless of whether it is wealthy or not./Everyone has only one lifetime whether he/she lives it this way or that — An expression used to advise people to live in a broad-minded and harmonious manner because everyone is equally given one life regardless of how it is lived./
