이례 이례 [irye] /unprecedented case; exceptional case — An extraordinary and unique case./
이례적 이례적 [iryejeog] /being unprecedented; being rare — Being extraordinary and unique./unprecedented; rare — Extraordinary and unique./
이론 이론 [iron] /theory — A proposition that logically generalizes certain knowledge or the reason of a certain phenomenon./theory — Ideological knowledge as opposed to practice./dissenting opinion; different opinion — A different theory or view./
이론가 이론가 [ironga] /theorist; theoretician — A person who studies theories and knows them well./theorist — A person who does not know something practically but emphasizes only related theories./
이론적 이론적 [ironjeog] /being theoretical — The quality of being based on a theory./being ideological — The quality of being just ideal, and impossible in reality./theoretical — Based on a theory./ideological; abstract — Just ideal, and impossible in reality./
이론화 이론화 [ironhwa] /theorization — The formulation of a theory by finding a law and setting a structure./
이론화되다 이론화되다 [ironhwadoeda] /be theorized — For a theory to be formulated by finding a law and setting a structure./
이론화하다 이론화하다 [ironhwahada] /theorize — To formulate a theory by finding a law and setting a structure./
이롭다 이롭다 [irobda] /beneficial; helpful — Giving help or an advantage./
