이를테면 이를테면 [ireultemyeon] /so to speak; as it were — In other words./for instance — For example./
이름 이름 [ireum] /name — A word used to refer to or address an animal, object, phenomenon, etc., to distinguish it from others./name; given name — A word used with the family name to refer to or address a specific person./name; full name — The combination of the family and given names that is used to refer to or address a specific person./name; identify — A word that is used to refer to or address a person, organization, etc., for the purpose of officially announcing an action they took./fame — The reputation that is known to the world./nickname — A word that encapsulates someone's appearance, personality, behavior, etc., used to refer to or address him/her./name; reputation; honor — The recognition of one's excellence by others and resulting honor./name — Something that one presents as an excuse or cause when he/she wants to engage in an undertaking./name — Authority or power that one depends on for support./
이름(이) 없다 이름(이) 없다 [ireum(i) eobsda] /have no name — For the name of someone or something to be not well-known to the world./
이름(이) 있다 이름(이) 있다 [ireum(i) issda] /have a name — For the name of someone or something to be well-known to the world./
이름값 이름값 [ireumgabs] /behavior that is suitable for a name — An act that is proper for one's status or reputation./
이름나다 이름나다 [ireumnada] /be famous; be well-known — For a reputation to be known to the world./
