입석 입석 [ibseog] /standing room — A space in which one has to stand as in a theater, train, etc. because no seats are available./
입선 입선 [ibseon] /being selected; being accepted; winning a prize — A state in which one's work is submitted, evaluated and then selected for a competition or an exhibition./
입선되다 입선되다 [ibseondoeda] /be selected; be accepted; win a prize — For one's work that has been submitted to a competition or an exhibition, to be evaluated and then selected./
입선작 입선작 [ibseonjag] /award-winning work; prize-winning work — A work submitted to a competition or an exhibition, which has been evaluated and then selected for a prize/
입선하다 입선하다 [ibseonhada] /be selected; be accepted; win a prize — For one's work that has been submitted to a competition or an exhibition, to be evaluated and then selected./
입성 입성 [ibseong] /entry into a castle — The act of going into a castle./entry into a fortress — The act of troops winning at war and occupying the enemy's territory./entry into a castle — (figurative) The act of going into a field as one has hoped, after a lot of efforts./
입성하다 입성하다 [ibseonghada] /enter into a castle — To go into a castle./enter into a fortress — For troops to win at war and occupy the enemy's territory./enter into a castle — (figurative) To go into a field as one has hoped, after a lot of efforts./
입소 입소 [ibso] /entrance; admission — A state of being sent or admitted to a training camp, research center, prison, etc./
입소하다 입소하다 [ibsohada] /enter; be admitted to — To be sent or admitted to a training camp, research center, prison, etc./
입속 입속 [ibsog] /inside of the mouth — A empty space from the mouth down to the throat./
입속말 입속말 [ibsogmal] /murmur; mumble — A low and instinct utterance that a person makes with his/her mouth partly closed so as to keep others from listening./
입수 입수 [ibsu] /obtaining; coming by; acquisition — A state in which something becomes one's possession, or an act of obtaining something./entry into water — The act of entering water./jumping into water to commit suicide — The act of throwing oneself into water to die./
입수되다 입수되다 [ibsudoeda] /be acquired; be obtained — For something to become one's possession./
입수하다 입수하다 [ibsuhada] /get; acquire; come by — To obtain something./enter water — To go into water./jump into water for suicide — To throw oneself into water to die./
입술 입술 [ibsul] /lips — The red and soft flesh that surrounds the opening of the mouth./
입술에 침 바른 소리 입술에 침 바른 소리 [ibsule chim bareun sori] /a remark made with one's lips moistened with saliva; lip service — Glib words without substance./
입술에 침이나 바르지 입술에 침이나 바르지 [ibsule chimina bareuji] /Why don't you moisten your lips? — An expression used to criticize a person who tells a palpable lie./
입술을 깨물다 입술을 깨물다 [ibsuleul kkaemulda] /bite one's lips — To make efforts to suppress one's feelings that surge up./bite one's lips — To be firmly determined to do something./
입술이 없으면 이가 시리다 입술이 없으면 이가 시리다 [ibsuli eobseumyeon iga sirida] /Your teeth will freeze if you do not have lips — For two things to be closely related to each other, so if one thing fails, the other one fails too./
입시 입시 [ibsi] /entrance examination — An examination that one has to take to enter a college, etc./
입시생 입시생 [ibsisaeng] /student preparing for an entrance exam — A student who is preparing for an entrance examination to be admitted to a college, etc./
입식 입식 [ibsig] /being stand-up — A way of doing something in a standing position, or any structure that requires such a position./
입신 입신 [ibsin] /being exquisite; being divine — A state in which one's art or skill is so superb as to reach the level of divine perfection./establishing oneself; rising in the world — An act of establishing one's status firmly by achieving social success./
입신양명 입신양명 [ibsinyangmyeong] /rising in the world and gaining fame — An act of rising to fame by achieving social success./
입신양명하다 입신양명하다 [ibsinyangmyeonghada] /rise in the world and gain fame — To rise to fame by achieving social success./
입신출세 입신출세 [ibsinchulse] /establishment of oneself and success in career — An act of rising in the world, being elevated to a higher position./
입신출세하다 입신출세하다 [ibsinchulsehada] /establish oneself and succeed in career — To rise in the world, being elevated to a higher position./
입실 입실 [ibsil] /entering a room; entrance — The act of entering a room in a building such as a guest room, classroom, ward, etc./hospitalization — The act of being hospitalized in a ward in the military, a prison, etc./
입심 입심 [ibsim] /eloquence — The ability to speak well and fluently./
입심(을) 겨루다 입심(을) 겨루다 [ibsim(eul) gyeoruda] /compete with each other on eloquence; have a battle of words — To have a quarrel with each other./
입씨름 입씨름 [ibssireum] /exchange of words; discussion — The act of just talking about something, instead of acting on it./bandying of words; argument; wrangle — The act of quarreling with each other./
입안 입안 [iban] /inside of the mouth — A empty space from the mouth down to the throat./plan; making a plan — Drafting a law, system, policy, etc., or the draft itself./
입안에서 뱅뱅 돌다 입안에서 뱅뱅 돌다 [ibaneseo baengbaeng dolda] /have something turn round and round inside one's mouth — To refrain from saying something that one wants to say or be unable to do it./have something turn round and round inside one's mouth — To be unable to think of a name or an appropriate expression./
입안하다 입안하다 [ibanhada] /make a plan; draw up a bill — To draft a law, system, policy, etc./
입양 입양 [ibyang] /adoption — Becoming the child of someone who is not their birth parent, or accepting someone as one's child by taking legal procedures./
입양되다 입양되다 [ibyangdoeda] /be adopted — To become the child of someone who is not his/her birth parent, by undergoing legal procedures./
입양아 입양아 [ibyanga] /adopted child — A person becoming the child of someone who is not his/her birth parent, by taking legal procedures./
입양하다 입양하다 [ibyanghada] /adopt — To accept someone as one's child by taking legal procedures./
입에 거미줄 치다 입에 거미줄 치다 [ibe geomijul chida] /spin a web in one's mouth — To starve due to lack of food./
입에 게거품을[거품을] 물다 입에 게거품을[거품을] 물다 [ibe gegeopumeul[geopumeul] mulda] /foam[froth] at one's mouth — To speak in a loud voice due to outrage and fury./
입에 달고 다니다[살다] 입에 달고 다니다[살다] [ibe dalgo danida[salda]] /get around[live] with something attached to one's mouth — To frequently use or repeat a certain word./get around[live] with something attached to one's mouth — To eat a certain food almost everyday./
입에 달라붙다 입에 달라붙다 [ibe dalrabutda] /stick to one's mouth — For food to be very delicious./
입에 담다 입에 담다 [ibe damda] /contain something in one's mouth — To speak out./
입에 대다 입에 대다 [ibe daeda] /touch something to one's mouth — To eat or drink something./
입에 맞는 떡 입에 맞는 떡 [ibe majneun tteog] /Tteok, rice cake, that satisfies one's mouth — Something that catches one's fancy./
입에 발린 소리 입에 발린 소리 [ibe balrin sori] /remarks that are plastered on one's lips; lip service — Words that do not reflect one's true feelings or intention./
입에 붙다 입에 붙다 [ibe butda] /stick to one's mouth — For something to grow into a habit as it has been repeatedly said./
입에 쓴 약이 몸에 좋다 입에 쓴 약이 몸에 좋다 [ibe sseun yagi mome johda] /Bitter medicine is good for your body — An expression meaning another person's advice or criticism may hurt for the moment, but it will eventually benefit you if you try to understand what it really means./
입에 오르내리다 입에 오르내리다 [ibe oreunaerida] /go up and down the mouths — To become the subject of others' conversations./
입에 자물쇠를 채우다 입에 자물쇠를 채우다 [ibe jamulsoereul chaeuda] /lock one's mouth — To not speak./lock someone's mouth — To prevent someone from talking about something./
입에 침이 마르다 입에 침이 마르다 [ibe chimi mareuda] /The saliva in one's mouth dries up — To talk much in order to complement someone or boast about something./
입에 풀칠하다 입에 풀칠하다 [ibe pulchilhada] /put glue on one's mouth; make ends meet; eke out a living — To live in severe poverty./
입에서 신물이 난다 입에서 신물이 난다 [ibeseo sinmuli nanda] /taste stomach acid in one's mouth — To be fed up with something./
입영 입영 [ibyeong] /joining the army; enlistment — Joining the army and becoming a soldier./
입영하다 입영하다 [ibyeonghada] /join the military; enlist — To join the military and become a soldier./
입욕 입욕 [ibyog] /taking a bath; going into a bathtub — The act of entering a tub containing water to wash one's body, or taking a bath./
입욕하다 입욕하다 [ibyoghada] /take a bath; go into a bathtub — To enter a tub containing water to wash one's body; to take a bath./
입원 입원 [ibwon] /hospitalization — Staying in a hospital for a certain period of time to have one's disease treated./
입원비 입원비 [ibwonbi] /hospital charges; hospital fees — The money charged for staying in a hospital for a certain period of time to have one's disease treated./
입원시키다 입원시키다 [ibwonsikida] /hospitalize — To make someone stay in a hospital for a certain period of time to have his/her disease treated./
입원실 입원실 [ibwonsil] /hospital room; patient's room; ward — A room where one stays in a hospital for a certain period of time to have one's disease treated./
입원하다 입원하다 [ibwonhada] /be hospitalized — To stay in a hospital for a certain period of time to have one's disease treated./
입은 비뚤어져도 말은 바로 해라[하랬다] 입은 비뚤어져도 말은 바로 해라[하랬다] [ibeun bittuleojyeodo maleun baro haera[haraessda]] /You should[are advised to] speak the right words even if you have a crooked mouth — An expression used to advise that one should be frank or tell the truth in any circumstance./
입을 딱 벌리다 입을 딱 벌리다 [ibeul ttag beolrida] /open one's mouth wide — To be very surprised or dumbfounded./
입을 봉하다 입을 봉하다 [ibeul bonghada] /seal one's mouth — To not talk./seal someone's mouth — To prevent someone from talking about something./
입의 혀 같다 입의 혀 같다 [ibui hyeo gatda] /be like a tongue in someone's mouth — To quickly catch someone's intention or preference and do as he/she pleases./
입이 (딱) 벌어지다 입이 (딱) 벌어지다 [ibi (ttag) beoleojida] /One's mouth is wide open — To be very surprised or pleased./
입이 가볍다 입이 가볍다 [ibi gabyeobda] /have a light mouth — To be talkative and frequently leak a secret./
입이 간지럽다 입이 간지럽다 [ibi ganjireobda] /feel itchy in one's mouth — To be dying to talk about something or reveal a secret./
입이 걸다 입이 걸다 [ibi geolda] /have a foul mouth — To talk in a crude and vulgar manner./
입이 귀밑까지 찢어지다 입이 귀밑까지 찢어지다 [ibi gwimitkkaji jjijeojida] /have one's mouth ripped to the roots of the ears — To laugh with one's mouth wide open for joy./
입이 달다 입이 달다 [ibi dalda] /have a sweet mouth — To have a good appetite and enjoy food./
입이 닳다 입이 닳다 [ibi dalhda] /have one's mouth worn out — To repeat the same words several times./
입이 떨어지다 입이 떨어지다 [ibi tteoleojida] /One's mouth is taken off — To start talking./
입이 마르다 입이 마르다 [ibi mareuda] /have one's mouth dry up — To repeat the same words several times./
입이 무겁다 입이 무겁다 [ibi mugeobda] /have a heavy mouth — To not talk much and keep a secret./
입이 심심하다 입이 심심하다 [ibi simsimhada] /feel bored in one's mouth — To feel like eating or saying something./
입이 싸다 입이 싸다 [ibi ssada] /have a cheap mouth — To be talkative and frequently leak a secret./
입이 쓰다 입이 쓰다 [ibi sseuda] /have a bitter mouth — To feel unpleasant because one is dissatisfied with something./have a bitter mouth — To have no appetite or be unable to enjoy food because one is tired or sick./
입이 열 개라도 할 말이 없다 입이 열 개라도 할 말이 없다 [ibi yeol gaerado hal mali eobsda] /have nothing to say even if one has ten mouths — To be unable to make any excuse because one's error was clearly revealed./
입이 짧다 입이 짧다 [ibi jjalbda] /have a short mouth — To hate or be unable to eat so many kinds of food and eat little./
입자 입자 [ibja] /particle — A tiny body that constitutes a substance./grain — A tiny body that constitutes a substance and has its own properties./
입장 입장 [ibjang] /admission; entrance — Entering the place of an event or performance./position; situation; standpoint; ground; stance — The state or situation one faces at the moment, or the attitude one takes in this position./
입장객 입장객 [ibjanggaeg] /audience; admitted person — A person who is admitted in the place where an event or performance is held./
입장권 입장권 [ibjanggwon] /admission ticket; entrance ticket — The ticket whose holder is allowed to enter the place of an event or performance./
입장단 입장단 [ibjangdan] /humming along to rhythm — Time that is beaten by making sounds with one's mouth when dancing, singing, or playing an instrument, etc./utterance in agreement — The act of uttering something to indicate that one agrees to what someone says./
입장료 입장료 [ibjangryo] /admission fee — The fee paid to enter the place of an event or performance./
입장하다 입장하다 [ibjanghada] /be admitted; enter; go in — To enter the place of an event or performance./
입주 입주 [ibju] /moving into — The act of leaving a place where one has lived, and moving into a new house or place./occupancy; tenancy — The act of an enterprise, store, facility, etc., occupying a certain area./
입주하다 입주하다 [ibjuhada] /move into — To leave a place where one has lived, and move into a new house or place./occupy; tenant — For an enterprise, store, facility, etc., to occupy a certain area./
입증 입증 [ibjeung] /giving proof; demonstration — Proving a certain fact by presenting proof./
입증되다 입증되다 [ibjeungdoeda] /be verified; be demonstrated — For a certain fact to be proved through proof./
입증하다 입증하다 [ibjeunghada] /give proof; vindicate; demonstrate — To prove a certain fact by presenting proof./
입지 입지 [ibji] /growing environment — The place or environment where a plant grows./position; standing — The base or status of an individual, group, etc., in a field./location — A place where one chooses for his/her economic activities./
입지전 입지전 [ibjijeon] /success story; biography of a self-made person — The biography of a successful person, who set a goal and made efforts to achieve it despite being in a difficult situation./
입질 입질 [ibjil] /bite; strike — The act of fish touching a bait at the end of a fishing rod ./
입질하다 입질하다 [ibjilhada] /bite; take a bait — For fish to touch a bait at the end of a fishing rod./
입찰 입찰 [ibchal] /bid; tender — An arrangement in which potential buyers and contractors submit prices they want, to buy goods or win a contract./
입천장 입천장 [ibcheonjang] /palate; roof of the mouth — The part making the ceiling of a mouth./
입체 입체 [ibche] /solid body; three-dimensional structure — An object with volume, surrounded by multiple flat and curved surfaces in three-dimensional space./
입체 도형 입체 도형 [ibche dohyeong] /solid figure; three-dimensional figure — A figure that has volume in three dimensions, such as a prism, pyramid, sphere, etc./
입체적 입체적 [ibchejeog] /cubic; three-dimensional — Giving the impression that one is seeing an object with volume in three-dimensional space./
입추 입추 [ibchu] /ipchu — One of the 24 seasonal divisions, said to be the day when fall begins; it falls on around August 8th./
입춘 입춘 [ibchun] /ipchun — One of the 24 seasonal divisions, said to be the day that spring begins; it falls on around February 4th./
입춘대길 입춘대길 [ibchundaegil] /ipchundaegil — Good Luck for Spring: The phrase posted on a wall or door on the day of the onset of spring, to bring good luck./
입출금 입출금 [ibchulgeum] /money received and paid — Money that is received and paid./deposit and withdrawal — The act of depositing money in or withdrawing it from a bank./
입하 입하 [ibha] /ipha — One of the 24 seasonal divisions, said to be the day when summer begins; it falls on around May 5th./
입학 입학 [ibhag] /admission to a school; entrance into a school — Starting to go to a school as a new student./
입학금 입학금 [ibhaggeum] /admission fee — The money paid by a student when admitted for the first time by a school./
입학률 입학률 [ibhagryul] /admission rate — The ratio between newly-admitted students and the number of applicants./
입학생 입학생 [ibhagsaeng] /new student; newly-enrolled student — A student going for the first time to school to study./
입학시키다 입학시키다 [ibhagsikida] /enroll — To make someone enter a school to study as a student./
입학시험 입학시험 [ibhagsiheom] /admission test; entrance examination — The examination taken by the applicants of a school to be selected as new students./
입학식 입학식 [ibhagsig] /entrance ceremony — The ceremony for new students who first go to a school./
입학하다 입학하다 [ibhaghada] /be enrolled at a school; enter a school — To enter a school to study as a student./
입헌 정치 입헌 정치 [ibheon jeongchi] /constitutional politics; constitutional government — Government conducted in accordance with the national constitution./
입헌주의 입헌주의 [ibheonjuui] /constitutionalism — A political idea that a nation must be managed according to its constitution, which was written based on the agreement of its people./
입회 입회 [ibhoe] /joining an organization — Becoming a new member of an organization./presence; attendance; witnessing — Being present at the site of an incident with many others and watching the scene./
입회비 입회비 [ibhoebi] /entrance fee — The money paid by a new member to join an organization./
입회인 입회인 [ibhoein] /observer; witness — A person asked or allowed to attend and observe something on site, as a potential witness./
입회하다 입회하다 [ibhoehada] /attend; witness — To be present at the site of an incident with many others and watch the scene./
입후보 입후보 [ibhubo] /running for; offering someone as a candidate for — The act of coming forward as a candidate for or putting up someone as a candidate for an election./candidate — A person who runs for an election./
입후보자 입후보자 [ibhuboja] /candidate — A person who is registered as a candidate in an election./
입후보하다 입후보하다 [ibhubohada] /run for; be a candidate for; offer someone as a candidate for — To come forward as a candidate for or put up someone as a candidate for an election./
입히다 입히다 [ibhida] /dress; clothe — To make a person or animal wear or hang clothes over his/her or its body./inflict; cause — To make a person or animal suffer a disaster or damage./coat; plate — To spread something on the surface of something else or cover something with something else./
잇다 잇다 [isda] /connect; link; join — To tie or glue two strings, cords, pieces, etc., together, or put things, etc., into contact./continue — To make something continue without being interrupted./line up — For many people or things to stand in a line./follow — To happen right after something./
잇달다 잇달다 [isdalda] /come one after another — For one thing to follow another thing./occur in succession; happen one after another — For certain incidents, actions, etc., to occur in succession./connect; link — To join one thing to another./
잇대다 잇대다 [isdaeda] /put together; attach; patch together — To make things connected, facing each other./continue; carry on — To continue without interruption./
잇따르다 잇따르다 [isttareuda] /follow — For one object to follow another./occur in succession — For one incident, act, etc., to happen after another./
잇몸 잇몸 [ismom] /gum — Hard flesh surrounding the roots of teeth./
잇새 잇새 [issae] /opening between teeth — The space between two teeth./
잇속 잇속 [issog] /shape of one´s teeth — The appearance of teeth growing in one's mouth./source of profit — The substance of something which is beneficial or profitable to oneself./
있다 있다 [issda] /be; stay — For a person or animal to remain in a certain place without leaving or getting out of it./work for; serve — To keep working for a company./keep — For a person or animal to maintain a certain state./(no equivalent expression) — For some time to pass./existent; existing — A person, an animal, an object, etc., being in existence./(no equivalent expression) — A fact or a phenomenon being existent./(no equivalent expression) — Something being planned to be realized or happen./rich; wealthy — Having enough or a lot of property./able to — Having an ability to do something./(no equivalent expression) — The possibility of something happening or something actually happening./(no equivalent expression) — A word used when emphasizing or confirming a certain object or fact./(no equivalent expression) — Something occupying a certain place or space and existing there./(no equivalent expression) — A person or animal staying or living in a certain place./(no equivalent expression) — A person working for a certain company./(no equivalent expression) — Being in a certain situation, level, stage, etc./(no equivalent expression) — A person, object, etc., being included in something./(no equivalent expression) — Having a certain object, qualification, ability, etc./(no equivalent expression) — Having a person with whom one has a certain relation./(no equivalent expression) — Something happening to someone./(no equivalent expression) — A word used when having the preceding noun as the subject of conversation or discussion./(no equivalent expression) — A person being in a certain social status or playing a certain role./(no equivalent expression) — A reason, possibility, etc., being established./itda — An auxiliary verb used to indicate the continuation of the state of the preceding statement./itda — An auxiliary verb used to indicate the continuation of the action of the preceding statement./itda — An auxiliary verb used to indicate the continuation of the result of the action of the preceding statement./
잉꼬 잉꼬 [ingkko] /parakeet — A small parrot, usually with green and yellow feathers./
잉꼬부부 잉꼬부부 [ingkkobubu] /devoted couple — (figurative) A couple loving each other, just like two parakeets do./
잉어 잉어 [ingeo] /carp — Fresh-water fish with a dark blue back, yellowish belly, large body, and whiskers near its mouth./
잉여 잉여 [ingyeo] /surplus; remainder — Something left after consumption./
잉잉 잉잉 [inging] /whimperingly — A word describing the sound or motion of a child crying with an ugly-looking, frowning face./with buzzing sounds; with humming sounds — A word imitating the sound made when an insect, etc., flies./with humming sounds — A word imitating the sound of a strong wind blowing against a thin, tight power line or string./
잉잉거리다 잉잉거리다 [inginggeorida] /whimper; pule — For a child to cry with an ugly-looking, frowning face continuously./buzz — For the sound of an insect, etc., flying to be heard continuously./hum — For the sound of a strong wind blowing against a thin, tense power line or string to be heard continuously./
잉잉대다 잉잉대다 [ingingdaeda] /whimper; pule — For a child to cry with an ugly-looking, frowning face continuously./buzz — For the sound of an insect, etc., flying to be heard continuously./hum — For the sound of a strong wind blowing against a thin, tense power line or string to be heard continuously./
잉잉하다 잉잉하다 [inginghada] /whimper; pule — For a child to cry with an ugly-looking, frowning face./buzz — For the sound of an insect, etc., flying to be heard./hum — For the sound of a strong wind blowing against a thin, tense power line or string to be heard./
잉태 잉태 [ingtae] /pregnancy; conception — The state of bearing a child or young in the womb./emergence — A process in which a certain phenomenon or fact is created and develops within something./
잉태되다 잉태되다 [ingtaedoeda] /be conceived — For a child or young to be conceived in the womb./be conceived — For a certain phenomenon or fact to be created and develop within something./
