차용되다 차용되다 [chayongdoeda] /be loaned — For money, objects, etc., to be borrowed./be borrowed — For a word, letter, expression, etc., to be appropriated from a foreign language./be adopted — For a certain form, theory, etc., to be accepted and used./
차용어 차용어 [chayongeo] /borrowed word; loan word — A word that has been naturalized after being adopted from a foreign language./
차용증 차용증 [chayongjeung] /promissory note — A document which proves that one borrowed some money or objects from another./
차용하다 차용하다 [chayonghada] /loan — To borrow money, objects, etc./borrow — To appropriate a word, letter, expression, etc., from a foreign language./adopt — To accept and use a certain form, theory, etc./
차원 차원 [chawon] /level — One's position on an object, or degree of psychological or intellectual profundity that constitutes a certain thought or opinion./dimension — In mathematics, a measure of spatial extent./
차이 차이 [chai] /difference — The state of being unlike, or the degree of the unlikeness./
차이다 차이다 [chaida] /be kicked — For something to be kicked or raised powerfully with one's foot./be kicked — For a person to be kicked powerfully by another person's foot./be dumped — (slang) For a romantic relationship of a man and a woman to be broken unilaterally by one of them./
차이점 차이점 [chaijeom] /difference — A part that is different from others./
차익 차익 [chaig] /profit; margin — A financial gain resulting from a transaction or from a change in a price or market price./
차일 차일 [chail] /sunshade — A cover that is used to block the sun./
차일피일 차일피일 [chailpiil] /(delaying) little by little — In the manner of repeatedly putting off one's promise to do something at a certain time or meet a deadline./
차입 차입 [chaib] /loan — An act of borrowing money or objects from an external source./
차입금 차입금 [chaibgeum] /loan; debt — Money borrowed from an external source./
차입하다 차입하다 [chaibhada] /borrow — To borrow money or objects from an external source./
차장 차장 [chajang] /deputy manager — A position below head manager that is responsible for a department in a public office, company , etc., or a person in such a position./conductor — A person who collects fares on trains, buses, streetcars, etc., or is in charge of matters related to passengers or the operation of the train, bus, streetcar, etc./
차전놀이 차전놀이 [chajeonnoli] /chajeonnori — juggernaut battle: A traditional Korean game played on the day of Daeboreum, First Full Moon Day, in which two teams compete to topple each other down to the ground, under the command of their leaders atop entwined logs./
차점자 차점자 [chajeomja] /runner-up — A person who gets the second highest score or number of votes just behind the highest score or standard./
차제 차제 [chaje] /opportunity — An opportunity given at the right time./
차종 차종 [chajong] /car model — The type of a car, railcar, etc./
차주 차주 [chaju] /vehicle owner — The owner of a vehicle./
차지 차지 [chaji] /possession — An act of taking an object, space, status, etc., and making it one's own, or such an object or space./
차지다 차지다 [chajida] /sticky; glutinous — A dough, rice, tteok, rice cake, etc., is sticky./meticulous — Strict and thorough in one's personality./
차지하다 차지하다 [chajihada] /possess; own — To take an object, space, status, etc., and make it one's own./take up — To occupy a certain space or percentage./
차질 차질 [chajil] /problem; setback — Something that takes longer than expected or is hard to deal with./
차차 차차 [chacha] /gradually — Little by little as time goes by in the change of the state or level of a matter or object./gradually — Little by little later on without rushing./
차창 차창 [chachang] /vehicle window — A window on a train, car, etc./
차체 차체 [chache] /vehicle body — The frame or chassis of a car, train, etc./
차출 차출 [chachul] /assignment; appointment — An act of assigning a certain task to someone./
차출되다 차출되다 [chachuldoeda] /be assigned; be appointed — For someone to be appointed and given a certain task./
차출하다 차출하다 [chachulhada] /assign; appoint — To assign a certain task to someone./
차츰 차츰 [chacheum] /gradually — Little by little as time goes by in the change of the state or level of something./
차츰차츰 차츰차츰 [chacheumchacheum] /gradually — In the manner of progressing or changing little by little./
차치하다 차치하다 [chachihada] /put something aside — To leave a matter or object aside and not think about it./
차편 차편 [chapyeon] /means of transportation — The means of transit used to carry passengers or cargo./
차표 차표 [chapyo] /bus ticket; train ticket — A ticket bought to board public transportations./
차후 차후 [chahu] /next — The time coming after the present time./
착 착 [chag] /stickily — In the manner of an object sticking to something./in a palatable way — In the manner of food being agreeable to the palate./calmly — In the manner of one's behavior or attitude being quiet and composed./droopingly — In the manner of hanging low or bending loosely./droopingly — In the manner of one's body sagging due to a lack of energy./gloomily — In the manner of an atmosphere, emotion, etc., being dark and depressed./in a low manner — In the manner of lowering one's gaze or voice./quickly without hesitation — In the manner of doing a certain act swiftly and without hesitation./
착각 착각 [chaggag] /illusion; delusion — A perception of an object or fact in a way different from what it is in reality./
착각되다 착각되다 [chaggagdoeda] /delude; mistake — For an object or fact to be perceived in a way that is different from how it really is./
착각하다 착각하다 [chaggaghada] /delude oneself; mistake — To perceive an object or fact in a way different from what it is like in reality./
착공 착공 [chaggong] /groundbreaking — The act of starting a construction project./
착공되다 착공되다 [chaggongdoeda] /(construction) be commenced — For a construction project to be started./
착공하다 착공하다 [chaggonghada] /break ground — To start a construction project./
착란 착란 [chagran] /derangement; mental unsoundness — A state of mental disturbance and disorientation./
착란하다 착란하다 [chagranhada] /deranged; mentally unsound — Being mentally disturbed and disoriented./
착륙 착륙 [chagryug] /landing — An act of an aircraft, etc., coming to land from the sky./
착륙하다 착륙하다 [chagryughada] /land; set down — For an aircraft, etc., to come down to the ground from the sky./
착복 착복 [chagbog] /embezzlement — An act of dishonestly using or taking money or property that one has been entrusted with./
착복하다 착복하다 [chagboghada] /embezzle; misappropriate — To dishonestly use or take money or property that one has been entrusted with./
착상 착상 [chagsang] /implantation — The act in which a fertilized egg attaches itself to the lining of the uterus and grows properly so that it can absorb nutrition from the mother's body./having an idea — An act of coming up with core concepts necessary to implement something or to create a work of art , or such an idea./
착상되다 착상되다 [chagsangdoeda] /(an idea) occur — For an idea for a project or creative work to come to one's mind./
착상하다 착상하다 [chagsanghada] /implant — For a fertilized egg to attach itself to the lining of the uterus and grow properly so that it can absorb nutrition from the mother's body./have an idea — To conceive an idea for a project or creative work./
착색 착색 [chagsaeg] /coloring; tinting — An act of dyeing or coloring something to give it a certain color./
착색되다 착색되다 [chagsaegdoeda] /be colored; be tinted — For something to be dyed or colored so as to take on a certain hue./
착색하다 착색하다 [chagsaeghada] /color; tint — To dye or color something to give it a certain hue./
착석 착석 [chagseog] /sit — An act of taking a seat./
착석하다 착석하다 [chagseoghada] /sit — To take a seat./
착수 착수 [chagsu] /start; commencement — An act of beginning something new./
착수금 착수금 [chagsugeum] /deposit — An initial, partial payment of a cost that one makes before starting work./
착수되다 착수되다 [chagsudoeda] /be started; be commenced — For something new to be begun./
착수하다 착수하다 [chagsuhada] /start; commence — To begin something new./
착시 착시 [chagsi] /optical illusion — The condition of perceiving something in a way different from the way it is in reality./
착실하다 착실하다 [chagsilhada] /diligent — Upright and consistent in doing something./sufficient — Adequate in level or amount without lacking./
착실히 착실히 [chagsilhi] /diligently — In the manner of being upright and consistent in doing something./sufficiently — In the manner of being adequate in level or amount without lacking./
착안 착안 [chagan] /conception; design — An act of observing something closely and forming an idea in order to achieve it./
착안되다 착안되다 [chagandoeda] /be conceived; be designed — For something to be observed closely and for an idea to be formed in order to achieve a goal./
착안하다 착안하다 [chaganhada] /conceive; design — To observe something closely and form an idea in order to achieve it./
착오 착오 [chago] /mistake; error — A state in which one gets the wrong idea or takes the wrong action due to an illusion, or such an idea or action./
착용 착용 [chagyong] /wear — An act of having clothes, shoes, etc., on one's body./
착용감 착용감 [chagyonggam] /wearing sensation; comfort of wearing — A sensation one feels when wearing clothes, shoes, etc./
착용되다 착용되다 [chagyongdoeda] /wear — To have clothes, shoes, etc., on one's body./
착용하다 착용하다 [chagyonghada] /wear — To have clothes, shoes, etc., on one's body./
착잡 착잡 [chagjab] /mixed feelings — A confused and unsettled state of the mind./
착잡하다 착잡하다 [chagjabhada] /having mixed feelings — One's thoughts being confused and unsettled./
착지 착지 [chagji] /landing; landing site — An act of coming down from the air to the ground, or such a place./landing — In sports such as gymnastics, etc., an act of finishing a jump or movement in the air and coming down to the ground, or such a movement./
착지하다 착지하다 [chagjihada] /land — To come down from the air to the ground./land — In sports such as gymnastics, etc., to finish a jump or movement in the air and come down to the ground./
착착 착착 [chagchag] /stickily — A word describing the manner of an object sticking to something./in a palatable way — A word describing the manner of food being agreeable to the palate./in a friendly manner — A word describing the manner of treating someone in a very friendly and polite way./quickly without hesitation — A word describing the manner of doing a certain act swiftly, vigorously, and without hesitation./easily — In the state of something going smoothly without any problems./steadily — In an orderly and systematic fashion./
착취 착취 [chagchwi] /exploitation; extortion — An act of forcefully taking resources, property, labor, etc., and unjustly utilizing them./
착취당하다 착취당하다 [chagchwidanghada] /have something exploited; have something extorted; have something wrung — To have resources, property, labor, etc., taken forcefully and utilized unjustly./
착취되다 착취되다 [chagchwidoeda] /be exploited; be extorted; be wrung — For resources, property, labor, etc., to be taken forcefully and utilized unjustly./
착취하다 착취하다 [chagchwihada] /exploit; extort; wring — To take resources, property, labor, etc., forcefully and utilize them unjustly./
착하다 착하다 [chaghada] /kind; generous — One's heart, behavior, etc., being honest, nice, and friendly./
찬 찬 [chan] /side dish — Food to eat with rice when having a meal./
찬가 찬가 [changa] /anthem — A piece of music or writing that glorifies or honors something beautiful or great./
찬거리 찬거리 [changeori] /groceries — Materials for making side dishes./
찬기 찬기 [changi] /chilly air; cold air — Cold air or a chill./coldness; chill — (figurative) A state in which a person is cold and unkind, or such attitude./chan-gi — dish; bowl; plate: A container, such as a plate, bowl, etc., for holding a side dish/
찬동 찬동 [chandong] /approval; support — An act of identifying oneself with a certain movement or opinion and acting on it together with others./
찬동하다 찬동하다 [chandonghada] /approve; support — To identify oneself with a certain movement or opinion and act on it together with others./
찬란하다 찬란하다 [chanranhada] /bright; radiant — Being in a state in which a bright light is flashing or many lights are shining, or the lights being very bright./splendid — The color, appearance, etc., of something being very magnificent or beautiful./glorious — A matter, ideal, etc., being very good and grand./bright; cheerful — One's emotion, etc., being very excited and joyful./
찬란히 찬란히 [chanranhi] /brightly; radiantly — In the state of a bright light flashing or many lights shining, or in the manner of the lights being very bright./splendidly — In the state of the color, appearance, etc., of something being very magnificent or beautiful./gloriously — In the state of a matter, ideal, etc., being very good and grand./
찬물 찬물 [chanmul] /cold water — Cold water./
찬물도 위아래가 있다 찬물도 위아래가 있다 [chanmuldo wiaraega issda] /Even cold water should be first served to a senior — You should do everything in due order./
찬물을 끼얹다 찬물을 끼얹다 [chanmuleul kkieonjda] /pour cold water — To jump into something that is going well and impede the progress or ruin the mood of it./
찬미 찬미 [chanmi] /praise; compliment — An act of speaking highly of something beautiful or great./
찬미하다 찬미하다 [chanmihada] /praise; compliment — To speak highly of something beautiful or great./
찬바람 찬바람 [chanbaram] /coldness; cold wind — (figurative) An energy or sensation that feels very cold and chilly./
