찬바람이 일다 찬바람이 일다 [chanbarami ilda] /Cold wind rises — For the mind, atmosphere, etc., to become cold and rough./
찬반 찬반 [chanban] /approval and disapproval — Pros and cons./
찬반양론 찬반양론 [chanbanyangron] /pros and cons — Two arguments that oppose each other as approval and disapproval./
찬밥 찬밥 [chanbab] /cold rice — Cooked rice that has become cold after some time./leftover rice — Leftover cooked rice./outcast — (figurative) Someone or something that is not important and thought nothing of./
찬밥 더운밥 가리다 찬밥 더운밥 가리다 [chanbab deounbab garida] /discriminate between cold rice and hot rice — For a desperate person to be choosy about things./
찬불가 찬불가 [chanbulga] /Buddhist hymn — A Buddhist song praising Sakyamuni's greatness./
찬비 찬비 [chanbi] /cold rain — Chilly rain./
찬사 찬사 [chansa] /praise; compliment — Words or a piece of writing that expresses one's admiration for someone or something./
찬성 찬성 [chanseong] /agreement; consent — An act of acknowledging another person's opinion, idea, etc., as meritorious and endorsing it./
찬성표 찬성표 [chanseongpyo] /approval vote; yes vote — A vote in favor of something./
찬성하다 찬성하다 [chanseonghada] /agree; consent — To acknowledge another person's opinion, idea, etc., as meritorious and endorse it./
찬송 찬송 [chansong] /praise — An act of honoring and complimenting a beautiful, great virtue./hymn — A Christian song of praise for God's love and blessings./glorification — In Christianity, an act of honoring and complimenting God's blessings, or such an act./
찬송가 찬송가 [chansongga] /hymn — A Christian song praising God's love and blessings./
