출렁 출렁 [chulreong] /in a splash — A word imitating the sound made when water, etc., forms a big ripple once and creates a wave, or describing such a scene./with a shock — A word describing the state of one's heart pounding, as when one is surprised or nervous./
출렁거리다 출렁거리다 [chulreonggeorida] /slash; roll; slosh — For water, etc., to form big ripples repeatedly and create waves./palpitate; sink — For one's heart to pound, as when one is surprised or nervous./
출렁이다 출렁이다 [chulreongida] /roll; slosh — For water, etc., to form big ripples repeatedly and create waves./palpitate; sink — For one's heart to pound, as when one is surprised or nervous./
출렁출렁 출렁출렁 [chulreongchulreong] /in splashes — A word imitating the sound made when water, etc., forms big ripples repeatedly and creates waves, or describing such a scene./with a shock — A word describing the state of one's heart pounding a lot, as when one is surprised or nervous./
출렁출렁하다 출렁출렁하다 [chulreongchulreonghada] /roll; slosh — For water, etc., to form big ripples repeatedly and create waves./palpitate; sink — For one's heart to pound, as when one is surprised or nervous./
출렁하다 출렁하다 [chulreonghada] /roll; slosh — For water, etc., to form a big ripple once and create a wave./palpitate; sink — For one's heart to pound, as when one is surprised or nervous./
