ts state./oil — To coat the bottom of a frying fan, etc., with some oil, to cook something./draw — To surround something with a curtain, screen, tent, etc.,/enclose; block — To surround a wall with something, blocking a passage./build — To make a temporary place to stay with a tent, etc./roll; wrap — To wrap or roll in long cloth such as denim or traditional Korean sock-suspenders, or bandages./raise; breed; keep — To raise livestock, animals, etc./branch out; root — For a plant to stretch its branches or roots more./give birth to — For an animal to give birth./run; lease — Usually for business, to let someone stay in one's house, facilities, etc./clear; dig up — To dig up or carry a dirty object or unnecessarily stacked objects, making the area clean./dig; dredge — To dig ground or arrange an area, to make a rice paddy or waterway./run over; knock down — For a car, etc., to hit a person hard./count — To calculate or count something./consider; value — To think or recognize something as a certain thing or to have a certain trait./include; consider — To put something into consideration or calculation./speak of — To think of something based on a certain thing./sift; sieve — To pour flour, etc., on a sieve and shake it, making the powder finer./
