타다 타다 [tada] /burn — For a fire to be ignited or spread, due to embers or heat./be tanned — For one’s skin to be exposed to the sunlight for a long time and for it to turn dark./be overcooked — For food to be overcooked until it becomes blackish./become worried — To come to feel anxious or worried./dry — To become very dry due to a lack of moisture./ride; get on; board — To mount a vehicle or the body of an animal used as a vehicle./take — To choose something as a route and move along it./climb; mount — To climb on or crawl down from a slope, tree, cliff, etc./get on; mount — To mount a person or object./take advantage of — To use a certain condition, time, opportunity, etc./be blown; flow — For something to move, as it is carried away by wind, stream, electric wave, etc./slide — To slip in or on a device on a very slippery floor or ground./ride — To sit or stand on such play equipment as a swing, seesaw, etc., and to move back and forth or up and down./mix; add — To put a small amount of liquid or powder into a large amount of liquid, and to mix it./receive — To receive money or an object as one’s share or as a prize./be born with — To have good luck, a talent, a destiny, etc., from one’s birth./play — To make a sound by pulling and releasing the strings, or by pressing the keys of a musical instrument./get dirty easily — For something to be easily attached to by stains or dirt./be easily stimulated — For one’s body to be severely stimulated easily./feel easily — To come to have a feeling easily or to sense a physical stimulation such as itchiness easily./be influenced easily — To be easily influenced by the weather or season./be worn out — For something to become weak or bad from being touched by many people./be stolen — For goods to disappear frequently because there are people who intend to steal them./
