탈탈 탈탈 [taltal] /tap-tap — A word imitating the sound made when something is beaten lightly and repeatedly to be dusted, or describing such a scene./completely — A word describing an act of shaking everything off, without anything left./with a clink — A word imitating the sound made when a broken or cracked, thin container, etc., is hit against something./ploddingly; slowly — A word describing one’s slow and sluggish walk./with a clatter — A word imitating the sound made when an old car, etc., rocks and runs slowly, or describing such a scene./completely — A word describing something that is completely empty./
탈탈거리다 탈탈거리다 [taltalgeorida] /keep walking slowly — To walk, with drowsy steps, slowly and continuously./keep running slowly — For an old car, etc., to run shakingly and slowly./
탈탈대다 탈탈대다 [taltaldaeda] /keep walking slowly — To walk, with drowsy steps, slowly and continuously./keep running slowly — For an old car, etc., to run shakingly and slowly./
탈탈하다 탈탈하다 [taltalhada] /keep walking slowly — To walk, with drowsy steps, slowly and continuously./keep running slowly — For an old car, etc., to run shakingly and slowly./
탈퇴 탈퇴 [taltoe] /withdrawal; dropping out; leaving — An act of ending one's relationship with an organization or group one had belonged to and leaving./
탈퇴하다 탈퇴하다 [taltoehada] /withdraw; drop out; leave — To end one's relationship with an organization or group one had belonged to and leave./
탈피 탈피 [talpi] /shedding; escape from — The state of completely coming out of a certain situation or state./molting; shedding the skin; slough — An act of an insect, reptile, etc., casting off its slough or skin, as it grows up./
탈피되다 탈피되다 [talpidoeda] /be molted; be shedded; be sloughed — For the slough or skin of an insect, reptile, etc., to be cast off , as it grows up./be made to shed; be made to escape from — For someone to be made to come out of a certain situation or state completely./
탈피하다 탈피하다 [talpihada] /molt; shed the skin; slough — For an insect, reptile, etc., to cast off its slough or skin, as it grows up./shed; escape from — To completely come out of a certain situation or state./
탈환 탈환 [talhwan] /recapture; recovery — An act of taking what has been taken away back./
탈환되다 탈환되다 [talhwandoeda] /be reclaimed; be won back; be recovered — For what has been taken away to be regained by its original owner./
탈환하다 탈환하다 [talhwanhada] /reclaim; win back — To take back something that has been taken away./
탐 탐 [tam] /covetousness; avarice; greed — The desire to own something./
탐관 탐관 [tamgwan] /corrupt official; greedy official — An official coveting and taking away people's property./
탐관오리 탐관오리 [tamgwanori] /corrupt official; greedy official — An official coveting and taking away people's property and acting corruptly./
탐구 탐구 [tamgu] /search; quest; investigation; pursuit — An act of digging into and looking into a field of study, etc., deeply./
탐구되다 탐구되다 [tamgudoeda] /be searched for; be investigated; be pursued — For a field of study, etc., to be dug into and looked into deeply./
탐구심 탐구심 [tamgusim] /spirit of inquiry — The spirit in which one would dig into and look into a field of study, etc., deeply./
탐구자 탐구자 [tamguja] /researcher — A person who digs into and looks into a field of study, etc., deeply./
탐구하다 탐구하다 [tamguhada] /search for; investigate; pursue — To dig into and look into a field of study, etc., deeply./
탐나다 탐나다 [tamnada] /be desirable; be tempting — To come to feel greed for something, because one wants to own it./
탐내다 탐내다 [tamnaeda] /desire; covet — To have greed, as one wants to own something./
탐닉 탐닉 [tamnig] /indulging in — The state of enjoying something too much, and getting lost in it while enjoying it./
탐닉하다 탐닉하다 [tamnighada] /indulge in — To enjoy something too much, and to get lost in it while enjoying it./
탐독 탐독 [tamdog] /devouring; reading avidly — An act of reading a certain piece of writing or book very attentively./enjoying; especially liking — The state of liking to read a specific piece of writing or book more than others./
탐독하다 탐독하다 [tamdoghada] /devour; read avidly — To read a certain piece of writing or book very attentively./enjoy; especially like — To like to read a specific piece of writing or book more than others./
탐라국 탐라국 [tamragug] /Tamnaguk — A kingdom that existed on today's Jejudo Island during the Three Kingdoms period; it was annexed to the Goryeo Dynasty in 1105./
탐문 탐문 [tammun] /inquiry; investigation by questioning — An act of visiting places and people here and there, asking questions, to find out an unknown fact or news./
탐문하다 탐문하다 [tammunhada] /inquire; investigate by questioning — To visit places and people here and there, asking questions, to find out an unknown fact or news./
탐미 탐미 [tammi] /love of beauty — One's state of seeking beauty to the extent that one gets lost./
탐미주의 탐미주의 [tammijuui] /aestheticism — A trend in literature in which writers view beauty as something of the highest value, and seek it./
탐미하다 탐미하다 [tammihada] /love beauty — To seek beauty so much that one gets lost./
탐방 탐방 [tambang] /visit; traveling — An act of visiting a place or a person to find out a certain fact or news./visit; traveling; field trip — An act of visiting a tourist attraction or historic site to look around./
탐방기 탐방기 [tambanggi] /travel journal; visit report — A piece of writing about the person one met or the place one visited./
탐방하다 탐방하다 [tambanghada] /visit; travel — To visit a place or a person to find out a certain fact or news./visit; travel; go on a field trip — To visit a tourist attraction or historic site to look around./
탐사 탐사 [tamsa] /investigation; probing — An act of looking for an unknown object or looking into an unknown fact, leaving nothing untouched./
탐사선 탐사선 [tamsaseon] /space probe — A flying object whose mission is to examine the Earth or other planets in space./
탐사하다 탐사하다 [tamsahada] /investigate; probe — To look for an unknown object or look into an unknown fact, leaving nothing untouched./
탐색 탐색 [tamsaeg] /search; hunt; location — An act of probing and looking around, in an attempt to discover an unknown object or reveal an unknown phenomenon./
탐색전 탐색전 [tamsaegjeon] /reconnoitering skirmish — An act of psychological warfare to find out the level, secret, etc., of the other party./
탐색하다 탐색하다 [tamsaeghada] /search; hunt; locate — To probe and look around, in an attempt to discover an unknown object or reveal an unknown phenomenon./
탐스럽다 탐스럽다 [tamseureobda] /desirable; appetizing — Aesthetically pleasing and attractive, provoking the desire to possess or even seize./
탐식 탐식 [tamsig] /voracity; edacity; gluttony — The state of coveting food, or an act of eating a lot of food as one is gluttonous./
탐식하다 탐식하다 [tamsighada] /eat voraciously; devour — To covet food, or to eat a lot of food as one is gluttonous./
탐욕 탐욕 [tamyog] /greed; covetousness — A strong desire to own too much of something./
탐욕스럽다 탐욕스럽다 [tamyogseureobda] /greedy; covetous — Having a strong desire for too much of something./
탐욕적 탐욕적 [tamyogjeog] /being greedy; being covetous — The state of having a strong desire for too much of something./greedy; covetous — Having a strong desire for too much of something./
탐정 탐정 [tamjeong] /detective — A person whose job it is to secretly investigate an incident or a crime./
탐정 소설 탐정 소설 [tamjeong soseol] /mystery novel; detective novel — A novel that deals with a process of investigating and solving a criminal case./
탐조등 탐조등 [tamjodeung] /searchlight — A device that projects light a long distance in order to light up or find something./
탐지 탐지 [tamji] /detection — An act of revealing the truth or locating an object, through an investigation or search./
탐지되다 탐지되다 [tamjidoeda] /be detected — For the truth to be revealed or for an object to be located, through an investigation or search./
탐지하다 탐지하다 [tamjihada] /detect — To investigate or search in order to reveal the truth or locate an object./
탐탁하다 탐탁하다 [tamtaghada] /satisfied; favorable — Feeling good about something and being satisfied./
탐하다 탐하다 [tamhada] /desire; covet — To have excessive greed, as one wants to own something./
탐험 탐험 [tamheom] /exploration; expedition — An act of going to a location to observe and study its characteristics, often in dangerous conditions./
탐험가 탐험가 [tamheomga] /explorer — A person who specializes in going to a location to observe and study its characteristics, often in dangerous conditions./
탐험대 탐험대 [tamheomdae] /expedition; party of explorers — A group of people who have gathered to go to a location to observe and study its characteristics, often in dangerous conditions./
탐험하다 탐험하다 [tamheomhada] /exploration; expedition — An act of going to a location to observe and study its characteristics, often in dangerous conditions./
탑 탑 [tab] /tower — An architectural structure in multi-layers, or a high and pointed one./pagoda — In Buddhism, a pointed architectural structure usually in multiple layers, built to hold the Buddha's remains or to pay tribute to his charitable deeds./
탑돌이 탑돌이 [tabdoli] /circling the pagoda — An event on the day of the Buddha's Birthday, in which people circle the pagoda all night while paying a tribute to his good deeds and making their own wishes./
탑승 탑승 [tabseung] /boarding — An act of getting on an airplane, ship, bus, etc./
탑승객 탑승객 [tabseunggaeg] /passenger — A guest who is on board an airplane, ship, car, etc./
탑승구 탑승구 [tabseunggu] /boarding gate; entrance — An entrance to an airplane, ship, bus, etc. which passengers go through to get on./
탑승자 탑승자 [tabseungja] /passenger — A person who is on board an airplane, ship, car, etc./
탑승하다 탑승하다 [tabseunghada] /board — To get on an airplane, ship, bus, etc./
