탕수육 탕수육 [tangsuyug] /sweet and sour pork — A Chinese dish made by frying flour-coated meat, and pouring a boiled mixture of vinegar, soybean sauce, sugar, vegetables, etc., over the meat./
탕아 탕아 [tanga] /debauchee; libertine — A man who behaves badly, indulging in liquor, women, gambling, etc./
탕약 탕약 [tangyag] /decoction; infusion of medicinal herbs — Medicinal herbs taken after being decocted./
탕진 탕진 [tangjin] /squandering; running through; wasting — An act of wasting one's property by using all of it./wasting; using up; burning out — An act of consuming all of one's time, energy, passion, etc./
탕진되다 탕진되다 [tangjindoeda] /be squandered; be run through; be wasted — For one's property to be wasted because one has spent all of it./be wasted; be used up; be burnt out — For all of one's time, energy, passion, etc. to be consumed./
탕진하다 탕진하다 [tangjinhada] /squander; run through; waste — To waste one's property by spending all of it./waste; use up; burn out — To consume all of one's time, energy, passion, etc./
탕탕 탕탕 [tangtang] /thump-thump — A word imitating the sound made when a small piece of iron or a hard object hits something repeatedly and strongly./bang-bang — A word imitating the sound made when a gun is fired repeatedly./
태 태 [tae] /being stylish — The state of looking beautiful and elegant thanks to one's clothes and demeanor./attitude; appearance — One's attitude or appearance which others can see./pretense — An attitude of showing something off, even by faking it./
