태국 태국 [taegug] /Thailand — A country located in the Indochinese Peninsula of Southeastern Asia; it's the Korean pronunciation for the Chinese characters for '타이(Thai)'./
태권도 태권도 [taegwondo] /taegwondo; taekwondo — Sport based on a traditional Korean martial arts, characterized by using hands and feet to perform an array of attacking or defending moves such as kicking, punching, blocking, etc./
태극기 태극기 [taegeuggi] /taegeukgi — The national flag of the Republic of Korea./
태극선 태극선 [taegeugseon] /taegeukseon — A round fan with taegeuk, a yin-yang symbol, painted on it./
태기 태기 [taegi] /signs of pregnancy — A feeling of being pregnant./
태도 태도 [taedo] /attitude — One's manner of moving one's body or dealing with a certain incident./stance; position — One's position or thought about a certain incident./
태동 태동 [taedong] /fetal movement — The movement of a fetus in the womb of its mother./brewing — The emergence of a sign indicating that something is about to happen./
태동하다 태동하다 [taedonghada] /move in a womb — For a fetus to move in the womb of its mother./brew — For a sign indicating that something is about to happen to emerge./
