태부족 태부족 [taebujog] /great lack — The state of being in a great shortage./
태부족하다 태부족하다 [taebujoghada] /greatly wanted — Being in a great shortage./
태산 태산 [taesan] /huge mountain — A high and big mountain./abundance — (figurative) The state of something being big and abundant./
태생 태생 [taesaeng] /origin; birth — One's birth in a certain place./viviparity — An act of a fetus growing up in the womb of its mother to a certain size and being born./
태세 태세 [taese] /setup; preparedness — One's attitude just before a certain incident or situation./
태아 태아 [taea] /fetus — A baby growing in the womb of its mother./
태양 태양 [taeyang] /sun — The star at the center of a solar system which is extremely hot and emits light./hope — (figurative) A very cherished existence which gives hope./
