태엽이 풀리다 태엽이 풀리다 [taeyeobi pulrida] /have one's spring unwind — (slang) For one's body and mind to become relaxed because tension has been eased./
태우다 태우다 [taeuda] /burn; ignite — To ignite something to make it burn./tan — To expose one’s skin to the sunlight for a long time and make it turn dark./overcook — To overcook food until it becomes blackish./smoke — To smoke a cigarette./be worried — To feel anxious or worried./make someone worry — To make someone feel anxious or worried./have someone mount — To have someone mount a vehicle such as a car or ship or the back of an animal./have someone slide — To have someone slide on a slippery floor using a certain device./have someone ride — To have someone use such play equipment as a swing, seesaw, etc./
태음력 태음력 [taeeumryeog] /lunar calendar — A calendar used to count days based on the time it takes the moon to orbit around the earth./
태자 태자 [taeja] /crown prince — A son of the king, who will be the next king./prince — A son of the emperor, who will be the next emperor./
태중 태중 [taejung] /period of maternity — The period during which a fetus grows in the womb./
태초 태초 [taecho] /beginning of the world; genesis — The very beginning of time, when the sky and the land formed./
태클 태클 [taekeul] /tackle — In soccer, an act of attacking the other team suddenly and taking away the ball, or such a technique./tackle — In rugby or American football, an act of a defensive player knocking down an attacking player to block the player carrying the ball or taking away the ball, or such a technique./tackle — In wrestling, an act of grabbing and knocking down the other player, or such a technique./provoking a quarrel — (slang) An act of picking a fight./
태평 태평 [taepyeong] /peace — The state of a nation being peaceful without worries or troubles./tranquility — The state of one's mind being serene without worries or troubles./
태평성대 태평성대 [taepyeongseongdae] /reign of peace — The world or age free from worries or troubles, in which a benevolent king rules well./
