터덜대다 터덜대다 [teodeoldaeda] /keep trudging; keep walking wearily — To keep walking weakly with heavy steps due to exhaustion or lack of energy./keep running loudly — For a loud noise to be continuously made when a car, empty cart, etc., runs on a bumpy road./
터덜터덜 터덜터덜 [teodeolteodeol] /trudgingly; ploddingly — A word imitating the sound made when one walks weakly with heavy steps due to exhaustion or lack of energy, or such a scene./with a clatter — A word imitating the sound made when a car, empty cart, etc., keeps running on a bumpy road loudly./
터덜터덜하다 터덜터덜하다 [teodeolteodeolhada] /keep trudging; keep walking wearily — To keep walking weakly with heavy steps due to exhaustion or lack of energy./keep running loudly — For a loud noise to be continuously made when a car, empty cart, etc., runs on a bumpy road./
