터지다 터지다 [teojida] /be broken down; be pierced — For an object surrounded and blocked by something to be broken down or pierced./be chapped — For the surface to be burst open./burst open — For a spot stitched to be torn off and be open./be cleared — For something to be open with nothing blocking or covering it./bleed; pour — For a nosebleed or stagnant water to run down suddenly./set off; spark — For something to be ignited and spark strongly./bloom — For a flower bud to start to open./burst — For suppressed or accumulated feelings to come out./burst — For applause, laughter, a cry, a noise, etc., to suddenly come out at once./occur — For a fight or accident to occur suddenly./score — In a sport game, for an awaited goal to be scored./be worried — To feel agony with concerns and worries./be lucky — For good events to rush ahead at once./be beaten — (slang) To be spanked or beaten up./teojida — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the speaker is displeased because the quality or state described by the preceding words is very severe./
터키 터키 [teoki] /Turkey — The English name of Türkiye./
터트리다 터트리다 [teoteurida] /pop; burst — To press the surface surrounding something and make it burst open./spark — To make a flame or light to spark hard./burst into bloom — For a plant to open a bud and bloom as a flower./burst — To laugh, cry, or scream suddenly and loudly./vent; burst — To suddenly express a bad feeling about someone or something to someone or in front of others./break; let out — To make something happen suddenly or be exposed outwardly./score — To score in a sports game such as soccer, baseball, etc./
턱 턱 [teog] /chin — The protruding part of a face, below the mouth./jaws — The organs located on the upper and lower parts of one’s mouth, which are used to pronounce sounds or chew food, etc./raised spot; sill; elevated place — A part on a flat surface that has been raised a little higher or that protrudes./treat; entertainment — An act of buying food for someone, when there is something to celebrate./reason; cause — A bound noun meaning a reason or cause that explains why something must be that way./level; situation — A bound noun meaning such a degree or situation./relaxingly — A word describing one suddenly becoming relaxed after being tense, etc./in a composed manner — A word describing an action, etc., being done in a mature and calm manner./with a grip — A word describing one's sudden and strong act of grabbing someone's shoulder, hand, etc./chokingly — A word describing one's sudden state of being short of breath, etc./with a thud — A word describing one's act of falling down weakly and suddenly./in a broad manner — A word describing one's shoulders, chest, etc., being very wide./spit — A word imitating the sound made when one spits out very strongly, or describing such a scene./thump; thud — A word imitating the sound made when something is hit or explodes slowly and strongly, or describing such a scene./with a sudden halt — A word describing a moving object suddenly stopping or being stuck./
턱걸이 턱걸이 [teoggeoli] /chin-up — An exercise in which one holds a bar with both hands and raises one's body, bringing one's chin above the bar./managing to — (figurative) The state of someone or something managing to meet a certain standard./
