토닥토닥하다 토닥토닥하다 [todagtodaghada] /keep tapping; keep patting — To repeatedly make a sound of hitting something lightly./
토담 토담 [todam] /earthen wall; adobe wall; mud wall — A wall built by stacking earth./
토대 토대 [todae] /foundation — The lowermost part of a building, which supports the building./foundation — (figurative) Basics that form the base of a certain task or object./
토대하다 토대하다 [todaehada] /be based on — To be based on or founded on something./
토라지다 토라지다 [torajida] /pout; sulk — To turn away, as one does not approve or is not satisfied with something./
토란 토란 [toran] /taro — A plant, 80 to 120 centimeter tall, whose wide, shield-shaped leaves are thick, and whose egg-shaped stem underground is eaten as food./
토로 토로 [toro] /laying bare one’s heart — An act of saying everything one has in mind./
토로하다 토로하다 [torohada] /lay bare one’s heart — To say everything one has in mind./
토록 토록 [torog] /torok — A postpositional particle used to indicate that the scope of something is until the degree or time limit mentioned in the preceding statement./
토론 토론 [toron] /discussion; debate — A debate by many people about an issue, while judging what is right and wrong./
토론되다 토론되다 [torondoeda] /be discussed; be debated — For an issue to be debated on by many people, while determining what is right and wrong./
토론자 토론자 [toronja] /panel; debater — A person who debates an issue, while judging what is right and wrong./
토론하다 토론하다 [toronhada] /discuss; debate — For many people to debate an issue, while determining what is right and wrong./
토론회 토론회 [toronhoe] /debate; panel discussion — A meeting in which many people debate an issue, while judging what is right and wrong./
토막 토막 [tomag] /piece; fragment — A rather large chunk of something./short message; short object — A very short bit of content or thing, compared with others./part; piece — A short part that has been cut off from the whole speech, piece of writing, thought, etc./piece; block; slice — The unit for counting sliced or cut chunks of something./
토막토막 토막토막 [tomagtomag] /each piece; pieces — Each and every piece or multiple pieces./in pieces; in chunks — A word describing something in several pieces or chunks./every piece; every chunk — For each piece or chunk./
토목 토목 [tomog] /soil and tree — A compound noun for soil and tree./civil engineering — A construction project to build a road, bridge, tunnel, bank, etc., by changing the land, stream, etc./
토목 공사 토목 공사 [tomog gongsa] /civil engineering project — A construction project to change land, stream, etc./
토박이 토박이 [tobagi] /native — A person who has long lived in a region./
토박이말 토박이말 [tobagimal] /native word — An original word that an ethnic language group has, or a word created based on such a word./
토방 토방 [tobang] /tobang — earth floor: A flat floor covered with soil, slightly raised, in front of the door to a room./
토벌 토벌 [tobeol] /conquest; subjugation — An act of attacking and eliminating a rebel army, etc./
토사 토사 [tosa] /earth and sand — Soil and sand./
토사곽란 토사곽란 [tosagwagran] /acute gastroenteritis; vomiting and diarrhea — A stomach disorder whose symptoms include vomiting, diarrhea, and stomachache./
토사구팽 토사구팽 [tosagupaeng] /killing the dog after hunting — An expression used to indicate the situation of using something when necessary and throwing it away unsympathetically when not, from its literal meaning of &quot;After a rabbit hunt is over, the now-useless hunting dog is boiled and eaten.&quot;/
토사물 토사물 [tosamul] /vomit — Food thrown up by someone./
토산물 토산물 [tosanmul] /products of a place; local produce — An object or food that is produced only or in greater quantities in a certain region./
토산품 토산품 [tosanpum] /products of a place; local produce — A commodity that is produced only or in greater quantity in a certain region./
토성 토성 [toseong] /Saturn — A planet that is sixth closest to the sun./wall of earth; mud wall — Fortifications made by stacking mud, soil, etc./
토속 토속 [tosog] /folkways; local customs — A special custom or practice that is unique to a specific region./
토속적 토속적 [tosogjeog] /being folksy — The state of something being similar to a special custom or practice that is unique to a specific region./folksy — Similar to a special custom or practice that is unique to a specific region./
토스 토스 [toseu] /toss — In basketball, an act of throwing the ball slightly upwards./toss — In baseball, an act of sending the ball to a player of one’s team who is nearby, by lightly throwing it./
토스터 토스터 [toseuteo] /toaster — A device to toast slices of plain bread using electricity./
토스트 토스트 [toseuteu] /toast — A thin slice of lightly-toasted plain bread./
토스하다 토스하다 [toseuhada] /toss — In basketball, to throw the ball upwards lightly./toss — In baseball, to send the ball to a player on one’s team who is nearby, by lightly throwing it./
토시 토시 [tosi] /arm warmer — Something pulled over one’s arms to keep them warm./oversleeve — While working, something pulled over one’s arms to keep the sleeves from becoming worn out or dirty./arm gear for hawk — A piece of gear pulled over a hunter’s arm for a hawk to sit on./
토실토실 토실토실 [tosiltosil] /plumply; chubbily — A word describing one's appearance being a little roundish, in a nice way./
토실토실하다 토실토실하다 [tosiltosilhada] /plump; chubby — Looking a little roundish, in a nice way./
토양 토양 [toyang] /soil; earth — Substance covering the surface of the Earth, consisting of small grains./soil; earth — Soil in which plants can grow./foundation; base — (figurative) The foundation for a certain task or activity./
토요일 토요일 [toyoil] /Saturday — The sixth day of a week starting from Monday./
토의 토의 [toui] /discussion; debate — An act of many people going over and sharing thoughts on the details of a certain issue./
토의되다 토의되다 [touidoeda] /be discussed; be debated — For the details of a certain issue to be gone over and for thoughts on them to be shared by many people./
토의하다 토의하다 [touihada] /discuss; debate — For many people to go over and share thoughts on the details of a certain issue./
토종 토종 [tojong] /native; indigenous — A seed that grows in an area originally./native — A person whose forebears had lived through generations in a region./
토종꿀 토종꿀 [tojongkkul] /native honey — Honey that is collected by bees which are native in an area originally./
토종닭 토종닭 [tojongdalg] /native chicken; indigenous chicken — A unique chicken that has grown in an area from the past originally./
토지 토지 [toji] /land; lot — The land used by people for living and doing activities./
토질 토질 [tojil] /quality of soil — The characteristic of soil./soil component — Substance that forms soil./
토착 토착 [tochag] /being native; being indigenous; settling down — The state of people being born and living through generations in a region, or an act of moving to and settling down in a region./
토착되다 토착되다 [tochagdoeda] /become native; become indigenous; get to settle down — To be made to be born and live through generations in a region, or be made to move to and settle down in a region./
토착하다 토착하다 [tochaghada] /be native; be indigenous; settle down — To be born and live through generations in a region, or move to and settle down in a region./
토착화 토착화 [tochaghwa] /naturalization; localization — The state of a certain system, custom, ideology, etc., taking root after being changed to be suitable for a region; or an act of making this happen./
