토착화하다 토착화하다 [tochaghwahada] /naturalize — For a certain system, custom, ideology, etc., to take root after being changed to be suitable for a region; or to make this happen./
토큰 토큰 [tokeun] /bus token — (archaic) A round object in the shape of a coin, paid as a bus fare, instead of cash./
토테미즘 토테미즘 [totemijeum] /totemism — A social system or religion in which an animal, plant, or natural object, believed to be sacred, is worshiped./
토템 토템 [totem] /totem — In a primitive society, an animal, plant, or natural object, held sacred due to a belief that it is specially related with a tribe or clan society./
토픽 토픽 [topig] /topic; title — The title of a story./topic; issue — The material or content that constitutes a story./
토핑 토핑 [toping] /topping — In the final stage of cooking, an act of placing an ingredient on an almost-completed dish or decorating it./
토하다 토하다 [tohada] /vomit; throw up — To let something one has eaten come out of one's  mouth./emit; gush out; blow out — To send out a gas, flame, smoke, etc./express; yell; shout — To express one's feeling or thoughts strongly in one's voice or speech./
토호 토호 [toho] /landed proprietor; powerful local resident — A person who has lived in a certain region for a long time and has a lot of influence./
톡 톡 [tog] /pop — A word imitating the sound made when a small thing suddenly pops up or bursts open, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when a small thing suddenly falls down, or describing such a scene./sharply — A word describing one’s act of talking sharply at someone./in one’s way — A word imitating the sound made when a small thing gets in someone's way or gets kicked, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when one gently taps or touches something, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when one gently shakes or bounces something, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when a bird gently pecks at something, or describing such a scene./simply — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly breaks suddenly and easily, or describing such a scene./bulgingly — A word describing a part of something protruding./pungently — A word describing the feeling of pungency at the tip of the tongue, nose, etc./
톡탁 톡탁 [togtag] /tap-tap; pat-pat — A word imitating the sound made when a hard object is hit lightly./with light jabs — A word imitating the sound made when people hit each other lightly, or describing such a scene./
톡탁거리다 톡탁거리다 [togtaggeorida] /keep tapping; keep patting — For the sounds of hitting a hard object repeatedly and lightly to be made, or to make such sounds./keep exchanging light jabs — For the sounds of hitting each other lightly and repeatedly to be made, or to make such sounds./
톡탁대다 톡탁대다 [togtagdaeda] /keep tapping; keep patting — For the sounds of hitting a hard object repeatedly and lightly to be made, or to make such sounds./keep exchanging light jabs — For the sounds of hitting each other lightly and repeatedly to be made, or to make such sounds./
톡탁이다 톡탁이다 [togtagida] /tap; pat — For the sound of hitting a hard object lightly to be made, or to make such a sound./exchange light jabs — For the sound of hitting each other lightly to be made./
톡탁톡탁 톡탁톡탁 [togtagtogtag] /tap-tap; pat-pat — A word imitating the sound made when a hard object keeps being hit lightly./with light jabs — A word imitating the sound made when people keep hitting each other lightly, or describing such a scene./
톡탁톡탁하다 톡탁톡탁하다 [togtagtogtaghada] /keep tapping; keep patting — For the sounds of hitting a hard object repeatedly and lightly to be made, or to make such sounds./keep exchanging light jabs — For the sounds of hitting each other lightly and repeatedly to be made, or to make such sounds./
톡탁하다 톡탁하다 [togtaghada] /tap; pat — For the sound of hitting a hard object lightly to be made, or to make such a sound./exchange light jabs — For the sound of hitting each other lightly to be made./
톡톡 톡톡 [togtog] /pop pop — In a manner of small things suddenly popping up or bursting open repeatedly, or such sound./gently — In a manner of small things suddenly falling down, or such sound./sharply — In a manner of a person talking sharply at others./repeatedly — In a manner of small things getting in someone's way or getting kicked repeatedly, or such sound./gently — In a manner of someone gently tapping or touching something, or such sound./gently — In a manner of someone gently shaking or bouncing something repeatedly, or such sound./gently — In a manner of a bird gently pecking at something repeatedly, or such sound./simply — In a manner of something suddenly breaking in an easy and repeated fashion, or such sound./here and there — In a manner of things popping up here and there./pungently — In a manner of the tip of the tongue, nose, etc., feeling pungency./
톡톡 털다 톡톡 털다 [togtog teolda] /empty gently — To give someone all the money in one's hands./
톡톡거리다 톡톡거리다 [togtoggeorida] /pop — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things to suddenly pop up or burst open./fall — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things suddenly fall./snap; shoot back — To talk sharply at someone repeatedly./be kicked — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things get in someone's way or get kicked./tap; touch — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one gently taps or touches something./shake; bounce — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one gently shakes or bounces something./peck — For sounds to be made repeatedly when a bird gently pecks at something./break — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one slightly and suddenly breaks something./
톡톡대다 톡톡대다 [togtogdaeda] /pop — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things to suddenly pop up or burst open./fall — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things suddenly fall./snap; shoot back — To talk sharply at someone repeatedly./be kicked — For sounds to be made repeatedly when small things get in someone's way or get kicked./tap; touch — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one gently taps or touches something./shake; bounce — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one gently shakes or bounces something./peck — For sounds to be made repeatedly when a bird gently pecks at something./break — For sounds to be made repeatedly when one slightly and suddenly breaks something./
톡톡하다 톡톡하다 [togtoghada] /thick — A cloth, etc., being a little thick as it is evenly and densely knitted with strong yarn./thick — Clothes being a little thick as lots of cotton has been stuffed in it./thick — Not weak as little liquid is contained./rich — Asset, home economy, etc., being substantial and abundant./harsh — The degree of criticism, humiliation, scolding, etc., being severe./responsible — One’s responsibility, role, etc., being satisfactory, as it is done appropriately./
톡톡히 톡톡히 [togtoghi] /thickly — In the manner of a cloth, etc., being a little thick as it is evenly and densely knitted with strong yarn./thickly — In the manner of clothes being a little thick as lots of cotton has been stuffed in it./thickly — In the manner of not being weak as little liquid is contained./richly — In the manner of asset, home economy, etc., being substantial and abundant./harshly — In the manner of the degree of criticism, humiliation, scolding, etc., being severe./responsibly — In the manner of one’s responsibility, role, etc., being satisfactory, as it is done appropriately./
