퇴장 퇴장 [toejang] /leaving; walkout — An act of leaving a certain place or going outside./exit; leaving the stage — In a theater play, etc., an act of a character leaving the stage./being sent to the bench; being taken out — During a sports game, an act of a player leaving the game, due to a foul, injury, etc./
퇴장하다 퇴장하다 [toejanghada] /leave; walk out — To leave a certain place or go outside./exit; leave the stage — In a theater play, etc., for a character to leave the stage./be sent to the bench; be taken out — During a sports game, for a player to leave the game, due to a foul, injury, etc./
퇴적 퇴적 [toejeog] /being accumulated; accumulation — The state of a large amount of something being stacked in layers; or an act of stacking a large amount of something in layers./being deposited — The state of a substance such as soil, the bones of dead creatures, etc., being delivered by streaming water, wind, an iceberg, etc., and being stacked in a certain place./
퇴적되다 퇴적되다 [toejeogdoeda] /be accumulated — For a large amount of something to be stacked in layers./be deposited — For substance such as soil, the bones of dead creatures, etc., to be delivered by streaming water, wind, an iceberg, etc., and stacked in a certain place./
퇴적물 퇴적물 [toejeogmul] /something accumulated — Something stacked in a large amount in layers./sediment deposit — Substance stacked in a certain place, as soil, the bones of dead creatures, etc., is delivered by streaming water, wind, an iceberg, etc./
퇴적암 퇴적암 [toejeogam] /sedimentary rock — A rock formed as substances such as soil, the bones of dead creatures, etc., are delivered by streaming water, wind, icebergs, etc., and stacked in a certain place./
퇴적층 퇴적층 [toejeogcheung] /sedimentary layer — A layer formed as a substance such as soil, the bones of dead creatures , etc., is delivered by streaming water, wind, an iceberg, etc., and is stacked in a certain place./
퇴적하다 퇴적하다 [toejeoghada] /be accumulated; accumulate — For a large amount of something to be stacked in layers, or to stack a large amount of something in layers./be deposited — For substance such as soil, the bones of dead creatures, etc., to be delivered by streaming water, wind, an iceberg, etc., and stacked in a certain place./
퇴조 퇴조 [toejo] /ebb tide; low water — The state of power, influence, etc., becoming weak./
퇴조되다 퇴조되다 [toejodoeda] /ebb — For power, influence, etc., to be made weak./
퇴조하다 퇴조하다 [toejohada] /ebb — For power, influence, etc., to become weak./
퇴직 퇴직 [toejig] /resignation; retirement — An act of resigning from one&apos;s present job or duty./
퇴직금 퇴직금 [toejiggeum] /severance pay; retirement allowance — The money that an employer gives to a person who resigns from a job./
퇴직하다 퇴직하다 [toejighada] /retire — To resign voluntarily from one's present job or duty./
퇴진 퇴진 [toejin] /decampment; retirement — An act of all the members or the head of a certain organization retiring./
퇴진하다 퇴진하다 [toejinhada] /decamp; retire; resign — For all the members or the head of a certain organization to retire./
퇴짜 퇴짜 [toejja] /rejection — The act of not accepting and refusing an item, opinion, person, etc., or such an item, opinion or person./
퇴짜(를) 놓다 퇴짜(를) 놓다 [toejja(reul) nohda] /reject; refuse; turn down — To not accept and reject an object, opinion, person, etc./
퇴짜(를) 맞다 퇴짜(를) 맞다 [toejja(reul) majda] /be rejected; be refused; be turned down — For an object, opinion, person, etc., to be rejected./
퇴출 퇴출 [toechul] /leaving; withdrawal — An act of leaving a post, place, etc., voluntarily, or being expelled./
퇴출하다 퇴출하다 [toechulhada] /leave; withdraw — To leave a post, place, etc., voluntarily, or to be expelled./
퇴치 퇴치 [toechi] /eradication; wiping out; elimination — An act of repulsing and getting rid of an enemy, a disease, etc./
퇴치되다 퇴치되다 [toechidoeda] /be eradicated; be wiped out; be eliminated — For an enemy, a disease, etc., to be repulsed and be gotten rid of./
퇴치하다 퇴치하다 [toechihada] /eradicate; wipe out; eliminate — To repulse and get rid of an enemy, a disease, etc./
퇴폐 퇴폐 [toepye] /degeneration; demoralization; decay — The state of morals, customs, culture, etc., becoming corrupt and not sound./
퇴폐적 퇴폐적 [toepyejeog] /being decadent; being declining — The state of morals, customs, culture, etc., being corrupt and not sound./decadent; declining — Morals, customs, culture, etc., being corrupt and not sound./
퇴폐주의 퇴폐주의 [toepyejuui] /decadence; decadentism — The state of morals, customs, culture, etc., becoming corrupt and not being sound; or such an attitude./
퇴폐하다 퇴폐하다 [toepyehada] /be demoralized; fall into decay — For morals, customs, culture, etc., to become corrupt and not sound./
퇴학 퇴학 [toehag] /leaving school — The state of a student who stops attending school./expulsion from school — A decision to make a student who behaves badly, for example by breaking school rules, leave school./
퇴학시키다 퇴학시키다 [toehagsikida] /expel someone from school — To make a student stop attending school./
퇴학하다 퇴학하다 [toehaghada] /leave school — For a student to stop attending school./
퇴행 퇴행 [toehaeng] /regression; retrogression — An act of going backward in space, or returning to the past in time./degeneration; moving back — An act of returning to the state before something was developed./
퇴행하다 퇴행하다 [toehaenghada] /regress; retrogress — To go backward in space, or to return to the past in time./degenerate; move back — To return to the state before something was developed./
퇴화 퇴화 [toehwa] /degeneration; moving back — An act of returning to the state before something was developed./atrophy — An act of an organ or tissue of a living creature changing to the form before its evolution or development, as it becomes simpler and smaller; or such a change./
퇴화되다 퇴화되다 [toehwadoeda] /be degenerated; be moved back — For something to return to the state before its development./be atrophied — For an organ or tissue of a living creature to be changed to the form before its evolution or development, as it becomes simpler and smaller./
퇴화하다 퇴화하다 [toehwahada] /degenerate; move back — To return to the state before something was developed./atrophy — For an organ or tissue of a living creature to change to the form before its evolution or development, as it becomes simpler and smaller./
툇마루 툇마루 [toesmaru] /toenmaru — A type of traditional Korean narrow wooden veranda made up of floorboards, which runs along the perimeter of the main floor./
투 투 [tu] /manner; fashion — A method which repeats habitually or is noticeable especially in someone's speech, writing, behavior, etc./
투계 투계 [tugye] /cockfight — An act of making roosters fight in competition; or such a game./fighting cock; gamecock — A rooster that is raised to fight in a cockfight./
투고 투고 [tugo] /unsolicited submission; unsolicited contribution — An act of someone not requested to write something sending a manuscript to a newspaper, magazine, etc., asking the media to run it, or such a manuscript./
투고되다 투고되다 [tugodoeda] /be submitted without being solicited — For a manuscript to be sent to a newspaper, magazine, etc., from someone not requested to write something, asking the media to run it./
투고란 투고란 [tugoran] /reader’s column page — In a newspaper, a magazine, etc., the page on which columns or letters from readers are printed./
투고하다 투고하다 [tugohada] /submit something without being solicited — For someone not requested to write something to send a manuscript to a newspaper, magazine, etc., asking the media to run it./
투과 투과 [tugwa] /penetration; going through — An act of light, liquid, sound, etc., making a hole or holes into a substance and passing through it./
투과되다 투과되다 [tugwadoeda] /be penetrated; being gone through — For light, liquid, sound, etc., to make a hole or holes into a substance and pass through it./
투과하다 투과하다 [tugwahada] /penetrate; go through — For light, liquid, sound, etc., to make a hole or holes in a substance and pass through it./
투구 투구 [tugu] /helmet; headpiece — (archaic) An iron cap, worn to protect a soldier's head during a battle./throwing a ball; pitching; thrown ball — In baseball, bowling, etc., an act of throwing a ball, or such a ball./
투기 투기 [tugi] /speculation — An act of investing money or buying and selling goods, in order to gain the profit created by a price change./jealousy — The hatred and dislike toward one's spouse or lover when he/she likes someone else./
투기꾼 투기꾼 [tugikkun] /speculator — A person whose job it is to invest money or to buy and sell goods, in order to gain the profit created by a price change./
투기성 투기성 [tugiseong] /being speculative — The characteristic of investing money or buying and selling goods, in order to gain the profit created by a price change./
투기하다 투기하다 [tugihada] /speculate — To invest money or to buy and sell goods, in order to gain the profit created by a price change./
투덜거리다 투덜거리다 [tudeolgeorida] /grumble — To repeatedly complain about something in a voice which is too small and low to be heard by others./
투덜투덜 투덜투덜 [tudeoltudeol] /grumblingly — A word describing someone repeatedly complaining about something in a voice which is too small and low to be heard by others./
투덜투덜하다 투덜투덜하다 [tudeoltudeolhada] /grumble — To repeatedly complain about something in a voice which is too small and low to be heard by others./
투두둑 투두둑 [tududug] /pitter patter — A word imitating the sound made when hailstones, raindrops, etc., strongly fall on the ground or leaves./
투망 투망 [tumang] /casting a net — An act of throwing a net into the water to catch fish./casting a net; throw a net — A net in the shape of a cone, with a net rope on the top and weights at the bottom./
투매 투매 [tumae] /sacrifice sale; dumping — An act of selling off a stock or bond at a cheap price, despite a loss./
투매하다 투매하다 [tumaehada] /sell at a loss; dump — To sell off a stock or bond at a cheap price, despite a loss./
투명 투명 [tumyeong] /clarity — The state of water, glass, etc., being transparent./certainty; clarity — The state of a person's words, attitude, situation, etc., being clear./certainty; clarity — The state of upcoming developments, future outlook, etc., being clear, making it possible to guess in advance./
투명하다 투명하다 [tumyeonghada] /clear — Water, glass, etc., being transparent./certain; clear — A person's words, attitude, situation, etc., being clear./certain; clear — Upcoming developments, future outlook, etc., being clear, making it possible to guess in advance./
투박스럽다 투박스럽다 [tubagseureobda] /crude; coarse — The appearance of someone or something being just tough and bad./unsophisticated — One’s words, behavior, etc., being tough and not refined./
투박하다 투박하다 [tubaghada] /crude; coarse — The appearance of someone or something being just dull and sturdy./unsophisticated — One’s words, behavior, etc., being tough and not refined./
투병 투병 [tubyeong] /fighting against a disease — An act of fighting a disease with a strong will to recover./
투병하다 투병하다 [tubyeonghada] /fight against a disease — To fight a disease with a strong will to recover./
투사 투사 [tusa] /shooting; throwing — An act of throwing or shooting a spear, cannonball, etc./projection — An act of waves of light or sound reaching an object./projection — The state of denying one's own situation, while blaming something else or saying that something else is responsible, when one cannot accept one's own personality, emotion, behavior, etc., or when one has an unsatisfiable desire./projection — An act of light penetrating an object./fighter — A person who fights on a battlefield or in an arena./activist — A person who actively protests at the front of a social movement, etc./
투사기 투사기 [tusagi] /projector — A machine used to enlarge and project video images onto a screen./
투사되다 투사되다 [tusadoeda] /be shot; be thrown — For a spear, cannonball, etc., to be thrown or shot./be projected — For waves of light or sound to be made to reach an object/be projected — For one's own situation to be denied, while blaming something else or saying that something else is responsible, when one cannot accept one's own personality, emotion, behavior, etc., or when one has an unsatisfiable desire./
투사하다 투사하다 [tusahada] /shoot; throw — To throw or shoot a spear, cannonball, etc./project — For waves of light or sound to reach an object./project — To deny one's own situation, while blaming something else or saying that something else is responsible, when one cannot accept one's own personality, emotion, behavior, etc., or when one has an unsatisfiable desire./project — For light to penetrate an object./
투서 투서 [tuseo] /sending an anonymous letter; anonymous letter — An act of writing and secretly sending a letter to an organization or a designated recipient, to report an unrevealed fact or someone's fault; or such a letter./
투서하다 투서하다 [tuseohada] /send an anonymous letter — To write and secretly send a letter to an organization or a designated recipient, to report an unrevealed fact or someone's fault./
투석 투석 [tuseog] /stone-throwing; thrown stone — An act of throwing a stone, or such a stone./
투수 투수 [tusu] /pitcher — In baseball, a player who throws a ball, which a hitter might hit with a bat, toward a catcher./
투숙 투숙 [tusug] /stay; being lodged — The state of staying in such lodging facilities as an inn, a hotel, etc/
투숙객 투숙객 [tusuggaeg] /guest; lodger — A person who stays in such lodging facilities as an inn, a hotel, etc./
투숙하다 투숙하다 [tusughada] /stay; be lodged — To stay in such lodging facilities as an inn, a hotel, etc./
투시 투시 [tusi] /seeing through; penetration — An act of seeing through a covered or blocked object./understanding — The state of understanding the hidden meaning of a certain subject./
투시되다 투시되다 [tusidoeda] /be seen through; be penetrated — For a covered or blocked object to be seen through./be understood — For the hidden meaning of a certain subject to be understood./
투시하다 투시하다 [tusihada] /see through; penetrate — To see through a covered or blocked object./understand — To understand the hidden meaning of a certain subject./
투신 투신 [tusin] /devotion; dedication — The state of passionately making all-out efforts in a certain task, job, field, etc./death-leap — An act of jumping from a high place to commit suicide./
투신하다 투신하다 [tusinhada] /devote oneself to; dedicate oneself to — To passionately  make one’s efforts in a certain task, job, field, etc./off oneself — To jump from a high place to commit suicide./
투약 투약 [tuyag] /administering a dose; injection — An act of prescribing medicine or giving an injection to a patient./
투약구 투약구 [tuyaggu] /pharmacist office; medicine window — A designated place in a drugstore, hospital, etc., where one can have one's prescription filled or receive medicine./
투약되다 투약되다 [tuyagdoeda] /be prescribed; be dosed; be injected — For medicine to be prescribed or for an injection to be given to a patient./
투약하다 투약하다 [tuyaghada] /administer a dose to a patient; administer a dose; inject — To prescribe medicine or give an injection to a patient./
투여 투여 [tuyeo] /dosage; medication — The act of feeding medicine to or giving a shot to someone./injection — The act of investing money or efforts into something./
투여하다 투여하다 [tuyeohada] /dose; administer — To give or inject medicine, etc., into a person/
투영 투영 [tuyeong] /projection; reflection — An act of reflecting the shadow of an object on the surface of another object, or the reflected shadow./reflection; mirroring — (figurative) An act of expressing something by reflecting it in something else./
투영하다 투영하다 [tuyeonghada] /project; reflect — To reflect the shadow of an object on the surface of another object./reflect; mirror — (figurative) To express something by reflecting it in something else./
투옥 투옥 [tuog] /imprisonment — An act of locking someone up in a prison./
투옥되다 투옥되다 [tuogdoeda] /be imprisoned; be jailed; be confined — To be locked up in a prison./
투옥하다 투옥하다 [tuoghada] /imprison; jail; confine — To lock someone up in a prison./
투우 투우 [tuu] /bullfighting; fighting bull — A game in which a bull fights another bull, or such a bull./bullfighting — An act of a person and a bull fighting, or such a game./
투우사 투우사 [tuusa] /bullfighter; matador — A person who fights a bull in a bullfight./
투입 투입 [tuib] /throwing in; inserting — An act of throwing something into something else./investment; spending; hiring — An act of putting a person, object, money, etc., where necessary./
투입구 투입구 [tuibgu] /slot; drop — A hole or slot through which one puts money, an object, etc./
투입되다 투입되다 [tuibdoeda] /be thrown in; be inserted — For something to be thrown into something else./be invested; be spent; be hired — For a person, object, money, etc., to be put where necessary./
투입하다 투입하다 [tuibhada] /throw in; insert — To throw something into something else./invest; spend; hire — To put a person, object, money, etc., in a place he/she/it is needed./
투자 투자 [tuja] /investment — An act of spending money, time, or energy in a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투자가 투자가 [tujaga] /investor — A person who spends money, time, or energy in a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투자되다 투자되다 [tujadoeda] /be invested — For money, time, or energy to be spent in a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투자액 투자액 [tujaaeg] /investment; amount of investment — An amount of money to be invested or already invested in a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투자자 투자자 [tujaja] /investor — A person who spends money, time, or energy in a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투자하다 투자하다 [tujahada] /invest — To spend money, time, or energy on a certain project or business, to gain a profit./
투쟁 투쟁 [tujaeng] /fight — A fight to beat a certain opponent./struggle; protest — In a social movement, labor movement, etc., an act of fighting against people of different beliefs or of different groups, to win something./
투쟁하다 투쟁하다 [tujaenghada] /fight — To fight to beat a certain opponent./struggle; protest — In a social movement, labor movement, etc., to fight against people of different beliefs or of different groups, to win something./
투정 투정 [tujeong] /complaining; grumbling; growling — An act of badgering someone for more of something or for a new one, when something is in shortage or is not satisfactory./
투정하다 투정하다 [tujeonghada] /complain; grumble; growl — To badger someone for more of something or for a new one, when something is in shortage or is not satisfactory./
투지 투지 [tuji] /combative spirit; fight — One's strong and firm intention to fight./
투지력 투지력 [tujiryeog] /combative spirit; fight — One's strong and firm intention or power to fight./
투척 투척 [tucheog] /throwing — An act of pitching an object, etc./
투척하다 투척하다 [tucheoghada] /throw — To pitch an object, etc./
투철하다 투철하다 [tucheolhada] /thorough — Knowledgeable and accurate in a field./clear; strong — Deeply clear and allowing neither mistake nor weakness./
투표 투표 [tupyo] /vote; ballot; poll — An act of indicating one's opinion in a ballot and submitting it, to elect someone or to make a decision about something./
투표권 투표권 [tupyogwon] /the right to vote — The right with which one can vote./
투표소 투표소 [tupyoso] /polling place — A place where one can vote./
투표용지 투표용지 [tupyoyongji] /ballot; ballot paper — The paper with a set form which is used for voting./
투표율 투표율 [tupyoyul] /voter turnout — The ratio of actual voters to the total number of eligible voters./
투표일 투표일 [tupyoil] /voting day; polling day — The day on which people vote./
투표자 투표자 [tupyoja] /voter — A person who votes./
투표장 투표장 [tupyojang] /polling place — A place where one can vote./
투표지 투표지 [tupyoji] /ballot; ballot paper — The paper with a fixed form which is used for voting./
투표하다 투표하다 [tupyohada] /vote; cast a ballot — To indicate one's opinion in a ballot and submit it, to elect someone or to make a decision about something./
투표함 투표함 [tupyoham] /ballot box — A box into which one puts a ballot on which one has indicated one's opinion, to elect someone or to make a decision about something./
투피스 투피스 [tupiseu] /two-piece suit; suit-dress — A woman's outer garment worn as a set, made of two pieces in the same fabric./
투하 투하 [tuha] /drop; airdrop — An act of throwing something down./investment — An act of putting supplies, money, efforts, etc., in where it is needed./
투하되다 투하되다 [tuhadoeda] /be dropped; be airdropped — For something to be thrown down./be invested — For supplies, money, efforts, etc., to be put in where it is needed./
투하하다 투하하다 [tuhahada] /drop; airdrop — To throw something down./invest — To put supplies, money, efforts, etc., in where it is needed./
투항 투항 [tuhang] /surrender — An act of capitulating to an enemy./
투항하다 투항하다 [tuhanghada] /surrender — To capitulate to an enemy./
투혼 투혼 [tuhon] /fighting spirit — A brave spirit which fights to the end./
툭 툭 [tug] /pop — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly pops up or bursts open, or describing such a scene./with a thump — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly falls down, or describing such a scene./bluntly — A word imitating the sound made when one talks bluntly or disapprovingly./in one’s way — A word imitating the sound made when something gets in someone's way or gets kicked, or describing such a scene./tap-tap; gently — A word imitating the sound made when one gently taps or touches something, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when one gently shakes or bounces something, or describing such a scene./simply; easily — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly breaks suddenly and easily, or describing such a scene./bulgingly — A word describing a part of something protruding./openly — A word describing a place with an open view, or someone speaking frankly./
툭툭 툭툭 [tugtug] /pop-pop — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly keeps popping up or bursting open, or describing such a scene./with a thump — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly keeps falling down, or describing such a scene./bluntly — A word describing someone who keeps talking bluntly or disapprovingly./in one’s way — A word imitating the sound made when something keeps getting in someone's way or getting kicked, or describing such a scene./tap-tap — A word imitating the sound made when one gently keeps tapping or touching something, or describing such a scene./gently — A word imitating the sound made when one gently keeps shaking or bouncing something, or describing such a scene./simply; easily — A word imitating the sound made when something suddenly keeps breaking suddenly and easily, or describing such a scene./bulgingly — A word describing several parts of something protruding here and there./
툭툭하다 툭툭하다 [tugtughada] /thick; close-woven — For a cloth, etc. being closely-knit with strong thread or being thick as much cotton is stuffed in it,/thick — Being a little thick as a little moisture is contained./rich — One’s property, household, etc., being abundant./loud — A voice being loud and rough./
툭하면 툭하면 [tughamyeon] /easily; readily — Immediately at the slightest provocation./
툴툴 툴툴 [tultul] /grumpily — A word describing someone complaining a lot, because he/she does not approve of something or someone./strongly — A word describing someone dusting off clothes, etc., strongly./courageously — A word describing one shaking off an inner thought, etc., or getting over a difficulty./
툴툴거리다 툴툴거리다 [tultulgeorida] /grumble; complain — To complain a lot, repeatedly, because one does not approve of something or someone./
툴툴대다 툴툴대다 [tultuldaeda] /grumble; complain — To complain a lot, repeatedly, because one does not approve of something or someone./
툴툴하다 툴툴하다 [tultulhada] /grumble; complain — To complain a lot because one does not approve of something or someone./
퉁 퉁 [tung] /with a thump — A word imitating the sound made when a big drum or an empty wooden pail is beaten./with a stamp — A word imitating the sound made when a foot stamps a hard spot strongly./in drops — A word imitating the sound made when a water drop, small lump, empty object, etc., falls./boom — A word imitating the sound made when a shell, etc., is fired./bouncily — A word describing the state of a bouncy object bouncing a little heavily./
퉁겨지다 퉁겨지다 [tunggyeojida] /be dislocated — For a supported or closely-weaved object to be twisted or to come out, as a result of being dislocated./slip; be disclosed — For a hidden incident or object to appear unintentionally./miss — For an opportunity one hoped for to not be realized unexpectedly./be dislocated — For a joint of bones to be dislocated./
퉁기다 퉁기다 [tunggida] /reject — To decline someone’s demand, opinion, etc./play; pluck — To pull and release the strings of a string instrument, producing sounds./
