퉁소 퉁소 [tungso] /tungso — A traditional Korean musical instrument with five holes in the front and one hole on the back, made of bamboo and held vertically while being played./
퉁퉁 퉁퉁 [tungtung] /fatly; corpulently — A word describing one’s wide body as a result of one’s putting on weight./swollenly — A word describing a protruding part of something as it has swelled up./with a thump — A word imitating the sound made when a big drum or an empty wooden pail is repeatedly beaten./with a stamp — A word imitating the sound made when a foot stamps a hard spot strongly and repeatedly./boom boom — A word imitating the sound made when shells, etc., are fired repeatedly./in drops — A word imitating the sound made when big water drops or small lumps keep falling./bouncily — A word imitating the sound made when a bouncy object keeps bouncing a little heavily, or describing such a scene./in operation — A word imitating the sound made when a big machine is operated./
퉁퉁하다 퉁퉁하다 [tungtunghada] /fat; corpulent — A person's body being wide as a result of putting on weight./swollen — A part of something protruding as it has swelled up./
