트이다 트이다 [teuida] /get cleared — For something that has been closed or blocked to be cleared and become passable./be open — For a market, etc., to be open./start business — For a business relationship or network to form./get lucky — For bad luck to pass, improving one's situation./be relieved; be refreshed — For one's mind or emotion to get over a worry or trouble./have an insight — For one's thought or intelligence to reach a substantially high level from a low level./have a clear voice — For a voice hardly heard due to a sore throat, etc., to be heard again./
트집 트집 [teujib] /fault; hole — To complain or make trouble for no reason by making a big deal out of a trivial mistake, or such complaint or trouble./
트집(을) 걸다 트집(을) 걸다 [teujib(eul) geolda] /find fault with; pick a hole — To make a complaint or cause trouble by finding fault with someone or making a false accusation against him/her./
