튼튼하다 튼튼하다 [teunteunhada] /strong — Very hard and firm./healthy — One's body, bones, teeth, etc., being hard, firm, and healthy./stable; strong — A group or an organization being stable and not easily collapsed,/strong; solid — One's ideology or mind not shaking and being certain./
튼튼히 튼튼히 [teunteunhi] /strongly — In the manner of being very hard and firm./healthily — In the manner of one's body, bones, teeth, etc., being hard, firm, and healthy./stably; strongly — In the manner of a group or an organization being stable and not easily collapsing,/strongly; solidly — In the manner of one's ideology or mind not shaking and being certain./
틀 틀 [teul] /mold — A frame that is used to produce the same things repeatedly in a solid or semi-solid state./frame; framework — Something that serves as a framework or basis for something else./framework; box — A certain manner or form./figure — The outer appearance or shape of the human body./
