틀다 틀다 [teulda] /twist — To twist and turn one’s body or part of one’s body in another direction./twist — To turn a screw, faucet, knob, etc./turn — To operate a device such as a water tap, making water run./turn on — To operate a machine or device./turn on; play — To operate a certain device, making a sound heard or image seen./twist; distort — To cause something which has proceeded well to become difficult or go wrong./do one’s hair up — To make one's hair into a mass and raise it on the top of one’s head with a topknot, chignon, etc./make; build; weave — To make a cottage, nest, straw mat, etc., by weaving it with straw, bamboo strips, etc./fluff — To spread cotton using a willowing machine./coil — For a snake to coil its body in circles./move — To make a pose by moving one’s body./turn — To turn an object moving in a certain direction to another direction./
틀리다 틀리다 [teulrida] /be wrong; be incorrect — For a calculation, answer, fact, etc., to not be correct./be frustrated; be baffled — For something hoped for or intended to go wrong./be warped; be twisted — For one's mind or behavior to be extremely twisted, not upright./be twisted — For a whole or a part of one's body to be turned around to a direction different from way one is facing./be twisted; be wound — For a screw, faucet, knob, etc., to be turned or wound./become angry — For one's emotion, psychological state, etc., to become worse./grow apart — For a relationship with someone to become bad./
틀림없다 틀림없다 [teulrimeobsda] /sure enough; invariably right; unfailing — Absolutely correct, not wrong at all./
틀림없이 틀림없이 [teulrimeobsi] /surely enough — Absolutely correctly, without a chance of being wrong./
틀어넣다 틀어넣다 [teuleoneohda] /squeeze; cram; stuff — To push something into a small space effortfully./
틀어막다 틀어막다 [teuleomagda] /fill; stuff; stop — To prevent flow along a passage by thrusting something into it./hide; shut — To intentionally prevent a fault from being known./
틀어박다 틀어박다 [teuleobagda] /squeeze; cram; stuff — To thrust and push something into a small space effortfully./store something randomly — To keep something in a certain place for a long period./
