틀어잡다 틀어잡다 [teuleojabda] /grasp — To hold something in one’s hand tightly./control — To make someone do as one wants him/her to do./
틀어쥐다 틀어쥐다 [teuleojwida] /grab — To hold something in one’s hands tightly./take control — To have absolute control over something./
틀어지다 틀어지다 [teuleojida] /be twisted — For something to become bent or twisted, to no longer be square or straight./be messed up — For an intended task to be made difficult or to go wrong./be turned — For someone or something to be turned o a certain direction, that is not the original direction./turn sulky — To become angry and sullen./be estranged — For two people in a relationship to grow apart./
틈 틈 [teum] /crack; crevice — The space forming in between when an object is divided./a spot inside a crowd — A spot among gathered people./opportunity — The chance to do a certain act./distance — The distance between people./time; meantime — A bound noun indicating the short time during which one can do something./
틈나다 틈나다 [teumnada] /have spare time — To get to have more time to do something./
틈바구니 틈바구니 [teumbaguni] /crack; crevice — (disparaging) A space forming in between when an object is divided./a spot inside a crowd — (disparaging) A spot among gathered people./opportunity — (disparaging) A chance to do a certain act./distance; gap — (disparaging) The distance between people./
틈바귀 틈바귀 [teumbagwi] /crevice — (disparaging) A space forming as something is split./through people — (disparaging) The inside of a cluster of people./opportunity — (disparaging) The opportunity to do a certain behavior./discord; grudge — (disparaging) An awkward or angry feeling created between people./
틈새 틈새 [teumsae] /crack; crevice — The space forming in between when an object is divided./a spot inside a crowd — A  spot among gathered people./opportunity — A  chance to do a certain act./distance — The distance between people./
틈새시장 틈새시장 [teumsaesijang] /niche market — A market whose supply side is empty, because the very product which buyers want is not available despite the availability of similar products./
틈서리 틈서리 [teumseori] /side of a crack — One edge of the cracked part of something./
틈타다 틈타다 [teumtada] /seize; take advantage of — To capture the right time for something or make the most of a chance./
틈틈이 틈틈이 [teumteumi] /in cracks — In every crack./in spare moments — Every time when one has more time./
틔다 틔다 [tuida] /get cleared — For something that has been closed or blocked to be cleared and become passable./start business — For a business relationship or network to form./get lucky — For bad luck to pass, improving one's situation./be relieved; be refreshed — For one's mind or emotion to get over a worry or trouble./have insight — For one's thought or intelligence to reach a substantially high level from a low level./have a clear voice — For a voice hardly heard due to a sore throat, etc., to be heard again./
틔우다 틔우다 [tuiuda] /clear; open — To remove blocking objects and make the part passable./freshen — To help one's mind or heart to escape from a heavy and stuffy state./bring on; improve — To make one's thought or intellectual capacity reach a significant level./clear — To make one's failing voice from a sore throat, etc., come out again./have someone start business with — To make one form a relationship with someone with whom one trades things mutually./make something sprout — To make a sprout, shoot, etc., start to newly spring up./
티 티 [ti] /dirt — A very tiny fragment like dust./fault; defect — A very trivial fault or defect./trace — A certain attitude or hint./trace — A word indicating “a certain attitude or hint”./T-shirt — A short-sleeved shirt that looks like the letter 'T'./tea — Tea, especially black tea./
티격태격 티격태격 [tigyeogtaegyeog] /in a quarrel — A word describing people not agreeing and arguing back and forth with each other, while trying to determine right from wrong./
티격태격하다 티격태격하다 [tigyeogtaegyeoghada] /bicker with each other; quarrel — To not agree and argue back and forth with someone, while trying to determine right from wrong./
티끌 티끌 [tikkeul] /dirt — Motes and dust./tiny amount — Something very tiny in size or quantity./
티끌 모아 태산 티끌 모아 태산 [tikkeul moa taesan] /Gathering dirt to make a big mountain; Many a mickle makes a muckle; Many drops make a shower; Little and often fills the purse — An expression meaning even very small things can become huge if they accumulate./
티눈 티눈 [tinun] /corn — A round, swollen callus that erupts on one's hand or foot./
티스푼 티스푼 [tiseupun] /teaspoon — A small spoon used when drinking tea./
티읕 티읕 [tieut] /tieut — The name of the consonant 'ㅌ' in the Korean alphabet./
팀 팀 [tim] /team — A group of people who do the same kind of work./team — In a sport game held in two groups, a group organized with two or more members./
팀원 팀원 [timwon] /team member — A member of a group of people that work together./
팀장 팀장 [timjang] /team leader — A person who leads a team whose members do the same kind of work for a company, etc./
팀파니 팀파니 [timpani] /timpani; kettledrum — A percussion instrument made by covering a hemispherical, copper body with cowhide, and producing sounds when a player beats the instrument with drumsticks./
팁 팁 [tib] /tip — In a hotel, restaurant, etc., extra money given to an attending person as a way to express gratitude, in addition to the fixed price, rate, etc./
파 파 [pa] /green onion; scallion — A vegetable whose long, pointy, cylindrical leaves are empty in the center, and which is often used as garnish or seasoning due to its unique smell and flavor./faction; party — A group of people divided over a philosophy, belief, thought, behavior, etc./clan — A line of people branched out from one ancestor./fa — The fourth major note in western music./
