팔딱팔딱 팔딱팔딱 [palttagpalttag] /hoppingly; lively — A word describing someone or something jumping lightly, bouncingly, and repeatedly./with a throb — A word describing one's heart or pulse throbbing lightly and repeatedly./angrily — A word describing one's state of being angry and repeatedly expressing one's anger, rather than controlling it./
팔딱팔딱하다 팔딱팔딱하다 [palttagpalttaghada] /jump; hop; leap — To jump lightly, bouncingly, and repeatedly./get mad; lose one's temper — To become very angry and repeatedly express one's anger, rather than controlling it./throb; palpitate; pulsate — For one's heart or pulse to throb slightly and repeatedly, or to make it move in such a manner./
팔딱하다 팔딱하다 [palttaghada] /jump; hop; leap — To jump lightly, and bouncingly./throb; palpitate; pulsate — For one's heart or pulse to throb slightly, or to make it move in such a manner./
팔뚝 팔뚝 [palttug] /forearm — The body part from the elbow to the wrist./upper arm — The body part from the shoulder to the elbow./
팔뚝을 뽐내다 팔뚝을 뽐내다 [palttugeul ppomnaeda] /boast of one's upper arms — To boast of one's strength by showing one's upper arms./
팔랑 팔랑 [palrang] /in a sway — A word describing the state of something being shaken by wind lightly and strongly./with a flutter — A word describing an act of a butterfly, leaf, etc., flying lightly here and there./
팔랑개비 팔랑개비 [palranggaebi] /pinwheel — A toy with sails of paper cut into multiple strips, bent into waves, and then pinned to a stick so that they revolve in the wind./windmill — A device using the power generated by wind-spun blades./wanderer; drifter; roamer — (figurative) A person who behaves carelessly and wanders here and there, instead of staying in one place./
팔랑거리다 팔랑거리다 [palranggeorida] /keep flying; keep swaying — To be continuously shaken by wind lightly and strongly, or to make this happen./keep fluttering — For a butterfly, leaf, etc., to fly lightly and continuously, here and there, or to make this happen./
팔랑대다 팔랑대다 [palrangdaeda] /keep flying; keep swaying — To be continuously shaken by wind lightly and strongly, or to make this happen./keep fluttering — For a butterfly, leaf, etc., to fly lightly and continuously, here and there, or to make this happen./
팔랑이다 팔랑이다 [palrangida] /fly; sway — To be shaken by wind lightly and strongly, or to make this happen./flutter — For a butterfly, leaf, etc., to fly lightly here and there./
팔랑팔랑 팔랑팔랑 [palrangpalrang] /in sways — A word describing the state of something being continuously shaken by wind lightly and strongly./with flutters — A word describing an act of a butterfly, leaf, etc., flying lightly here and there continuously./
팔랑팔랑하다 팔랑팔랑하다 [palrangpalranghada] /keep flying; keep swaying — To be continuously shaken by wind lightly and strongly, or to make this happen./keep fluttering — For a butterfly, leaf, etc., to fly lightly and continuously, here and there, or to make this happen./
팔랑하다 팔랑하다 [palranghada] /fly; sway — To be shaken by wind lightly and strongly, or to make this happen./flutter — For a butterfly, leaf, etc., to fly lightly here and there./
팔리다 팔리다 [palrida] /be sold — For an object or a right to be given to someone or for one’s effort, etc., to be provided to someone after money is received for it./be pimped; (a woman) be sold — For a woman to be handed over to a brothel or a pimp for money./(a person) be traded — For a person to be traded like goods, for money./get distracted — For one's attention to be turned to something else, instead of focusing on the thing to which it should have been paid./be popular — For one’s face or name to be known widely./
팔만대장경 팔만대장경 [palmandaejanggyeong] /Palmandaejanggyeong — Tripitaka Koreana: A complete collection of Buddhist scriptures carved on over eighty thousand wooden printing blocks during the Goryeo Dynasty, located in the Haeinsa Temple in Gyeongsangnam-do, or South Gyeongsang Province; designed to thwart the Mongolian invasion through the power of Buddha, the heritage clearly attests to the excellence of the art of wood engraving during the Goryeo Dynasty./
팔매질 팔매질 [palmaejil] /throwing; slinging; hurling — An act of grabbing a small and hard stone in one's hand, shaking one's arm with all one's strength, and throwing it far./
팔매질하다 팔매질하다 [palmaejilhada] /throw a stone — To hold a small and hard stone in one's hand and throw it far by moving one's arm at full strength./criticize — (figurative) To curse or criticize someone./
팔목 팔목 [palmog] /wrist — The lower part of the arm that connects the hand and the arm./
팔방 팔방 [palbang] /all directions; all sides — Multiple directions, or multiple sides./
팔방미인 팔방미인 [palbangmiin] /beauty — A  beautiful woman with no weak spots./jack-of-all-trades — (figurative) A person who is talented in many different fields./
팔베개 팔베개 [palbegae] /pillowing one's head on someone's arm; pillow of one's arm — An act of pillowing one's head on someone's arm; or the arm used in such a manner./
팔보채 팔보채 [palbochae] /palbochae — Stir-fried seafood and vegetables, a Chinese dish made by stir-frying eight ingredients such as sea cucumbers, squid, bamboo shoots, mushrooms, shrimps, etc., in oil, adding meat stock and seasonings, and boiling it down./
팔불출 팔불출 [palbulchul] /good-for-nothing fellow — A very stupid person./
팔삭둥이 팔삭둥이 [palsagdungi] /premature infant born after eight months — A baby born two months early, not being able to complete the full pregnancy in its mother's womb./
팔소매 팔소매 [palsomae] /sleeve — Either of the parts of an upper garment that cover the arms./
팔소매를 걷다 팔소매를 걷다 [palsomaereul geodda] /roll up one's sleeves — To take the lead actively in doing something./
팔소매를 걷어붙이다 팔소매를 걷어붙이다 [palsomaereul geodeobutida] /roll up one's sleeves — To take the lead actively in doing something./
팔순 팔순 [palsun] /eightieth year since one's birth — The age of eighty./
팔십 팔십 [palsib] /eighty — The number that is the product of eight times ten./eighty — Being the number eighty./eightieth — Being in the eightieth place./
팔씨름 팔씨름 [palssireum] /arm wrestling — A competition of arm strength/
팔아넘기다 팔아넘기다 [palaneomgida] /sell — To give an object or a right to someone or provide one’s effort, etc., to someone after receiving money for it./send one's child to work — To get a child hired at an inappropriate place to make money./sell a person — To trade a person like goods, for money./lie; betray — To go against one’s own conscience or throw away one's principles, in order to gain a profit./
팔아먹다 팔아먹다 [palameogda] /sell — To give an object or a right to someone, after receiving money for it./get distracted — To turn one’s attention or glance to other things./send a child to work — (disparaging) To send one’s child to an inappropriate place to make money./sell a woman; pimp — To hand over a woman to a brothel or a pimp for money, or to trade a person like goods for money./marry a young child; send a child to work — To send one’s child to another family as a young daughter-in-law, or son-in-law, for money; or to make a child work at a certain place./work — To provide one’s effort or labor for money./prostitute — For a woman to have sex with a man for money./betray — To deceive oneself or give up one’s conscience to gain an inappropriate advantage./depend on — To borrow someone’s power or rely on it, to gain one’s own advantage./waste time — To waste one’s time, not gaining anything./buy crops — To buy grain by paying money./
팔월 팔월 [palwol] /August — The eighth month of a year, out of twelve months./
팔을 걷고 나서다 팔을 걷고 나서다 [paleul geodgo naseoda] /roll one's arms up and take the lead; roll one's sleeves up and take the lead — To actively take the lead in doing something./
팔을 걷어붙이다 팔을 걷어붙이다 [paleul geodeobutida] /roll one's arms up; roll one's sleeves up — To actively take the lead in doing something./
팔이 안으로 굽는다 팔이 안으로 굽는다 [pali aneuro gubneunda] /Arms bend inwardly; Men are blind in their own cause — To side with someone who is close to oneself or favor something which is related to oneself to one's own advantage./
팔자 팔자 [palja] /destiny — The fate of a person's entire life that is believed to be determined by the year, month, day and time of his/her birth./
팔자(가) 늘어지다 팔자(가) 늘어지다 [palja(ga) neuleojida] /have a leisurely destiny — To live a very carefree and comfortable life./
팔자(를) 고치다 팔자(를) 고치다 [palja(reul) gochida] /fix one's destiny — For a woman to remarry./fix one's destiny — To suddenly become much wealthier than one used to be./
팔자걸음 팔자걸음 [paljageoleum] /swaggering gait — One's way of walking slowly with one's toes pointing outwards./
팔자에 없다 팔자에 없다 [paljae eobsda] /Something is not in one's destiny — For something to be ill-matched with oneself because it is uncommon or beyond one's means./
팔짝 팔짝 [paljjag] /with a jump; in flight — A word describing a sudden, light, powerful jump or flight./suddenly — A word describing one suddenly opening a door or the lid of something./
팔짝팔짝 팔짝팔짝 [paljjagpaljjag] /with jumps; in flights — A word describing a sudden, light, repeated, and powerful jump or flight./suddenly — A word describing one suddenly and repeatedly opening a door or the lid of something./
팔짱 팔짱 [paljjang] /arms crossed — The bodily position where the two arms are crossed and the hands are under the armpits./arm in arm — Of two persons being side by side, the act of one person interwining his/her arm with the other person's arm./
팔짱(을) 끼고 보다 팔짱(을) 끼고 보다 [paljjang(eul) kkigo boda] /watch with one's arms crossed — To sit by and watch without trying to solve a problem./
팔찌 팔찌 [paljji] /bracelet — A decoration item made of gold, silver, leather, etc., which is worn around one's wrist./
팔팔 팔팔 [palpal] /hard — A word describing the state of a small amount of water, oil, etc., boiling loudly and continuously./with fever — A word describing the state of one's body or the floor of a room being very hot with a high heat./boundingly — A word describing an act of a small thing flying or jumping strongly./in great flakes — A word describing the state of dust, snowflakes, powder, etc., flying violently in the wind./fiercely — A word describing the state of a flame rising in a little small scale./
팔팔하다 팔팔하다 [palpalhada] /powerful; energetic — One's energy being full and strong./short-tempered; impatient — One's personality being tough and hasty./
팔푼이 팔푼이 [palpuni] /fool; simpleton; half-wit — (disparaging) A person who is stupid and has a lot of deficiencies./
팝 팝 [pab] /western popular song — Contemporary, popular western music which many people enjoy singing./
팝송 팝송 [pabsong] /western popular song — A popular song in the west./
팝콘 팝콘 [pabkon] /popcorn — Seasoned and fried corn./
팡파짐하다 팡파짐하다 [pangpajimhada] /broad and rounded — The shape of something dilated being roundishly wide or flat./
팡팡 팡팡 [pangpang] /boom; pop — A word imitating the sound made when a balloon, bomb, etc., explodes suddenly and repeatedly./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when small holes are made repeatedly, or describing such a scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when a ball, etc., is kicked strongly and repeatedly, or describing such a scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when an elastic object is hit repeatedly, or describing such a scene./(no equivalent expression) — A word imitating the sound made when an object pops suddenly and repeatedly, or describing such a scene./with a gush — A word imitating the sound made when water or liquid pours out strongly through a slightly wide hole, or describing such a scene./heavily; cats and dogs — A word describing the state of snow or rain falling down strongly./not sparingly — A word describing an act of spending money, using water, etc., without thinking./lazily — A word describing one idling and goofing around instead of working./in hunger — A word describing one’s state of skipping meals without a choice./
팥 팥 [pat] /red bean — A dark purple grain with savory flavor that is used as an ingredient in porridge, tteok, rice cake, or bread./
팥고물 팥고물 [patgomul] /patgomul — Powdered red beans, powder made by boiling and then grinding red beans to be used for coating tteok, rice cake./
팥빙수 팥빙수 [patbingsu] /patbingsu; shaved ice with red bean topping — A desert made from finely shaved ice topped with well-cooked red beans, sugar, etc./
팥으로 메주를 쑨대도 곧이듣는다 팥으로 메주를 쑨대도 곧이듣는다 [pateuro mejureul ssundaedo godideudneunda] /believe someone's claim that a fermented soybean lump can be made from red beans — (teasing) To blindly believe what someone says./
팥을 심으면 팥이 나오고 콩을 심으면 콩이 나온다 팥을 심으면 팥이 나오고 콩을 심으면 콩이 나온다 [pateul simeumyeon pati naogo kongeul simeumyeon kongi naonda] /Red beans grow if red beans were sowed, beans grow if beans were sowed; As one sows, so shall he reap; An onion will not produce a rose — Everything has a cause and produces a result that corresponds to the cause./
팥을 콩이라 해도 곧이듣는다 팥을 콩이라 해도 곧이듣는다 [pateul kongira haedo godideudneunda] /believe someone's claim that red beans are soy beans — (teasing) To blindly believe what someone says./
팥죽 팥죽 [patjug] /patjuk; red bean porridge — A juk, a porridge, made by mashing steamed red beans and straining water from them, and then adding rice and boiling it./
팥쥐 팥쥐 [patjwi] /Patjwi — A heroine in Kongjwi Patjwi, a novel of the Joseon Dynasty; as a greedy and mean character, she works with her mother to give her stepsister Kongjwi a hard time./
패 패 [pae] /failure; loss; defeat — A failure in doing something, or an act of losing a fight, game, etc./tag; label — A small piece of paper or small wood piece on which the name, ingredients, characteristics, etc., of a certain object are indicated./nickname; bad reputation — A nickname given to someone usually as a result of a bad incident./card; tile — Each piece of card or tile in a game of flower cards or other card games; or the content indicated by each piece./group; party — A group of people who hang out together./bunch; group; gang — A unit for counting groups of people./wit; trick — A trick with which one deceives someone in a witty and clever manner./number of losses — In a sports game, a bound noun that serves as a unit for counting the number of losses./
패가망신 패가망신 [paegamangsin] /ruining both oneself and one's family — The state of wasting one's family property and losing one's health./
패거리 패거리 [paegeori] /gang — (disparaging) A group of people who hang around together./
패권 패권 [paegwon] /supreme power — The right and power one obtains by taking the highest position in a certain field./
패기 패기 [paegi] /spirit; vigor — A strong spirit in which one would try to seek a goal, despite any difficulties./
패기만만하다 패기만만하다 [paegimanmanhada] /being full of go; vigorous; ebullient — Being full of a strong spirit in which one would try to seek a goal, despite any difficulties./
패널 패널 [paeneol] /panelist — A person whose role is to give an opinion during a discussion, or to help a show host at a broadcasting program, etc.; or such a group./
패다 패다 [paeda] /come out — For an ear of a grain to come out./beat — To hit someone here and there wildly./sink; cave in — For a hole or pit to be made./be inscribed — For a hard object to be cut and for images or characters to be inscribed./cut around — A part of a cloth or paper to be cut around something./
패드 패드 [paedeu] /pad — A thick cloth put in the shoulder part of a suit jacket, to make it fit better./pad; falsies — A piece of fabric put in the chest or hip part of a woman's clothes to make her figure look nicer./sanitary pad — An object to attach to a woman's underwear during her menstruation period, so that blood will be absorbed and not leak./
패륜 패륜 [paeryun] /immorality; obliquity — An act of doing something against the morality that a person should have, or such a behavior./
패륜아 패륜아 [paeryuna] /immoral person; depraved person — Someone who does something against the basic principles of morality that a person should have./
패망 패망 [paemang] /collapse; fall — The state of perishing after losing a fight or war, etc./
패망하다 패망하다 [paemanghada] /collapse; fall — To perish after losing a fight or war, etc./
패물 패물 [paemul] /personal ornaments; accessories — An ornament made of precious metal, etc., which is attached to one's body or clothes to decorate one's looks,/
패배 패배 [paebae] /loss; defeat — An act of losing a fight, competition, etc./
패배감 패배감 [paebaegam] /sense of defeat — A sense of weakness felt when one is not confident of winning a fight, competition, etc., or the despair or shame felt after one is defeated in a fight, competition, etc./
패배시키다 패배시키다 [paebaesikida] /defeat — To make someone lose a fight, competition, etc./
패배자 패배자 [paebaeja] /loser — A person who loses a fight or game./
패배주의 패배주의 [paebaejuui] /defeatism — An attitude of voluntarily giving up something before actually trying it, because of one’s lack of confidence about victory or success./
패배하다 패배하다 [paebaehada] /lose; be defeated — To lose a fight, competition, etc./
패소 패소 [paeso] /losing a case — A failure to win a lawsuit./
패소하다 패소하다 [paesohada] /lose a case — To lose a lawsuit./
패스트푸드 패스트푸드 [paeseuteupudeu] /fast food; junk food — Food served instantly after an order is taken, like a hamburger./
패스포트 패스포트 [paeseupoteu] /passport — The document proving the identity or nationality of a person who travels to another country, and asking a hosting country to protect its holder./
패싸움 패싸움 [paessaum] /gang fight — An act of many people fighting in groups./
패악 패악 [paeag] /wickedness; viciousness — One's tendency to do things against the morality that a person should have; and one's personality being bad./
패악스럽다 패악스럽다 [paeagseureobda] /wicked; vicious — Tending to do things against the morality that a person should have; and one's personality being bad./
패악하다 패악하다 [paeaghada] /wicked; vicious — Tending to do things against the morality that a person should have; and one's personality being bad./
패인 패인 [paein] /cause of defeat; cause of failure — A cause of one's failure or loss./
패자 패자 [paeja] /loser — A person who loses a fight or game./
패자 부활전 패자 부활전 [paeja buhwaljeon] /consolation match; repechage — In a tournament, a match or game held between losers or losing teams to give another chance to participate in a match or game./
패자전 패자전 [paejajeon] /consolation match — In a fight, game, etc., a match or game held between losers or losing teams../
패잔병 패잔병 [paejanbyeong] /remnant of the enemy; straggler — A surviving soldier of the army that lost a war or battle./
패전 패전 [paejeon] /lost battle; defeat — An act of losing a fight, war, etc./
패전국 패전국 [paejeongug] /defeated country; vanquished nation — A country that lost a war./
패전하다 패전하다 [paejeonhada] /lose a battle; be defeated — To lose a fight, war, etc./
패하다 패하다 [paehada] /fail; lose; be defeated — To fail in doing a certain task, or to lose a fight or game./
패혈증 패혈증 [paehyeoljeung] /septicemia; blood poisoning — A disease causing serious poisoning or acute inflammation, as germs or toxins flow into one's veins from a pus-producing, festering wound, etc./
팩 팩 [paeg] /pack — A method of skin care, in which one applies or attaches to one's skin, etc., a mixture or dough of various chemicals, nutritional supplements, fruits, etc., made on a base of flour, eggs, red clay, etc.; or such a cosmetic product./pack — A small container made of paper or plastic paper./
팬 팬 [paen] /fan — A person who passionately loves a sport, specific art genre, or an athlete, actor, singer, etc./pan — A shallow pot with a handle, used to stir-fry or panfry food./
팬츠 팬츠 [paencheu] /panties; briefs — A very short underwear worn on one's lower body./shorts; gym pants — Shorts worn during an exercise or sports game./
팬티 팬티 [paenti] /panties; briefs — Very short underwear worn on one's lower body./
팬티스타킹 팬티스타킹 [paentiseutaking] /panty hose — A pair of stockings covering the feet to the waist./
팻말 팻말 [paesmal] /notice board; bulletin board — A board attached to a wall or a post standing on the ground, on which characters, signs, images, etc., are inscribed or  printed to inform people of something./
팽 팽 [paeng] /round and round — A word describing an act of turning around a small area once./dizzily — A word describing one's feeling of sudden blurriness and dizziness./in tears — A word describing suddenly having tears in one's eyes./
팽개치다 팽개치다 [paenggaechida] /throw; dump — To throw or dump an object because one feels annoyed or does not like it./quit — To stop what one has been doing in the middle, or to give up what one has taken care of, instead of completing one’s responsibility./
팽그르르 팽그르르 [paenggeureureu] /round and round — A word describing one’s body or an object spinning in a small area./in tears — A word describing tears suddenly forming in one’s eyes./dizzily — A word describing one’s consciousness suddenly becoming vague and dizzy./
팽배 팽배 [paengbae] /overflow; surge — The state of a certain energy, ideological trend, etc., rising very strongly./
팽배하다 팽배하다 [paengbaehada] /overflow; surge — For a certain energy, ideological trend, etc., to rise very strongly./
팽이 팽이 [paengi] /top — A toy, whipped to spin, with a round and short body, which is made by sharpening one end of its body and inserting a tip./
팽이버섯 팽이버섯 [paengibeoseos] /enoki mushroom; flammulina velutipes — A slightly yellowish, edible mushroom with a small cap and long stem./
팽이치기 팽이치기 [paengichigi] /paeng-ichigi — whipping a top: A game to make a paengi, a top, spin by whipping it./
팽창 팽창 [paengchang] /expansion — The state of something becoming bigger because it has been inflated./growth; rise — The state of a number, size, power, etc., becoming bigger./
팽창되다 팽창되다 [paengchangdoeda] /be expanded — For something to become bigger because it has been inflated./be grown; be raised — For a number, size, power, etc., to become bigger./
팽창하다 팽창하다 [paengchanghada] /expand — For something to become bigger because it has been inflated./grow; rise — For a number, size, power, etc., to become bigger./
팽팽 팽팽 [paengpaeng] /round and round — A word describing an act of spinning repeatedly in a small area./dizzily — A word describing the state of one’s consciousness becoming hazy and dizzy./brilliantly — A word describing the state of one’s brain working fast and effectively./
팽팽하다 팽팽하다 [paengpaenghada] /tight; taut — An object being straight, not being loose./even; close — The power of two things being similar./tight — Something being just tight, neither excessive nor short./difficult to please — One's personality being picky, not generous./tense — A situation, atmosphere, etc., being very stiff, not smooth./
팽팽히 팽팽히 [paengpaenghi] /tightly; tautly — In the manner of an object being straight, not being loose./evenly; closely — In the manner of two people or two objects being similar in power./tightly — In a tight amount, being neither too much nor short./fastidiously — In the personality of being picky, not generous./tensely — In a situation, atmosphere, etc., which is very stiff, not smooth./
퍼내다 퍼내다 [peonaeda] /scoop — To scoop up what is inside or stagnant and carry it outside./rattle on; shoot off one's mouth — (figurative) To keep talking or speak without thinking./
퍼덕 퍼덕 [peodeog] /with a flap; with a flutter — A word imitating the sound made when a big bird flaps its wings lightly, yet with significant motion, or describing such a scene./with a flick; with a swish — A word imitating the sound made when a big fish moves its tail lightly, yet with significant motion, or describing such a scene./with a flutter — A word imitating the sound made when a big flag, hung laundry, etc., flies in the wind strongly. or describing such a scene./
퍼덕거리다 퍼덕거리다 [peodeoggeorida] /keep flapping — For a big bird to repeatedly flap its wings lightly, yet with significant motion./keep flicking; keep swishing — For a big fish to repeatedly move its tail lightly, yet with significant motion./keep fluttering — For a big flag, hung laundry, etc., to repeatedly fly in the wind strongly./
퍼덕대다 퍼덕대다 [peodeogdaeda] /keep flapping — For a big bird to repeatedly flap its wings lightly, yet with significant motion./keep flicking; keep swishing — For a big fish to repeatedly move its tail lightly, yet with significant motion./keep fluttering — For a big flag, hung laundry, etc., to repeatedly fly in the wind strongly./
퍼덕이다 퍼덕이다 [peodeogida] /flap — For a big bird to flap its wings lightly, yet with significant motion./flick; swish — For a big fish to move its tail lightly, yet with significant motion./flutter — For a big flag, hung laundry, etc., to fly in the wind strongly./
퍼덕퍼덕 퍼덕퍼덕 [peodeogpeodeog] /with a flap; with a flutter — A word imitating the sound made when a big bird keeps flapping its wings lightly, yet with significant motion, or describing such a scene./with a flick; with a swish — A word imitating the sound made when a big fish keeps moving its tail lightly, yet with significant motion, or describing such a scene./with a flutter — A word imitating the sound made when a big flag, hung laundry, etc., keeps flying in the wind strongly. or describing such a scene./
퍼덕퍼덕하다 퍼덕퍼덕하다 [peodeogpeodeoghada] /keep flapping — For a big bird to repeatedly flap its wings lightly, yet with significant motion./keep flicking; keep swishing — For a big fish to repeatedly move its tail lightly, yet with significant motion./keep fluttering — For a big flag, hung laundry, etc., to repeatedly fly in the wind strongly./
퍼덕하다 퍼덕하다 [peodeoghada] /flap — For a big bird to flap its wings lightly, yet with significant motion./flick; swish — For a big fish to move its tail lightly, yet with significant motion./flutter — For a big flag, hung laundry, etc., to fly in the wind strongly./
