푹 푹 [pug] /soundly — A word describing an act of falling asleep or taking a good rest to recover from fatigue./with a thrust — A word describing an act of stabbing or poking something strongly and deeply./well; completely — A word describing an act of covering or wrapping something without any missing part, so that the content cannot be seen./enough; well — A word describing an act of steaming, simmering, or boiling something until it is completely cooked./completely; severely — A word describing the state of something being seriously rotten, fermented, or wet./deeply — A word describing the state of something being deeply and clearly dug or sunken./deeply; completely — A word describing the state of something deeply falling or sinking into a place./heavily — A word describing an act of falling heavily and instantly./fully — A word describing an act of scooping out a great quantity of things with a shovel, spoon, etc./deeply — A word describing an act of bending one's head very deeply./densely; much — A word imitating the sound made when powder, smoke, etc., strongly comes out through a hole, or describing such a scene./suddenly; steeply — A word describing the state of a power, ability, or quantity being greatly reduced./completely — A word describing the state of something being covered with much powder, dust, etc./
