하급생 하급생 [hageubsaeng] /junior student; underclassman — A student in a lower class in school./
하기는 하기는 [hagineun] /in fact; in truth; indeed; actually — To tell the truth./
하기야 하기야 [hagiya] /in fact; actually; in truth; as a matter of fact — Indeed, roughly speaking./
하긴 하긴 [hagin] /in fact; in truth; indeed; actually — To tell the truth./
하나 하나 [hana] /one — The state of sameness or consensus in a cause, mind, thought, etc./one — The word that is used to indicate a particular thing or person among many./only one — The word that means &quot;the only thing.&quot;/none — Not at all, not in the least./one — The word that means &quot;some&quot; without specifying anything, or a certain type./one — The very first number when counting numbers./
하나 가득 하나 가득 [hana gadeug] /full in one — Filling the whole size of a certain space./
하나같다 하나같다 [hanagatda] /as one; same; uniform — Different things or people being exactly the same in their thoughts, opinions, etc./
하나같이 하나같이 [hanagati] /uniformly; without exception — In such a manner that two or more persons or things are not a bit different from each other in appearance, reaction, etc./
하나님 하나님 [hananim] /God — A name used by Protestantism to address a god '하느님' believed by Christianity./
하나를 듣고[들으면] 열을 안다 하나를 듣고[들으면] 열을 안다 [hanareul deudgo[deuleumyeon] yeoleul anda] /know ten things after[if] listening to one thing; be quick on the uptake; have a very perceptive mind — An expression used to describe a person who is smart enough to understand many things even after he/she has listened to only a single word./
하나를 보고[보면] 열[백]을 안다 하나를 보고[보면] 열[백]을 안다 [hanareul bogo[bomyeon] yeol[baeg]eul anda] /know ten[one hundred] things after[if] watching one thing; be quick on the uptake; have a very perceptive mind — An expression meaning you can easily understand the entire situation of something only by taking a look at some aspects of it./
하나만 알고 둘을 모른다 하나만 알고 둘을 모른다 [hanaman algo duleul moreunda] /know only one thing, and not know two things — An expression meaning you look at only one aspect of something and miss the entire situation of it./
하나부터 열까지 하나부터 열까지 [hanabuteo yeolkkaji] /from one to ten — Everything whatever it is./
하나하나 하나하나 [hanahana] /each; one by one — Every single item that constitutes the whole of something./one at a time; separately — One by one./singly; individually; one by one — One person by one person./in full; fully — In detail, one by one./in everything; in every case — Every time, with a lot of conditions, excuses, etc./
하녀 하녀 [hanyeo] /maid; servant — A woman working in the kitchen or doing the chores in another's house./
하느님 하느님 [haneunim] /god — A mysterious being that is thought to have created the universe and rule the world./god; lord — In Christianity, the name that Catholics use to refer to the god they believe in./
하느님 맙소사 하느님 맙소사 [haneunim mabsosa] /Oh My God; Oh Lord — An exclamation used with a sigh when one is astonished or dumbfounded./
