하늘가 하늘가 [haneulga] /the edge of the sky; the border of the sky — The edge of the sky that appears to be bordered by the land./
하늘거리다 하늘거리다 [haneulgeorida] /sway; flutter; waver — To droop feebly and sway lightly, repeatedly; or to make it happen./fall apart — Be soft-textured so that it sways or cannot hold its shape./fool around; idle away — To enjoy one's life in a leisurely manner without being tied down to a job, work, etc./
하늘과 땅 하늘과 땅 [haneulgwa ttang] /the sky and the earth — For two things to be completely different./
하늘나라 하늘나라 [haneulnara] /heaven; paradise — In Christianity, a place governed by God, where people who believe in Jesus can go after death./
하늘대다 하늘대다 [haneuldaeda] /sway; flutter; waver — To droop feebly and sway lightly, repeatedly; or to make this happen./fall apart — Be soft-textured so that it sways or cannot hold its shape./fool around; idle away — To enjoy one's life in a leisurely manner without being tied down to a job, work, etc./
하늘빛 하늘빛 [haneulbich] /color of sky — The color of the sky./sky blue — Pale blue like the color of a clear sky./
하늘색 하늘색 [haneulsaeg] /sky blue — A pale blue color like that of a clear sky./
하늘소 하늘소 [haneulso] /longicorn beetle — An insect with a slender body, hard wings, and long antenna./
하늘에 닿다 하늘에 닿다 [haneule dahda] /reach the sky — For one's effort, devotion, love, etc., to be very huge to such an extent that it reaches the sky./
하늘에 맡기다 하늘에 맡기다 [haneule matgida] /leave something to god — To accept the result of something and take one's fate./
하늘에서 뚝 떨어지다 하늘에서 뚝 떨어지다 [haneuleseo ttug tteoleojida] /suddenly fall from the sky — To gain something as a windfall without any due efforts./
하늘은 스스로 돕는 자를 돕는다 하늘은 스스로 돕는 자를 돕는다 [haneuleun seuseuro dobneun jareul dobneunda] /Heaven helps those who help themselves — An expression meaning Heaven will help those who make efforts to succeed, and therefore it is important to make efforts to achieve something./
하늘을 보아야 별을 따다 하늘을 보아야 별을 따다 [haneuleul boaya byeoleul ttada] /You have to look up at the sky in order to pick a star — An expression meaning achieving a certain result requires effort, preparation, opportunities or adequate conditions provided/
하늘을 지붕 삼다 하늘을 지붕 삼다 [haneuleul jibung samda] /make the sky a roof — To sleep anywhere and wander from place to place without settling down./
하늘을 찌르다 하늘을 찌르다 [haneuleul jjireuda] /pierce the sky — For one's energy or force to be very strong./pierce the sky — For a mountain, tree, building, etc., to stand very high./
하늘의 별 따기 하늘의 별 따기 [haneului byeol ttagi] /picking a star in the sky — An expression used to describe something that is very hard to gain or achieve./
하늘이 노랗다 하늘이 노랗다 [haneuli norahda] /The sky is yellow — For one's energy to substantially weaken./
하늘이 노래지다 하늘이 노래지다 [haneuli noraejida] /The sky turns yellow — To feel dizzy and stunned by a sudden shock./
하늘이 두 쪽이 나도 하늘이 두 쪽이 나도 [haneuli du jjogi nado] /even if the sky splits into two pieces — No matter what happens./
하늘이 무너져도 솟아날 구멍이 있다 하늘이 무너져도 솟아날 구멍이 있다 [haneuli muneojyeodo sosanal gumeongi issda] /You will have a hole to soar through even if the sky collapses — An expression meaning there is always a way to get through hardships or difficulties no matter how severe they may be./
하늘이 무너지는 한이 있어도 하늘이 무너지는 한이 있어도 [haneuli muneojineun hani isseodo] /even if the sky collapses — No matter what happens./
하늘이 캄캄하다 하늘이 캄캄하다 [haneuli kamkamhada] /The sky is pitch-dark — To be at a loss about what to do./
하늘이 캄캄해지다 하늘이 캄캄해지다 [haneuli kamkamhaejida] /The sky turns pitch-dark — To feel dizzy and stunned by a shock./
하늘처럼 믿다 하늘처럼 믿다 [haneulcheoreom midda] /trust someone like god — To completely trust and depend on someone./
하늘하늘 하늘하늘 [haneulhaneul] /lightly; flutteringly — In the manner of drooping feebly and swaying lightly, repeatedly./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing the state of being soft-textured so that it sways or cannot hold its shape./leisurely; idly — In the state of enjoying one's life in a leisurely manner without being tied down to a job, work, etc./(no equivalent expression) — A word describing the motion of steam, smoke, heat, haze, etc., rising up little by little, repeatedly./
하늘하늘하다 하늘하늘하다 [haneulhaneulhada] /sway; flutter; waver — To droop feebly and sway lightly, repeatedly; or to make this happen./fall apart — Be soft-textured so that it repeatedly sways or cannot hold its shape./fool around; idle away — To enjoy one's life in a leisurely manner without being tied down to a job, work, etc./rise up; hover; arise — For steam, smoke, heat, haze, etc., to rise up little by little, repeatedly./fluttering; wavy; floaty — Light and soft to the extent of drooping feebly and swaying repeatedly./spongy; pulpy; squashy — An object being soft-textured so that it repeatedly sways or cannot hold its shape./
하늬바람 하늬바람 [hanuibaram] /west wind; westerly wind — Wind that blows from the west./
하다 하다 [hada] /do; perform — To perform a certain move, action, activity, etc./make — To make or buy something./wear — To wear a certain look on the face or exhibit an attitude./do; drink; smoke — To eat, drink, or smoke a cigarette, etc./wear — Wear an accessory, etc., or get dressed./work; run; engage in — To have an occupation or job, or run a business, etc./serve; play; do — To assume a position or role./get; become — To achieve certain results./buy; take — To own something by buying or receving it from someone else./cost — For the price to reach a certain level./prove; live up to — To do something that is expected of one./distinguish — To make a distinction./handle — To deal with an incident, problem, etc./pick out; choose — To select or designate something for a certain purpose./put — To place something in a certain position./decide; make up one's mind — To make a certain decision./call; name — To name and call someone./result from — To be a cause of something. OR to be the cause of something./make a transit — To go to a place for transfer./reach — To get to a certain time or period./say — To select something as a subject for conversation./say — To talk about something./say — The word that refers to a preceding phrase that describes someone's words, thoughts, etc., and modifies the following word./treat — To exert a certain influence on or deal with others./do — To complete an action in a certain way./do — The word that indicates a series or repetition of two or more things./think; figure — To think or guess./say — To say this and that./do — The word that signals a certain situation is bound to be followed by another./sound; go — To sound or make a sound in a certain way./say — The word that indicates the preceding phrase is a quote./mean — The word that means 'but,' 'so,' 'then,' 'consequently,' or 'as a result.'/hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that someone or something makes another do an action in the preceding word or falls into the state mentioned in the preceding word./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate one's hope that another person will do an action or fall into the state in the preceding word./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that one thinks a certain action should be taken or hopes that it will happen in such a way./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that one is attempting or intends to do an action in the preceding statement./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that one has no choice but to do an action in the preceding statement./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that one also does an action in the preceding word./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that the fact mentioned in the preceding statement is the reason or basis for the following statement./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that a certain action is repeated or happens often./hada — An auxiliary verb used to indicate that one has a certain feeling toward the object mentioned in the preceding word./hada — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the speaker admits or emphasizes in some way the state mentioned in the present statement./hada — An auxiliary adjective used to indicate that the fact mentioned in the present statement is the reason or evidence for the following statement./
하다못해 하다못해 [hadamoshae] /at least — Even in the worst case./
하단 하단 [hadan] /lower tier — The lower tier of something that consists of several tiers like drawers or bookshelves./lower part; bottom — The lower part in a piece of writing or page./
