형기 형기 [hyeonggi] /term in prison; jail term — The period that an offender is required to serve in prison./
형님 형님 [hyeongnim] /older brother — (honorific) A word used only by a male to refer to or address his male siblings or cousins older than himself./big brother — (honorific) A word used chiefly among men to refer to or address a person who is older than oneself./brother-in-law — A word used to refer to or address one's wife's elder brother, who is older than oneself./sister-in-law — A word used to refer to or address the elder sister of one's husband./sister-in-law — A word used to refer to or address the wife of one's husband's elder brother./older sister — A word used by an old woman to refer to or address another female older than herself in a friendly manner./
형량 형량 [hyeongryang] /sentence; penalty — The amount or severity of punishment imposed on an offender./
