확고히 확고히 [hwaggohi] /firmly; determinedly; unshakably — In the manner of one's attitude or situation, etc., being clear and unchanging./
확답 확답 [hwagdab] /definite answer; clear answer — An act of giving an answer with certainty; or such an answer./
확답하다 확답하다 [hwagdabhada] /give a definite answer — To give an answer with certainty./
확대 확대 [hwagdae] /expansion; extension; enlargement — An act of widening something to make it larger./expansion; enlargement; increase — An act of making the shape or size, etc., bigger than it was./
확대경 확대경 [hwagdaegyeong] /magnifying glass; reading glasses — Glasses made of a covex lens to make small things look larger; or a convex lens./magnifying glass — An implement made of a convex lens to make an object look larger than it really is./
확대되다 확대되다 [hwagdaedoeda] /be expanded; be extended; be enlarged — To be widened to become larger./be expanded; be enlarged; be increased — For the shape or size, etc., to be made bigger than it was./
확대하다 확대하다 [hwagdaehada] /expand; extend; enlarge — To widen something to make it larger./expand; enlarge; increase — To make the shape or size, etc., bigger than it was./
확률 확률 [hwagryul] /probability; chance — The degree of possibility that a certain event will take place under a certain condition; or the number obtained by calcuating such a degree./
확립 확립 [hwagrib] /establishment; building; forging — A state in which a thought or system, etc., becomes firm and clear; or an act of making this happen./
확립되다 확립되다 [hwagribdoeda] /be established; be built; be forged — For a thought or system, etc., to become firm and clear./
확립하다 확립하다 [hwagribhada] /establish; build; forge — To make a thought or system, etc., firm and clear./
확보 확보 [hwagbo] /securing; obtaining; reserve — An act of making sure to possess something./
확보되다 확보되다 [hwagbodoeda] /be secured; be retained; be reserved — To make sure that something is available./
확보하다 확보하다 [hwagbohada] /secure; retain; reserve — To make sure to possess something./
확산 확산 [hwagsan] /spread; dispersion; diffusion; proliferation — A state of scattering and spreading out./diffusion — A phenomenon in which  substances with different levels of concentrations gradually reach the same level of concetration over time when they are mixed./
확산되다 확산되다 [hwagsandoeda] /spread; be dispersed; be diffused; proliferate — To be scattered and spread out./be diffused — To come to reach the same level of concentration gradually over time when substances with different levels of concentration are mixed./
확산하다 확산하다 [hwagsanhada] /spread; disperse; diffuse; proliferate — To scatter and spread out./diffuse — To gradually reach the same level of concetration over time when substances with different levels of concentrations are mixed./
확성기 확성기 [hwagseonggi] /speaker — A device that makes a sound louder so that it can reach farther./
확신 확신 [hwagsin] /belief; conviction; confidence — An act of believeing firmly in something; or such a state of mind./
확신하다 확신하다 [hwagsinhada] /be convinced; be sure; be certain — To believe firmly in something./
확실성 확실성 [hwagsilseong] /certainty; sureness — A quality being certain./
확실시되다 확실시되다 [hwagsilsidoeda] /be certain; become clear — To be considered as certain./
확실시하다 확실시하다 [hwagsilsihada] /make certain; make clear — To consider something as certain./
확실하다 확실하다 [hwagsilhada] /certain; sure; confident; definite — Being absolutely true or being certain of something./
확실히 확실히 [hwagsilhi] /certainly; surely; confidently; definitely — In the manner of being absolutely true or being certain of something./
확약 확약 [hwagyag] /promise; pledge; committment — An act of promising to do something definitely; or such a promise./
확약하다 확약하다 [hwagyaghada] /promise; pledge; commit — To promise to do something definitely./
확언 확언 [hwageon] /assertion; assurance; affirmation — An act of saying that something is definitely true; or such a remark./
확언하다 확언하다 [hwageonhada] /assert; guarantee; affirm — To say that something is definitely true./
확연하다 확연하다 [hwagyeonhada] /clear; definite; obvious; certain — Being very clear./
확연히 확연히 [hwagyeonhi] /clearly; definitely; obviously — Very clearly./
확인 확인 [hwagin] /check; affirmation; confirmation; verification — An act of finding out if something is true or admitting that it is true./
확인되다 확인되다 [hwagindoeda] /be checked; be confirmed; be verified — For the truth of something to be found out or admitted./
확인서 확인서 [hwaginseo] /confirmation; certificate — A statement or document confirming that a certain assertion is true./
확인시키다 확인시키다 [hwaginsikida] /check; confirm; verify — To make another find out if something is true or admit that it is true./
확인하다 확인하다 [hwaginhada] /check; affirm; confirm; verify — To find out if something is true or admit that it is true./
확장 확장 [hwagjang] /expansion; extension; broadening — An act of increasing the size or scope of a facility, business, force, etc., to make it larger./
확장되다 확장되다 [hwagjangdoeda] /be expanded; be extended; be broadened — For the size or scope of a facility, business, force, etc., to be increased to become larger./
확장하다 확장하다 [hwagjanghada] /expand; extend; broaden — To increase the size or scope of a facility, business, force, etc., to make it larger./
확정 확정 [hwagjeong] /decision; determination; finalization — The act of making a definite decision./
확정되다 확정되다 [hwagjeongdoeda] /be decided; be determined; be finalized — For a definite decision to be made./
확정적 확정적 [hwagjeongjeog] /being definitive; being conclusive; being decisive — A state of being definitely determined./definitive; conclusive; decisive — A definite decision being made./
확정하다 확정하다 [hwagjeonghada] /decide; determine; finalize — To make a definite decision./
확증 확증 [hwagjeung] /proof positive; clear evidence — The act of proving clearly and explicitly; or such a proof./
확증되다 확증되다 [hwagjeungdoeda] /be proved; be confirmed — To be proven clearly and explicitly./
확증하다 확증하다 [hwagjeunghada] /prove; confirm — To prove clearly and explicitly./
확충 확충 [hwagchung] /increase; expansion; replenishment — An act of increasing the scope of something and filling up a deficiency./
확충되다 확충되다 [hwagchungdoeda] /be increased; be expanded; be replenished — For the scope of something to increase and for a deficiency to be filled up./
확충하다 확충하다 [hwagchunghada] /increase; expand; replenish — To increase the scope of something and fill up a deficiency./
확확 확확 [hwaghwag] /strongly; powerfully — In the manner of wind, a smell, or energy emerging suddenly, strongly, and continuously./suddenly; instantly; strongly; fiercely — A word describing the motion of fire surging suddenly, strongly, continuously./suddenly; abruptly — In the state of one's face suddenly feeling hot and turning red continuously./quickly; in an instant; in a flash; powerfully — In the manner of a series of events progressing quickly, powerfully./suddenly; powerfully — A word describing something that is tied up or shut closed suddenly untying or opening powerfully, continuously./
환 환 [hwan] /pill — A small, round type of herbal medicine, formulated by making medicinal herb powders and kneading them./pill — A unit for counting the number of small, round pieces of medicine, formulated by making medicinal herb powders and kneading them./
환각 환각 [hwangag] /hallucination — A state of perceving a certain object as real although it is not real./
환각되다 환각되다 [hwangagdoeda] /be hallucinated — To come to perceive a certain object as real although it is not real./
환각제 환각제 [hwangagje] /hallucinogen — A drug that causes one to perceive a certain object as real although it is not real./
환각하다 환각하다 [hwangaghada] /hallucinate — To perceive a certain object as real although it is not real./
환갑 환갑 [hwangab] /age 60; 60th birthday — The 60th birthday of a person./
환갑 진갑 다 지내다 환갑 진갑 다 지내다 [hwangab jingab da jinaeda] /pass one's 60th and 61st birthday — To have lived long enough./
환갑잔치 환갑잔치 [hwangabjanchi] /one's sixtieth birthday party — A party held to celebrate one's sixtieth birthday./
환경 환경 [hwangyeong] /environment — The state of nature affecting the life of living creatures./condition; situation; circumstances — The condition or situation of the surroundings affecting humans./environment; situation — The state of surroundings in which a person is living./
환경 오염 환경 오염 [hwangyeong oyeom] /environmental pollution — A phenomenon in which the natural environment is destroyed by resource developement or becomes polluted because of exhaust  from cars, waste water from factories, etc./
환경미화원 환경미화원 [hwangyeongmihwawon] /cleaner — A person who cleans a street, road, public facility, etc./
환관 환관 [hwangwan] /hwan-gwan — eunuch: A castrated man who served a king at the palace in olden times./
환국 환국 [hwangug] /homecoming; return to one´s country — The return of a person living in a foreign country to his/her own country./
환국하다 환국하다 [hwangughada] /return to one's country — For a person living in a foreign country to go back or come back to his/her own country./
환궁 환궁 [hwangung] /return to the palace — The return of a king, queen, prince, etc., to their palace./
환궁하다 환궁하다 [hwangunghada] /return to the palace — For a king, queen, prince, etc., to return to his or her palace./
환금 환금 [hwangeum] /conversion — The act of selling goods and exchanging them for money./exchange; change — The act of changing one country's currency into another's./
환기 환기 [hwangi] /arousal; awakening; stirring up — An act of bringing a person's attention to a certain matter, or stirring up public opinion, thought, etc./ventilation — An act of changing dirty, stuffy air into fresh air./
환기되다 환기되다 [hwangidoeda] /be aroused; be awakened; be stirred up — For a person's attention to be brought to a certain matter, or for public opinion, thought, etc., to be stirred up./be ventilated — For dirty, stuffy air to be changed into fresh air./
환기통 환기통 [hwangitong] /ventilator; ventilator pipe; ventilation stack — A hole made to connect the inside to the outside of a building to replace dirty, stuffy air with fresh air./
환기하다 환기하다 [hwangihada] /arouse; awaken; stir up — To bring a person's attention to a certain matter, or stir up public opinion, thought, etc./ventilate — To change dirty, stuffy air into fresh air./
환난 환난 [hwannan] /hardship; adversity; ordeal; suffering — An extremely worrying and painful situation./
환담 환담 [hwandam] /talk; chat; conversation — An act of having a friendly, agreeable conversation; or such a conversation./
환담하다 환담하다 [hwandamhada] /have a friendly talk; chat enjoyably — To have a friendly, agreeable conversation./
환대 환대 [hwandae] /hospitabillity; friendly reception — An act of welcoming a visitor warmly and treating him/her in a sincere manner./
환대하다 환대하다 [hwandaehada] /treat hospitably; treat cordially — To welcome a visitor warmly and treat him/her in a sincere manner./
환도 환도 [hwando] /return to the capital — The return of a government to its capital after it has been forced to abandon that capital temporarily due to  war, etc., and has moved to a different place./
환도하다 환도하다 [hwandohada] /return to the capital — For a government to return to the capital after having abandoned its capital temporarily due to a war, etc., and moved to a different place./
환락 환락 [hwanrag] /pleasure; amusement; delight — A state of being extremely happy and delightful; or a source of such a happiness and delight./
환락가 환락가 [hwanragga] /adult entertainment district — A street where there are many bars or gambling houses, etc./
환락하다 환락하다 [hwanraghada] /seek pleasure; entertain oneself — To feel extremely happy while enjoying doing something./
환멸 환멸 [hwanmyeol] /disillusion; disenchantment; letdown — A state in which one's dream or expectation falls to pieces; or a feeling of agony that one has in such a situation./
환부 환부 [hwanbu] /affected area; wounded part — An area of the body that is affected by illness or where a wound forms./
환불 환불 [hwanbul] /refund; money back — An act of giving back money that has been paid./
환불하다 환불하다 [hwanbulhada] /refund; give money back — To give back money that has been paid./
환산 환산 [hwansan] /conversion; change — An act of calculating and expressing a number in a different unit./
환산되다 환산되다 [hwansandoeda] /be converted; be changed — For a number to be calculated and expressed in a different unit./
환산표 환산표 [hwansanpyo] /conversion table — A table that makes conversion easier by comparing and listing quantities in differrent units of measurement./
환산하다 환산하다 [hwansanhada] /convert; change — To calculate and express a number in a different unit./
환상 환상 [hwansang] /illusion; fantasy — A vain thought that is unlikely or impossible to come true in reality./
환상곡 환상곡 [hwansanggog] /fantasia — A romantic musical composition that is produced freely without being restricted by formality./
환상적 환상적 [hwansangjeog] /being illusionary; being dreamy; being fantastic — A state in which a thought, etc., is considered empty, unlikely or impossible to come true in reality./illusionary; dreamy; fantastic — A thought, etc., being considered unrealistic, unlikely or impossible to come true in reality./
환생 환생 [hwansaeng] /reincarnation; revival — A state of coming alive again./rebirth; revival; resurrection — A state of returning from the dead./
환생하다 환생하다 [hwansaenghada] /appear; manifest — To appear like an illusion although one does not exist any more./reincarnate; revive — In Buddhism, to be born again in a different figure./
환성 환성 [hwanseong] /cheer; shout; cry — A loud and powerful sound made by many people shouting all together./cheer; shout for joy — A sound made when feeling happy and excited./
환속 환속 [hwansog] /returning to lay life; leaving the priesthood — In Buddhism, an act of quitting living as a monk and going back to a secular world./
환속하다 환속하다 [hwansoghada] /return to lay life; leave the priesthood — In Buddhism, to quit living as a monk and go back to the secular world./
환송 환송 [hwansong] /farewell; saying good-bye — The act of sending off with pleasure someone who is leaving./
환송하다 환송하다 [hwansonghada] /see off; say good-bye — To send off with pleasure someone who is leaving./
환송회 환송회 [hwansonghoe] /farewell party; going-away party — A gathering arranged to send off with pleasure someone who is leaving./
환수 환수 [hwansu] /redemption; retrieval; confiscation — An act of getting something back again./
환수되다 환수되다 [hwansudoeda] /be redeemed; be retrieved; be confiscated — To be recovered./
환수하다 환수하다 [hwansuhada] /redeem; retrieve; confiscate — To get something back again./
환승 환승 [hwanseung] /transfer; change — An act of switching to another route or means of transportation./
환승역 환승역 [hwanseungyeog] /transfer station; interchange station — A subway or rail station where one can transfer to another line./
환승하다 환승하다 [hwanseunghada] /transfer; change — To switch to another route or means of transportation./
환심 환심 [hwansim] /favor; grace; approval — A feeling of happiness and joy toward another./
환언되다 환언되다 [hwaneondoeda] /be paraphrased; be put in other words — For the preceding words to be expressed in a different way without change in their meaning./
환언하다 환언하다 [hwaneonhada] /paraphrase; put in other words — To express the preceding words in a different way without changing their meaning./
환영 환영 [hwanyeong] /phantom; ghost; hallucination — An object that seems to exist although it is not real./welcome — The act of receiving someone gladly and cordially upon his/her arrival./
환영사 환영사 [hwanyeongsa] /welcome address; welcome speech — A greeting offered to show that one receives another arriving gladly and cordially./
환영하다 환영하다 [hwanyeonghada] /welcome; greet — To receive someone arriving gladly and cordially./
환영회 환영회 [hwanyeonghoe] /welcome party; reception — A gathering arranged for greeting the arrival of someone gladly and cordially./
환원 환원 [hwanwon] /return; giving back; restoration — An act of going back to the original state; or an act of making this happen./reduction — In philosophy, an act of changing miscellaneous things or phenomena into fundamental ones./reduction — In chemistry, a phenomenon in which a substance mixed with oxygen loses the oxygen, or a substance combines with hydrogen, or certain atoms, molecules, ions, etc., acquire electrons./
환원되다 환원되다 [hwanwondoeda] /be returned; be restored — To go back to the original state./be reduced — In philosophy, for miscellaneous things or phenomena to be changed into fundamental ones./be reduced — In chemistry, for the oxygen to be removed from a substance mixed with oxygen, or for a substance to come to combine with hydrogen, or for certain atoms, molecules, ions, etc., to come to acquire electrons./
환원주의 환원주의 [hwanwonjuui] /reductionism — In philosophy, the tendency to explain a variety of phenomena through a single, fundamental principle./reductionism — In philosophy, the idea that all propositions should be reduced to observable ones./
환원하다 환원하다 [hwanwonhada] /return; restore; give back — To go back to the original state or to make this happen./reduce — In philosophy, for miscellaneous things or phenomena to change into fundamental ones; or to make this happen./reduce — In chemistry, for a substance mixed with oxygen to lose the oxygen, or for a substance to combine with hydrogen, or for certain atoms, molecules, ions, etc., to acquire electrons./
환율 환율 [hwanyul] /exchange rate — In economics, the rate at which the currency of one country is changed into that of another country./
환자 환자 [hwanja] /patient; sick person — A person who is ill due to a disease or injury./
환자복 환자복 [hwanjabog] /patient clothing; hospital gown — Clothing worn by a patient staying at a hospital./
환장 환장 [hwanjang] /going crazy; going mad; being out of one's mind — A state in which one's state of mind or behavior becomes abnormal./obssession; mania; preoccupation — (slang) A state of being so excessively obssessed with or concentrated on something that one loses one's reason./
환장되다 환장되다 [hwanjangdoeda] /go crazy; go mad; be out of one's mind — For one's state of mind or behavior to become abnormal./be obssessed; be preoccupied; be maniacal — (slang) To fall into a state of being so excessively obssessed with or concentrated on something that one loses one's reason./
환장하다 환장하다 [hwanjanghada] /go crazy; go mad; be out of one's mind — For one's state of mind or behavior to become abnormal./be obssessed; be preoccupied; be maniacal — (slang) To fall into a state of being so excessively obssessed with or concentrated on something that one loses one's reason./
환쟁이 환쟁이 [hwanjaengi] /painter; artist — (disparaging) A person who paints pictures professionally./
환전 환전 [hwanjeon] /foreign exchange; money exchange — The act of changing one country's currency into another's./
환전소 환전소 [hwanjeonso] /currency exchange counter — A place for changing money into foreign currencies or small bills or coins, etc./
환전하다 환전하다 [hwanjeonhada] /change; exchange — To exchange the currency of a country for another country's currency./
환절기 환절기 [hwanjeolgi] /change of seasons — The time when a season changes into another season./
환청 환청 [hwancheong] /auditory hallucination — A phenomenon in which one thinks one hears a sound when there is no actual sound; or such a sound./
환풍기 환풍기 [hwanpunggi] /ventilator; exhaust fan — An implement that sends out dirty and murky indoor air and lets fresh outdoor air in./
환하다 환하다 [hwanhada] /bright; light; radiant — Being very clear and bright as light shines./open; clear — Something imparting a feeling of not being confined, because it has an open view./clear; obvious — The progress or intention of a certain event being clear./fine-looking; attractive-looking — Having a pleasing, neat, and attractive appearance./bright; beaming; radiant — One's face or personality being bright and cheerful./bright; light — Color being bright and clear./familiar; knowledgeable — Having an accurate and deep knowledge about a certain task or object./refreshed — Feeling tingly, clean, and refreshed in one's mouth/
환호 환호 [hwanho] /cheer; shout of joy — An act of shouting loudly, feeling happy./
환호성 환호성 [hwanhoseong] /cheer; shout of joy — A loud shout made when feeling happy./
환호하다 환호하다 [hwanhohada] /cheer; shout for joy — To shout loudly, feeling happy./
환희 환희 [hwanhui] /delight; joy; happiness — A state of being extremely happy; or a feeling of great joy./
환희하다 환희하다 [hwanhuihada] /rejoice; exult — To be greatly joyful./
환히 환히 [hwanhi] /brightly; radiantly — In the state of being very clear and bright as light shines./openly; clearly — In the state of something imparting a feeling of not being confined, because it has an open view./clearly; obviously — In the manner of the progress or intention of a certain event being clear./attractively; finely; neatly — In the state of having a pleasing, neat, and attractive appearance./brightly; beamingly; radiantly — In the state of one's face or personality being bright and cheerful./
활 활 [hwal] /bow — A weapon used to shoot arrows, made by bending wood or iron into a half-moon shape and fastening a string to both ends./bow — An implement used for rubbing the strings in a stringed instrument./
활강 활강 [hwalgang] /downhill; sliding down — A state of sliding down a slope on skis or in a car, etc./
활강하다 활강하다 [hwalganghada] /go downhill; slide down — To slide down a slope on skis or in a car, etc./
활개 활개 [hwalgae] /limb — The part that includes the shoulder and arm or the butt and leg on both sides of the human body./wings — Both wings of a bird that are fully spread./
활개(를) 젓다 활개(를) 젓다 [hwalgae(reul) jeosda] /wave one's limbs — To walk swinging one's arms back and forth alternately./
활개(를) 치다 활개(를) 치다 [hwalgae(reul) chida] /swing one's limbs — To walk vigorously swinging one's arms back and forth./swing one's limbs — To behave in a triumphant or arrogant manner./swing the limbs — For something negative to be rampant./flap one's wings — For a bird to spread and flap its wings./
활개(를) 펴다 활개(를) 펴다 [hwalgae(reul) pyeoda] /spread out one's limbs — To stretch out one's arms and legs./spread out one's limbs — To behave in a confident manner without being swayed by others./
활극 활극 [hwalgeug] /action movie — A movie or play focusing on fights, escapes, adventure, etc./melee; fight scene — (figurative) An episode or a scene featuring violent and cruel words or actions./
활기 활기 [hwalgi] /vitality; energy; life — A lively spirit./
활기차다 활기차다 [hwalgichada] /energetic; lively; vibrant — Full of power and vitality./
활달하다 활달하다 [hwaldalhada] /broad-minded; great-hearted — Being broad-minded and big-hearted./vigorous; lively; outgoing — Being lively and cheerful./
활달히 활달히 [hwaldalhi] /broad-mindedly; great-heartedly — In the manner of being broad-minded and big-hearted./vigorously; energetically; spiritedly — In the manner of being lively and cheerful./
활동 활동 [hwaldong] /activity; movement — An act of moving one's body to perform some action./activity; effort; campaign — An act of striving to achieve a good result in a certain task./
활동가 활동가 [hwaldongga] /activist — A person who works hard to achieve a good result in a certain task./
활동력 활동력 [hwaldongryeog] /energy; power; vitality; activity — The power to move one's body to do an act or the energy to work hard to achieve a good result in a certain task./
