흐르다 흐르다 [heureuda] /flow; run — For a liquid like water, etc., to move to a lower place or pass a certain location./pass — For time or years to go by./flow; blow — To glide in the air or on the water./flow; pass — For gas, electricity, etc., to move along a cable or pipe./flow; run — For blood, sweat, tears, etc., to come out and fall from the body./run; flow; leak — For powder or particles to leak or fall through a small hole./flow — For light, sound, smell, etc., to spread gently./run — For a certain energy, state, etc., to show on the outside./run — For a certain mood, thought, etc., to continue in a certain way./show — For gloss, luster, etc., to show in a shiny manner./go; be overcome — For a person or thing to take on a tendency or to move disproportionately in a direction./
흐름 흐름 [heureum] /flow; stream; passage — A state of flowing./flow; stream; tendency; inclination — (figurative) A phenomenon that proceeds toward a certain direction./
흐리다 흐리다 [heurida] /adulterate — To mix a pure substance with foreign matter to make it unclear./cloud; blur — To not make one's words or thought clear./cloud; have a long face; look gloomy — To look gloomy, being worried or upset about something./tarnish — To ruin the mood, or hurt another's reputation or image./dim; vague; blurred — One's memory or thought not being clear./muddy; murky; turbid — A pure substance becoming unclear because it has had a foreign matter added to it./dim; blurred — Not being clear or vivid./hazy — One's calculation not being accurate./cloud; foggy — The weather not being clear due to clouds or fog./gloomy; cloudy; long-faced — Looking worried./dim; subdued — Light not being bright./
